{"parentUuid":"08f43a5a-ba3d-4906-8304-e1ca27ee6327","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0813e2c2-9e63-40ae-82ae-61cde2f8fc2a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014csKS8qnJyy3W3dmkTcFk4","type":"tool_result","content":"=== 1. HOW THE QUERY IS BUILT ===\n  if [ \"${EG_PREFETCH:-0}\" = 1 ]; then\n    pf_q=$(\"$PY\" -c \"\nimport re,sys\nt=open('$ps_file',errors='ignore').read()\nt=re.sub(r'\\`\\`\\`.*?\\`\\`\\`','',t,flags=re.S)\nt=re.sub(r'\\s+',' ',t).strip()\nprint(' '.join(t.split()[:40]))\")\n    # BUG FIX: the prefetch call must NOT consume the agent's search budget. eg-q enforces\n    # GQ_SEARCH_CAP by counting lines in $GQLOG, and the prefetch writes to that same file — so\n    # with GQ_SEARCH_CAP=1 the agent had ZERO searches available for the whole session. Measured:\n    # PF_opus_eg logged exactly 1.00 graph calls/session (the prefetch), PF_haiku_eg refused 17/17\n    # agent attempts. Point the prefetch at its own log so the agent keeps its budget.\n    GQLOG=\"$out/prefetch_calls.log\" \"$gq\" search \"$pf_q\" > \"$out/prefetch.payload\" 2>/dev/null || true\n    # EG_PREFETCH_IMPACT=1 — SECOND prefetch stage: expand the locate CHAIN.\n    #\n    # Measured: pre-edit code location is 26-44% of all tool calls (Opus 9.95/session) and the graph\n\n=== 2. HOW THE IMPACT ANCHOR IS PICKED ===\n    if [ \"${EG_PREFETCH_IMPACT:-0}\" = 1 ] && [ -s \"$out/prefetch.payload\" ]; then\n      # Parse the top hit's symbol out of the text payload stage 1 already wrote. The wrapper does\n      # NOT pass --format json through (it has its own formatting pipeline and returns empty), so\n      # asking it for JSON silently yields nothing -- verified on 3/3 instances.\n      pf_sym=$(\"$PY\" -c \"\nimport re,sys\ntry:\n    for ln in open('$out/prefetch.payload', errors='ignore'):\n        m = re.search(r'symbol=(\\S+)', ln)\n        if m:\n            print(m.group(1)); break\nexcept Exception: pass\" 2>/dev/null)\n      if [ -n \"$pf_sym\" ]; then\n        GQLOG=\"$out/prefetch_calls.log\" \"$gq\" impact \"$pf_sym\" > \"$out/prefetch_impact.payload\" 2>/dev/null || true\n      fi\n    fi\n\n=== 3. ACTUAL QUERIES SENT (first 150 chars) ===\n  carbon-2752                    Bug in method `->is()`, date with month october return true in to ask if is january <!-- 🛑 DON'T REMOVE ME. This issue template applies to all - bug\n  jekyll-8167                    slugify replaces Tamil vowel marks with hyphen - I updated to the latest `github-pages` - I ran `bundle exec jekyll doctor` to check my configuratio\n  prometheus-10633               PuppetDB Service Discovery - Numerical parameters not converted to __meta_puppetdb_parameter labels ### What did you do? Hi, We use puppetdb_sd to p\n  gson-1014                      Bug when skipping a value while using the JsonTreeReader When using a `JsonReader` to read a JSON object, `skipValue()` skips the structure successf\n\n=== 4. DO PAYLOAD BODIES CARRY LINE NUMBERS? (prompt promises 'at its real line numbers') ===\n  carbon-2752            body lines=55   carrying line numbers=0\n  redis-10095            body lines=107  carrying line numbers=0\n  lucene-13170           body lines=79   carrying line numbers=0\n\n=== 5. ARE HITS SORTED BY SCORE? ===\n  redis-10095            scores=[37.0447, 34.3022, 37.0347]  sorted=False\n  gson-1014              scores=[127.3938, 122.8574, 118.8087, 115.1544]  sorted=True\n  fmt-1683               scores=[33.6807, 30.8525, 23.3652]  sorted=True\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/suhaan/devenv","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3b76ce7e-020e-494b-a899-e39ae251a032","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:10:47.835Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== 1. HOW THE QUERY IS BUILT ===\n  if [ \"${EG_PREFETCH:-0}\" = 1 ]; then\n    pf_q=$(\"$PY\" -c \"\nimport re,sys\nt=open('$ps_file',errors='ignore').read()\nt=re.sub(r'\\`\\`\\`.*?\\`\\`\\`','',t,flags=re.S)\nt=re.sub(r'\\s+',' ',t).strip()\nprint(' '.join(t.split()[:40]))\")\n    # BUG FIX: the prefetch call must NOT consume the agent's search budget. eg-q enforces\n    # GQ_SEARCH_CAP by counting lines in $GQLOG, and the prefetch writes to that same file — so\n    # with GQ_SEARCH_CAP=1 the agent had ZERO searches available for the whole session. Measured:\n    # PF_opus_eg logged exactly 1.00 graph calls/session (the prefetch), PF_haiku_eg refused 17/17\n    # agent attempts. Point the prefetch at its own log so the agent keeps its budget.\n    GQLOG=\"$out/prefetch_calls.log\" \"$gq\" search \"$pf_q\" > \"$out/prefetch.payload\" 2>/dev/null || true\n    # EG_PREFETCH_IMPACT=1 — SECOND prefetch stage: expand the locate CHAIN.\n    #\n    # Measured: pre-edit code location is 26-44% of all tool calls (Opus 9.95/session) and the graph\n\n=== 2. HOW THE IMPACT ANCHOR IS PICKED ===\n    if [ \"${EG_PREFETCH_IMPACT:-0}\" = 1 ] && [ -s \"$out/prefetch.payload\" ]; then\n      # Parse the top hit's symbol out of the text payload stage 1 already wrote. The wrapper does\n      # NOT pass --format json through (it has its own formatting pipeline and returns empty), so\n      # asking it for JSON silently yields nothing -- verified on 3/3 instances.\n      pf_sym=$(\"$PY\" -c \"\nimport re,sys\ntry:\n    for ln in open('$out/prefetch.payload', errors='ignore'):\n        m = re.search(r'symbol=(\\S+)', ln)\n        if m:\n            print(m.group(1)); break\nexcept Exception: pass\" 2>/dev/null)\n      if [ -n \"$pf_sym\" ]; then\n        GQLOG=\"$out/prefetch_calls.log\" \"$gq\" impact \"$pf_sym\" > \"$out/prefetch_impact.payload\" 2>/dev/null || true\n      fi\n    fi\n\n=== 3. ACTUAL QUERIES SENT (first 150 chars) ===\n  carbon-2752                    Bug in method `->is()`, date with month october return true in to ask if is january <!-- 🛑 DON'T REMOVE ME. This issue template applies to all - bug\n  jekyll-8167                    slugify replaces Tamil vowel marks with hyphen - I updated to the latest `github-pages` - I ran `bundle exec jekyll doctor` to check my configuratio\n  prometheus-10633               PuppetDB Service Discovery - Numerical parameters not converted to __meta_puppetdb_parameter labels ### What did you do? Hi, We use puppetdb_sd to p\n  gson-1014                      Bug when skipping a value while using the JsonTreeReader When using a `JsonReader` to read a JSON object, `skipValue()` skips the structure successf\n\n=== 4. DO PAYLOAD BODIES CARRY LINE NUMBERS? (prompt promises 'at its real line numbers') ===\n  carbon-2752            body lines=55   carrying line numbers=0\n  redis-10095            body lines=107  carrying line numbers=0\n  lucene-13170           body lines=79   carrying line numbers=0\n\n=== 5. ARE HITS SORTED BY SCORE? ===\n  redis-10095            scores=[37.0447, 34.3022, 37.0347]  sorted=False\n  gson-1014              scores=[127.3938, 122.8574, 118.8087, 115.1544]  sorted=True\n  fmt-1683               scores=[33.6807, 30.8525, 23.3652]  sorted=True","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/suhaan/devenv","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"08f43a5a-ba3d-4906-8304-e1ca27ee6327","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"3b76ce7e-020e-494b-a899-e39ae251a032","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgGLfdojxWT6QVDYLPzB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2784,"cache_read_input_tokens":480882,"output_tokens":6969,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2784,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6969,"cache_read_input_tokens":480882,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2784,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2784},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgGLaH6SJp9gkqXjdbBo","type":"assistant","uuid":"dbf15eb8-8f3e-4a96-923b-aac04ad8a082","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:11:09.974Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"dbf15eb8-8f3e-4a96-923b-aac04ad8a082","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgGLfdojxWT6QVDYLPzB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four confirmed independently. Your thesis is correct — the locate phase isn't being dismantled, and here is exactly why:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2784,"cache_read_input_tokens":480882,"output_tokens":6969,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2784,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6969,"cache_read_input_tokens":480882,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2784,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2784},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgGLaH6SJp9gkqXjdbBo","type":"assistant","uuid":"a2728dbe-9c97-4535-9944-56c0478b4c9e","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:11:10.529Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"a2728dbe-9c97-4535-9944-56c0478b4c9e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgGLfdojxWT6QVDYLPzB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EzBKLp1rbkPUVbLTS935mW","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/modular-cooking-cupcake.md","content":"# Make the graph actually dismantle the locate phase — Opus 20-sample to −25%\n\n## Context\n\nFair baseline: Opus, Anthropic's published SWE-bench prompt verbatim to both arms, cap 120, 20\ninstances from the official 300. **tokens −11.2% CI [−27.8, +9.6], winners 12/20.**\n\nThe thesis under test: these are all large repos, so a working code index should collapse the locate\nphase on **every** instance, not half of them. Measured reality:\n\n| | measured |\n|---|---|\n| graph share of all locate operations | **0.7%** |\n| agent-initiated graph calls / session | **0.20** (16 of 20 sessions: zero) |\n| pre-edit locate, baseline → eg | 13.9 → 15.0 (**+8%**) — the tool does not reduce hunting |\n| post-edit ops that re-hunt text the payload already printed | **~40%** (5.58–7.25 / session) |\n\nSo the locate phase is not being dismantled; it is being **duplicated**. I read the transcripts and\nthe harness source and found the reasons. Four are verified by me directly; the rest come from a\n5-agent forensic sweep of all 20 sessions (38 findings) whose adversarial verification is still\nrunning, so they are marked as such.\n\n---\n\n## ROOT CAUSE 1 — the query is issue-template boilerplate, truncated at 40 words\n\n`tools/run_3arm.sh:157–161` builds the search query as: strip code fences, collapse whitespace,\n**take the first 40 words of the raw issue body.** Nothing else is removed.\n\nActual queries sent (verified from `prefetch_calls.log`):\n\n| instance | query as sent |\n|---|---|\n| carbon **+107%** | `Bug in method \\`->is()\\`, date with month october return true in to ask if is january <!-- 🛑 DON'T REMOVE ME. This issue template applies to all - bug` |\n| jekyll | `slugify replaces Tamil vowel marks with hyphen - I updated to the latest \\`github-pages\\` - I ran \\`bundle exec jekyll doctor\\` to check my configuratio` |\n| prometheus **+20%** | `PuppetDB Service Discovery - Numerical parameters not converted… ### What did you do? Hi, We use puppetdb_sd to p` |\n\nThree of four sampled queries spend most of their 40-word budget on GitHub issue-template\nboilerplate, HTML comments, or contributor checklists. Consequences found in the payloads:\ncarbon's query **self-matched the repo's own `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE.md`** (gold file absent from the\npayload entirely); jekyll ranked Markdown docs above the gold code file; prometheus's 40-word cap\n**truncated away the issue's own file+line pointer**, and path literals are not extracted or boosted\nat all.\n\n**Fix.** Before scoring: strip HTML comment blocks, issue/PR-template boilerplate, `- I ran/I read`\nchecklists and `| Software | Version |` env tables. Extract repo-relative path literals and\n`#Lnn-Lnn` anchors from the **full** text before truncating and pass them as a hard path boost.\nExclude `.github/**` and template markdown from the searchable set. Raise/replace the flat 40-word\ncap with a distinctive-token budget.\n\nBlast radius: **every instance.** This is the difference between the graph searching for the issue\nand searching for GitHub's issue template.\n\n---\n\n## ROOT CAUSE 2 — the payload is not addressable, so the agent must re-read the file\n\nThe eg prompt promises, verbatim: *\"the complete body of the enclosing function is printed verbatim\nbeneath that header, **at its real line numbers**\"*.\n\nVerified count of body lines carrying a line number:\n\n| instance | body lines | carrying line numbers |\n|---|---|---|\n| carbon | 55 | **0** |\n| redis-10095 | 107 | **0** |\n| lucene | 79 | **0** |\n\nZero, everywhere. The header carries a span (`:74-94`) but no interior line is addressable. To build\nan `Edit` anchor, a `sed -n` range, or to reason about hunk positions, the agent has to open the file\nit was just shown.\n\n**This is the mechanism behind the 40% \"re-finds payload text\" figure** — the largest single block of\nrecoverable waste in the cell, and it is present in winners (5.58/session) as much as losers\n(7.25/session).\n\n**Fix.** Prefix every printed body line with its real line number (5–6 chars/line — the header\nalready knows the span). Make `focus=` point at the highest-scoring **interior** line rather than\ncollapsing to the definition line.\n\nBlast radius: **every instance, winners included.** This is the fix that makes the tool benefit\neverything rather than only the instances whose baseline happened to flail.\n\n---\n\n## ROOT CAUSE 3 — `impact` is blind-chained to rank-1 with no gate\n\n`tools/run_3arm.sh:184–191` takes the **first `symbol=` string in the text payload** and runs\n`impact` on it. No relevance check, no kind check, no margin check. The result is injected under a\nheader telling the agent *\"You do not need to look these up yourself.\"*\n\nWhat that produced (from the payloads):\n\n| instance | impact anchor | what it actually is |\n|---|---|---|\n| carbon | `CarbonPeriod.removeFilter` | unrelated symbol; **49% of prefetch bytes** |\n| jekyll | `GitHub-Pages` | a **Markdown heading** → all-zero blast radius |\n| redis-10095 | `lpopCommand` | 3-line pure delegator |\n| phpspreadsheet | `LookupRef.VLOOKUP` | `@deprecated`, 4 lines, 0 callers |\n| gson | `JsonReader.skipValue` | **wrong class** — gold was rank 2 |\n| fmt-1683 | `PrintfTest` | 43-way ambiguity dump + a broken format string (`\"22 of 0 this query files failed to parse\"`) |\n| prometheus | — | 1,181 B of `- none` |\n\n**Fix.** Gate the chain: require a resolved code symbol (not a doc heading/test), require a score\nmargin over rank 2, require at least one post-boilerplate query term to match the symbol name or\nbody; follow `@deprecated`/`@see` redirects; if the top hit is a pure delegator whose callee is also\nin top-k, anchor on the callee; if nothing qualifies, **emit no impact block at all.** Pass the\n`file:line` selector the search hit already prints so ambiguity cannot arise.\n\nBlast radius: 9 of 20 blocks, ~1.9 KB each of near-zero-value context re-read every turn.\n\n---\n\n## ROOT CAUSE 4 — ranking hygiene\n\nVerified: **redis-10095's hits are not in score order** — printed sequence `[37.0447, 34.3022,\n37.0347]`. Graph-expanded hits are appended positionally while the prompt claims \"ranked hits\", so\nthe largest body in the payload is an unrelated symbol.\n\nAgent-found, pending verification, same family:\n- **Comments outrank code.** fmt-1683's rank 1 is a doc-comment fragment (score 33.68 vs 23.37 for\n  the best real code), with no `symbol=` and no `kind=` — and COVERING TEST, VERIFY and impact all\n  anchor off it.\n- **Generated docs indexed as call sites.** gson's `Callers … who breaks if behavior changes` leads\n  with `JsonReader (gson/docs/javadocs/…JsonReader.html:134)`; three.js spends 6 lines on localized\n  docs.\n- **Symbol names wrong.** C++ symbols named after return type / template parameter (fmt-1683's gold\n  is indexed as `iterator`, so no query can name it); and an **off-by-one truncation** —\n  `ranges_tes`, `format_tes` — in fmt-2457, caddy, three.js.\n- **Graph-expansion hits get full bodies with zero lexical match.** gson's `doPeek` is 58% of its\n  search payload, wrong class, `signals=graph:calls` only. `EG_MAXBYTES=24576` never binds at top-k 5.\n- **`SAME-CONCEPT LITERAL` substring-matches without word boundaries.** redis: `lpopCommand` matched\n  `blpopCommand`; 3 of 5 listed sites wrong, 2 of them labelled `EDIT`.\n- **`COVERING TEST` prints a mid-body window under a whole-symbol label** (5/5 affected).\n\n**Fix.** Stable-sort by score after graph expansion and assert monotonicity; exclude comment-only\nspans and generated/markup paths (`*.html`, `docs/`, `javadocs/`, `*.min.js`) from ranked hits and\nfrom CALLS extraction; take the symbol name from the declarator in the already-captured `signature`\nfield; word-boundary the literal scan; print covering-test hits at their real span.\n\n---\n\n## MEASUREMENT INTEGRITY — two problems that must be fixed before any number is quoted\n\n1. **The baseline can read the fix.** caddy's baseline arm ran\n   `sed -n 130,200p ~/go/pkg/mod/github.com/caddyserver/caddy/v2@v2.11.4/replacer.go` and diffed\n   against it — a **released upstream version containing both the fix and its test** — spending 27 of\n   66 calls there. The shared `GOMODCACHE` is not isolated. Fix: per-instance isolated\n   `GOMODCACHE`/`GOPATH`, and the npm/gem equivalents, or deny-read the module cache.\n2. **The wrapper lives inside the harness output tree.** `eg-q.run` is at\n   `results/<cell>/<instance>/eg-q.run` and its absolute path appears **5×** in the prompt. Agents\n   `ls`-ed that directory (redis-11734, caddy). From there, `tasks/opus20_official.json` — which\n   contains **every gold patch** — is reachable. No leak observed, but it is one `cat` away. Fix:\n   install the wrapper inside the checkout under a neutral name and never print a suite path.\n\n---\n\n## Plan\n\n### 1. Fix in blast-radius order, one commit each\n| # | fix | where | affects |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | query cleaning + path-literal extraction + no 40-word truncation of locators | `run_3arm.sh:157–161` | all 20 |\n| 2 | **line-number every printed body line**; `focus=` → interior line | `eg-consolidated` search render | all 20 |\n| 3 | gate the impact chain; no block when nothing qualifies | `run_3arm.sh:184–191` | 9+ |\n| 4 | sort-by-score assertion; drop comment-only + generated paths; declarator-based symbol names; word-boundary literals | `eg-consolidated/internal/sem/` | 8+ |\n| 5 | VERIFY: provisioning prefix instead of `return nil`; anchor on the nominated edit site | `internal/sem/search_verify.go:911`, `:1066` | carbon, phpspreadsheet, redis ×2, gson |\n| 6 | isolate GOMODCACHE; move the wrapper out of the results tree | harness | integrity |\n\nFix 5 detail: `search_verify.go:911` returns nil when `vendor/bin/phpunit` is absent — which is\nalways true in a fresh checkout. The same file already establishes the correct pattern for CMake at\nline 1010 (*\"The CONFIGURE STEP IS PART OF THE STRING deliberately\"*), so emit\n`composer install --no-interaction && vendor/bin/phpunit <rel>`. Separately `:1066` requires an\n*indexed* covering test, and redis's tests are `.tcl` (unindexed), so C repos get nothing.\n\n### 2. EMULATE EVERY INSTANCE OFFLINE — free, before any session spend\nFor all 20, using the recorded query in `prefetch_calls.log`, the worktree in `replay-wt/<inst>`, the\npatched binary and a **fresh `--cache-dir`** (the index cache is tree-keyed, not binary-keyed — reuse\nit and you get the old binary's answer):\n1. gold file present in payload, and **gold LINES inside a printed body** — count before/after;\n2. every body line carries a line number;\n3. hit scores monotonically non-increasing;\n4. impact block either absent or anchored on a symbol passing the gate;\n5. emitted `VERIFY` **actually executes** in that worktree (bounded timeout) — exit 0 or a genuine\n   test failure, never \"command not found\"/\"no such target\". A command that cannot run is worse than\n   none, which is exactly why line 911 bails today;\n6. **the 12 winners' gold-line coverage must not decrease.**\nGate: any instance failing (5) or (6) blocks the cell.\n\n### 3. Re-run the 20, pre-registered\nPublished prompt, cap 120, `EG_PREFETCH_NOSUPPRESS=1`, patched binary, fresh cache, isolated\nGOMODCACHE. Written before the run:\n- **Primary gate: no instance currently better than −15% may regress by more than 10pt.**\n- Leading indicator, checkable before scoring: **pre-edit locate must fall below the baseline.** It\n  is currently +8% (winners) / +13% (losers); the tool cannot be said to dismantle the locate phase\n  until this is negative.\n- Second leading indicator: post-edit \"re-finds payload text\" must fall from 5.58/7.25 per session.\n- Arithmetic (measured): 12 winners contribute ln-sum −5.369, 8 losers +2.996.\n  Fixing all 8 losers to parity = **−23.5%, short of goal.** All 8 at −10% = **−26.7%** ✓.\n  So the losers must convert to wins, and fixes 1+2 must additionally deepen the winners.\n\n### 4. Replicate before claiming\nSecond independent cell. Three configs today looked strong at n≤12 and reversed by n=20.\n\n## Verification\n- `tools/model_cmp.py`; geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI; cost classes separately.\n- Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped symmetrically.\n- `CENSORED` (`error_max_turns`) must stay 0 — baseline averages 50.2 turns, so a 50-cap censors the\n  baseline specifically and understates its cost.\n- Prompt symmetry by line diff + coaching-language scan = 0 in both arms.\n- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config — ten silent plumbing failures this session.\n\n## Files\n- `tools/run_3arm.sh` — query construction `:157–161`; impact anchor `:184–191`; wrapper install path.\n- `eg-consolidated/internal/sem/` — body rendering (line numbers), ranking sort, symbol naming from\n  declarator, literal word-boundaries, `search_verify.go:911`/`:1066`.\n- `eg-consolidated/internal/sem/search_verify_test.go` and neighbours — a regression case per fix.\n- `/tmp/mcptest/pubworker.sh` — new binary, `EG_PREFETCH_NOSUPPRESS=1`, isolated GOMODCACHE.\n\n## Honest expectation\nRoot causes 1 and 2 are the ones that match your thesis, and they are the first defects found that\naffect **all 20** rather than only the losers: the tool is currently searching with GitHub's issue\ntemplate as its query, and delivering bodies the agent cannot address without re-opening the file.\nFixing those should move pre-edit locate negative for the first time and cut the 40% re-find tax,\nwhich lifts winners and losers together.\n\nI will not predict a number. Every mechanism-based prediction I made today was wrong in sign or\nmagnitude at least once, and the honest position is that these are six independent changes whose\ninteraction is unknown. What I can commit to is the gate: pre-edit locate negative and winners\nun-regressed, or the change does not ship.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2784,"cache_read_input_tokens":480882,"output_tokens":6969,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2784,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6969,"cache_read_input_tokens":480882,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2784,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2784},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgGLaH6SJp9gkqXjdbBo","type":"assistant","uuid":"3554d2a0-2668-4945-a10f-977d9807a07e","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:12:16.367Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"3554d2a0-2668-4945-a10f-977d9807a07e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0813e2c2-9e63-40ae-82ae-61cde2f8fc2a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EzBKLp1rbkPUVbLTS935mW","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/modular-cooking-cupcake.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"bb952eca-560d-40b8-959c-6b6b9c33d1ec","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:12:16.441Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/modular-cooking-cupcake.md","content":"# Make the graph actually dismantle the locate phase — Opus 20-sample to −25%\n\n## Context\n\nFair baseline: Opus, Anthropic's published SWE-bench prompt verbatim to both arms, cap 120, 20\ninstances from the official 300. **tokens −11.2% CI [−27.8, +9.6], winners 12/20.**\n\nThe thesis under test: these are all large repos, so a working code index should collapse the locate\nphase on **every** instance, not half of them. Measured reality:\n\n| | measured |\n|---|---|\n| graph share of all locate operations | **0.7%** |\n| agent-initiated graph calls / session | **0.20** (16 of 20 sessions: zero) |\n| pre-edit locate, baseline → eg | 13.9 → 15.0 (**+8%**) — the tool does not reduce hunting |\n| post-edit ops that re-hunt text the payload already printed | **~40%** (5.58–7.25 / session) |\n\nSo the locate phase is not being dismantled; it is being **duplicated**. I read the transcripts and\nthe harness source and found the reasons. Four are verified by me directly; the rest come from a\n5-agent forensic sweep of all 20 sessions (38 findings) whose adversarial verification is still\nrunning, so they are marked as such.\n\n---\n\n## ROOT CAUSE 1 — the query is issue-template boilerplate, truncated at 40 words\n\n`tools/run_3arm.sh:157–161` builds the search query as: strip code fences, collapse whitespace,\n**take the first 40 words of the raw issue body.** Nothing else is removed.\n\nActual queries sent (verified from `prefetch_calls.log`):\n\n| instance | query as sent |\n|---|---|\n| carbon **+107%** | `Bug in method \\`->is()\\`, date with month october return true in to ask if is january <!-- 🛑 DON'T REMOVE ME. This issue template applies to all - bug` |\n| jekyll | `slugify replaces Tamil vowel marks with hyphen - I updated to the latest \\`github-pages\\` - I ran \\`bundle exec jekyll doctor\\` to check my configuratio` |\n| prometheus **+20%** | `PuppetDB Service Discovery - Numerical parameters not converted… ### What did you do? Hi, We use puppetdb_sd to p` |\n\nThree of four sampled queries spend most of their 40-word budget on GitHub issue-template\nboilerplate, HTML comments, or contributor checklists. Consequences found in the payloads:\ncarbon's query **self-matched the repo's own `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE.md`** (gold file absent from the\npayload entirely); jekyll ranked Markdown docs above the gold code file; prometheus's 40-word cap\n**truncated away the issue's own file+line pointer**, and path literals are not extracted or boosted\nat all.\n\n**Fix.** Before scoring: strip HTML comment blocks, issue/PR-template boilerplate, `- I ran/I read`\nchecklists and `| Software | Version |` env tables. Extract repo-relative path literals and\n`#Lnn-Lnn` anchors from the **full** text before truncating and pass them as a hard path boost.\nExclude `.github/**` and template markdown from the searchable set. Raise/replace the flat 40-word\ncap with a distinctive-token budget.\n\nBlast radius: **every instance.** This is the difference between the graph searching for the issue\nand searching for GitHub's issue template.\n\n---\n\n## ROOT CAUSE 2 — the payload is not addressable, so the agent must re-read the file\n\nThe eg prompt promises, verbatim: *\"the complete body of the enclosing function is printed verbatim\nbeneath that header, **at its real line numbers**\"*.\n\nVerified count of body lines carrying a line number:\n\n| instance | body lines | carrying line numbers |\n|---|---|---|\n| carbon | 55 | **0** |\n| redis-10095 | 107 | **0** |\n| lucene | 79 | **0** |\n\nZero, everywhere. The header carries a span (`:74-94`) but no interior line is addressable. To build\nan `Edit` anchor, a `sed -n` range, or to reason about hunk positions, the agent has to open the file\nit was just shown.\n\n**This is the mechanism behind the 40% \"re-finds payload text\" figure** — the largest single block of\nrecoverable waste in the cell, and it is present in winners (5.58/session) as much as losers\n(7.25/session).\n\n**Fix.** Prefix every printed body line with its real line number (5–6 chars/line — the header\nalready knows the span). Make `focus=` point at the highest-scoring **interior** line rather than\ncollapsing to the definition line.\n\nBlast radius: **every instance, winners included.** This is the fix that makes the tool benefit\neverything rather than only the instances whose baseline happened to flail.\n\n---\n\n## ROOT CAUSE 3 — `impact` is blind-chained to rank-1 with no gate\n\n`tools/run_3arm.sh:184–191` takes the **first `symbol=` string in the text payload** and runs\n`impact` on it. No relevance check, no kind check, no margin check. The result is injected under a\nheader telling the agent *\"You do not need to look these up yourself.\"*\n\nWhat that produced (from the payloads):\n\n| instance | impact anchor | what it actually is |\n|---|---|---|\n| carbon | `CarbonPeriod.removeFilter` | unrelated symbol; **49% of prefetch bytes** |\n| jekyll | `GitHub-Pages` | a **Markdown heading** → all-zero blast radius |\n| redis-10095 | `lpopCommand` | 3-line pure delegator |\n| phpspreadsheet | `LookupRef.VLOOKUP` | `@deprecated`, 4 lines, 0 callers |\n| gson | `JsonReader.skipValue` | **wrong class** — gold was rank 2 |\n| fmt-1683 | `PrintfTest` | 43-way ambiguity dump + a broken format string (`\"22 of 0 this query files failed to parse\"`) |\n| prometheus | — | 1,181 B of `- none` |\n\n**Fix.** Gate the chain: require a resolved code symbol (not a doc heading/test), require a score\nmargin over rank 2, require at least one post-boilerplate query term to match the symbol name or\nbody; follow `@deprecated`/`@see` redirects; if the top hit is a pure delegator whose callee is also\nin top-k, anchor on the callee; if nothing qualifies, **emit no impact block at all.** Pass the\n`file:line` selector the search hit already prints so ambiguity cannot arise.\n\nBlast radius: 9 of 20 blocks, ~1.9 KB each of near-zero-value context re-read every turn.\n\n---\n\n## ROOT CAUSE 4 — ranking hygiene\n\nVerified: **redis-10095's hits are not in score order** — printed sequence `[37.0447, 34.3022,\n37.0347]`. Graph-expanded hits are appended positionally while the prompt claims \"ranked hits\", so\nthe largest body in the payload is an unrelated symbol.\n\nAgent-found, pending verification, same family:\n- **Comments outrank code.** fmt-1683's rank 1 is a doc-comment fragment (score 33.68 vs 23.37 for\n  the best real code), with no `symbol=` and no `kind=` — and COVERING TEST, VERIFY and impact all\n  anchor off it.\n- **Generated docs indexed as call sites.** gson's `Callers … who breaks if behavior changes` leads\n  with `JsonReader (gson/docs/javadocs/…JsonReader.html:134)`; three.js spends 6 lines on localized\n  docs.\n- **Symbol names wrong.** C++ symbols named after return type / template parameter (fmt-1683's gold\n  is indexed as `iterator`, so no query can name it); and an **off-by-one truncation** —\n  `ranges_tes`, `format_tes` — in fmt-2457, caddy, three.js.\n- **Graph-expansion hits get full bodies with zero lexical match.** gson's `doPeek` is 58% of its\n  search payload, wrong class, `signals=graph:calls` only. `EG_MAXBYTES=24576` never binds at top-k 5.\n- **`SAME-CONCEPT LITERAL` substring-matches without word boundaries.** redis: `lpopCommand` matched\n  `blpopCommand`; 3 of 5 listed sites wrong, 2 of them labelled `EDIT`.\n- **`COVERING TEST` prints a mid-body window under a whole-symbol label** (5/5 affected).\n\n**Fix.** Stable-sort by score after graph expansion and assert monotonicity; exclude comment-only\nspans and generated/markup paths (`*.html`, `docs/`, `javadocs/`, `*.min.js`) from ranked hits and\nfrom CALLS extraction; take the symbol name from the declarator in the already-captured `signature`\nfield; word-boundary the literal scan; print covering-test hits at their real span.\n\n---\n\n## MEASUREMENT INTEGRITY — two problems that must be fixed before any number is quoted\n\n1. **The baseline can read the fix.** caddy's baseline arm ran\n   `sed -n 130,200p ~/go/pkg/mod/github.com/caddyserver/caddy/v2@v2.11.4/replacer.go` and diffed\n   against it — a **released upstream version containing both the fix and its test** — spending 27 of\n   66 calls there. The shared `GOMODCACHE` is not isolated. Fix: per-instance isolated\n   `GOMODCACHE`/`GOPATH`, and the npm/gem equivalents, or deny-read the module cache.\n2. **The wrapper lives inside the harness output tree.** `eg-q.run` is at\n   `results/<cell>/<instance>/eg-q.run` and its absolute path appears **5×** in the prompt. Agents\n   `ls`-ed that directory (redis-11734, caddy). From there, `tasks/opus20_official.json` — which\n   contains **every gold patch** — is reachable. No leak observed, but it is one `cat` away. Fix:\n   install the wrapper inside the checkout under a neutral name and never print a suite path.\n\n---\n\n## Plan\n\n### 1. Fix in blast-radius order, one commit each\n| # | fix | where | affects |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | query cleaning + path-literal extraction + no 40-word truncation of locators | `run_3arm.sh:157–161` | all 20 |\n| 2 | **line-number every printed body line**; `focus=` → interior line | `eg-consolidated` search render | all 20 |\n| 3 | gate the impact chain; no block when nothing qualifies | `run_3arm.sh:184–191` | 9+ |\n| 4 | sort-by-score assertion; drop comment-only + generated paths; declarator-based symbol names; word-boundary literals | `eg-consolidated/internal/sem/` | 8+ |\n| 5 | VERIFY: provisioning prefix instead of `return nil`; anchor on the nominated edit site | `internal/sem/search_verify.go:911`, `:1066` | carbon, phpspreadsheet, redis ×2, gson |\n| 6 | isolate GOMODCACHE; move the wrapper out of the results tree | harness | integrity |\n\nFix 5 detail: `search_verify.go:911` returns nil when `vendor/bin/phpunit` is absent — which is\nalways true in a fresh checkout. The same file already establishes the correct pattern for CMake at\nline 1010 (*\"The CONFIGURE STEP IS PART OF THE STRING deliberately\"*), so emit\n`composer install --no-interaction && vendor/bin/phpunit <rel>`. Separately `:1066` requires an\n*indexed* covering test, and redis's tests are `.tcl` (unindexed), so C repos get nothing.\n\n### 2. EMULATE EVERY INSTANCE OFFLINE — free, before any session spend\nFor all 20, using the recorded query in `prefetch_calls.log`, the worktree in `replay-wt/<inst>`, the\npatched binary and a **fresh `--cache-dir`** (the index cache is tree-keyed, not binary-keyed — reuse\nit and you get the old binary's answer):\n1. gold file present in payload, and **gold LINES inside a printed body** — count before/after;\n2. every body line carries a line number;\n3. hit scores monotonically non-increasing;\n4. impact block either absent or anchored on a symbol passing the gate;\n5. emitted `VERIFY` **actually executes** in that worktree (bounded timeout) — exit 0 or a genuine\n   test failure, never \"command not found\"/\"no such target\". A command that cannot run is worse than\n   none, which is exactly why line 911 bails today;\n6. **the 12 winners' gold-line coverage must not decrease.**\nGate: any instance failing (5) or (6) blocks the cell.\n\n### 3. Re-run the 20, pre-registered\nPublished prompt, cap 120, `EG_PREFETCH_NOSUPPRESS=1`, patched binary, fresh cache, isolated\nGOMODCACHE. Written before the run:\n- **Primary gate: no instance currently better than −15% may regress by more than 10pt.**\n- Leading indicator, checkable before scoring: **pre-edit locate must fall below the baseline.** It\n  is currently +8% (winners) / +13% (losers); the tool cannot be said to dismantle the locate phase\n  until this is negative.\n- Second leading indicator: post-edit \"re-finds payload text\" must fall from 5.58/7.25 per session.\n- Arithmetic (measured): 12 winners contribute ln-sum −5.369, 8 losers +2.996.\n  Fixing all 8 losers to parity = **−23.5%, short of goal.** All 8 at −10% = **−26.7%** ✓.\n  So the losers must convert to wins, and fixes 1+2 must additionally deepen the winners.\n\n### 4. Replicate before claiming\nSecond independent cell. Three configs today looked strong at n≤12 and reversed by n=20.\n\n## Verification\n- `tools/model_cmp.py`; geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI; cost classes separately.\n- Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped symmetrically.\n- `CENSORED` (`error_max_turns`) must stay 0 — baseline averages 50.2 turns, so a 50-cap censors the\n  baseline specifically and understates its cost.\n- Prompt symmetry by line diff + coaching-language scan = 0 in both arms.\n- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config — ten silent plumbing failures this session.\n\n## Files\n- `tools/run_3arm.sh` — query construction `:157–161`; impact anchor `:184–191`; wrapper install path.\n- `eg-consolidated/internal/sem/` — body rendering (line numbers), ranking sort, symbol naming from\n  declarator, literal word-boundaries, `search_verify.go:911`/`:1066`.\n- `eg-consolidated/internal/sem/search_verify_test.go` and neighbours — a regression case per fix.\n- `/tmp/mcptest/pubworker.sh` — new binary, `EG_PREFETCH_NOSUPPRESS=1`, isolated GOMODCACHE.\n\n## Honest expectation\nRoot causes 1 and 2 are the ones that match your thesis, and they are the first defects found that\naffect **all 20** rather than only the losers: the tool is currently searching with GitHub's issue\ntemplate as its query, and delivering bodies the agent cannot address without re-opening the file.\nFixing those should move pre-edit locate negative for the first time and cut the 40% re-find tax,\nwhich lifts winners and losers together.\n\nI will not predict a number. Every mechanism-based prediction I made today was wrong in sign or\nmagnitude at least once, and the honest position is that these are six independent changes whose\ninteraction is unknown. What I can commit to is the gate: pre-edit locate negative and winners\nun-regressed, or the change does not ship.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":150,"newStart":1,"newLines":230,"lines":["-# Opus to −25% on the 20-sample: two confirmed deriver bugs, emulated per instance","+# Make the graph actually dismantle the locate phase — Opus 20-sample to −25%"," "," ## Context"," ","-Fair baseline: Opus, Anthropic's published SWE-bench prompt verbatim to both arms, cap 120,","-20 instances from the official 300. **tokens −11.2% CI [−27.8, +9.6], winners 12/20.**","+Fair baseline: Opus, Anthropic's published SWE-bench prompt verbatim to both arms, cap 120, 20","+instances from the official 300. **tokens −11.2% CI [−27.8, +9.6], winners 12/20.**"," ","-I stopped doing statistics and read the transcripts. Two concrete bugs found in the VERIFY deriver,","-both confirmed against source, both explaining specific catastrophic instances.","+The thesis under test: these are all large repos, so a working code index should collapse the locate","+phase on **every** instance, not half of them. Measured reality:"," ","-### The arithmetic constraint (measured, not assumed)","+| | measured |","+|---|---|","+| graph share of all locate operations | **0.7%** |","+| agent-initiated graph calls / session | **0.20** (16 of 20 sessions: zero) |","+| pre-edit locate, baseline → eg | 13.9 → 15.0 (**+8%**) — the tool does not reduce hunting |","+| post-edit ops that re-hunt text the payload already printed | **~40%** (5.58–7.25 / session) |"," ","-| scenario | geomean |","+So the locate phase is not being dismantled; it is being **duplicated**. I read the transcripts and","+the harness source and found the reasons. Four are verified by me directly; the rest come from a","+5-agent forensic sweep of all 20 sessions (38 findings) whose adversarial verification is still","+running, so they are marked as such.","+","+---","+","+## ROOT CAUSE 1 — the query is issue-template boilerplate, truncated at 40 words","+","+`tools/run_3arm.sh:157–161` builds the search query as: strip code fences, collapse whitespace,","+**take the first 40 words of the raw issue body.** Nothing else is removed.","+","+Actual queries sent (verified from `prefetch_calls.log`):","+","+| instance | query as sent |"," |---|---|","-| fix the 4 worst losers to parity | −20.3% |","-| **fix ALL 8 losers to parity** | **−23.5% — still short of goal** |","-| fix all 8 to −10% each | **−26.7%** ✓ |","-| fix all 8 to −15% each | −28.4% ✓ |","+| carbon **+107%** | `Bug in method \\`->is()\\`, date with month october return true in to ask if is january <!-- 🛑 DON'T REMOVE ME. This issue template applies to all - bug` |","+| jekyll | `slugify replaces Tamil vowel marks with hyphen - I updated to the latest \\`github-pages\\` - I ran \\`bundle exec jekyll doctor\\` to check my configuratio` |","+| prometheus **+20%** | `PuppetDB Service Discovery - Numerical parameters not converted… ### What did you do? Hi, We use puppetdb_sd to p` |"," ","-**−25% cannot be reached by eliminating losses.** The 12 winners contribute ln-sum −5.369; the 8","-losers +2.996. Every loser must become a modest win, not merely stop losing. Arm B has already","-demonstrated conversion is possible: ruff **+35% → −8%** (−44pt).","+Three of four sampled queries spend most of their 40-word budget on GitHub issue-template","+boilerplate, HTML comments, or contributor checklists. Consequences found in the payloads:","+carbon's query **self-matched the repo's own `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE.md`** (gold file absent from the","+payload entirely); jekyll ranked Markdown docs above the gold code file; prometheus's 40-word cap","+**truncated away the issue's own file+line pointer**, and path literals are not extracted or boosted","+at all."," ","-## Bug 1 — PHP deriver bails out exactly when the repo is unprovisioned","+**Fix.** Before scoring: strip HTML comment blocks, issue/PR-template boilerplate, `- I ran/I read`","+checklists and `| Software | Version |` env tables. Extract repo-relative path literals and","+`#Lnn-Lnn` anchors from the **full** text before truncating and pass them as a hard path boost.","+Exclude `.github/**` and template markdown from the searchable set. Raise/replace the flat 40-word","+cap with a distinctive-token budget."," ","-`eg-consolidated/internal/sem/search_verify.go:911`","+Blast radius: **every instance.** This is the difference between the graph searching for the issue","+and searching for GitHub's issue template."," ","-```go","-if !evidence.exists(searchVerifyJoin(dir, \"vendor/bin/phpunit\")) {","-    return nil        // no VERIFY emitted at all","-}","-```","+---"," ","-A fresh SWE-bench checkout never has `vendor/`, so PHP repos always take this branch. carbon then","-falls through to the `.php` lint (`php -l`, line 531); phpspreadsheet gets nothing.","+## ROOT CAUSE 2 — the payload is not addressable, so the agent must re-read the file"," ","-**Transcript evidence — carbon (+107%), 52 calls vs baseline's 34:**","+The eg prompt promises, verbatim: *\"the complete body of the enclosing function is printed verbatim","+beneath that header, **at its real line numbers**\"*."," ","-| | baseline | eg |","+Verified count of body lines carrying a line number:","+","+| instance | body lines | carrying line numbers |"," |---|---|---|","-| `ls vendor` | call 7 | call 10 |","-| `composer.json` + `which composer` | call **8** | **never** |","-| `composer install` | call **9** | call **35** |","-| first edit | 18 | 25 |","+| carbon | 55 | **0** |","+| redis-10095 | 107 | **0** |","+| lucene | 79 | **0** |"," ","-eg hand-wrote its own autoloader (`/tmp/auto.php`, calls 11–12), then spent calls 14–23 unzipping","-cached Carbon tarballs out of `~/Library/Caches/composer` to read upstream source, then rebuilt","-verification harnesses by hand (27–34), then finally ran the `composer install` the baseline ran at","-call 9 — and finished with calls 48–52 deleting `vendor`, `composer.lock` and","-`.phpunit.result.cache` to keep its diff clean. **~25 calls of avoidable archaeology.**","+Zero, everywhere. The header carries a span (`:74-94`) but no interior line is addressable. To build","+an `Edit` anchor, a `sed -n` range, or to reason about hunk positions, the agent has to open the file","+it was just shown."," ","-The lint is what licensed it: `php -l` tells the agent verification needs no dependency tree.","+**This is the mechanism behind the 40% \"re-finds payload text\" figure** — the largest single block of","+recoverable waste in the cell, and it is present in winners (5.58/session) as much as losers","+(7.25/session)."," ","-**The fix is already established in this same file, for CMake, at line 1010:**","-> *\"The CONFIGURE STEP IS PART OF THE STRING deliberately: a bare `cmake --build build` fails in a","-> fresh checkout because build/ does not exist, which is exactly what happened.\"*","+**Fix.** Prefix every printed body line with its real line number (5–6 chars/line — the header","+already knows the span). Make `focus=` point at the highest-scoring **interior** line rather than","+collapsing to the definition line."," ","-So: emit `composer install --no-interaction --no-progress && vendor/bin/phpunit <relative>` instead","-of returning nil. Same pattern, same justification, different ecosystem. Also: never fall back to a","-lint when a real runner is derivable — prefer the test, keep the lint only as last resort.","+Blast radius: **every instance, winners included.** This is the fix that makes the tool benefit","+everything rather than only the instances whose baseline happened to flail."," ","-Targets **carbon +107%**, **phpspreadsheet +31%**.","+---"," ","-## Bug 2 — Make deriver requires an *indexed* covering test, so tcl-tested C repos get nothing","+## ROOT CAUSE 3 — `impact` is blind-chained to rank-1 with no gate"," ","-`search_verify.go:1066` — `deriveSearchVerifyMake` returns nil when `subject.testPath == \"\"`.","-redis's tests are `.tcl` (`tests/unit/bitops.tcl`, `tests/unit/type/list.tcl`), which the graph does","-not index, so `testPath` is always empty and the Make deriver never fires — despite redis's root","-Makefile declaring a `test` target.","+`tools/run_3arm.sh:184–191` takes the **first `symbol=` string in the text payload** and runs","+`impact` on it. No relevance check, no kind check, no margin check. The result is injected under a","+header telling the agent *\"You do not need to look these up yourself.\"*"," ","-**Transcript evidence — redis-11734 (+96%), 62 calls vs baseline's 39:** eg invoked `make` four","-separate times with escalating `CFLAGS=\"-DMAC_OS_X_VERSION_10_6=1060\"` (calls 15, 22, 34, 53)","-fighting the macOS toolchain, probed `which tclsh` at 38, then ran `make clean` twice (59, 61) to","-scrub build artifacts from its diff. First edit at call **25** vs the baseline's **12**.","+What that produced (from the payloads):"," ","-Fix: recognise the tcl harness (`tests/test_helper.tcl` + `tests/unit/**.tcl`) as a covering-test","-source so `testPath` resolves, and emit build-then-test as one string per the CMake precedent:","-`make -j -C src redis-server && ./runtest --single unit/<name>`, mapping `t_list.c → unit/type/list`,","-`bitops.c → unit/bitops` by redis's own directory convention.","+| instance | impact anchor | what it actually is |","+|---|---|---|","+| carbon | `CarbonPeriod.removeFilter` | unrelated symbol; **49% of prefetch bytes** |","+| jekyll | `GitHub-Pages` | a **Markdown heading** → all-zero blast radius |","+| redis-10095 | `lpopCommand` | 3-line pure delegator |","+| phpspreadsheet | `LookupRef.VLOOKUP` | `@deprecated`, 4 lines, 0 callers |","+| gson | `JsonReader.skipValue` | **wrong class** — gold was rank 2 |","+| fmt-1683 | `PrintfTest` | 43-way ambiguity dump + a broken format string (`\"22 of 0 this query files failed to parse\"`) |","+| prometheus | — | 1,181 B of `- none` |"," ","-Targets **redis-11734 +96%**, **redis-10095 +65%**.","+**Fix.** Gate the chain: require a resolved code symbol (not a doc heading/test), require a score","+margin over rank 2, require at least one post-boilerplate query term to match the symbol name or","+body; follow `@deprecated`/`@see` redirects; if the top hit is a pure delegator whose callee is also","+in top-k, anchor on the callee; if nothing qualifies, **emit no impact block at all.** Pass the","+`file:line` selector the search hit already prints so ambiguity cannot arise."," ","-## Bug 3 — already fixed and measured: the prefetch preamble","+Blast radius: 9 of 20 blocks, ~1.9 KB each of near-zero-value context re-read every turn."," ","-`run_3arm.sh` told the agent *\"you do not need to run it yourself\"*. Replaced behind","-`EG_PREFETCH_NOSUPPRESS=1`. Probe result on ruff: **+35% → −8%**. Costs nothing, keep it on.","-Caveat: at n=1 it also moved caddy −56→−39 and jekyll −58→−45, which the full run must check.","+---"," ","-**Not pursued:** Arm A (no prefetch, cap lifted) tripled graph usage 0.20→3.00 calls/session and got","-**worse** — caddy −56% → −13%, mean +17.8pt. Graph usage is not the lever; that is now measured.","+## ROOT CAUSE 4 — ranking hygiene"," ","+Verified: **redis-10095's hits are not in score order** — printed sequence `[37.0447, 34.3022,","+37.0347]`. Graph-expanded hits are appended positionally while the prompt claims \"ranked hits\", so","+the largest body in the payload is an unrelated symbol.","+","+Agent-found, pending verification, same family:","+- **Comments outrank code.** fmt-1683's rank 1 is a doc-comment fragment (score 33.68 vs 23.37 for","+  the best real code), with no `symbol=` and no `kind=` — and COVERING TEST, VERIFY and impact all","+  anchor off it.","+- **Generated docs indexed as call sites.** gson's `Callers … who breaks if behavior changes` leads","+  with `JsonReader (gson/docs/javadocs/…JsonReader.html:134)`; three.js spends 6 lines on localized","+  docs.","+- **Symbol names wrong.** C++ symbols named after return type / template parameter (fmt-1683's gold","+  is indexed as `iterator`, so no query can name it); and an **off-by-one truncation** —","+  `ranges_tes`, `format_tes` — in fmt-2457, caddy, three.js.","+- **Graph-expansion hits get full bodies with zero lexical match.** gson's `doPeek` is 58% of its","+  search payload, wrong class, `signals=graph:calls` only. `EG_MAXBYTES=24576` never binds at top-k 5.","+- **`SAME-CONCEPT LITERAL` substring-matches without word boundaries.** redis: `lpopCommand` matched","+  `blpopCommand`; 3 of 5 listed sites wrong, 2 of them labelled `EDIT`.","+- **`COVERING TEST` prints a mid-body window under a whole-symbol label** (5/5 affected).","+","+**Fix.** Stable-sort by score after graph expansion and assert monotonicity; exclude comment-only","+spans and generated/markup paths (`*.html`, `docs/`, `javadocs/`, `*.min.js`) from ranked hits and","+from CALLS extraction; take the symbol name from the declarator in the already-captured `signature`","+field; word-boundary the literal scan; print covering-test hits at their real span.","+","+---","+","+## MEASUREMENT INTEGRITY — two problems that must be fixed before any number is quoted","+","+1. **The baseline can read the fix.** caddy's baseline arm ran","+   `sed -n 130,200p ~/go/pkg/mod/github.com/caddyserver/caddy/v2@v2.11.4/replacer.go` and diffed","+   against it — a **released upstream version containing both the fix and its test** — spending 27 of","+   66 calls there. The shared `GOMODCACHE` is not isolated. Fix: per-instance isolated","+   `GOMODCACHE`/`GOPATH`, and the npm/gem equivalents, or deny-read the module cache.","+2. **The wrapper lives inside the harness output tree.** `eg-q.run` is at","+   `results/<cell>/<instance>/eg-q.run` and its absolute path appears **5×** in the prompt. Agents","+   `ls`-ed that directory (redis-11734, caddy). From there, `tasks/opus20_official.json` — which","+   contains **every gold patch** — is reachable. No leak observed, but it is one `cat` away. Fix:","+   install the wrapper inside the checkout under a neutral name and never print a suite path.","+","+---","+"," ## Plan"," ","-### 1. Patch the two derivers","-`eg-consolidated/internal/sem/search_verify.go` only:","-- `deriveSearchVerifyComposer` — provisioning prefix instead of `return nil`; drop the lint fallback","-  when a runner is derivable.","-- `deriveSearchVerifyMake` / covering-test resolution — accept the tcl harness; emit build+test.","-- Existing tests: `internal/sem/search_verify_test.go`. Add a case per bug. `go build`, `go test ./internal/sem/`.","+### 1. Fix in blast-radius order, one commit each","+| # | fix | where | affects |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| 1 | query cleaning + path-literal extraction + no 40-word truncation of locators | `run_3arm.sh:157–161` | all 20 |","+| 2 | **line-number every printed body line**; `focus=` → interior line | `eg-consolidated` search render | all 20 |","+| 3 | gate the impact chain; no block when nothing qualifies | `run_3arm.sh:184–191` | 9+ |","+| 4 | sort-by-score assertion; drop comment-only + generated paths; declarator-based symbol names; word-boundary literals | `eg-consolidated/internal/sem/` | 8+ |","+| 5 | VERIFY: provisioning prefix instead of `return nil`; anchor on the nominated edit site | `internal/sem/search_verify.go:911`, `:1066` | carbon, phpspreadsheet, redis ×2, gson |","+| 6 | isolate GOMODCACHE; move the wrapper out of the results tree | harness | integrity |"," ","-### 2. EMULATE EACH LOSER OFFLINE — free, deterministic, before any session spend","-For all 8 losers, using the recorded query in `results/PUB_r1_eg/eg/<inst>/prefetch_calls.log` and the","-worktree in `replay-wt/<inst>`, with the patched binary and a **fresh `--cache-dir`** (the index cache","-is tree-keyed, not binary-keyed — reuse and it serves the old binary's answer):","-1. assert a `VERIFY:` line is now emitted where one was missing;","-2. **actually execute it** in that worktree, bounded by timeout, and assert exit 0 or a genuine test","-   failure — not \"command not found\" / \"no such target\". A command that cannot run is worse than none,","-   which is the very reason line 911 bails today;","-3. assert nothing else in the payload moved (byte-diff outside the VERIFY block);","-4. assert the 12 winners' payloads are **byte-identical** to before.","-Gate: if (2) fails for an instance, that instance's fix is wrong — do not run the cell on hope.","+Fix 5 detail: `search_verify.go:911` returns nil when `vendor/bin/phpunit` is absent — which is","+always true in a fresh checkout. The same file already establishes the correct pattern for CMake at","+line 1010 (*\"The CONFIGURE STEP IS PART OF THE STRING deliberately\"*), so emit","+`composer install --no-interaction && vendor/bin/phpunit <rel>`. Separately `:1066` requires an","+*indexed* covering test, and redis's tests are `.tcl` (unindexed), so C repos get nothing."," ","+### 2. EMULATE EVERY INSTANCE OFFLINE — free, before any session spend","+For all 20, using the recorded query in `prefetch_calls.log`, the worktree in `replay-wt/<inst>`, the","+patched binary and a **fresh `--cache-dir`** (the index cache is tree-keyed, not binary-keyed — reuse","+it and you get the old binary's answer):","+1. gold file present in payload, and **gold LINES inside a printed body** — count before/after;","+2. every body line carries a line number;","+3. hit scores monotonically non-increasing;","+4. impact block either absent or anchored on a symbol passing the gate;","+5. emitted `VERIFY` **actually executes** in that worktree (bounded timeout) — exit 0 or a genuine","+   test failure, never \"command not found\"/\"no such target\". A command that cannot run is worse than","+   none, which is exactly why line 911 bails today;","+6. **the 12 winners' gold-line coverage must not decrease.**","+Gate: any instance failing (5) or (6) blocks the cell.","+"," ### 3. Re-run the 20, pre-registered","-Published prompt, cap 120, `EG_PREFETCH_NOSUPPRESS=1`, patched binary, fresh cache dir. Written","-before the run:","+Published prompt, cap 120, `EG_PREFETCH_NOSUPPRESS=1`, patched binary, fresh cache, isolated","+GOMODCACHE. Written before the run:"," - **Primary gate: no instance currently better than −15% may regress by more than 10pt.**","-- carbon, phpspreadsheet, redis-11734, redis-10095 must each improve by ≥30pt.","-- Aggregate target −25% requires the 8 losers to average ≤ −10%; parity only yields −23.5%.","-- Falsification: if the VERIFY lines execute cleanly (step 2 passed) but the losers do not improve,","-  then env-provisioning was not the cost driver and I revert the product change.","+- Leading indicator, checkable before scoring: **pre-edit locate must fall below the baseline.** It","+  is currently +8% (winners) / +13% (losers); the tool cannot be said to dismantle the locate phase","+  until this is negative.","+- Second leading indicator: post-edit \"re-finds payload text\" must fall from 5.58/7.25 per session.","+- Arithmetic (measured): 12 winners contribute ln-sum −5.369, 8 losers +2.996.","+  Fixing all 8 losers to parity = **−23.5%, short of goal.** All 8 at −10% = **−26.7%** ✓.","+  So the losers must convert to wins, and fixes 1+2 must additionally deepen the winners."," "," ### 4. Replicate before claiming"," Second independent cell. Three configs today looked strong at n≤12 and reversed by n=20."," "," ## Verification","-- Scorer `tools/model_cmp.py`; geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI; classes separately.","+- `tools/model_cmp.py`; geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI; cost classes separately."," - Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped symmetrically."," - `CENSORED` (`error_max_turns`) must stay 0 — baseline averages 50.2 turns, so a 50-cap censors the","-  baseline specifically.","+  baseline specifically and understates its cost."," - Prompt symmetry by line diff + coaching-language scan = 0 in both arms."," - Verify on emitted artifacts, never config — ten silent plumbing failures this session.","-- Per-instance first-edit call index is the leading indicator: eg reaches its first edit LATER than","-  the baseline in all three severe losers (25 vs 12, 10 vs 7, 25 vs 18). That gap must close."," "," ## Files","-- `eg-consolidated/internal/sem/search_verify.go` — the only product change (lines ~884–925, ~1053–1086).","-- `eg-consolidated/internal/sem/search_verify_test.go` — a regression case per bug.","-- `tools/run_3arm.sh` — `EG_PREFETCH_NOSUPPRESS` already wired; no further prompt change.","-- `/tmp/mcptest/pubworker.sh` — add `EG_PREFETCH_NOSUPPRESS=1`, point at the new binary.","+- `tools/run_3arm.sh` — query construction `:157–161`; impact anchor `:184–191`; wrapper install path.","+- `eg-consolidated/internal/sem/` — body rendering (line numbers), ranking sort, symbol naming from","+  declarator, literal word-boundaries, `search_verify.go:911`/`:1066`.","+- `eg-consolidated/internal/sem/search_verify_test.go` and neighbours — a regression case per fix.","+- `/tmp/mcptest/pubworker.sh` — new binary, `EG_PREFETCH_NOSUPPRESS=1`, isolated GOMODCACHE."," "," ## Honest expectation","-This is the first time I have a mechanism traced to a specific `return nil` with transcript evidence","-of what it costs, and a precedent in the same file for the correct behaviour. Fixing both plausibly","-converts the four worst instances, which is worth ~9pt (−11.2% → −20.3% at parity).","+Root causes 1 and 2 are the ones that match your thesis, and they are the first defects found that","+affect **all 20** rather than only the losers: the tool is currently searching with GitHub's issue","+template as its query, and delivering bodies the agent cannot address without re-opening the file.","+Fixing those should move pre-edit locate negative for the first time and cut the 40% re-find tax,","+which lifts winners and losers together."," ","-But the arithmetic says that is not enough: **all eight losers must average −10%**, and I have direct","-evidence for only one conversion of that size (ruff, via Bug 3). So the honest expectation is","-**−20% to −24%**, with −25% requiring the mid-losers (ruff, fmt-1683, prometheus, gson) to convert","-too — for which I currently have no mechanism beyond Bug 3. I will report the number I get rather","-than stopping at the first framing that clears the bar.","+I will not predict a number. Every mechanism-based prediction I made today was wrong in sign or","+magnitude at least once, and the honest position is that these are six independent changes whose","+interaction is unknown. What I can commit to is the gate: pre-edit locate negative and winners","+un-regressed, or the change does not ship."]}],"originalFile":"# Opus to −25% on the 20-sample: two confirmed deriver bugs, emulated per instance\n\n## Context\n\nFair baseline: Opus, Anthropic's published SWE-bench prompt verbatim to both arms, cap 120,\n20 instances from the official 300. **tokens −11.2% CI [−27.8, +9.6], winners 12/20.**\n\nI stopped doing statistics and read the transcripts. Two concrete bugs found in the VERIFY deriver,\nboth confirmed against source, both explaining specific catastrophic instances.\n\n### The arithmetic constraint (measured, not assumed)\n\n| scenario | geomean |\n|---|---|\n| fix the 4 worst losers to parity | −20.3% |\n| **fix ALL 8 losers to parity** | **−23.5% — still short of goal** |\n| fix all 8 to −10% each | **−26.7%** ✓ |\n| fix all 8 to −15% each | −28.4% ✓ |\n\n**−25% cannot be reached by eliminating losses.** The 12 winners contribute ln-sum −5.369; the 8\nlosers +2.996. Every loser must become a modest win, not merely stop losing. Arm B has already\ndemonstrated conversion is possible: ruff **+35% → −8%** (−44pt).\n\n## Bug 1 — PHP deriver bails out exactly when the repo is unprovisioned\n\n`eg-consolidated/internal/sem/search_verify.go:911`\n\n```go\nif !evidence.exists(searchVerifyJoin(dir, \"vendor/bin/phpunit\")) {\n    return nil        // no VERIFY emitted at all\n}\n```\n\nA fresh SWE-bench checkout never has `vendor/`, so PHP repos always take this branch. carbon then\nfalls through to the `.php` lint (`php -l`, line 531); phpspreadsheet gets nothing.\n\n**Transcript evidence — carbon (+107%), 52 calls vs baseline's 34:**\n\n| | baseline | eg |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ls vendor` | call 7 | call 10 |\n| `composer.json` + `which composer` | call **8** | **never** |\n| `composer install` | call **9** | call **35** |\n| first edit | 18 | 25 |\n\neg hand-wrote its own autoloader (`/tmp/auto.php`, calls 11–12), then spent calls 14–23 unzipping\ncached Carbon tarballs out of `~/Library/Caches/composer` to read upstream source, then rebuilt\nverification harnesses by hand (27–34), then finally ran the `composer install` the baseline ran at\ncall 9 — and finished with calls 48–52 deleting `vendor`, `composer.lock` and\n`.phpunit.result.cache` to keep its diff clean. **~25 calls of avoidable archaeology.**\n\nThe lint is what licensed it: `php -l` tells the agent verification needs no dependency tree.\n\n**The fix is already established in this same file, for CMake, at line 1010:**\n> *\"The CONFIGURE STEP IS PART OF THE STRING deliberately: a bare `cmake --build build` fails in a\n> fresh checkout because build/ does not exist, which is exactly what happened.\"*\n\nSo: emit `composer install --no-interaction --no-progress && vendor/bin/phpunit <relative>` instead\nof returning nil. Same pattern, same justification, different ecosystem. Also: never fall back to a\nlint when a real runner is derivable — prefer the test, keep the lint only as last resort.\n\nTargets **carbon +107%**, **phpspreadsheet +31%**.\n\n## Bug 2 — Make deriver requires an *indexed* covering test, so tcl-tested C repos get nothing\n\n`search_verify.go:1066` — `deriveSearchVerifyMake` returns nil when `subject.testPath == \"\"`.\nredis's tests are `.tcl` (`tests/unit/bitops.tcl`, `tests/unit/type/list.tcl`), which the graph does\nnot index, so `testPath` is always empty and the Make deriver never fires — despite redis's root\nMakefile declaring a `test` target.\n\n**Transcript evidence — redis-11734 (+96%), 62 calls vs baseline's 39:** eg invoked `make` four\nseparate times with escalating `CFLAGS=\"-DMAC_OS_X_VERSION_10_6=1060\"` (calls 15, 22, 34, 53)\nfighting the macOS toolchain, probed `which tclsh` at 38, then ran `make clean` twice (59, 61) to\nscrub build artifacts from its diff. First edit at call **25** vs the baseline's **12**.\n\nFix: recognise the tcl harness (`tests/test_helper.tcl` + `tests/unit/**.tcl`) as a covering-test\nsource so `testPath` resolves, and emit build-then-test as one string per the CMake precedent:\n`make -j -C src redis-server && ./runtest --single unit/<name>`, mapping `t_list.c → unit/type/list`,\n`bitops.c → unit/bitops` by redis's own directory convention.\n\nTargets **redis-11734 +96%**, **redis-10095 +65%**.\n\n## Bug 3 — already fixed and measured: the prefetch preamble\n\n`run_3arm.sh` told the agent *\"you do not need to run it yourself\"*. Replaced behind\n`EG_PREFETCH_NOSUPPRESS=1`. Probe result on ruff: **+35% → −8%**. Costs nothing, keep it on.\nCaveat: at n=1 it also moved caddy −56→−39 and jekyll −58→−45, which the full run must check.\n\n**Not pursued:** Arm A (no prefetch, cap lifted) tripled graph usage 0.20→3.00 calls/session and got\n**worse** — caddy −56% → −13%, mean +17.8pt. Graph usage is not the lever; that is now measured.\n\n## Plan\n\n### 1. Patch the two derivers\n`eg-consolidated/internal/sem/search_verify.go` only:\n- `deriveSearchVerifyComposer` — provisioning prefix instead of `return nil`; drop the lint fallback\n  when a runner is derivable.\n- `deriveSearchVerifyMake` / covering-test resolution — accept the tcl harness; emit build+test.\n- Existing tests: `internal/sem/search_verify_test.go`. Add a case per bug. `go build`, `go test ./internal/sem/`.\n\n### 2. EMULATE EACH LOSER OFFLINE — free, deterministic, before any session spend\nFor all 8 losers, using the recorded query in `results/PUB_r1_eg/eg/<inst>/prefetch_calls.log` and the\nworktree in `replay-wt/<inst>`, with the patched binary and a **fresh `--cache-dir`** (the index cache\nis tree-keyed, not binary-keyed — reuse and it serves the old binary's answer):\n1. assert a `VERIFY:` line is now emitted where one was missing;\n2. **actually execute it** in that worktree, bounded by timeout, and assert exit 0 or a genuine test\n   failure — not \"command not found\" / \"no such target\". A command that cannot run is worse than none,\n   which is the very reason line 911 bails today;\n3. assert nothing else in the payload moved (byte-diff outside the VERIFY block);\n4. assert the 12 winners' payloads are **byte-identical** to before.\nGate: if (2) fails for an instance, that instance's fix is wrong — do not run the cell on hope.\n\n### 3. Re-run the 20, pre-registered\nPublished prompt, cap 120, `EG_PREFETCH_NOSUPPRESS=1`, patched binary, fresh cache dir. Written\nbefore the run:\n- **Primary gate: no instance currently better than −15% may regress by more than 10pt.**\n- carbon, phpspreadsheet, redis-11734, redis-10095 must each improve by ≥30pt.\n- Aggregate target −25% requires the 8 losers to average ≤ −10%; parity only yields −23.5%.\n- Falsification: if the VERIFY lines execute cleanly (step 2 passed) but the losers do not improve,\n  then env-provisioning was not the cost driver and I revert the product change.\n\n### 4. Replicate before claiming\nSecond independent cell. Three configs today looked strong at n≤12 and reversed by n=20.\n\n## Verification\n- Scorer `tools/model_cmp.py`; geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI; classes separately.\n- Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped symmetrically.\n- `CENSORED` (`error_max_turns`) must stay 0 — baseline averages 50.2 turns, so a 50-cap censors the\n  baseline specifically.\n- Prompt symmetry by line diff + coaching-language scan = 0 in both arms.\n- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config — ten silent plumbing failures this session.\n- Per-instance first-edit call index is the leading indicator: eg reaches its first edit LATER than\n  the baseline in all three severe losers (25 vs 12, 10 vs 7, 25 vs 18). That gap must close.\n\n## Files\n- `eg-consolidated/internal/sem/search_verify.go` — the only product change (lines ~884–925, ~1053–1086).\n- `eg-consolidated/internal/sem/search_verify_test.go` — a regression case per bug.\n- `tools/run_3arm.sh` — `EG_PREFETCH_NOSUPPRESS` already wired; no further prompt change.\n- `/tmp/mcptest/pubworker.sh` — add `EG_PREFETCH_NOSUPPRESS=1`, point at the new binary.\n\n## Honest expectation\nThis is the first time I have a mechanism traced to a specific `return nil` with transcript evidence\nof what it costs, and a precedent in the same file for the correct behaviour. Fixing both plausibly\nconverts the four worst instances, which is worth ~9pt (−11.2% → −20.3% at parity).\n\nBut the arithmetic says that is not enough: **all eight losers must average −10%**, and I have direct\nevidence for only one conversion of that size (ruff, via Bug 3). So the honest expectation is\n**−20% to −24%**, with −25% requiring the mid-losers (ruff, fmt-1683, prometheus, gson) to convert\ntoo — for which I currently have no mechanism beyond Bug 3. I will report the number I get rather\nthan stopping at the first framing that clears the bar.\n","userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3554d2a0-2668-4945-a10f-977d9807a07e","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
