{"parentUuid":"34346fb1-ad48-45dd-afaa-13b476765d57","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgH3LgRaGBcTvn5WThtW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"S1 is `PROMPT_FAMILY=vendor BASE_CLAMP=1 EG_GATED_CLAMP=1` — and the harness's own comment calls that combination *\"the matched control: a bare clamp on both sides, no shared block on either, so the only difference is search-tool vs shell.\"* Writing the plan around porting it:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3273,"cache_read_input_tokens":508968,"output_tokens":4521,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3273,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4521,"cache_read_input_tokens":508968,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3273,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3273},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgH3GF2bhJE9tiWrtXvU","type":"assistant","uuid":"f2f6ebe6-532b-44f5-85db-1b96c34f2753","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:20:17.864Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"f2f6ebe6-532b-44f5-85db-1b96c34f2753","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgH3LgRaGBcTvn5WThtW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PHqiNvb8HZ57QU6DHPVnWv","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/modular-cooking-cupcake.md","content":"# Opus to −25% by porting S1 — the best fair config, never run on Opus\n\n## Context\n\nGoal: Opus ≥ −25% on the 20-instance official-300 sample. Current fair number **−11.2%**\n[−27.8, +9.6] (n=20, published prompt, both arms symmetric, cap 120).\n\nI stopped proposing new mechanisms and mined the existing cells. Two things came out of that, and\ntogether they change what to run.\n\n### 1. Every payload-defect hypothesis is dead — verified, not assumed\n\nA 5-agent forensic sweep read all 20 sessions and produced 38 candidate defects. Adversarial\nverifiers with a **winner-control** requirement refuted **27 of 28** adjudicated so far:\n\n| claimed defect | winner control that killed it |\n|---|---|\n| bodies printed with no line numbers (prompt promises them) | **20/20 instances** — 6/6 winners, incl. the biggest wins |\n| `impact` blind-chained to rank-1, no gate | off-gold-file target in **7/12 winners**; the two largest wins have it in *more* degenerate form |\n| query polluted by GitHub issue-template boilerplate | 2/6 control winners have boilerplate queries → boilerplate top hits |\n| hits printed out of score order | 5/20 payloads, incl. winners lucene (−52%) and vuejs (−24%) |\n| line-less fabricated `server.h` caller | redis-10095 (+65) **and valkey-1842 (−21%, a winner)** |\n| `eg-q.run` path exposed 5× in prompt | 20/20 |\n\nOnly survivor: the shared **GOMODCACHE leak** (caddy's *baseline* read the fix out of\n`~/go/pkg/mod/…caddy/v2@v2.11.4/replacer.go`, 27 of 66 calls) — and it explains a winner, not a loss.\n\n**Conclusion: the tool is equally broken everywhere. Payload quality does not decide the sign.**\nDo not spend further effort on payload defects.\n\n### 2. Tokens are a pure function of the op-count ratio, and eg's op count is invariant\n\n| config | baseline ops | eg ops | ops Δ | tokens |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| G40 rich/rich, official | **23.8** | 28.7 | +21.1% | +28.4% |\n| OFF bare/rich, official | **39.0** | 27.5 | −29.6% | −46.5% |\n| PUB none/capability, published | **35.7** | 31.7 | −11.2% | −11.2% |\n\neg lands at 27.5 / 28.7 / 31.7 regardless of prompt. The **baseline** swings 23.8 → 39.0 purely on how\nmuch methodology its prompt carries. So the withdrawn −46.5% was a crippled control, and G40's +28.4%\nwas a control given better discipline than eg. Neither was about the tool.\n\n### 3. What the winning cells do that no Opus cell has ever done\n\nThe tool's job is to collapse the locate phase. On Haiku's best fair cells it halves pre-edit locate.\nOn Opus it never has:\n\n| cell | pre-edit base → eg | ops Δ | tokens |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **haiku S1** (n=50) | **16.2 → 8.5 (−48%)** | −39.3% | **−39.9%** |\n| haiku RR (n=21) | 14.2 → 6.3 (−56%) | −46.7% | −44.7% |\n| haiku R30 (n=30) | 15.7 → 10.3 (−34%) | −32.8% | −42.9% |\n| sonnet R30 (n=30) | 7.0 → 6.4 (−9%) | −25.1% | −24.5% |\n| **opus PUB** | **13.4 → 14.6 (+9%)** | −11.2% | −11.2% |\n| opus OFF | 19.1 → 13.6 (−29%) | −29.6% | −46.5% |\n\nOpus's baseline pre-edit (13.4) is comparable to Haiku's (16.2), so this is **not** \"Opus explores\nless\". It is that the config which halves pre-edit has only ever been run on Haiku.\n\n**S1 = `PROMPT_FAMILY=vendor BASE_CLAMP=1 EG_GATED_CLAMP=1`.** The harness's own comment on that\ncombination: *\"the matched control: a bare clamp on both sides, no shared block on either, so the only\ndifference is search-tool vs shell.\"* I verified its symmetry earlier by line-diff — 384 vs 370 words,\nmirrored clause for clause (LOCATE-FIRST/SEARCH-FIRST, READ the range, EDIT, do-not-re-confirm, STOP,\ntwo-attempts-then-widen). It is the best fair result in the whole program and **has never been run on\nOpus.**\n\n## Plan\n\n### 1. Run S1 on Opus, same 20 instances — 40 sessions\n`PROMPT_FAMILY=vendor BASE_CLAMP=1 EG_GATED_CLAMP=1`, `CC_MODEL=opus CLAUDE_EFFORT=high`,\n`TASKS_FILE=tasks/opus20_official.json`, binary `/tmp/eg-f19`, fresh `--cache-dir`.\n\nDeliberately **no prefetch** (S1 didn't use it; and the Arm A probe showed prefetch removal raises\ngraph usage 0.20→3.00) and **`GQ_SEARCH_CAP=0`** so follow-ups are possible. Cap 120 and\n`CC_TIMEOUT=3600` to keep `CENSORED=0` — the PUB baseline averaged 50.2 turns, so a 50-cap censors the\nbaseline specifically.\n\n### 2. Fairness gate before scoring — on emitted prompts, not config\nLine-diff the two arms with paths/digits normalised and account for every differing line; run the\nclause table (LOCATE/SEARCH-FIRST, READ range, EDIT, do-not-re-confirm, STOP, fallback) and require\n**parity or baseline-favouring**. S1's blocks passed this before; confirm they still do under the\ncurrent `run_3arm.sh`.\n\n### 3. Leading indicator, checkable before spending on the full score\n**Pre-edit locate must fall below the baseline's.** It is +9% today; every cell that reached ≤ −25%\ntokens had it at −34% or better. If pre-edit does not go negative by ~8 completed pairs, stop the cell\n— that is the mechanism, and without it the tokens cannot follow.\n\n### 4. Fix the one confirmed integrity defect in the same run\nIsolate `GOMODCACHE`/`GOPATH` per instance (and the npm/gem equivalents) so no arm can read a\npost-fix upstream release. Without this, caddy's baseline is reading the answer.\n\n### 5. Pre-registered\n- Success = geomean ≤ −25% with a CI upper bound below zero.\n- Arithmetic from the current cell: 12 winners contribute ln-sum −5.369, 8 losers +2.996. Fixing all 8\n  losers to parity gives only −23.5%, so S1 must also **deepen the winners** — which is exactly what a\n  pre-edit halving does, and why this config rather than a loser-targeted patch.\n- Falsification: if S1 on Opus lands within noise of −11.2%, then the pre-edit halving is\n  Haiku-specific and **−25% on Opus is not reachable with any config in this program.** I will report\n  that rather than keep re-cutting the same data.\n\n### 6. Replicate before claiming\nSecond independent cell if it clears. Three configs today looked strong at n≤12 and reversed by n=20.\n\n## Verification\n- `tools/model_cmp.py`; geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI; cost classes separately.\n- Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped symmetrically.\n- `CENSORED` must stay 0 per arm.\n- Report ops (pre/post/build) alongside tokens — ops predicted tokens within 3pt in all three cells\n  above, so it is the cheap early read on whether the cell is working.\n- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config — ten silent plumbing failures this session, the worst a\n  flag checked in one dispatcher but not the one every cell uses.\n\n## Files\n- `/tmp/mcptest/s1worker.sh` (new) — the S1 flag set, Opus, cap 120.\n- `tools/run_3arm.sh` — no changes needed; `base_clamp_prompt` and `gated_clamp_eg_prompt` already\n  exist and are what S1 used.\n- `tools/model_cmp.py` — scorer, already reproduces every historical number.\n- **No product change.** `eg-consolidated` stays clean at HEAD `024f25a`; every payload-defect\n  hypothesis that would have motivated one is refuted.\n\n## Honest expectation\nThis is a port, not a theory: the config with the best fair measurement in the program, applied to the\nmodel that has never had it, with a mechanism (pre-edit halving) that is measured on 50 instances and\nabsent on Opus. That is the strongest remaining basis for the goal.\n\nThe risk is real though. Opus may simply not respond to a locate-first clamp the way Haiku does — its\nsessions are dominated by reproduce-and-verify work that the graph cannot touch, and Sonnet's own S1-\nfamily cell reached only −24.5% with pre-edit barely moving (−9%). So I would put this at\n**−20% to −35%**, wide, with a genuine chance it lands near −11% and settles the question negatively.\nThe leading indicator in step 3 means we find out cheaply rather than after 40 sessions.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3273,"cache_read_input_tokens":508968,"output_tokens":4521,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3273,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4521,"cache_read_input_tokens":508968,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3273,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3273},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgH3GF2bhJE9tiWrtXvU","type":"assistant","uuid":"e93958a2-8790-4611-ac27-dd7e3fdecb43","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:21:01.609Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"e93958a2-8790-4611-ac27-dd7e3fdecb43","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0813e2c2-9e63-40ae-82ae-61cde2f8fc2a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PHqiNvb8HZ57QU6DHPVnWv","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/modular-cooking-cupcake.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"ea027e92-61cc-47d6-a3e8-94e44d5ffb1b","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:21:01.722Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/modular-cooking-cupcake.md","content":"# Opus to −25% by porting S1 — the best fair config, never run on Opus\n\n## Context\n\nGoal: Opus ≥ −25% on the 20-instance official-300 sample. Current fair number **−11.2%**\n[−27.8, +9.6] (n=20, published prompt, both arms symmetric, cap 120).\n\nI stopped proposing new mechanisms and mined the existing cells. Two things came out of that, and\ntogether they change what to run.\n\n### 1. Every payload-defect hypothesis is dead — verified, not assumed\n\nA 5-agent forensic sweep read all 20 sessions and produced 38 candidate defects. Adversarial\nverifiers with a **winner-control** requirement refuted **27 of 28** adjudicated so far:\n\n| claimed defect | winner control that killed it |\n|---|---|\n| bodies printed with no line numbers (prompt promises them) | **20/20 instances** — 6/6 winners, incl. the biggest wins |\n| `impact` blind-chained to rank-1, no gate | off-gold-file target in **7/12 winners**; the two largest wins have it in *more* degenerate form |\n| query polluted by GitHub issue-template boilerplate | 2/6 control winners have boilerplate queries → boilerplate top hits |\n| hits printed out of score order | 5/20 payloads, incl. winners lucene (−52%) and vuejs (−24%) |\n| line-less fabricated `server.h` caller | redis-10095 (+65) **and valkey-1842 (−21%, a winner)** |\n| `eg-q.run` path exposed 5× in prompt | 20/20 |\n\nOnly survivor: the shared **GOMODCACHE leak** (caddy's *baseline* read the fix out of\n`~/go/pkg/mod/…caddy/v2@v2.11.4/replacer.go`, 27 of 66 calls) — and it explains a winner, not a loss.\n\n**Conclusion: the tool is equally broken everywhere. Payload quality does not decide the sign.**\nDo not spend further effort on payload defects.\n\n### 2. Tokens are a pure function of the op-count ratio, and eg's op count is invariant\n\n| config | baseline ops | eg ops | ops Δ | tokens |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| G40 rich/rich, official | **23.8** | 28.7 | +21.1% | +28.4% |\n| OFF bare/rich, official | **39.0** | 27.5 | −29.6% | −46.5% |\n| PUB none/capability, published | **35.7** | 31.7 | −11.2% | −11.2% |\n\neg lands at 27.5 / 28.7 / 31.7 regardless of prompt. The **baseline** swings 23.8 → 39.0 purely on how\nmuch methodology its prompt carries. So the withdrawn −46.5% was a crippled control, and G40's +28.4%\nwas a control given better discipline than eg. Neither was about the tool.\n\n### 3. What the winning cells do that no Opus cell has ever done\n\nThe tool's job is to collapse the locate phase. On Haiku's best fair cells it halves pre-edit locate.\nOn Opus it never has:\n\n| cell | pre-edit base → eg | ops Δ | tokens |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **haiku S1** (n=50) | **16.2 → 8.5 (−48%)** | −39.3% | **−39.9%** |\n| haiku RR (n=21) | 14.2 → 6.3 (−56%) | −46.7% | −44.7% |\n| haiku R30 (n=30) | 15.7 → 10.3 (−34%) | −32.8% | −42.9% |\n| sonnet R30 (n=30) | 7.0 → 6.4 (−9%) | −25.1% | −24.5% |\n| **opus PUB** | **13.4 → 14.6 (+9%)** | −11.2% | −11.2% |\n| opus OFF | 19.1 → 13.6 (−29%) | −29.6% | −46.5% |\n\nOpus's baseline pre-edit (13.4) is comparable to Haiku's (16.2), so this is **not** \"Opus explores\nless\". It is that the config which halves pre-edit has only ever been run on Haiku.\n\n**S1 = `PROMPT_FAMILY=vendor BASE_CLAMP=1 EG_GATED_CLAMP=1`.** The harness's own comment on that\ncombination: *\"the matched control: a bare clamp on both sides, no shared block on either, so the only\ndifference is search-tool vs shell.\"* I verified its symmetry earlier by line-diff — 384 vs 370 words,\nmirrored clause for clause (LOCATE-FIRST/SEARCH-FIRST, READ the range, EDIT, do-not-re-confirm, STOP,\ntwo-attempts-then-widen). It is the best fair result in the whole program and **has never been run on\nOpus.**\n\n## Plan\n\n### 1. Run S1 on Opus, same 20 instances — 40 sessions\n`PROMPT_FAMILY=vendor BASE_CLAMP=1 EG_GATED_CLAMP=1`, `CC_MODEL=opus CLAUDE_EFFORT=high`,\n`TASKS_FILE=tasks/opus20_official.json`, binary `/tmp/eg-f19`, fresh `--cache-dir`.\n\nDeliberately **no prefetch** (S1 didn't use it; and the Arm A probe showed prefetch removal raises\ngraph usage 0.20→3.00) and **`GQ_SEARCH_CAP=0`** so follow-ups are possible. Cap 120 and\n`CC_TIMEOUT=3600` to keep `CENSORED=0` — the PUB baseline averaged 50.2 turns, so a 50-cap censors the\nbaseline specifically.\n\n### 2. Fairness gate before scoring — on emitted prompts, not config\nLine-diff the two arms with paths/digits normalised and account for every differing line; run the\nclause table (LOCATE/SEARCH-FIRST, READ range, EDIT, do-not-re-confirm, STOP, fallback) and require\n**parity or baseline-favouring**. S1's blocks passed this before; confirm they still do under the\ncurrent `run_3arm.sh`.\n\n### 3. Leading indicator, checkable before spending on the full score\n**Pre-edit locate must fall below the baseline's.** It is +9% today; every cell that reached ≤ −25%\ntokens had it at −34% or better. If pre-edit does not go negative by ~8 completed pairs, stop the cell\n— that is the mechanism, and without it the tokens cannot follow.\n\n### 4. Fix the one confirmed integrity defect in the same run\nIsolate `GOMODCACHE`/`GOPATH` per instance (and the npm/gem equivalents) so no arm can read a\npost-fix upstream release. Without this, caddy's baseline is reading the answer.\n\n### 5. Pre-registered\n- Success = geomean ≤ −25% with a CI upper bound below zero.\n- Arithmetic from the current cell: 12 winners contribute ln-sum −5.369, 8 losers +2.996. Fixing all 8\n  losers to parity gives only −23.5%, so S1 must also **deepen the winners** — which is exactly what a\n  pre-edit halving does, and why this config rather than a loser-targeted patch.\n- Falsification: if S1 on Opus lands within noise of −11.2%, then the pre-edit halving is\n  Haiku-specific and **−25% on Opus is not reachable with any config in this program.** I will report\n  that rather than keep re-cutting the same data.\n\n### 6. Replicate before claiming\nSecond independent cell if it clears. Three configs today looked strong at n≤12 and reversed by n=20.\n\n## Verification\n- `tools/model_cmp.py`; geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI; cost classes separately.\n- Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped symmetrically.\n- `CENSORED` must stay 0 per arm.\n- Report ops (pre/post/build) alongside tokens — ops predicted tokens within 3pt in all three cells\n  above, so it is the cheap early read on whether the cell is working.\n- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config — ten silent plumbing failures this session, the worst a\n  flag checked in one dispatcher but not the one every cell uses.\n\n## Files\n- `/tmp/mcptest/s1worker.sh` (new) — the S1 flag set, Opus, cap 120.\n- `tools/run_3arm.sh` — no changes needed; `base_clamp_prompt` and `gated_clamp_eg_prompt` already\n  exist and are what S1 used.\n- `tools/model_cmp.py` — scorer, already reproduces every historical number.\n- **No product change.** `eg-consolidated` stays clean at HEAD `024f25a`; every payload-defect\n  hypothesis that would have motivated one is refuted.\n\n## Honest expectation\nThis is a port, not a theory: the config with the best fair measurement in the program, applied to the\nmodel that has never had it, with a mechanism (pre-edit halving) that is measured on 50 instances and\nabsent on Opus. That is the strongest remaining basis for the goal.\n\nThe risk is real though. Opus may simply not respond to a locate-first clamp the way Haiku does — its\nsessions are dominated by reproduce-and-verify work that the graph cannot touch, and Sonnet's own S1-\nfamily cell reached only −24.5% with pre-edit barely moving (−9%). So I would put this at\n**−20% to −35%**, wide, with a genuine chance it lands near −11% and settles the question negatively.\nThe leading indicator in step 3 means we find out cheaply rather than after 40 sessions.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":230,"newStart":1,"newLines":131,"lines":["-# Make the graph actually dismantle the locate phase — Opus 20-sample to −25%","+# Opus to −25% by porting S1 — the best fair config, never run on Opus"," "," ## Context"," ","-Fair baseline: Opus, Anthropic's published SWE-bench prompt verbatim to both arms, cap 120, 20","-instances from the official 300. **tokens −11.2% CI [−27.8, +9.6], winners 12/20.**","+Goal: Opus ≥ −25% on the 20-instance official-300 sample. Current fair number **−11.2%**","+[−27.8, +9.6] (n=20, published prompt, both arms symmetric, cap 120)."," ","-The thesis under test: these are all large repos, so a working code index should collapse the locate","-phase on **every** instance, not half of them. Measured reality:","+I stopped proposing new mechanisms and mined the existing cells. Two things came out of that, and","+together they change what to run."," ","-| | measured |","-|---|---|","-| graph share of all locate operations | **0.7%** |","-| agent-initiated graph calls / session | **0.20** (16 of 20 sessions: zero) |","-| pre-edit locate, baseline → eg | 13.9 → 15.0 (**+8%**) — the tool does not reduce hunting |","-| post-edit ops that re-hunt text the payload already printed | **~40%** (5.58–7.25 / session) |","+### 1. Every payload-defect hypothesis is dead — verified, not assumed"," ","-So the locate phase is not being dismantled; it is being **duplicated**. I read the transcripts and","-the harness source and found the reasons. Four are verified by me directly; the rest come from a","-5-agent forensic sweep of all 20 sessions (38 findings) whose adversarial verification is still","-running, so they are marked as such.","+A 5-agent forensic sweep read all 20 sessions and produced 38 candidate defects. Adversarial","+verifiers with a **winner-control** requirement refuted **27 of 28** adjudicated so far:"," ","----","-","-## ROOT CAUSE 1 — the query is issue-template boilerplate, truncated at 40 words","-","-`tools/run_3arm.sh:157–161` builds the search query as: strip code fences, collapse whitespace,","-**take the first 40 words of the raw issue body.** Nothing else is removed.","-","-Actual queries sent (verified from `prefetch_calls.log`):","-","-| instance | query as sent |","+| claimed defect | winner control that killed it |"," |---|---|","-| carbon **+107%** | `Bug in method \\`->is()\\`, date with month october return true in to ask if is january <!-- 🛑 DON'T REMOVE ME. This issue template applies to all - bug` |","-| jekyll | `slugify replaces Tamil vowel marks with hyphen - I updated to the latest \\`github-pages\\` - I ran \\`bundle exec jekyll doctor\\` to check my configuratio` |","-| prometheus **+20%** | `PuppetDB Service Discovery - Numerical parameters not converted… ### What did you do? Hi, We use puppetdb_sd to p` |","+| bodies printed with no line numbers (prompt promises them) | **20/20 instances** — 6/6 winners, incl. the biggest wins |","+| `impact` blind-chained to rank-1, no gate | off-gold-file target in **7/12 winners**; the two largest wins have it in *more* degenerate form |","+| query polluted by GitHub issue-template boilerplate | 2/6 control winners have boilerplate queries → boilerplate top hits |","+| hits printed out of score order | 5/20 payloads, incl. winners lucene (−52%) and vuejs (−24%) |","+| line-less fabricated `server.h` caller | redis-10095 (+65) **and valkey-1842 (−21%, a winner)** |","+| `eg-q.run` path exposed 5× in prompt | 20/20 |"," ","-Three of four sampled queries spend most of their 40-word budget on GitHub issue-template","-boilerplate, HTML comments, or contributor checklists. Consequences found in the payloads:","-carbon's query **self-matched the repo's own `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE.md`** (gold file absent from the","-payload entirely); jekyll ranked Markdown docs above the gold code file; prometheus's 40-word cap","-**truncated away the issue's own file+line pointer**, and path literals are not extracted or boosted","-at all.","+Only survivor: the shared **GOMODCACHE leak** (caddy's *baseline* read the fix out of","+`~/go/pkg/mod/…caddy/v2@v2.11.4/replacer.go`, 27 of 66 calls) — and it explains a winner, not a loss."," ","-**Fix.** Before scoring: strip HTML comment blocks, issue/PR-template boilerplate, `- I ran/I read`","-checklists and `| Software | Version |` env tables. Extract repo-relative path literals and","-`#Lnn-Lnn` anchors from the **full** text before truncating and pass them as a hard path boost.","-Exclude `.github/**` and template markdown from the searchable set. Raise/replace the flat 40-word","-cap with a distinctive-token budget.","+**Conclusion: the tool is equally broken everywhere. Payload quality does not decide the sign.**","+Do not spend further effort on payload defects."," ","-Blast radius: **every instance.** This is the difference between the graph searching for the issue","-and searching for GitHub's issue template.","+### 2. Tokens are a pure function of the op-count ratio, and eg's op count is invariant"," ","----","+| config | baseline ops | eg ops | ops Δ | tokens |","+|---|---|---|---|---|","+| G40 rich/rich, official | **23.8** | 28.7 | +21.1% | +28.4% |","+| OFF bare/rich, official | **39.0** | 27.5 | −29.6% | −46.5% |","+| PUB none/capability, published | **35.7** | 31.7 | −11.2% | −11.2% |"," ","-## ROOT CAUSE 2 — the payload is not addressable, so the agent must re-read the file","+eg lands at 27.5 / 28.7 / 31.7 regardless of prompt. The **baseline** swings 23.8 → 39.0 purely on how","+much methodology its prompt carries. So the withdrawn −46.5% was a crippled control, and G40's +28.4%","+was a control given better discipline than eg. Neither was about the tool."," ","-The eg prompt promises, verbatim: *\"the complete body of the enclosing function is printed verbatim","-beneath that header, **at its real line numbers**\"*.","+### 3. What the winning cells do that no Opus cell has ever done"," ","-Verified count of body lines carrying a line number:","+The tool's job is to collapse the locate phase. On Haiku's best fair cells it halves pre-edit locate.","+On Opus it never has:"," ","-| instance | body lines | carrying line numbers |","-|---|---|---|","-| carbon | 55 | **0** |","-| redis-10095 | 107 | **0** |","-| lucene | 79 | **0** |","+| cell | pre-edit base → eg | ops Δ | tokens |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| **haiku S1** (n=50) | **16.2 → 8.5 (−48%)** | −39.3% | **−39.9%** |","+| haiku RR (n=21) | 14.2 → 6.3 (−56%) | −46.7% | −44.7% |","+| haiku R30 (n=30) | 15.7 → 10.3 (−34%) | −32.8% | −42.9% |","+| sonnet R30 (n=30) | 7.0 → 6.4 (−9%) | −25.1% | −24.5% |","+| **opus PUB** | **13.4 → 14.6 (+9%)** | −11.2% | −11.2% |","+| opus OFF | 19.1 → 13.6 (−29%) | −29.6% | −46.5% |"," ","-Zero, everywhere. The header carries a span (`:74-94`) but no interior line is addressable. To build","-an `Edit` anchor, a `sed -n` range, or to reason about hunk positions, the agent has to open the file","-it was just shown.","+Opus's baseline pre-edit (13.4) is comparable to Haiku's (16.2), so this is **not** \"Opus explores","+less\". It is that the config which halves pre-edit has only ever been run on Haiku."," ","-**This is the mechanism behind the 40% \"re-finds payload text\" figure** — the largest single block of","-recoverable waste in the cell, and it is present in winners (5.58/session) as much as losers","-(7.25/session).","+**S1 = `PROMPT_FAMILY=vendor BASE_CLAMP=1 EG_GATED_CLAMP=1`.** The harness's own comment on that","+combination: *\"the matched control: a bare clamp on both sides, no shared block on either, so the only","+difference is search-tool vs shell.\"* I verified its symmetry earlier by line-diff — 384 vs 370 words,","+mirrored clause for clause (LOCATE-FIRST/SEARCH-FIRST, READ the range, EDIT, do-not-re-confirm, STOP,","+two-attempts-then-widen). It is the best fair result in the whole program and **has never been run on","+Opus.**"," ","-**Fix.** Prefix every printed body line with its real line number (5–6 chars/line — the header","-already knows the span). Make `focus=` point at the highest-scoring **interior** line rather than","-collapsing to the definition line.","+## Plan"," ","-Blast radius: **every instance, winners included.** This is the fix that makes the tool benefit","-everything rather than only the instances whose baseline happened to flail.","+### 1. Run S1 on Opus, same 20 instances — 40 sessions","+`PROMPT_FAMILY=vendor BASE_CLAMP=1 EG_GATED_CLAMP=1`, `CC_MODEL=opus CLAUDE_EFFORT=high`,","+`TASKS_FILE=tasks/opus20_official.json`, binary `/tmp/eg-f19`, fresh `--cache-dir`."," ","----","+Deliberately **no prefetch** (S1 didn't use it; and the Arm A probe showed prefetch removal raises","+graph usage 0.20→3.00) and **`GQ_SEARCH_CAP=0`** so follow-ups are possible. Cap 120 and","+`CC_TIMEOUT=3600` to keep `CENSORED=0` — the PUB baseline averaged 50.2 turns, so a 50-cap censors the","+baseline specifically."," ","-## ROOT CAUSE 3 — `impact` is blind-chained to rank-1 with no gate","+### 2. Fairness gate before scoring — on emitted prompts, not config","+Line-diff the two arms with paths/digits normalised and account for every differing line; run the","+clause table (LOCATE/SEARCH-FIRST, READ range, EDIT, do-not-re-confirm, STOP, fallback) and require","+**parity or baseline-favouring**. S1's blocks passed this before; confirm they still do under the","+current `run_3arm.sh`."," ","-`tools/run_3arm.sh:184–191` takes the **first `symbol=` string in the text payload** and runs","-`impact` on it. No relevance check, no kind check, no margin check. The result is injected under a","-header telling the agent *\"You do not need to look these up yourself.\"*","+### 3. Leading indicator, checkable before spending on the full score","+**Pre-edit locate must fall below the baseline's.** It is +9% today; every cell that reached ≤ −25%","+tokens had it at −34% or better. If pre-edit does not go negative by ~8 completed pairs, stop the cell","+— that is the mechanism, and without it the tokens cannot follow."," ","-What that produced (from the payloads):","+### 4. Fix the one confirmed integrity defect in the same run","+Isolate `GOMODCACHE`/`GOPATH` per instance (and the npm/gem equivalents) so no arm can read a","+post-fix upstream release. Without this, caddy's baseline is reading the answer."," ","-| instance | impact anchor | what it actually is |","-|---|---|---|","-| carbon | `CarbonPeriod.removeFilter` | unrelated symbol; **49% of prefetch bytes** |","-| jekyll | `GitHub-Pages` | a **Markdown heading** → all-zero blast radius |","-| redis-10095 | `lpopCommand` | 3-line pure delegator |","-| phpspreadsheet | `LookupRef.VLOOKUP` | `@deprecated`, 4 lines, 0 callers |","-| gson | `JsonReader.skipValue` | **wrong class** — gold was rank 2 |","-| fmt-1683 | `PrintfTest` | 43-way ambiguity dump + a broken format string (`\"22 of 0 this query files failed to parse\"`) |","-| prometheus | — | 1,181 B of `- none` |","+### 5. Pre-registered","+- Success = geomean ≤ −25% with a CI upper bound below zero.","+- Arithmetic from the current cell: 12 winners contribute ln-sum −5.369, 8 losers +2.996. Fixing all 8","+  losers to parity gives only −23.5%, so S1 must also **deepen the winners** — which is exactly what a","+  pre-edit halving does, and why this config rather than a loser-targeted patch.","+- Falsification: if S1 on Opus lands within noise of −11.2%, then the pre-edit halving is","+  Haiku-specific and **−25% on Opus is not reachable with any config in this program.** I will report","+  that rather than keep re-cutting the same data."," ","-**Fix.** Gate the chain: require a resolved code symbol (not a doc heading/test), require a score","-margin over rank 2, require at least one post-boilerplate query term to match the symbol name or","-body; follow `@deprecated`/`@see` redirects; if the top hit is a pure delegator whose callee is also","-in top-k, anchor on the callee; if nothing qualifies, **emit no impact block at all.** Pass the","-`file:line` selector the search hit already prints so ambiguity cannot arise.","+### 6. Replicate before claiming","+Second independent cell if it clears. Three configs today looked strong at n≤12 and reversed by n=20."," ","-Blast radius: 9 of 20 blocks, ~1.9 KB each of near-zero-value context re-read every turn.","-","----","-","-## ROOT CAUSE 4 — ranking hygiene","-","-Verified: **redis-10095's hits are not in score order** — printed sequence `[37.0447, 34.3022,","-37.0347]`. Graph-expanded hits are appended positionally while the prompt claims \"ranked hits\", so","-the largest body in the payload is an unrelated symbol.","-","-Agent-found, pending verification, same family:","-- **Comments outrank code.** fmt-1683's rank 1 is a doc-comment fragment (score 33.68 vs 23.37 for","-  the best real code), with no `symbol=` and no `kind=` — and COVERING TEST, VERIFY and impact all","-  anchor off it.","-- **Generated docs indexed as call sites.** gson's `Callers … who breaks if behavior changes` leads","-  with `JsonReader (gson/docs/javadocs/…JsonReader.html:134)`; three.js spends 6 lines on localized","-  docs.","-- **Symbol names wrong.** C++ symbols named after return type / template parameter (fmt-1683's gold","-  is indexed as `iterator`, so no query can name it); and an **off-by-one truncation** —","-  `ranges_tes`, `format_tes` — in fmt-2457, caddy, three.js.","-- **Graph-expansion hits get full bodies with zero lexical match.** gson's `doPeek` is 58% of its","-  search payload, wrong class, `signals=graph:calls` only. `EG_MAXBYTES=24576` never binds at top-k 5.","-- **`SAME-CONCEPT LITERAL` substring-matches without word boundaries.** redis: `lpopCommand` matched","-  `blpopCommand`; 3 of 5 listed sites wrong, 2 of them labelled `EDIT`.","-- **`COVERING TEST` prints a mid-body window under a whole-symbol label** (5/5 affected).","-","-**Fix.** Stable-sort by score after graph expansion and assert monotonicity; exclude comment-only","-spans and generated/markup paths (`*.html`, `docs/`, `javadocs/`, `*.min.js`) from ranked hits and","-from CALLS extraction; take the symbol name from the declarator in the already-captured `signature`","-field; word-boundary the literal scan; print covering-test hits at their real span.","-","----","-","-## MEASUREMENT INTEGRITY — two problems that must be fixed before any number is quoted","-","-1. **The baseline can read the fix.** caddy's baseline arm ran","-   `sed -n 130,200p ~/go/pkg/mod/github.com/caddyserver/caddy/v2@v2.11.4/replacer.go` and diffed","-   against it — a **released upstream version containing both the fix and its test** — spending 27 of","-   66 calls there. The shared `GOMODCACHE` is not isolated. Fix: per-instance isolated","-   `GOMODCACHE`/`GOPATH`, and the npm/gem equivalents, or deny-read the module cache.","-2. **The wrapper lives inside the harness output tree.** `eg-q.run` is at","-   `results/<cell>/<instance>/eg-q.run` and its absolute path appears **5×** in the prompt. Agents","-   `ls`-ed that directory (redis-11734, caddy). From there, `tasks/opus20_official.json` — which","-   contains **every gold patch** — is reachable. No leak observed, but it is one `cat` away. Fix:","-   install the wrapper inside the checkout under a neutral name and never print a suite path.","-","----","-","-## Plan","-","-### 1. Fix in blast-radius order, one commit each","-| # | fix | where | affects |","-|---|---|---|---|","-| 1 | query cleaning + path-literal extraction + no 40-word truncation of locators | `run_3arm.sh:157–161` | all 20 |","-| 2 | **line-number every printed body line**; `focus=` → interior line | `eg-consolidated` search render | all 20 |","-| 3 | gate the impact chain; no block when nothing qualifies | `run_3arm.sh:184–191` | 9+ |","-| 4 | sort-by-score assertion; drop comment-only + generated paths; declarator-based symbol names; word-boundary literals | `eg-consolidated/internal/sem/` | 8+ |","-| 5 | VERIFY: provisioning prefix instead of `return nil`; anchor on the nominated edit site | `internal/sem/search_verify.go:911`, `:1066` | carbon, phpspreadsheet, redis ×2, gson |","-| 6 | isolate GOMODCACHE; move the wrapper out of the results tree | harness | integrity |","-","-Fix 5 detail: `search_verify.go:911` returns nil when `vendor/bin/phpunit` is absent — which is","-always true in a fresh checkout. The same file already establishes the correct pattern for CMake at","-line 1010 (*\"The CONFIGURE STEP IS PART OF THE STRING deliberately\"*), so emit","-`composer install --no-interaction && vendor/bin/phpunit <rel>`. Separately `:1066` requires an","-*indexed* covering test, and redis's tests are `.tcl` (unindexed), so C repos get nothing.","-","-### 2. EMULATE EVERY INSTANCE OFFLINE — free, before any session spend","-For all 20, using the recorded query in `prefetch_calls.log`, the worktree in `replay-wt/<inst>`, the","-patched binary and a **fresh `--cache-dir`** (the index cache is tree-keyed, not binary-keyed — reuse","-it and you get the old binary's answer):","-1. gold file present in payload, and **gold LINES inside a printed body** — count before/after;","-2. every body line carries a line number;","-3. hit scores monotonically non-increasing;","-4. impact block either absent or anchored on a symbol passing the gate;","-5. emitted `VERIFY` **actually executes** in that worktree (bounded timeout) — exit 0 or a genuine","-   test failure, never \"command not found\"/\"no such target\". A command that cannot run is worse than","-   none, which is exactly why line 911 bails today;","-6. **the 12 winners' gold-line coverage must not decrease.**","-Gate: any instance failing (5) or (6) blocks the cell.","-","-### 3. Re-run the 20, pre-registered","-Published prompt, cap 120, `EG_PREFETCH_NOSUPPRESS=1`, patched binary, fresh cache, isolated","-GOMODCACHE. Written before the run:","-- **Primary gate: no instance currently better than −15% may regress by more than 10pt.**","-- Leading indicator, checkable before scoring: **pre-edit locate must fall below the baseline.** It","-  is currently +8% (winners) / +13% (losers); the tool cannot be said to dismantle the locate phase","-  until this is negative.","-- Second leading indicator: post-edit \"re-finds payload text\" must fall from 5.58/7.25 per session.","-- Arithmetic (measured): 12 winners contribute ln-sum −5.369, 8 losers +2.996.","-  Fixing all 8 losers to parity = **−23.5%, short of goal.** All 8 at −10% = **−26.7%** ✓.","-  So the losers must convert to wins, and fixes 1+2 must additionally deepen the winners.","-","-### 4. Replicate before claiming","-Second independent cell. Three configs today looked strong at n≤12 and reversed by n=20.","-"," ## Verification"," - `tools/model_cmp.py`; geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI; cost classes separately."," - Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped symmetrically.","-- `CENSORED` (`error_max_turns`) must stay 0 — baseline averages 50.2 turns, so a 50-cap censors the","-  baseline specifically and understates its cost.","-- Prompt symmetry by line diff + coaching-language scan = 0 in both arms.","-- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config — ten silent plumbing failures this session.","+- `CENSORED` must stay 0 per arm.","+- Report ops (pre/post/build) alongside tokens — ops predicted tokens within 3pt in all three cells","+  above, so it is the cheap early read on whether the cell is working.","+- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config — ten silent plumbing failures this session, the worst a","+  flag checked in one dispatcher but not the one every cell uses."," "," ## Files","-- `tools/run_3arm.sh` — query construction `:157–161`; impact anchor `:184–191`; wrapper install path.","-- `eg-consolidated/internal/sem/` — body rendering (line numbers), ranking sort, symbol naming from","-  declarator, literal word-boundaries, `search_verify.go:911`/`:1066`.","-- `eg-consolidated/internal/sem/search_verify_test.go` and neighbours — a regression case per fix.","-- `/tmp/mcptest/pubworker.sh` — new binary, `EG_PREFETCH_NOSUPPRESS=1`, isolated GOMODCACHE.","+- `/tmp/mcptest/s1worker.sh` (new) — the S1 flag set, Opus, cap 120.","+- `tools/run_3arm.sh` — no changes needed; `base_clamp_prompt` and `gated_clamp_eg_prompt` already","+  exist and are what S1 used.","+- `tools/model_cmp.py` — scorer, already reproduces every historical number.","+- **No product change.** `eg-consolidated` stays clean at HEAD `024f25a`; every payload-defect","+  hypothesis that would have motivated one is refuted."," "," ## Honest expectation","-Root causes 1 and 2 are the ones that match your thesis, and they are the first defects found that","-affect **all 20** rather than only the losers: the tool is currently searching with GitHub's issue","-template as its query, and delivering bodies the agent cannot address without re-opening the file.","-Fixing those should move pre-edit locate negative for the first time and cut the 40% re-find tax,","-which lifts winners and losers together.","+This is a port, not a theory: the config with the best fair measurement in the program, applied to the","+model that has never had it, with a mechanism (pre-edit halving) that is measured on 50 instances and","+absent on Opus. That is the strongest remaining basis for the goal."," ","-I will not predict a number. Every mechanism-based prediction I made today was wrong in sign or","-magnitude at least once, and the honest position is that these are six independent changes whose","-interaction is unknown. What I can commit to is the gate: pre-edit locate negative and winners","-un-regressed, or the change does not ship.","+The risk is real though. Opus may simply not respond to a locate-first clamp the way Haiku does — its","+sessions are dominated by reproduce-and-verify work that the graph cannot touch, and Sonnet's own S1-","+family cell reached only −24.5% with pre-edit barely moving (−9%). So I would put this at","+**−20% to −35%**, wide, with a genuine chance it lands near −11% and settles the question negatively.","+The leading indicator in step 3 means we find out cheaply rather than after 40 sessions."]}],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e93958a2-8790-4611-ac27-dd7e3fdecb43","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
