ready showed you. Spend your turns on the FIX, not on looking\n +around: every turn re-reads your whole context, and that is what this task costs.\n +DISCOVERY IS CLAMPED - FINISHING IS NOT. Before you stop, all three must be true:\n +(N) VERIFIED - you compiled the change or ran the nearest existing test at least ONCE. Pick the\n +    narrowest command that would still catch a syntax, type, name or arity error. A patch that does\n +    not build fails the whole task; this is the cheapest turn you will spend. Then stop verifying -\n +    read the error, fix what it names, re-run once. Do NOT hunt a green suite.\n +(N) SWEPT - you checked the RELATED SITES the search result listed (callers, siblings, near-dupes)\n +    and fixed every one that has the same bug. A fix is usually not one edit in one place.\n +(N) COMPLETE - you handled the edge cases the issue names (empty, nil, negative, unicode, error\n +    paths).\n +If a search did not land it, search again with different words; if TWO searches miss, fall back to\n +the shell in ONE batched call. Never stop merely because you have made an edit - stop when (N),\n +(N) and (N) hold.\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/suhaan/devenv","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"399e178b-0447-43fe-b080-13e6f00e69a2","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:24:11.682Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"syntax OK\n=== FAIRNESS GATE: full line diff, paths/digits normalised ===\nbaseline 57 lines / eg 64 lines\n --- baseline\n +++ eg\n @@ -46,12 +46,19 @@\n -Locate the fix with the shell BEFORE reading anything. Your FIRST action is ONE batched search:\n -put every probe you already know you need into a single call joined by ';' — start from the most\n -distinctive literal the issue gives you (an error message, an option name, an identifier).\n -Then open the best hit with your native Read tool (pass a line range around the matched line), make\n -the minimal edit, and STOP. The strongest match is the fix site on most tasks — go straight there\n -and edit; do NOT r