{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:25:05.244Z","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>w6onanu3a</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01XrZAm4ccwrbCzwxH7wFE7S</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208/tasks/w6onanu3a.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Investigate every eg arm on the fair Opus cell for real defects, control against winners, rank fixes\" completed</summary>\n<result>{\"survivorCount\":1,\"survivors\":[{\"title\":\"MEASUREMENT: shared GOMODCACHE leaks the post-fix upstream release + the gold test fixture; only the baseline arm consumed it\",\"instances\":[\"caddyserver__caddy-5995\"],\"evidence\":\"Baseline op 42 `sed -n 130,200p ~/go/pkg/mod/github.com/caddyserver/caddy/v2@v2.11.4/replacer.go`; op 43 `diff &lt;(sed -n '/^scan:/,/flush any unwritten remainder/p' ~/go/pkg/mod/.../v2@v2.11.4/replacer.go) &lt;(... replacer.go)`; op 48 `cat /Users/suhaan/go/pkg/mod/github.com/caddyserver/caddy/v2@v2.11.4/caddytest/integration/caddyfile_adapt/uri_replace_brace_escape.caddyfiletest` which returns exactly the issue's Caddyfile (`uri replace \\\"\\\\}\\\" %7D` / `uri replace \\\"\\\\{\\\" %7B`) -- a fixture ADDED by the PR under benchmark; op 50 copies it into the checkout (`cp /Users/suhaan/go/pkg/mod/.../uri_replace_brace_escape.caddyfiletest /tmp/... &amp;&amp; cp ... caddytest/integration`). Ops 40-66 (27 of the baseline's 66 tool calls) are this detour. No eg-arm op references `go/pkg/mod`. Baseline 105 assistant msgs vs eg 54.\",\"mechanism\":\"The instance runs against the user's real GOPATH, which holds a released version containing both the fix and its test. The baseline arm stumbled into it and spent 41% of its ops there; the eg arm did not. That asymmetry is scored as an eg token saving, so a large share of caddy's -56% (the cell's #2 winner) is environment contamination, not tool merit.\",\"proposed_fix\":\"Run each instance with an isolated GOMODCACHE/GOPATH (and the npm cache / GEM_HOME equivalents) vendored to pre-fix versions, or deny-read the module cache, so no arm can read a fixed upstream copy of the file under test.\",\"est_tokens_at_stake\":\"27 of 66 baseline tool calls x 6,197,434 cache_read / 105 msgs = 59.0K per msg ~= 1.6M cache-read positions, ~26% of the baseline session -- comparable in size to the whole -56% gap this instance contributes to the cell mean.\",\"winner_control\":\"Not refutable by winner control — the claim explains a WINNER rather than proposing a loss mechanism. Frequency check across all 40 sessions: reads of the module cache for the repo UNDER TEST occur in exactly 1/40 (baseline caddy, 12/66 ops touch ~/go/pkg/mod directly). The only other cache reads are benign dependency lookups: baseline hugo 2/81 ops (spf13/cast) and eg gson 11/25 ops (~/.m2 junit/hamcrest jars for a classpath) — neither is the repo under test.\",\"verifier_reason\":\"Verified and STRONGER than claimed. /Users/suhaan/go/pkg/mod/github.com/caddyserver/caddy/v2@v2.11.4/replacer.go:179 contains the exact gold line `if !strings.Contains(input, string(phOpen)) &amp;&amp; !strings.Contains(input, string(phClose)) {`. Baseline ops 42-44 read and diffed it; op 48 cat'd .../caddytest/integration/caddyfile_adapt/uri_replace_brace_escape.caddyfiletest, which is byte-identical to the instance's own test_patch new file caddyfile_adapt/uri_replace_brace_escape.txt; op 50 copied it into the checkout; op 54 then wrote zz_tmp_urireplace_test.go reproducing test_patch's TestUriReplace including `admin localhost:2999`, `http_port 9080`, `uri replace \\\"\\\\}\\\" %7D` and the expected `test=%7B%20content%20%7D`. That is a FAIL_TO_PASS test leak plus the fixed source, into the baseline arm only. Magnitude: baseline 3,920,247 total tokens vs eg 1,713,808 (ratio 0.437 = -56.3%, matches the reported -56); ops 40-66 are 27 of 66 baseline tool calls at ~36K cache_read/msg, so the detour plausibly accounts for a large fraction of the gap in the cell's #2 winner. Caveats: the claimed cache_read totals (6,197,434 / 2,687,366) are ~1.6x the cc_out.json values (3,806,114 / 1,624,458), so the 1.6M figure is inflated; and part of ops 55-65 is legitimate revert/reapply differential verification. Fix is concrete: isolated GOMODCACHE/GOPATH pinned pre-fix, or deny-read the module cache.\"}],\"remediation\":\"## Prioritised remediation list\\n\\nProtected set (gate: currently better than −15%, may not regress &gt;10pt): jekyll −58, caddy −56, preact −54, lucene −52, fpm −40, docusaurus −38, vuejs −24, valkey −21, three.js −18, fmt-2457 −18. (hugo recomputes to −14.5, outside.)\\n\\n| # | Defect (evidence) | Generality | Severity + derivation | Fix goes in | Winner risk vs gate | Falsifiable prediction |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| **P0** | **Shared package-cache leaks the post-fix upstream file.** Verified twice, once per arm. baseline caddy: `cat ~/go/pkg/mod/.../caddy/v2@v2.11.4/caddytest/integration/caddyfile_adapt/uri_replace_brace_escape.caddyfiletest` → the PR's own new fixture; `~/go/pkg/mod/.../v2@v2.11.4/replacer.go:179` holds the gold line verbatim. **NEW: eg carbon-2752** ops 13–19 `for f in ~/Library/Caches/composer/files/nesbot/carbon/*.zip; do … unzip` → op 17 returns `'/^(?:january\\\\|…\\\\|december)(?:\\\\s+\\\\d+)?$/i'`, byte-identical to the gold patch's `+` line; eg's `patch.diff` transcribes it plus a second block lifted from the same zip. netjail already blocks `curl`/`wget` (baseline carbon + fmt-1683 curls both returned `netjail: 'curl' is blocked`), so caches are the **only surviving leak channel** | 2/20 instances (caddy, carbon) — **one per arm**. Degrades a winner AND a loser. Other cache reads are benign deps (baseline hugo spf13/cast, eg gson ~/.m2 jars, eg fpm ~/.gem rspec) | caddy: 27/66 baseline ops = 41% of ops; 3,920,247 tok / 105 msgs = 37.3K/msg × ~43 msgs ≈ 1.6M ≈ 41% of that session. carbon: 7/52 eg ops; 3,639,280 / 93 = 39.1K/msg × ~12 msgs ≈ 470K ≈ 13%. Cell mean impact is small because they cancel: drop both → −11.9% (vs published −11.2%) | **harness** — `tools/run_3arm.sh` ~L1528 netjail block. Add `GOMODCACHE`/`GOPATH`/`COMPOSER_HOME`/`GEM_HOME`/`M2_REPO`/`CARGO_HOME`/`npm_config_cache` redirected to a per-instance empty dir, or deny-read `$HOME` caches. netjail dir already exists to hang it on | **BREACHES.** caddy −56.3 → −25 to −41 (15–31pt regression). This is unavoidable and correct: the gate is protecting a contaminated number | caddy baseline ops 66→~39, tokens 3.92M→~2.3M, ratio −56.3%→−25±8. carbon eg ops 52→~45, \\\\|Δratio\\\\|≥25pt (direction unknown — the leak both cost 7 ops and supplied the answer). Cell mean stays within 2pt of −11.9% |\\n| **P1** | **`impact` returns a disambiguation menu instead of an answer.** caddy `prefetch_impact.payload` is *entirely* `Ambiguous symbol \\\"parseCaddyfile\\\" matched 12 definitions; rerun with the selector printed beside the one you mean` + 12 menu lines. Non-interactive prefetch cannot rerun. The needed selector (`--file modules/caddyhttp/fileserver/caddyfile.go --line 47`) is printed in the menu *and* already known to the caller — `prefetch_calls.log` shows the call was `impact parseCaddyfile`, bare name only | 1/20 total failure (caddy). Latent wherever rank-1 symbol name is non-unique — Go `parseCaddyfile`, Rust trait methods, PHP interface methods | 2.0KB / ~500 tok of payload delivering zero information, 1 of the 2 payload blocks. Small in tokens; the point is the block is 100% dead | **both**: `eg-consolidated` `impact` should resolve against the anchor's file:line when supplied and never emit a menu to a non-tty; `tools/run_3arm.sh` prefetch must pass `--symbol/--file/--line` parsed from the rank-1 hit header it already has | caddy is −56.3, protected. Replacing a menu with a real blast radius rewrites that winner's prompt → unbounded. Flag | 0/20 impact payloads contain `Ambiguous symbol`. caddy impact payload gains ≥1 `Blast radius:` line |\\n| **P2** | **C/C++ index loss + declaration-as-caller.** `Completeness: degraded for C (130 of 676 C files failed to parse)` (redis-11734), 109/538 (redis-10095), 134/735 (valkey) = 18–20% of C files dropped. Consequence: `Callers (1 direct, 0 transitive; who breaks if behavior changes): - server.h (src/server.h)` — a **prototype in a header counted as a call site**, so the entire caller answer for `bitcountCommand` and `lpopCommand` is a lie. redis-11734 rank-2 hit (score 60.17) is `src/server.h:3643-3647`, a 5-line block of forward declarations | Callers-bug\n... (truncated 11526 chars, full result in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208/tasks/w6onanu3a.output)</result>\n<diagnostics>Per-agent results: /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208/subagents/workflows/wf_bfae27bf-047/journal.jsonl — one {\"type\":\"result\",...} line per completed agent with its full return value.\nIf the result above is empty or unexpected, Read this file BEFORE diagnosing — do not assume agents returned non-empty results.\nTo re-run with edited post-processing: Workflow({scriptPath: '/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208/workflows/scripts/eg-loser-forensics-wf_bfae27bf-047.js', resumeFromRunId: 'wf_bfae27bf-047'}) — agents whose (prompt, opts) are unchanged replay from cache.</diagnostics>\n<usage><agent_count>11</agent_count><agents_done>11</agents_done><agents_error>0</agents_error><agents_skipped>0</agents_skipped><agents_empty_result>0</agents_empty_result><subagent_tokens>1477980</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>383</tool_uses><duration_ms>2139406</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
