it.\",\"proposed_fix\":\"Run each instance with an isolated GOMODCACHE/GOPATH (and the npm cache / GEM_HOME equivalents) vendored to pre-fix versions, or deny-read the module cache, so no arm can read a fixed upstream copy of the file under test.\",\"est_tokens_at_stake\":\"27 of 66 baseline tool calls x 6,197,434 cache_read / 105 msgs = 59.0K per msg ~= 1.6M cache-read positions, ~26% of the baseline session -- comparable in size to the whole -56% gap this instance contributes to the cell mean.\",\"winner_control\":\"Not refutable by winner control — the claim explains a WINNER rather than proposing a loss mechanism. Frequency check across all 40 sessions: reads of the module cache for the repo UNDER TEST occur in exactly 1/40 (baseline caddy, 12/66 ops touch ~/go/pkg/mod directly). The only other cache reads are benign dependency lookups: baseline hugo 2/81 ops (spf13/cast) and eg gson 11/25 ops (~/.m2 junit/hamcrest jars for a classpath) — neither is the repo under test.\",\"verifier_reason\":\"Verified and STRONGER than claimed. /Users/suhaan/go/pkg/mod/github.com/caddyserver/caddy/v2@v2.11.4/replacer.go:179 contains the exact gold line `if !strings.Contains(input, string(phOpen)) &amp;&amp; !strings.Contains(input, string(phClose)) {`. Baseline ops 42-44 read and diffed it; op 48 cat'd .../caddytest/integration/caddyfile_adapt/uri_replace_brace_escape.caddyfiletest, which is byte-identical to the instance's own test_patch new file caddyfile_adapt/uri_replace_brace_escape.txt; op 50 copied it into the checkout; op 54 then wrote zz_tmp_urireplace_test.go reproducing test_patch's TestUriReplace including `admin localhost:2999`, `http_port 9080`, `uri replace \\\"\\\\}\\\" %7D` and the expected `test=%7B%20content%20%7D`. That is a FAIL_TO_PASS test leak plus the fixed source, into the baseline arm only. Magnitude: baseline 3,920,247 total tokens vs eg 1,713,808 (ratio 0.437 = -56.3%, matches the reported -56); ops 40-66 are 27 of 66 baseline tool calls at ~36K cac