{"parentUuid":"0743bc3c-203f-4dab-bd8a-426ad39734ce","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/tmp/mcptest/s1worker.sh","snippet":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\n2\tcd /Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench/agentic-swebench\n3\tIFS='|' read -r rep arm iid <<< \"$1\"\n4\texec 0</dev/null\n5\tif [ -z \"$rep\" ] || [ -z \"$arm\" ] || [ -z \"$iid\" ]; then echo \"BADJOB: [$1]\"; exit 9; fi\n6\t\n7\t# S1 = PROMPT_FAMILY=vendor BASE_CLAMP=1 EG_SHIPPED_PROMPT=1 EG_SHIPPED_PROMPT_ACK=1.\n8\t# run_3arm.sh's own comment on this combination: \"the matched control: a bare clamp on both sides,\n9\t# no shared block on either, so the only difference is search-tool vs shell.\"\n10\t# Best fair result in the program (haiku -39.9% n=50, siblings -44.7/-32.0/-27.8) and NEVER run on\n11\t# Opus. Its mechanism is the one Opus has never shown: pre-edit locate 16.2 -> 8.5 (-48%), versus\n12\t# Opus PUB's 13.4 -> 14.6 (+9%).\n13\texport TASKS_FILE=tasks/opus20_official.json CLAUDE_EFFORT=high CC_MODEL=opus\n14\texport ENTIRE_GRAPH=/tmp/eg-f19\n15\texport PROMPT_FAMILY=vendor BASE_CLAMP=1 EG_SHIPPED_PROMPT=1 EG_SHIPPED_PROMPT_ACK=1\n16\t# No prefetch: S1 did not use it, and the probe showed removing it raises agent graph calls\n17\t# 0.20 -> 3.00. Cap lifted so follow-up searches are possible at all.\n18\texport EG_PREFETCH=0 EG_PREFETCH_IMPACT=0 GQ_SEARCH_CAP=0\n19\texport EG_TOPK=5 EG_CONF_TIER=0 EG_TOPK_SHOW=10 EG_MAXBYTES=24576 EG_SNIPPET=6 EG_MAX_PER_FILE=3\n20\texport EG_VERIFY_MODE=full EG_PROFILE=full EG_TIER=0\n21\t# Cap 120 + matching timeout: the PUB baseline averaged 50.2 turns, so a 50-cap right-censors the\n22\t# BASELINE specifically and understates its cost.\n23\texport CC_MAX_TURNS=120 CC_TIMEOUT=3600"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"2cdd24de-d463-4dbc-b7bc-efa7e278dab7","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:25:08.981Z","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-