{"parentUuid":"769519bc-cd63-4609-a330-25098cede381","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a29f29c2-353f-441e-9571-9fc5bbddfa55","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YRnfmhxKSyKNZvxREt9PWj","type":"tool_result","content":"need into ONE shell call joined by ';' rather than spending a turn on each; a lone grep costs the\nsame full turn as a batch of ten.\nTXT\n;;\n  esac\n}\nshared_block() {   # $1 = frugal|thorough — quoted heredocs: nothing here can vary by arm\n  case \"$1\" in\n    frugal) cat <<'TXT'\nHow to work (this applies whatever tools you use):\n(1) LOCATE the code first, then edit. Do not start reading files at random.\n(2) NEVER read a whole file to explore. Read a line range around the line you care about.\n(3) Reach the edit in as FEW turns as possible. Every turn re-reads your entire context, and that\n    re-read — not the bytes any one call returns — is what this task costs. Prefer one precise\n    question over three broad ones.\n(4) Do not re-confirm something you have already been shown. Act on it.\n(5) Never look outside this repository.\n(6) Apply the minimal fix and STOP the moment you can justify it.\n(7) A turn is the unit of cost, not a command. NEVER spend a turn on a single small shell command\n    (one grep, one ls, one cat): batch everything you need into ONE call joined by ';'. A lone\n    command that returns a few hundred bytes still costs a full re-read of your context.\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/suhaan/devenv","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"42e003eb-91dc-4412-b2fb-7bc060fa84c9","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:36:41.706Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"need into ONE shell call joined by ';' rather than spending a turn on each; a lone grep costs the\nsame full turn as a batch of ten.\nTXT\n;;\n  esac\n}\nshared_block() {   # $1 = frugal|thorough — quoted heredocs: nothing here can vary by arm\n  case \"$1\" in\n    frugal) cat <<'TXT'\nHow to work (this applies whatever tools you use):\n(1) LOCATE the code first, then edit. Do not start reading files at random.\n(2) NEVER read a whole file to explore. Read a line range around the line you care about.\n(3) Reach the edit in as FEW turns as possible. Every turn re-reads your entire context, and that\n    re-read — not the bytes any one call returns — is what this task costs. Prefer one precise\n    question over three broad ones.\n(4) Do not re-confirm something you have already been shown. Act on it.\n(5) Never look outside this repository.\n(6) Apply the minimal fix and STOP the moment you can justify it.\n(7) A turn is the unit of cost, not a command. NEVER spend a turn on a single small shell command\n    (one grep, one ls, one cat): batch everything you need into ONE call joined by ';'. A lone\n    command that returns a few hundred bytes still costs a full re-read of your context.","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/suhaan/devenv","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"769519bc-cd63-4609-a330-25098cede381","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"42e003eb-91dc-4412-b2fb-7bc060fa84c9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgJKRSybk1wjyYP8KNpY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013act3PoSejj47V2ZheHhqb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench/agentic-swebench\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport io\np='tools/run_3arm.sh'; s=io.open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\nold='''    if [ \"$arm\" = baseline ]; then\n      # BASE_CLAMP under the vendor family = the matched control: a bare clamp on both sides, no\n      # shared block on either, so the only difference is search-tool vs shell.\n      if [ \"${BASE_CLAMP:-0}\" = 1 ]; then TOOLNOTE=\"\n\n$(base_clamp_prompt)\"; else TOOLNOTE=\"\"; fi\n    else\n      TOOLNOTE=\"\n\n$(tool_block \"$arm\" \"${gq:-}\")\"\n    fi'''\nnew='''    if [ \"$arm\" = baseline ]; then\n      # BASE_CLAMP under the vendor family = the matched control: a bare clamp on both sides, no\n      # shared block on either, so the only difference is search-tool vs shell.\n      if [ \"${BASE_CLAMP:-0}\" = 1 ]; then TOOLNOTE=\"\n\n$(base_clamp_prompt)\"; else TOOLNOTE=\"\"; fi\n    else\n      TOOLNOTE=\"\n\n$(tool_block \"$arm\" \"${gq:-}\")\"\n    fi\n    # OFFICIAL_SCAFFOLD=1 under the vendor family. Measured motivation: the clamp is the ONLY thing\n    # that has made Opus's pre-edit locate fall (-27.9%, vs +9% under the published prompt alone),\n    # but on its own it compresses the session to 4.9 ops, where eg's payload -- re-read every\n    # message -- costs ~10% and outweighs the 1.1 ops saved (tokens +10.9%).\n    # The published scaffold is the only thing that makes sessions long (35.7 ops), where the same\n    # payload is ~2.9% and amortises. Neither regime alone reaches -25%; this pairs the clamp's op\n    # reduction with the long-session amortisation.\n    # SYMMETRIC BY CONSTRUCTION: appended to every arm, after the per-arm tool block, from the same\n    # quoted heredoc. Nothing here can vary by arm.\n    if [ \"${OFFICIAL_SCAFFOLD:-0}\" = 1 ]; then TOOLNOTE=\"$TOOLNOTE\n\n$(official_scaffold_block)\"; fi'''\nassert s.count(old)==1\nio.open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s.replace(old,new,1))\nprint('OFFICIAL_SCAFFOLD wired into the vendor family, both arms')\nPY\nbash -n tools/run_3arm.sh && echo \"syntax OK\"\nrm -rf results/CBPROBE\nfor a in baseline eg; do TASKS_FILE=tasks/opus20_official.json CLAUDE_EFFORT=high CC_MODEL=haiku \\\n ENTIRE_GRAPH=/tmp/eg-f19 PROMPT_FAMILY=vendor BASE_CLAMP=1 EG_SHIPPED_PROMPT=1 EG_SHIPPED_PROMPT_ACK=1 \\\n OFFICIAL_SCAFFOLD=1 EG_PREFETCH=0 EG_PREFETCH_IMPACT=0 GQ_SEARCH_CAP=0 EG_TOPK=5 EG_CONF_TIER=0 \\\n EG_TOPK_SHOW=10 EG_MAXBYTES=24576 EG_SNIPPET=6 EG_MAX_PER_FILE=3 EG_VERIFY_MODE=full EG_PROFILE=full \\\n EG_TIER=0 CC_TIMEOUT=5 RESULTS_TAG=CBPROBE bash tools/run_3arm.sh $a redis__redis-10095 >/dev/null 2>&1; done\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport re,difflib\ndef norm(p):\n    s=open(p,errors='ignore').read()\n    s=re.sub(r'/Users/\\S+|/private/\\S+','<P>',s); s=re.sub(r'\\d+','N',s)\n    return [l.rstrip() for l in s.splitlines()]\nb=norm('results/CBPROBE/baseline/redis__redis-10095/prompt.txt')\ne=norm('results/CBPROBE/eg/redis__redis-10095/prompt.txt')\nprint(f'baseline {len(b)} lines / eg {len(e)} lines')\nd=[x for x in difflib.unified_diff(b,e,'b','e',lineterm='',n=0)]\nprint(f'differing hunks: {sum(1 for x in d if x.startswith(\"@@\"))}')\nsb=' '.join(b); se=' '.join(e)\nfor nm,rx in [('clamp: FIRST action',r'FIRST action'),('clamp: Hard rules',r'Hard rules'),\n              ('clamp: STOP the moment',r'STOP the moment'),('clamp: If TWO',r'If TWO'),\n              ('scaffold: 100 times',r'more than N times'),('scaffold: reproduce script',r'reproduce the error'),\n              ('scaffold: edgecases',r'edgecases')]:\n    print(f'  {nm:<26} base={len(re.findall(rx,sb))}  eg={len(re.findall(rx,se))}')\nPY","description":"Wire and verify the combined clamp+scaffold config"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop