{"parentUuid":"32484c5c-f191-4fbe-90e9-2698a4d233f9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgJYr7f8Kjng7UwGvHoW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Update — S1O is complete and it failed significantly. CB is 2 jobs in.**\n\n**S1 clamp on Opus — FINAL, n=19:**\n\n| | base | eg |\n|---|---|---|\n| pre-edit | 3.7 | 3.2 (**−14.1%**) |\n| total ops | 4.6 | 4.3 (−8.0%) |\n| ktok/session | 175k | **223k** |\n\n**tokens +18.2%, CI [+2.3, +37.2] — excludes zero, so this is a confirmed loss**, winners 7/19.\n\nThe −27.9% pre-edit I reported at n=15 decayed to −14.1% at n=19, and the op saving to −8.0%. The payload costs +48k tokens per session against 0.3 saved ops. That's the fourth independent configuration to fail, and the S1 port — my strongest remaining hypothesis — is refuted on Opus.\n\n**CB (clamp + scaffold), n=1:** base 4.0 ops → eg **1.0** ops (−75%), tokens −24.9%, 117k → 88k.\n\nTwo honest observations about that:\n\n1. **My stated premise is already falsified.** I projected CB would run long sessions (35.7 baseline ops) so the payload would amortise. It's running **4.0** — the clamp dominates the scaffold, post-edit and build are both zero. So the amortisation argument I used to justify this cell does not apply.\n2. **But a different mechanism is visible.** eg used 1 graph call and *zero* shell greps — the tool replaced the locate phase outright rather than supplementing it. A 75% op cut can outrun a 10% payload tax even in a short session. That's not what I predicted, and n=1 is worth nothing, but it's the first time eg has run a 1-op locate phase.\n\nSo the live question has changed from \"does amortisation save it\" to \"does near-total locate elimination hold up past n=1\". Given that today's n≤4 signals have reversed repeatedly — including the one I reported an hour ago on this very config family — I'm treating −24.9% as noise until there are ~12 pairs.\n\nLetting CB run. If it converges near +18% like S1O, that's five independent configurations and I'll report the ceiling rather than keep spending."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2073,"cache_read_input_tokens":555816,"output_tokens":1759,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2073,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1759,"cache_read_input_tokens":555816,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2073,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2073},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgJYmRszNdFzWHyY9iBs","type":"assistant","uuid":"4cee9e5f-1e8c-4566-b156-73165270e8dd","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:40:14.844Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
