{"parentUuid":"29ca5f71-ca08-4aef-b876-65c9c3cc168a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgJgyB3HeZPZ1qNVfXq3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013BwwvTrqWApybMfph1wMvT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench/agentic-swebench\necho \"=== baseline-side blocks that exist ===\"\ngrep -n \"^base_[a-z_]*prompt()\" tools/run_3arm.sh\necho\necho \"=== the eg gated clamp: discovery clamped, finishing NOT ===\"\nsed -n '/^gated_clamp_eg_prompt/,/^}/p' tools/run_3arm.sh | sed -n '1,30p'","description":"Check for a matched baseline gated-clamp block"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2022,"cache_read_input_tokens":561750,"output_tokens":1835,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2022,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1835,"cache_read_input_tokens":561750,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2022,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2022},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgJgtGrveEPToEu5GAsN","type":"assistant","uuid":"1c21d869-f6e2-4691-ba9e-f2b059d2f91b","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:42:04.537Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"1c21d869-f6e2-4691-ba9e-f2b059d2f91b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b3e4c981-5907-4b29-be6c-3d1a4cb51ab5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013BwwvTrqWApybMfph1wMvT","type":"tool_result","content":"=== baseline-side blocks that exist ===\n859:base_clamp_prompt() {\n\n=== the eg gated clamp: discovery clamped, finishing NOT ===\ngated_clamp_eg_prompt() {  # $1 = wrapper command\n  cat <<TXT\nA precomputed code-search tool is available: $1 . Use it to LOCATE the fix BEFORE any\ngrep/find. Your FIRST action must be ONE search:\n  $1 search \"<the bug in one sentence>\"   <-- ranked relevant code (file:line + source)\nThen open the top hit's file with your native Read tool (pass a line range around the reported\nline) and edit. The top hit is the fix site on most tasks - go straight there; do NOT re-search or\ngrep to 'confirm' what the result already showed you. Spend your turns on the FIX, not on looking\naround: every turn re-reads your whole context, and that is what this task costs.\nDISCOVERY IS CLAMPED - FINISHING IS NOT. Before you stop, all three must be true:\n(1) VERIFIED - you compiled the change or ran the nearest existing test at least ONCE. Pick the\n    narrowest command that would still catch a syntax, type, name or arity error. A patch that does\n    not build fails the whole task; this is the cheapest turn you will spend. Then stop verifying -\n    read the error, fix what it names, re-run once. Do NOT hunt a green suite.\n(2) SWEPT - you checked the RELATED SITES the search result listed (callers, siblings, near-dupes)\n    and fixed every one that has the same bug. A fix is usually not one edit in one place.\n(3) COMPLETE - you handled the edge cases the issue names (empty, nil, negative, unicode, error\n    paths).\nIf a search did not land it, search again with different words; if TWO searches miss, fall back to\nthe shell in ONE batched call. Never stop merely because you have made an edit - stop when (1),\n(2) and (3) hold.\nTXT\n}\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/suhaan/devenv","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"df59c093-996f-4607-a548-4a6b12fb506e","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:42:04.599Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== baseline-side blocks that exist ===\n859:base_clamp_prompt() {\n\n=== the eg gated clamp: discovery clamped, finishing NOT ===\ngated_clamp_eg_prompt() {  # $1 = wrapper command\n  cat <<TXT\nA precomputed code-search tool is available: $1 . Use it to LOCATE the fix BEFORE any\ngrep/find. Your FIRST action must be ONE search:\n  $1 search \"<the bug in one sentence>\"   <-- ranked relevant code (file:line + source)\nThen open the top hit's file with your native Read tool (pass a line range around the reported\nline) and edit. The top hit is the fix site on most tasks - go straight there; do NOT re-search or\ngrep to 'confirm' what the result already showed you. Spend your turns on the FIX, not on looking\naround: every turn re-reads your whole context, and that is what this task costs.\nDISCOVERY IS CLAMPED - FINISHING IS NOT. Before you stop, all three must be true:\n(1) VERIFIED - you compiled the change or ran the nearest existing test at least ONCE. Pick the\n    narrowest command that would still catch a syntax, type, name or arity error. A patch that does\n    not build fails the whole task; this is the cheapest turn you will spend. Then stop verifying -\n    read the error, fix what it names, re-run once. Do NOT hunt a green suite.\n(2) SWEPT - you checked the RELATED SITES the search result listed (callers, siblings, near-dupes)\n    and fixed every one that has the same bug. A fix is usually not one edit in one place.\n(3) COMPLETE - you handled the edge cases the issue names (empty, nil, negative, unicode, error\n    paths).\nIf a search did not land it, search again with different words; if TWO searches miss, fall back to\nthe shell in ONE batched call. Never stop merely because you have made an edit - stop when (1),\n(2) and (3) hold.\nTXT\n}","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/suhaan/devenv","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1c21d869-f6e2-4691-ba9e-f2b059d2f91b","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"df59c093-996f-4607-a548-4a6b12fb506e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgJjD2Y2LXcSeGEjaMny","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2527,"cache_read_input_tokens":563772,"output_tokens":4759,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2527,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4759,"cache_read_input_tokens":563772,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2527,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2527},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgJixtUaLorUtaymUAB5","type":"assistant","uuid":"99da562e-c70e-4141-983d-8730cbdb4c1d","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:42:23.756Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"99da562e-c70e-4141-983d-8730cbdb4c1d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgJjD2Y2LXcSeGEjaMny","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed: only `base_clamp_prompt()` exists. There is **no baseline mirror** of the gated clamp — which is exactly why `EG_GATED_CLAMP` failed my fairness gate earlier. That's a fixable gap, and it's the one config shape the evidence actually points at."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2527,"cache_read_input_tokens":563772,"output_tokens":4759,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2527,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4759,"cache_read_input_tokens":563772,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2527,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2527},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgJixtUaLorUtaymUAB5","type":"assistant","uuid":"34db5d43-1a50-4b54-ba2b-7cf6ff5335fa","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:42:25.175Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"34db5d43-1a50-4b54-ba2b-7cf6ff5335fa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgJjD2Y2LXcSeGEjaMny","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015o7qV5KiTtw7w4Uo18XS4K","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/modular-cooking-cupcake.md","content":"# Opus to −25%: the gated clamp, made symmetric\n\n## Context\n\nGoal: Opus ≥ −25% tokens on the 20-instance official-300 sample. Five configurations measured today.\nThe complete, fair evidence:\n\n| config | session size | baseline ops | eg ops | ops Δ | **tokens** | n |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| OFF — bare base / rich eg, official | long, 39.0 | 39.0 | 27.5 | −29.6% | −46.5% | 19 — **INVALID, asymmetric** |\n| G40 — rich/rich, official | long, 23.8 | 23.8 | 28.7 | +21.1% | +28.4% | 19 |\n| **PUB — published prompt, capability** | **long, 35.7** | 35.7 | 31.7 | −11.2% | **−11.2%** | 20 |\n| S1O — S1 clamp, no scaffold | **short, 4.6** | 4.6 | 4.3 | −8.0% | **+18.2%** [+2.3,+37.2] | 19 |\n| FRUGAL — rich/rich, frugal shared | short, 7.0 | 7.0 | 5.0 | −28.6% | −14.0% | 23 |\n| CB — clamp + scaffold | short, 4.0 | 4.0 | 1.0 | −75% | −24.9% | **1, in flight** |\n\n### The governing relation, measured\n\n**tokens ≈ ops ratio + payload tax**, and the payload tax depends only on session size:\n~**10%** at a 175k-token session (S1O: −8.0% ops → +18.2% tokens), ~**3%** at a 2.4M-token session\n(PUB: −11.2% ops → −11.2% tokens).\n\nSo −25% requires **both** conditions at once:\n- **ops ratio ≤ −28%**, and\n- **a long session**, so the payload amortises to ~3%.\n\nNo config has achieved both. PUB is long but cuts only 11% of ops — because its eg pre-edit locate\n*rises* (13.4 → 14.6, +9%). The clamp cells cut ops but collapse the session to 4–7 ops, where the\n10% tax eats the gain. FRUGAL is the clearest illustration: −28.6% ops became only −14.0% tokens\nbecause the tax took 14 points.\n\n### Why the clamp collapses the session, and what fixes it\n\n`base_clamp_prompt` / `shipped_eg_prompt` clamp *everything* — \"Apply the minimal fix and STOP the\nmoment you can justify it.\" Result: post-edit 0.3 ops, build 0.6 ops. The agent edits and leaves.\nCB tested whether appending the official scaffold would restore length; at n=1 it did **not** (still\n4.0 ops, post-edit and build both zero). **The clamp dominates an appended scaffold.**\n\n`gated_clamp_eg_prompt` already exists and is built for exactly this: it clamps discovery while\nexplicitly mandating completion —\n\n> DISCOVERY IS CLAMPED — FINISHING IS NOT. Before you stop, all three must be true:\n> (1) **VERIFIED** — you compiled the change or ran the nearest existing test at least ONCE …\n> (2) **SWEPT** — you checked the RELATED SITES the search result listed … and fixed every one …\n> (3) **COMPLETE** — you handled the edge cases the issue names …\n> Never stop merely because you have made an edit — stop when (1), (2) and (3) hold.\n\nThat is the only construct in the harness that cuts pre-edit *without* cutting the phases that make\na session long. **It has never been run, because it fails the fairness gate:** I checked, and\n`base_clamp_prompt()` is the *only* baseline-side block — there is no mirror, so eg would get\nVERIFIED/SWEPT/COMPLETE and the baseline nothing.\n\n## Plan\n\n### 1. Write `base_gated_clamp_prompt()` — the missing mirror\nIn `tools/run_3arm.sh`, beside `base_clamp_prompt()` (line 859). Clause-for-clause mirror of\n`gated_clamp_eg_prompt`, shell-worded:\n\n| eg clause | baseline mirror |\n|---|---|\n| FIRST action must be ONE search | FIRST action is ONE batched shell search |\n| open the top hit, read a line range, edit | open the best hit, read a line range, edit |\n| do NOT re-search to 'confirm' | do NOT re-grep to 'confirm' |\n| DISCOVERY IS CLAMPED — FINISHING IS NOT | identical, verbatim |\n| (1) VERIFIED … narrowest command … do NOT hunt a green suite | identical, verbatim |\n| (2) SWEPT — the RELATED SITES the search result listed | **SWEPT — grep the distinctive literal once more to enumerate the other sites** |\n| (3) COMPLETE — edge cases the issue names | identical, verbatim |\n| if TWO searches miss, fall back to the shell | if TWO batched searches miss, widen the pattern once |\n\n**Disclose the one clause that cannot be literal:** SWEPT. eg has a printed RELATED SITES list; the\nshell has none, so the baseline is told how to *produce* the equivalent list. This is the same real\nproduct difference already disclosed for `base_clamp_prompt` (\"only the baseline is told to Read the\nfile\"). It is baseline-favouring in wording (it gets an explicit instruction eg gets for free) and\nmust be reported as the one non-literal mirror.\n\nAdd `BASE_GATED_CLAMP=1` to the baseline branch of `tool_block`, next to the existing\n`BASE_CLAMP` check at line 1165.\n\n### 2. Fairness gate — on emitted prompts, before any spend\nLine-diff both arms, paths/digits normalised, and require **exactly one differing hunk** (the tool\nparagraph). Clause table must be 1:1 on: FIRST-action, read-line-range, do-not-re-confirm,\nDISCOVERY-IS-CLAMPED, VERIFIED, SWEPT, COMPLETE, never-stop-merely, TWO-then-fallback. Watch for\nline-wrap false negatives — collapse newlines before matching (this bit me once today).\n\n### 3. Run on Opus — 40 sessions, same 20 instances\n`PROMPT_FAMILY=vendor BASE_GATED_CLAMP=1 EG_GATED_CLAMP=1`, no prefetch, `GQ_SEARCH_CAP=0`,\n`CC_MAX_TURNS=120 CC_TIMEOUT=3600`, binary `/tmp/eg-f19`, fresh `--cache-dir`, and the per-instance\ncache isolation already built into `/tmp/mcptest/s1worker.sh` (`GOMODCACHE`, `GOPATH`, `GOCACHE`,\n`COMPOSER_HOME`, `CARGO_HOME`, `GEM_HOME`, `npm_config_cache`, `maven.repo.local`).\n\n### 4. Two leading indicators, both free, both checkable at ~8 pairs\n| indicator | required | why |\n|---|---|---|\n| **baseline total ops** | **≥ 20** | if the gate clamps finishing too, the session collapses to ~4 ops and the 10% payload tax returns — the S1O failure mode. Kill the cell. |\n| **eg pre-edit vs baseline** | **≤ −25%** | PUB is +9%; every cell reaching ≤−25% tokens had pre-edit ≤−28%. Without this the ops ratio cannot get there. |\n\nIf either fails at 8 pairs, stop — do not pay for 40 sessions to confirm a known failure mode.\n\n### 5. Pre-registered\n- Success = geomean ≤ −25% with CI upper bound < 0.\n- Required shape: baseline ops ≈ 25–35, eg ops ≈ 18–25, i.e. ops ratio ≈ −28% at long-session\n  amortisation (~3% tax) → tokens ≈ −25%.\n- Falsification: if ops fall ≥28% and tokens still miss −25%, the payload tax does not amortise the\n  way PUB implies, and **−25% on Opus is unreachable** — that would be the sixth independent\n  configuration and I will report the ceiling instead of running a seventh.\n- Replicate with a second independent cell before any claim. Today's n≤4 signals reversed\n  repeatedly, including on this very config family an hour ago.\n\n## Verification\n- `tools/model_cmp.py`: geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI, cost classes separately.\n- Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped symmetrically.\n- `CENSORED` (`error_max_turns`) = 0 per arm.\n- Report ops (pre/post/build) beside tokens every update — ops predicted tokens within 3pt in the\n  long-session cells and is the cheap early read.\n- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config. Eleven silent plumbing failures today; the worst was a\n  flag checked in one dispatcher but not the one every cell uses.\n\n## Files\n- `tools/run_3arm.sh` — add `base_gated_clamp_prompt()` near line 859; wire `BASE_GATED_CLAMP` in the\n  baseline branch near line 1165. `gated_clamp_eg_prompt` and the vendor-family assembly already exist.\n- `/tmp/mcptest/gcworker.sh` (new) — copy of `s1worker.sh` with the two clamp flags swapped in.\n- **No product change.** `eg-consolidated` stays clean at HEAD `024f25a`; all 27 payload-defect\n  hypotheses that would have motivated one were refuted on winner-control.\n\n## Honest expectation\nThis is the last untried config shape, and it is the only one that targets both required conditions\nrather than one. The mechanism is specific: clamp discovery to cut pre-edit, mandate finishing to keep\nthe session long enough that the payload costs 3% rather than 10%.\n\nAgainst it: the clamp's own wording has collapsed the session in both cells that used it, and CB shows\nan appended scaffold does not prevent that. The gated clamp puts the finishing mandate *inside* the\nclamp, which is why it might behave differently — but \"might\" is the honest word. I put this at\n**−15% to −28%**, and I will report the ceiling rather than run a seventh cell if it misses.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2527,"cache_read_input_tokens":563772,"output_tokens":4759,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2527,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4759,"cache_read_input_tokens":563772,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2527,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2527},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgJixtUaLorUtaymUAB5","type":"assistant","uuid":"fd77f485-64cb-4fb6-aeef-47b606099b93","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:43:09.108Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"fd77f485-64cb-4fb6-aeef-47b606099b93","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b3e4c981-5907-4b29-be6c-3d1a4cb51ab5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015o7qV5KiTtw7w4Uo18XS4K","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/modular-cooking-cupcake.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"7e1e20e8-b6a0-4417-8f5e-f91df7373605","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:43:09.191Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/modular-cooking-cupcake.md","content":"# Opus to −25%: the gated clamp, made symmetric\n\n## Context\n\nGoal: Opus ≥ −25% tokens on the 20-instance official-300 sample. Five configurations measured today.\nThe complete, fair evidence:\n\n| config | session size | baseline ops | eg ops | ops Δ | **tokens** | n |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| OFF — bare base / rich eg, official | long, 39.0 | 39.0 | 27.5 | −29.6% | −46.5% | 19 — **INVALID, asymmetric** |\n| G40 — rich/rich, official | long, 23.8 | 23.8 | 28.7 | +21.1% | +28.4% | 19 |\n| **PUB — published prompt, capability** | **long, 35.7** | 35.7 | 31.7 | −11.2% | **−11.2%** | 20 |\n| S1O — S1 clamp, no scaffold | **short, 4.6** | 4.6 | 4.3 | −8.0% | **+18.2%** [+2.3,+37.2] | 19 |\n| FRUGAL — rich/rich, frugal shared | short, 7.0 | 7.0 | 5.0 | −28.6% | −14.0% | 23 |\n| CB — clamp + scaffold | short, 4.0 | 4.0 | 1.0 | −75% | −24.9% | **1, in flight** |\n\n### The governing relation, measured\n\n**tokens ≈ ops ratio + payload tax**, and the payload tax depends only on session size:\n~**10%** at a 175k-token session (S1O: −8.0% ops → +18.2% tokens), ~**3%** at a 2.4M-token session\n(PUB: −11.2% ops → −11.2% tokens).\n\nSo −25% requires **both** conditions at once:\n- **ops ratio ≤ −28%**, and\n- **a long session**, so the payload amortises to ~3%.\n\nNo config has achieved both. PUB is long but cuts only 11% of ops — because its eg pre-edit locate\n*rises* (13.4 → 14.6, +9%). The clamp cells cut ops but collapse the session to 4–7 ops, where the\n10% tax eats the gain. FRUGAL is the clearest illustration: −28.6% ops became only −14.0% tokens\nbecause the tax took 14 points.\n\n### Why the clamp collapses the session, and what fixes it\n\n`base_clamp_prompt` / `shipped_eg_prompt` clamp *everything* — \"Apply the minimal fix and STOP the\nmoment you can justify it.\" Result: post-edit 0.3 ops, build 0.6 ops. The agent edits and leaves.\nCB tested whether appending the official scaffold would restore length; at n=1 it did **not** (still\n4.0 ops, post-edit and build both zero). **The clamp dominates an appended scaffold.**\n\n`gated_clamp_eg_prompt` already exists and is built for exactly this: it clamps discovery while\nexplicitly mandating completion —\n\n> DISCOVERY IS CLAMPED — FINISHING IS NOT. Before you stop, all three must be true:\n> (1) **VERIFIED** — you compiled the change or ran the nearest existing test at least ONCE …\n> (2) **SWEPT** — you checked the RELATED SITES the search result listed … and fixed every one …\n> (3) **COMPLETE** — you handled the edge cases the issue names …\n> Never stop merely because you have made an edit — stop when (1), (2) and (3) hold.\n\nThat is the only construct in the harness that cuts pre-edit *without* cutting the phases that make\na session long. **It has never been run, because it fails the fairness gate:** I checked, and\n`base_clamp_prompt()` is the *only* baseline-side block — there is no mirror, so eg would get\nVERIFIED/SWEPT/COMPLETE and the baseline nothing.\n\n## Plan\n\n### 1. Write `base_gated_clamp_prompt()` — the missing mirror\nIn `tools/run_3arm.sh`, beside `base_clamp_prompt()` (line 859). Clause-for-clause mirror of\n`gated_clamp_eg_prompt`, shell-worded:\n\n| eg clause | baseline mirror |\n|---|---|\n| FIRST action must be ONE search | FIRST action is ONE batched shell search |\n| open the top hit, read a line range, edit | open the best hit, read a line range, edit |\n| do NOT re-search to 'confirm' | do NOT re-grep to 'confirm' |\n| DISCOVERY IS CLAMPED — FINISHING IS NOT | identical, verbatim |\n| (1) VERIFIED … narrowest command … do NOT hunt a green suite | identical, verbatim |\n| (2) SWEPT — the RELATED SITES the search result listed | **SWEPT — grep the distinctive literal once more to enumerate the other sites** |\n| (3) COMPLETE — edge cases the issue names | identical, verbatim |\n| if TWO searches miss, fall back to the shell | if TWO batched searches miss, widen the pattern once |\n\n**Disclose the one clause that cannot be literal:** SWEPT. eg has a printed RELATED SITES list; the\nshell has none, so the baseline is told how to *produce* the equivalent list. This is the same real\nproduct difference already disclosed for `base_clamp_prompt` (\"only the baseline is told to Read the\nfile\"). It is baseline-favouring in wording (it gets an explicit instruction eg gets for free) and\nmust be reported as the one non-literal mirror.\n\nAdd `BASE_GATED_CLAMP=1` to the baseline branch of `tool_block`, next to the existing\n`BASE_CLAMP` check at line 1165.\n\n### 2. Fairness gate — on emitted prompts, before any spend\nLine-diff both arms, paths/digits normalised, and require **exactly one differing hunk** (the tool\nparagraph). Clause table must be 1:1 on: FIRST-action, read-line-range, do-not-re-confirm,\nDISCOVERY-IS-CLAMPED, VERIFIED, SWEPT, COMPLETE, never-stop-merely, TWO-then-fallback. Watch for\nline-wrap false negatives — collapse newlines before matching (this bit me once today).\n\n### 3. Run on Opus — 40 sessions, same 20 instances\n`PROMPT_FAMILY=vendor BASE_GATED_CLAMP=1 EG_GATED_CLAMP=1`, no prefetch, `GQ_SEARCH_CAP=0`,\n`CC_MAX_TURNS=120 CC_TIMEOUT=3600`, binary `/tmp/eg-f19`, fresh `--cache-dir`, and the per-instance\ncache isolation already built into `/tmp/mcptest/s1worker.sh` (`GOMODCACHE`, `GOPATH`, `GOCACHE`,\n`COMPOSER_HOME`, `CARGO_HOME`, `GEM_HOME`, `npm_config_cache`, `maven.repo.local`).\n\n### 4. Two leading indicators, both free, both checkable at ~8 pairs\n| indicator | required | why |\n|---|---|---|\n| **baseline total ops** | **≥ 20** | if the gate clamps finishing too, the session collapses to ~4 ops and the 10% payload tax returns — the S1O failure mode. Kill the cell. |\n| **eg pre-edit vs baseline** | **≤ −25%** | PUB is +9%; every cell reaching ≤−25% tokens had pre-edit ≤−28%. Without this the ops ratio cannot get there. |\n\nIf either fails at 8 pairs, stop — do not pay for 40 sessions to confirm a known failure mode.\n\n### 5. Pre-registered\n- Success = geomean ≤ −25% with CI upper bound < 0.\n- Required shape: baseline ops ≈ 25–35, eg ops ≈ 18–25, i.e. ops ratio ≈ −28% at long-session\n  amortisation (~3% tax) → tokens ≈ −25%.\n- Falsification: if ops fall ≥28% and tokens still miss −25%, the payload tax does not amortise the\n  way PUB implies, and **−25% on Opus is unreachable** — that would be the sixth independent\n  configuration and I will report the ceiling instead of running a seventh.\n- Replicate with a second independent cell before any claim. Today's n≤4 signals reversed\n  repeatedly, including on this very config family an hour ago.\n\n## Verification\n- `tools/model_cmp.py`: geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI, cost classes separately.\n- Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped symmetrically.\n- `CENSORED` (`error_max_turns`) = 0 per arm.\n- Report ops (pre/post/build) beside tokens every update — ops predicted tokens within 3pt in the\n  long-session cells and is the cheap early read.\n- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config. Eleven silent plumbing failures today; the worst was a\n  flag checked in one dispatcher but not the one every cell uses.\n\n## Files\n- `tools/run_3arm.sh` — add `base_gated_clamp_prompt()` near line 859; wire `BASE_GATED_CLAMP` in the\n  baseline branch near line 1165. `gated_clamp_eg_prompt` and the vendor-family assembly already exist.\n- `/tmp/mcptest/gcworker.sh` (new) — copy of `s1worker.sh` with the two clamp flags swapped in.\n- **No product change.** `eg-consolidated` stays clean at HEAD `024f25a`; all 27 payload-defect\n  hypotheses that would have motivated one were refuted on winner-control.\n\n## Honest expectation\nThis is the last untried config shape, and it is the only one that targets both required conditions\nrather than one. The mechanism is specific: clamp discovery to cut pre-edit, mandate finishing to keep\nthe session long enough that the payload costs 3% rather than 10%.\n\nAgainst it: the clamp's own wording has collapsed the session in both cells that used it, and CB shows\nan appended scaffold does not prevent that. The gated clamp puts the finishing mandate *inside* the\nclamp, which is why it might behave differently — but \"might\" is the honest word. I put this at\n**−15% to −28%**, and I will report the ceiling rather than run a seventh cell if it misses.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":131,"newStart":1,"newLines":133,"lines":["-# Opus to −25% by porting S1 — the best fair config, never run on Opus","+# Opus to −25%: the gated clamp, made symmetric"," "," ## Context"," ","-Goal: Opus ≥ −25% on the 20-instance official-300 sample. Current fair number **−11.2%**","-[−27.8, +9.6] (n=20, published prompt, both arms symmetric, cap 120).","+Goal: Opus ≥ −25% tokens on the 20-instance official-300 sample. Five configurations measured today.","+The complete, fair evidence:"," ","-I stopped proposing new mechanisms and mined the existing cells. Two things came out of that, and","-together they change what to run.","+| config | session size | baseline ops | eg ops | ops Δ | **tokens** | n |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| OFF — bare base / rich eg, official | long, 39.0 | 39.0 | 27.5 | −29.6% | −46.5% | 19 — **INVALID, asymmetric** |","+| G40 — rich/rich, official | long, 23.8 | 23.8 | 28.7 | +21.1% | +28.4% | 19 |","+| **PUB — published prompt, capability** | **long, 35.7** | 35.7 | 31.7 | −11.2% | **−11.2%** | 20 |","+| S1O — S1 clamp, no scaffold | **short, 4.6** | 4.6 | 4.3 | −8.0% | **+18.2%** [+2.3,+37.2] | 19 |","+| FRUGAL — rich/rich, frugal shared | short, 7.0 | 7.0 | 5.0 | −28.6% | −14.0% | 23 |","+| CB — clamp + scaffold | short, 4.0 | 4.0 | 1.0 | −75% | −24.9% | **1, in flight** |"," ","-### 1. Every payload-defect hypothesis is dead — verified, not assumed","+### The governing relation, measured"," ","-A 5-agent forensic sweep read all 20 sessions and produced 38 candidate defects. Adversarial","-verifiers with a **winner-control** requirement refuted **27 of 28** adjudicated so far:","+**tokens ≈ ops ratio + payload tax**, and the payload tax depends only on session size:","+~**10%** at a 175k-token session (S1O: −8.0% ops → +18.2% tokens), ~**3%** at a 2.4M-token session","+(PUB: −11.2% ops → −11.2% tokens)."," ","-| claimed defect | winner control that killed it |","-|---|---|","-| bodies printed with no line numbers (prompt promises them) | **20/20 instances** — 6/6 winners, incl. the biggest wins |","-| `impact` blind-chained to rank-1, no gate | off-gold-file target in **7/12 winners**; the two largest wins have it in *more* degenerate form |","-| query polluted by GitHub issue-template boilerplate | 2/6 control winners have boilerplate queries → boilerplate top hits |","-| hits printed out of score order | 5/20 payloads, incl. winners lucene (−52%) and vuejs (−24%) |","-| line-less fabricated `server.h` caller | redis-10095 (+65) **and valkey-1842 (−21%, a winner)** |","-| `eg-q.run` path exposed 5× in prompt | 20/20 |","+So −25% requires **both** conditions at once:","+- **ops ratio ≤ −28%**, and","+- **a long session**, so the payload amortises to ~3%."," ","-Only survivor: the shared **GOMODCACHE leak** (caddy's *baseline* read the fix out of","-`~/go/pkg/mod/…caddy/v2@v2.11.4/replacer.go`, 27 of 66 calls) — and it explains a winner, not a loss.","+No config has achieved both. PUB is long but cuts only 11% of ops — because its eg pre-edit locate","+*rises* (13.4 → 14.6, +9%). The clamp cells cut ops but collapse the session to 4–7 ops, where the","+10% tax eats the gain. FRUGAL is the clearest illustration: −28.6% ops became only −14.0% tokens","+because the tax took 14 points."," ","-**Conclusion: the tool is equally broken everywhere. Payload quality does not decide the sign.**","-Do not spend further effort on payload defects.","+### Why the clamp collapses the session, and what fixes it"," ","-### 2. Tokens are a pure function of the op-count ratio, and eg's op count is invariant","+`base_clamp_prompt` / `shipped_eg_prompt` clamp *everything* — \"Apply the minimal fix and STOP the","+moment you can justify it.\" Result: post-edit 0.3 ops, build 0.6 ops. The agent edits and leaves.","+CB tested whether appending the official scaffold would restore length; at n=1 it did **not** (still","+4.0 ops, post-edit and build both zero). **The clamp dominates an appended scaffold.**"," ","-| config | baseline ops | eg ops | ops Δ | tokens |","-|---|---|---|---|---|","-| G40 rich/rich, official | **23.8** | 28.7 | +21.1% | +28.4% |","-| OFF bare/rich, official | **39.0** | 27.5 | −29.6% | −46.5% |","-| PUB none/capability, published | **35.7** | 31.7 | −11.2% | −11.2% |","+`gated_clamp_eg_prompt` already exists and is built for exactly this: it clamps discovery while","+explicitly mandating completion —"," ","-eg lands at 27.5 / 28.7 / 31.7 regardless of prompt. The **baseline** swings 23.8 → 39.0 purely on how","-much methodology its prompt carries. So the withdrawn −46.5% was a crippled control, and G40's +28.4%","-was a control given better discipline than eg. Neither was about the tool.","+> DISCOVERY IS CLAMPED — FINISHING IS NOT. Before you stop, all three must be true:","+> (1) **VERIFIED** — you compiled the change or ran the nearest existing test at least ONCE …","+> (2) **SWEPT** — you checked the RELATED SITES the search result listed … and fixed every one …","+> (3) **COMPLETE** — you handled the edge cases the issue names …","+> Never stop merely because you have made an edit — stop when (1), (2) and (3) hold."," ","-### 3. What the winning cells do that no Opus cell has ever done","+That is the only construct in the harness that cuts pre-edit *without* cutting the phases that make","+a session long. **It has never been run, because it fails the fairness gate:** I checked, and","+`base_clamp_prompt()` is the *only* baseline-side block — there is no mirror, so eg would get","+VERIFIED/SWEPT/COMPLETE and the baseline nothing."," ","-The tool's job is to collapse the locate phase. On Haiku's best fair cells it halves pre-edit locate.","-On Opus it never has:","+## Plan"," ","-| cell | pre-edit base → eg | ops Δ | tokens |","-|---|---|---|---|","-| **haiku S1** (n=50) | **16.2 → 8.5 (−48%)** | −39.3% | **−39.9%** |","-| haiku RR (n=21) | 14.2 → 6.3 (−56%) | −46.7% | −44.7% |","-| haiku R30 (n=30) | 15.7 → 10.3 (−34%) | −32.8% | −42.9% |","-| sonnet R30 (n=30) | 7.0 → 6.4 (−9%) | −25.1% | −24.5% |","-| **opus PUB** | **13.4 → 14.6 (+9%)** | −11.2% | −11.2% |","-| opus OFF | 19.1 → 13.6 (−29%) | −29.6% | −46.5% |","+### 1. Write `base_gated_clamp_prompt()` — the missing mirror","+In `tools/run_3arm.sh`, beside `base_clamp_prompt()` (line 859). Clause-for-clause mirror of","+`gated_clamp_eg_prompt`, shell-worded:"," ","-Opus's baseline pre-edit (13.4) is comparable to Haiku's (16.2), so this is **not** \"Opus explores","-less\". It is that the config which halves pre-edit has only ever been run on Haiku.","+| eg clause | baseline mirror |","+|---|---|","+| FIRST action must be ONE search | FIRST action is ONE batched shell search |","+| open the top hit, read a line range, edit | open the best hit, read a line range, edit |","+| do NOT re-search to 'confirm' | do NOT re-grep to 'confirm' |","+| DISCOVERY IS CLAMPED — FINISHING IS NOT | identical, verbatim |","+| (1) VERIFIED … narrowest command … do NOT hunt a green suite | identical, verbatim |","+| (2) SWEPT — the RELATED SITES the search result listed | **SWEPT — grep the distinctive literal once more to enumerate the other sites** |","+| (3) COMPLETE — edge cases the issue names | identical, verbatim |","+| if TWO searches miss, fall back to the shell | if TWO batched searches miss, widen the pattern once |"," ","-**S1 = `PROMPT_FAMILY=vendor BASE_CLAMP=1 EG_GATED_CLAMP=1`.** The harness's own comment on that","-combination: *\"the matched control: a bare clamp on both sides, no shared block on either, so the only","-difference is search-tool vs shell.\"* I verified its symmetry earlier by line-diff — 384 vs 370 words,","-mirrored clause for clause (LOCATE-FIRST/SEARCH-FIRST, READ the range, EDIT, do-not-re-confirm, STOP,","-two-attempts-then-widen). It is the best fair result in the whole program and **has never been run on","-Opus.**","+**Disclose the one clause that cannot be literal:** SWEPT. eg has a printed RELATED SITES list; the","+shell has none, so the baseline is told how to *produce* the equivalent list. This is the same real","+product difference already disclosed for `base_clamp_prompt` (\"only the baseline is told to Read the","+file\"). It is baseline-favouring in wording (it gets an explicit instruction eg gets for free) and","+must be reported as the one non-literal mirror."," ","-## Plan","+Add `BASE_GATED_CLAMP=1` to the baseline branch of `tool_block`, next to the existing","+`BASE_CLAMP` check at line 1165."," ","-### 1. Run S1 on Opus, same 20 instances — 40 sessions","-`PROMPT_FAMILY=vendor BASE_CLAMP=1 EG_GATED_CLAMP=1`, `CC_MODEL=opus CLAUDE_EFFORT=high`,","-`TASKS_FILE=tasks/opus20_official.json`, binary `/tmp/eg-f19`, fresh `--cache-dir`.","+### 2. Fairness gate — on emitted prompts, before any spend","+Line-diff both arms, paths/digits normalised, and require **exactly one differing hunk** (the tool","+paragraph). Clause table must be 1:1 on: FIRST-action, read-line-range, do-not-re-confirm,","+DISCOVERY-IS-CLAMPED, VERIFIED, SWEPT, COMPLETE, never-stop-merely, TWO-then-fallback. Watch for","+line-wrap false negatives — collapse newlines before matching (this bit me once today)."," ","-Deliberately **no prefetch** (S1 didn't use it; and the Arm A probe showed prefetch removal raises","-graph usage 0.20→3.00) and **`GQ_SEARCH_CAP=0`** so follow-ups are possible. Cap 120 and","-`CC_TIMEOUT=3600` to keep `CENSORED=0` — the PUB baseline averaged 50.2 turns, so a 50-cap censors the","-baseline specifically.","+### 3. Run on Opus — 40 sessions, same 20 instances","+`PROMPT_FAMILY=vendor BASE_GATED_CLAMP=1 EG_GATED_CLAMP=1`, no prefetch, `GQ_SEARCH_CAP=0`,","+`CC_MAX_TURNS=120 CC_TIMEOUT=3600`, binary `/tmp/eg-f19`, fresh `--cache-dir`, and the per-instance","+cache isolation already built into `/tmp/mcptest/s1worker.sh` (`GOMODCACHE`, `GOPATH`, `GOCACHE`,","+`COMPOSER_HOME`, `CARGO_HOME`, `GEM_HOME`, `npm_config_cache`, `maven.repo.local`)."," ","-### 2. Fairness gate before scoring — on emitted prompts, not config","-Line-diff the two arms with paths/digits normalised and account for every differing line; run the","-clause table (LOCATE/SEARCH-FIRST, READ range, EDIT, do-not-re-confirm, STOP, fallback) and require","-**parity or baseline-favouring**. S1's blocks passed this before; confirm they still do under the","-current `run_3arm.sh`.","+### 4. Two leading indicators, both free, both checkable at ~8 pairs","+| indicator | required | why |","+|---|---|---|","+| **baseline total ops** | **≥ 20** | if the gate clamps finishing too, the session collapses to ~4 ops and the 10% payload tax returns — the S1O failure mode. Kill the cell. |","+| **eg pre-edit vs baseline** | **≤ −25%** | PUB is +9%; every cell reaching ≤−25% tokens had pre-edit ≤−28%. Without this the ops ratio cannot get there. |"," ","-### 3. Leading indicator, checkable before spending on the full score","-**Pre-edit locate must fall below the baseline's.** It is +9% today; every cell that reached ≤ −25%","-tokens had it at −34% or better. If pre-edit does not go negative by ~8 completed pairs, stop the cell","-— that is the mechanism, and without it the tokens cannot follow.","+If either fails at 8 pairs, stop — do not pay for 40 sessions to confirm a known failure mode."," ","-### 4. Fix the one confirmed integrity defect in the same run","-Isolate `GOMODCACHE`/`GOPATH` per instance (and the npm/gem equivalents) so no arm can read a","-post-fix upstream release. Without this, caddy's baseline is reading the answer.","-"," ### 5. Pre-registered","-- Success = geomean ≤ −25% with a CI upper bound below zero.","-- Arithmetic from the current cell: 12 winners contribute ln-sum −5.369, 8 losers +2.996. Fixing all 8","-  losers to parity gives only −23.5%, so S1 must also **deepen the winners** — which is exactly what a","-  pre-edit halving does, and why this config rather than a loser-targeted patch.","-- Falsification: if S1 on Opus lands within noise of −11.2%, then the pre-edit halving is","-  Haiku-specific and **−25% on Opus is not reachable with any config in this program.** I will report","-  that rather than keep re-cutting the same data.","+- Success = geomean ≤ −25% with CI upper bound < 0.","+- Required shape: baseline ops ≈ 25–35, eg ops ≈ 18–25, i.e. ops ratio ≈ −28% at long-session","+  amortisation (~3% tax) → tokens ≈ −25%.","+- Falsification: if ops fall ≥28% and tokens still miss −25%, the payload tax does not amortise the","+  way PUB implies, and **−25% on Opus is unreachable** — that would be the sixth independent","+  configuration and I will report the ceiling instead of running a seventh.","+- Replicate with a second independent cell before any claim. Today's n≤4 signals reversed","+  repeatedly, including on this very config family an hour ago."," ","-### 6. Replicate before claiming","-Second independent cell if it clears. Three configs today looked strong at n≤12 and reversed by n=20.","-"," ## Verification","-- `tools/model_cmp.py`; geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI; cost classes separately.","+- `tools/model_cmp.py`: geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI, cost classes separately."," - Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped symmetrically.","-- `CENSORED` must stay 0 per arm.","-- Report ops (pre/post/build) alongside tokens — ops predicted tokens within 3pt in all three cells","-  above, so it is the cheap early read on whether the cell is working.","-- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config — ten silent plumbing failures this session, the worst a","+- `CENSORED` (`error_max_turns`) = 0 per arm.","+- Report ops (pre/post/build) beside tokens every update — ops predicted tokens within 3pt in the","+  long-session cells and is the cheap early read.","+- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config. Eleven silent plumbing failures today; the worst was a","   flag checked in one dispatcher but not the one every cell uses."," "," ## Files","-- `/tmp/mcptest/s1worker.sh` (new) — the S1 flag set, Opus, cap 120.","-- `tools/run_3arm.sh` — no changes needed; `base_clamp_prompt` and `gated_clamp_eg_prompt` already","-  exist and are what S1 used.","-- `tools/model_cmp.py` — scorer, already reproduces every historical number.","-- **No product change.** `eg-consolidated` stays clean at HEAD `024f25a`; every payload-defect","-  hypothesis that would have motivated one is refuted.","+- `tools/run_3arm.sh` — add `base_gated_clamp_prompt()` near line 859; wire `BASE_GATED_CLAMP` in the","+  baseline branch near line 1165. `gated_clamp_eg_prompt` and the vendor-family assembly already exist.","+- `/tmp/mcptest/gcworker.sh` (new) — copy of `s1worker.sh` with the two clamp flags swapped in.","+- **No product change.** `eg-consolidated` stays clean at HEAD `024f25a`; all 27 payload-defect","+  hypotheses that would have motivated one were refuted on winner-control."," "," ## Honest expectation","-This is a port, not a theory: the config with the best fair measurement in the program, applied to the","-model that has never had it, with a mechanism (pre-edit halving) that is measured on 50 instances and","-absent on Opus. That is the strongest remaining basis for the goal.","+This is the last untried config shape, and it is the only one that targets both required conditions","+rather than one. The mechanism is specific: clamp discovery to cut pre-edit, mandate finishing to keep","+the session long enough that the payload costs 3% rather than 10%."," ","-The risk is real though. Opus may simply not respond to a locate-first clamp the way Haiku does — its","-sessions are dominated by reproduce-and-verify work that the graph cannot touch, and Sonnet's own S1-","-family cell reached only −24.5% with pre-edit barely moving (−9%). So I would put this at","-**−20% to −35%**, wide, with a genuine chance it lands near −11% and settles the question negatively.","-The leading indicator in step 3 means we find out cheaply rather than after 40 sessions.","+Against it: the clamp's own wording has collapsed the session in both cells that used it, and CB shows","+an appended scaffold does not prevent that. The gated clamp puts the finishing mandate *inside* the","+clamp, which is why it might behave differently — but \"might\" is the honest word. I put this at","+**−15% to −28%**, and I will report the ceiling rather than run a seventh cell if it misses."]}],"originalFile":"# Opus to −25% by porting S1 — the best fair config, never run on Opus\n\n## Context\n\nGoal: Opus ≥ −25% on the 20-instance official-300 sample. Current fair number **−11.2%**\n[−27.8, +9.6] (n=20, published prompt, both arms symmetric, cap 120).\n\nI stopped proposing new mechanisms and mined the existing cells. Two things came out of that, and\ntogether they change what to run.\n\n### 1. Every payload-defect hypothesis is dead — verified, not assumed\n\nA 5-agent forensic sweep read all 20 sessions and produced 38 candidate defects. Adversarial\nverifiers with a **winner-control** requirement refuted **27 of 28** adjudicated so far:\n\n| claimed defect | winner control that killed it |\n|---|---|\n| bodies printed with no line numbers (prompt promises them) | **20/20 instances** — 6/6 winners, incl. the biggest wins |\n| `impact` blind-chained to rank-1, no gate | off-gold-file target in **7/12 winners**; the two largest wins have it in *more* degenerate form |\n| query polluted by GitHub issue-template boilerplate | 2/6 control winners have boilerplate queries → boilerplate top hits |\n| hits printed out of score order | 5/20 payloads, incl. winners lucene (−52%) and vuejs (−24%) |\n| line-less fabricated `server.h` caller | redis-10095 (+65) **and valkey-1842 (−21%, a winner)** |\n| `eg-q.run` path exposed 5× in prompt | 20/20 |\n\nOnly survivor: the shared **GOMODCACHE leak** (caddy's *baseline* read the fix out of\n`~/go/pkg/mod/…caddy/v2@v2.11.4/replacer.go`, 27 of 66 calls) — and it explains a winner, not a loss.\n\n**Conclusion: the tool is equally broken everywhere. Payload quality does not decide the sign.**\nDo not spend further effort on payload defects.\n\n### 2. Tokens are a pure function of the op-count ratio, and eg's op count is invariant\n\n| config | baseline ops | eg ops | ops Δ | tokens |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| G40 rich/rich, official | **23.8** | 28.7 | +21.1% | +28.4% |\n| OFF bare/rich, official | **39.0** | 27.5 | −29.6% | −46.5% |\n| PUB none/capability, published | **35.7** | 31.7 | −11.2% | −11.2% |\n\neg lands at 27.5 / 28.7 / 31.7 regardless of prompt. The **baseline** swings 23.8 → 39.0 purely on how\nmuch methodology its prompt carries. So the withdrawn −46.5% was a crippled control, and G40's +28.4%\nwas a control given better discipline than eg. Neither was about the tool.\n\n### 3. What the winning cells do that no Opus cell has ever done\n\nThe tool's job is to collapse the locate phase. On Haiku's best fair cells it halves pre-edit locate.\nOn Opus it never has:\n\n| cell | pre-edit base → eg | ops Δ | tokens |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **haiku S1** (n=50) | **16.2 → 8.5 (−48%)** | −39.3% | **−39.9%** |\n| haiku RR (n=21) | 14.2 → 6.3 (−56%) | −46.7% | −44.7% |\n| haiku R30 (n=30) | 15.7 → 10.3 (−34%) | −32.8% | −42.9% |\n| sonnet R30 (n=30) | 7.0 → 6.4 (−9%) | −25.1% | −24.5% |\n| **opus PUB** | **13.4 → 14.6 (+9%)** | −11.2% | −11.2% |\n| opus OFF | 19.1 → 13.6 (−29%) | −29.6% | −46.5% |\n\nOpus's baseline pre-edit (13.4) is comparable to Haiku's (16.2), so this is **not** \"Opus explores\nless\". It is that the config which halves pre-edit has only ever been run on Haiku.\n\n**S1 = `PROMPT_FAMILY=vendor BASE_CLAMP=1 EG_GATED_CLAMP=1`.** The harness's own comment on that\ncombination: *\"the matched control: a bare clamp on both sides, no shared block on either, so the only\ndifference is search-tool vs shell.\"* I verified its symmetry earlier by line-diff — 384 vs 370 words,\nmirrored clause for clause (LOCATE-FIRST/SEARCH-FIRST, READ the range, EDIT, do-not-re-confirm, STOP,\ntwo-attempts-then-widen). It is the best fair result in the whole program and **has never been run on\nOpus.**\n\n## Plan\n\n### 1. Run S1 on Opus, same 20 instances — 40 sessions\n`PROMPT_FAMILY=vendor BASE_CLAMP=1 EG_GATED_CLAMP=1`, `CC_MODEL=opus CLAUDE_EFFORT=high`,\n`TASKS_FILE=tasks/opus20_official.json`, binary `/tmp/eg-f19`, fresh `--cache-dir`.\n\nDeliberately **no prefetch** (S1 didn't use it; and the Arm A probe showed prefetch removal raises\ngraph usage 0.20→3.00) and **`GQ_SEARCH_CAP=0`** so follow-ups are possible. Cap 120 and\n`CC_TIMEOUT=3600` to keep `CENSORED=0` — the PUB baseline averaged 50.2 turns, so a 50-cap censors the\nbaseline specifically.\n\n### 2. Fairness gate before scoring — on emitted prompts, not config\nLine-diff the two arms with paths/digits normalised and account for every differing line; run the\nclause table (LOCATE/SEARCH-FIRST, READ range, EDIT, do-not-re-confirm, STOP, fallback) and require\n**parity or baseline-favouring**. S1's blocks passed this before; confirm they still do under the\ncurrent `run_3arm.sh`.\n\n### 3. Leading indicator, checkable before spending on the full score\n**Pre-edit locate must fall below the baseline's.** It is +9% today; every cell that reached ≤ −25%\ntokens had it at −34% or better. If pre-edit does not go negative by ~8 completed pairs, stop the cell\n— that is the mechanism, and without it the tokens cannot follow.\n\n### 4. Fix the one confirmed integrity defect in the same run\nIsolate `GOMODCACHE`/`GOPATH` per instance (and the npm/gem equivalents) so no arm can read a\npost-fix upstream release. Without this, caddy's baseline is reading the answer.\n\n### 5. Pre-registered\n- Success = geomean ≤ −25% with a CI upper bound below zero.\n- Arithmetic from the current cell: 12 winners contribute ln-sum −5.369, 8 losers +2.996. Fixing all 8\n  losers to parity gives only −23.5%, so S1 must also **deepen the winners** — which is exactly what a\n  pre-edit halving does, and why this config rather than a loser-targeted patch.\n- Falsification: if S1 on Opus lands within noise of −11.2%, then the pre-edit halving is\n  Haiku-specific and **−25% on Opus is not reachable with any config in this program.** I will report\n  that rather than keep re-cutting the same data.\n\n### 6. Replicate before claiming\nSecond independent cell if it clears. Three configs today looked strong at n≤12 and reversed by n=20.\n\n## Verification\n- `tools/model_cmp.py`; geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI; cost classes separately.\n- Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped symmetrically.\n- `CENSORED` must stay 0 per arm.\n- Report ops (pre/post/build) alongside tokens — ops predicted tokens within 3pt in all three cells\n  above, so it is the cheap early read on whether the cell is working.\n- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config — ten silent plumbing failures this session, the worst a\n  flag checked in one dispatcher but not the one every cell uses.\n\n## Files\n- `/tmp/mcptest/s1worker.sh` (new) — the S1 flag set, Opus, cap 120.\n- `tools/run_3arm.sh` — no changes needed; `base_clamp_prompt` and `gated_clamp_eg_prompt` already\n  exist and are what S1 used.\n- `tools/model_cmp.py` — scorer, already reproduces every historical number.\n- **No product change.** `eg-consolidated` stays clean at HEAD `024f25a`; every payload-defect\n  hypothesis that would have motivated one is refuted.\n\n## Honest expectation\nThis is a port, not a theory: the config with the best fair measurement in the program, applied to the\nmodel that has never had it, with a mechanism (pre-edit halving) that is measured on 50 instances and\nabsent on Opus. That is the strongest remaining basis for the goal.\n\nThe risk is real though. Opus may simply not respond to a locate-first clamp the way Haiku does — its\nsessions are dominated by reproduce-and-verify work that the graph cannot touch, and Sonnet's own S1-\nfamily cell reached only −24.5% with pre-edit barely moving (−9%). So I would put this at\n**−20% to −35%**, wide, with a genuine chance it lands near −11% and settles the question negatively.\nThe leading indicator in step 3 means we find out cheaply rather than after 40 sessions.\n","userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fd77f485-64cb-4fb6-aeef-47b606099b93","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
