{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01P6EtEZrtka8BvMWBZeka4V","lastSequenceNum":0}
{"parentUuid":"088826ac-2037-42dc-bc2d-a8a66701a137","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgJoqQuXsfPZFDMYKekQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EZoxk6pqa8XGEAe4SwjjYC","name":"ExitPlanMode","input":{"plan":"# Opus to −25%: the gated clamp, made symmetric\n\n## Context\n\nGoal: Opus ≥ −25% tokens on the 20-instance official-300 sample. Five configurations measured today.\nThe complete, fair evidence:\n\n| config | session size | baseline ops | eg ops | ops Δ | **tokens** | n |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| OFF — bare base / rich eg, official | long, 39.0 | 39.0 | 27.5 | −29.6% | −46.5% | 19 — **INVALID, asymmetric** |\n| G40 — rich/rich, official | long, 23.8 | 23.8 | 28.7 | +21.1% | +28.4% | 19 |\n| **PUB — published prompt, capability** | **long, 35.7** | 35.7 | 31.7 | −11.2% | **−11.2%** | 20 |\n| S1O — S1 clamp, no scaffold | **short, 4.6** | 4.6 | 4.3 | −8.0% | **+18.2%** [+2.3,+37.2] | 19 |\n| FRUGAL — rich/rich, frugal shared | short, 7.0 | 7.0 | 5.0 | −28.6% | −14.0% | 23 |\n| CB — clamp + scaffold | short, 4.0 | 4.0 | 1.0 | −75% | −24.9% | **1, in flight** |\n\n### The governing relation, measured\n\n**tokens ≈ ops ratio + payload tax**, and the payload tax depends only on session size:\n~**10%** at a 175k-token session (S1O: −8.0% ops → +18.2% tokens), ~**3%** at a 2.4M-token session\n(PUB: −11.2% ops → −11.2% tokens).\n\nSo −25% requires **both** conditions at once:\n- **ops ratio ≤ −28%**, and\n- **a long session**, so the payload amortises to ~3%.\n\nNo config has achieved both. PUB is long but cuts only 11% of ops — because its eg pre-edit locate\n*rises* (13.4 → 14.6, +9%). The clamp cells cut ops but collapse the session to 4–7 ops, where the\n10% tax eats the gain. FRUGAL is the clearest illustration: −28.6% ops became only −14.0% tokens\nbecause the tax took 14 points.\n\n### Why the clamp collapses the session, and what fixes it\n\n`base_clamp_prompt` / `shipped_eg_prompt` clamp *everything* — \"Apply the minimal fix and STOP the\nmoment you can justify it.\" Result: post-edit 0.3 ops, build 0.6 ops. The agent edits and leaves.\nCB tested whether appending the official scaffold would restore length; at n=1 it did **not** (still\n4.0 ops, post-edit and build both zero). **The clamp dominates an appended scaffold.**\n\n`gated_clamp_eg_prompt` already exists and is built for exactly this: it clamps discovery while\nexplicitly mandating completion —\n\n> DISCOVERY IS CLAMPED — FINISHING IS NOT. Before you stop, all three must be true:\n> (1) **VERIFIED** — you compiled the change or ran the nearest existing test at least ONCE …\n> (2) **SWEPT** — you checked the RELATED SITES the search result listed … and fixed every one …\n> (3) **COMPLETE** — you handled the edge cases the issue names …\n> Never stop merely because you have made an edit — stop when (1), (2) and (3) hold.\n\nThat is the only construct in the harness that cuts pre-edit *without* cutting the phases that make\na session long. **It has never been run, because it fails the fairness gate:** I checked, and\n`base_clamp_prompt()` is the *only* baseline-side block — there is no mirror, so eg would get\nVERIFIED/SWEPT/COMPLETE and the baseline nothing.\n\n## Plan\n\n### 1. Write `base_gated_clamp_prompt()` — the missing mirror\nIn `tools/run_3arm.sh`, beside `base_clamp_prompt()` (line 859). Clause-for-clause mirror of\n`gated_clamp_eg_prompt`, shell-worded:\n\n| eg clause | baseline mirror |\n|---|---|\n| FIRST action must be ONE search | FIRST action is ONE batched shell search |\n| open the top hit, read a line range, edit | open the best hit, read a line range, edit |\n| do NOT re-search to 'confirm' | do NOT re-grep to 'confirm' |\n| DISCOVERY IS CLAMPED — FINISHING IS NOT | identical, verbatim |\n| (1) VERIFIED … narrowest command … do NOT hunt a green suite | identical, verbatim |\n| (2) SWEPT — the RELATED SITES the search result listed | **SWEPT — grep the distinctive literal once more to enumerate the other sites** |\n| (3) COMPLETE — edge cases the issue names | identical, verbatim |\n| if TWO searches miss, fall back to the shell | if TWO batched searches miss, widen the pattern once |\n\n**Disclose the one clause that cannot be literal:** SWEPT. eg has a printed RELATED SITES list; the\nshell has none, so the baseline is told how to *produce* the equivalent list. This is the same real\nproduct difference already disclosed for `base_clamp_prompt` (\"only the baseline is told to Read the\nfile\"). It is baseline-favouring in wording (it gets an explicit instruction eg gets for free) and\nmust be reported as the one non-literal mirror.\n\nAdd `BASE_GATED_CLAMP=1` to the baseline branch of `tool_block`, next to the existing\n`BASE_CLAMP` check at line 1165.\n\n### 2. Fairness gate — on emitted prompts, before any spend\nLine-diff both arms, paths/digits normalised, and require **exactly one differing hunk** (the tool\nparagraph). Clause table must be 1:1 on: FIRST-action, read-line-range, do-not-re-confirm,\nDISCOVERY-IS-CLAMPED, VERIFIED, SWEPT, COMPLETE, never-stop-merely, TWO-then-fallback. Watch for\nline-wrap false negatives — collapse newlines before matching (this bit me once today).\n\n### 3. Run on Opus — 40 sessions, same 20 instances\n`PROMPT_FAMILY=vendor BASE_GATED_CLAMP=1 EG_GATED_CLAMP=1`, no prefetch, `GQ_SEARCH_CAP=0`,\n`CC_MAX_TURNS=120 CC_TIMEOUT=3600`, binary `/tmp/eg-f19`, fresh `--cache-dir`, and the per-instance\ncache isolation already built into `/tmp/mcptest/s1worker.sh` (`GOMODCACHE`, `GOPATH`, `GOCACHE`,\n`COMPOSER_HOME`, `CARGO_HOME`, `GEM_HOME`, `npm_config_cache`, `maven.repo.local`).\n\n### 4. Two leading indicators, both free, both checkable at ~8 pairs\n| indicator | required | why |\n|---|---|---|\n| **baseline total ops** | **≥ 20** | if the gate clamps finishing too, the session collapses to ~4 ops and the 10% payload tax returns — the S1O failure mode. Kill the cell. |\n| **eg pre-edit vs baseline** | **≤ −25%** | PUB is +9%; every cell reaching ≤−25% tokens had pre-edit ≤−28%. Without this the ops ratio cannot get there. |\n\nIf either fails at 8 pairs, stop — do not pay for 40 sessions to confirm a known failure mode.\n\n### 5. Pre-registered\n- Success = geomean ≤ −25% with CI upper bound < 0.\n- Required shape: baseline ops ≈ 25–35, eg ops ≈ 18–25, i.e. ops ratio ≈ −28% at long-session\n  amortisation (~3% tax) → tokens ≈ −25%.\n- Falsification: if ops fall ≥28% and tokens still miss −25%, the payload tax does not amortise the\n  way PUB implies, and **−25% on Opus is unreachable** — that would be the sixth independent\n  configuration and I will report the ceiling instead of running a seventh.\n- Replicate with a second independent cell before any claim. Today's n≤4 signals reversed\n  repeatedly, including on this very config family an hour ago.\n\n## Verification\n- `tools/model_cmp.py`: geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI, cost classes separately.\n- Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped symmetrically.\n- `CENSORED` (`error_max_turns`) = 0 per arm.\n- Report ops (pre/post/build) beside tokens every update — ops predicted tokens within 3pt in the\n  long-session cells and is the cheap early read.\n- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config. Eleven silent plumbing failures today; the worst was a\n  flag checked in one dispatcher but not the one every cell uses.\n\n## Files\n- `tools/run_3arm.sh` — add `base_gated_clamp_prompt()` near line 859; wire `BASE_GATED_CLAMP` in the\n  baseline branch near line 1165. `gated_clamp_eg_prompt` and the vendor-family assembly already exist.\n- `/tmp/mcptest/gcworker.sh` (new) — copy of `s1worker.sh` with the two clamp flags swapped in.\n- **No product change.** `eg-consolidated` stays clean at HEAD `024f25a`; all 27 payload-defect\n  hypotheses that would have motivated one were refuted on winner-control.\n\n## Honest expectation\nThis is the last untried config shape, and it is the only one that targets both required conditions\nrather than one. The mechanism is specific: clamp discovery to cut pre-edit, mandate finishing to keep\nthe session long enough that the payload costs 3% rather than 10%.\n\nAgainst it: the clamp's own wording has collapsed the session in both cells that used it, and CB shows\nan appended scaffold does not prevent that. The gated clamp puts the finishing mandate *inside* the\nclamp, which is why it might behave differently — but \"might\" is the honest word. I put this at\n**−15% to −28%**, and I will report the ceiling rather than run a seventh cell if it misses.\n","planFilePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/modular-cooking-cupcake.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4950,"cache_read_input_tokens":566299,"output_tokens":31,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4950,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":31,"cache_read_input_tokens":566299,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4950,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4950},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgJoibdqd5mxVViuSfT1","type":"assistant","uuid":"b3321996-efb6-4db2-bb59-bbe5c0b2953b","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:43:14.182Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"b3321996-efb6-4db2-bb59-bbe5c0b2953b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b3e4c981-5907-4b29-be6c-3d1a4cb51ab5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"User has approved your plan. You can now start coding. Start with updating your todo list if applicable\n\nYour plan has been saved to: /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/modular-cooking-cupcake.md\nYou can refer back to it if needed during implementation.\n\n## Approved Plan:\n# Opus to −25%: the gated clamp, made symmetric\n\n## Context\n\nGoal: Opus ≥ −25% tokens on the 20-instance official-300 sample. Five configurations measured today.\nThe complete, fair evidence:\n\n| config | session size | baseline ops | eg ops | ops Δ | **tokens** | n |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| OFF — bare base / rich eg, official | long, 39.0 | 39.0 | 27.5 | −29.6% | −46.5% | 19 — **INVALID, asymmetric** |\n| G40 — rich/rich, official | long, 23.8 | 23.8 | 28.7 | +21.1% | +28.4% | 19 |\n| **PUB — published prompt, capability** | **long, 35.7** | 35.7 | 31.7 | −11.2% | **−11.2%** | 20 |\n| S1O — S1 clamp, no scaffold | **short, 4.6** | 4.6 | 4.3 | −8.0% | **+18.2%** [+2.3,+37.2] | 19 |\n| FRUGAL — rich/rich, frugal shared | short, 7.0 | 7.0 | 5.0 | −28.6% | −14.0% | 23 |\n| CB — clamp + scaffold | short, 4.0 | 4.0 | 1.0 | −75% | −24.9% | **1, in flight** |\n\n### The governing relation, measured\n\n**tokens ≈ ops ratio + payload tax**, and the payload tax depends only on session size:\n~**10%** at a 175k-token session (S1O: −8.0% ops → +18.2% tokens), ~**3%** at a 2.4M-token session\n(PUB: −11.2% ops → −11.2% tokens).\n\nSo −25% requires **both** conditions at once:\n- **ops ratio ≤ −28%**, and\n- **a long session**, so the payload amortises to ~3%.\n\nNo config has achieved both. PUB is long but cuts only 11% of ops — because its eg pre-edit locate\n*rises* (13.4 → 14.6, +9%). The clamp cells cut ops but collapse the session to 4–7 ops, where the\n10% tax eats the gain. FRUGAL is the clearest illustration: −28.6% ops became only −14.0% tokens\nbecause the tax took 14 points.\n\n### Why the clamp collapses the session, and what fixes it\n\n`base_clamp_prompt` / `shipped_eg_prompt` clamp *everything* — \"Apply the minimal fix and STOP the\nmoment you can justify it.\" Result: post-edit 0.3 ops, build 0.6 ops. The agent edits and leaves.\nCB tested whether appending the official scaffold would restore length; at n=1 it did **not** (still\n4.0 ops, post-edit and build both zero). **The clamp dominates an appended scaffold.**\n\n`gated_clamp_eg_prompt` already exists and is built for exactly this: it clamps discovery while\nexplicitly mandating completion —\n\n> DISCOVERY IS CLAMPED — FINISHING IS NOT. Before you stop, all three must be true:\n> (1) **VERIFIED** — you compiled the change or ran the nearest existing test at least ONCE …\n> (2) **SWEPT** — you checked the RELATED SITES the search result listed … and fixed every one …\n> (3) **COMPLETE** — you handled the edge cases the issue names …\n> Never stop merely because you have made an edit — stop when (1), (2) and (3) hold.\n\nThat is the only construct in the harness that cuts pre-edit *without* cutting the phases that make\na session long. **It has never been run, because it fails the fairness gate:** I checked, and\n`base_clamp_prompt()` is the *only* baseline-side block — there is no mirror, so eg would get\nVERIFIED/SWEPT/COMPLETE and the baseline nothing.\n\n## Plan\n\n### 1. Write `base_gated_clamp_prompt()` — the missing mirror\nIn `tools/run_3arm.sh`, beside `base_clamp_prompt()` (line 859). Clause-for-clause mirror of\n`gated_clamp_eg_prompt`, shell-worded:\n\n| eg clause | baseline mirror |\n|---|---|\n| FIRST action must be ONE search | FIRST action is ONE batched shell search |\n| open the top hit, read a line range, edit | open the best hit, read a line range, edit |\n| do NOT re-search to 'confirm' | do NOT re-grep to 'confirm' |\n| DISCOVERY IS CLAMPED — FINISHING IS NOT | identical, verbatim |\n| (1) VERIFIED … narrowest command … do NOT hunt a green suite | identical, verbatim |\n| (2) SWEPT — the RELATED SITES the search result listed | **SWEPT — grep the distinctive literal once more to enumerate the other sites** |\n| (3) COMPLETE — edge cases the issue names | identical, verbatim |\n| if TWO searches miss, fall back to the shell | if TWO batched searches miss, widen the pattern once |\n\n**Disclose the one clause that cannot be literal:** SWEPT. eg has a printed RELATED SITES list; the\nshell has none, so the baseline is told how to *produce* the equivalent list. This is the same real\nproduct difference already disclosed for `base_clamp_prompt` (\"only the baseline is told to Read the\nfile\"). It is baseline-favouring in wording (it gets an explicit instruction eg gets for free) and\nmust be reported as the one non-literal mirror.\n\nAdd `BASE_GATED_CLAMP=1` to the baseline branch of `tool_block`, next to the existing\n`BASE_CLAMP` check at line 1165.\n\n### 2. Fairness gate — on emitted prompts, before any spend\nLine-diff both arms, paths/digits normalised, and require **exactly one differing hunk** (the tool\nparagraph). Clause table must be 1:1 on: FIRST-action, read-line-range, do-not-re-confirm,\nDISCOVERY-IS-CLAMPED, VERIFIED, SWEPT, COMPLETE, never-stop-merely, TWO-then-fallback. Watch for\nline-wrap false negatives — collapse newlines before matching (this bit me once today).\n\n### 3. Run on Opus — 40 sessions, same 20 instances\n`PROMPT_FAMILY=vendor BASE_GATED_CLAMP=1 EG_GATED_CLAMP=1`, no prefetch, `GQ_SEARCH_CAP=0`,\n`CC_MAX_TURNS=120 CC_TIMEOUT=3600`, binary `/tmp/eg-f19`, fresh `--cache-dir`, and the per-instance\ncache isolation already built into `/tmp/mcptest/s1worker.sh` (`GOMODCACHE`, `GOPATH`, `GOCACHE`,\n`COMPOSER_HOME`, `CARGO_HOME`, `GEM_HOME`, `npm_config_cache`, `maven.repo.local`).\n\n### 4. Two leading indicators, both free, both checkable at ~8 pairs\n| indicator | required | why |\n|---|---|---|\n| **baseline total ops** | **≥ 20** | if the gate clamps finishing too, the session collapses to ~4 ops and the 10% payload tax returns — the S1O failure mode. Kill the cell. |\n| **eg pre-edit vs baseline** | **≤ −25%** | PUB is +9%; every cell reaching ≤−25% tokens had pre-edit ≤−28%. Without this the ops ratio cannot get there. |\n\nIf either fails at 8 pairs, stop — do not pay for 40 sessions to confirm a known failure mode.\n\n### 5. Pre-registered\n- Success = geomean ≤ −25% with CI upper bound < 0.\n- Required shape: baseline ops ≈ 25–35, eg ops ≈ 18–25, i.e. ops ratio ≈ −28% at long-session\n  amortisation (~3% tax) → tokens ≈ −25%.\n- Falsification: if ops fall ≥28% and tokens still miss −25%, the payload tax does not amortise the\n  way PUB implies, and **−25% on Opus is unreachable** — that would be the sixth independent\n  configuration and I will report the ceiling instead of running a seventh.\n- Replicate with a second independent cell before any claim. Today's n≤4 signals reversed\n  repeatedly, including on this very config family an hour ago.\n\n## Verification\n- `tools/model_cmp.py`: geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI, cost classes separately.\n- Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped symmetrically.\n- `CENSORED` (`error_max_turns`) = 0 per arm.\n- Report ops (pre/post/build) beside tokens every update — ops predicted tokens within 3pt in the\n  long-session cells and is the cheap early read.\n- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config. Eleven silent plumbing failures today; the worst was a\n  flag checked in one dispatcher but not the one every cell uses.\n\n## Files\n- `tools/run_3arm.sh` — add `base_gated_clamp_prompt()` near line 859; wire `BASE_GATED_CLAMP` in the\n  baseline branch near line 1165. `gated_clamp_eg_prompt` and the vendor-family assembly already exist.\n- `/tmp/mcptest/gcworker.sh` (new) — copy of `s1worker.sh` with the two clamp flags swapped in.\n- **No product change.** `eg-consolidated` stays clean at HEAD `024f25a`; all 27 payload-defect\n  hypotheses that would have motivated one were refuted on winner-control.\n\n## Honest expectation\nThis is the last untried config shape, and it is the only one that targets both required conditions\nrather than one. The mechanism is specific: clamp discovery to cut pre-edit, mandate finishing to keep\nthe session long enough that the payload costs 3% rather than 10%.\n\nAgainst it: the clamp's own wording has collapsed the session in both cells that used it, and CB shows\nan appended scaffold does not prevent that. The gated clamp puts the finishing mandate *inside* the\nclamp, which is why it might behave differently — but \"might\" is the honest word. I put this at\n**−15% to −28%**, and I will report the ceiling rather than run a seventh cell if it misses.\n","tool_use_id":"toolu_01EZoxk6pqa8XGEAe4SwjjYC"}]},"uuid":"642e39d4-44b4-4f30-b150-5f95886b1ec6","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:43:37.157Z","toolUseResult":{"plan":"# Opus to −25%: the gated clamp, made symmetric\n\n## Context\n\nGoal: Opus ≥ −25% tokens on the 20-instance official-300 sample. Five configurations measured today.\nThe complete, fair evidence:\n\n| config | session size | baseline ops | eg ops | ops Δ | **tokens** | n |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| OFF — bare base / rich eg, official | long, 39.0 | 39.0 | 27.5 | −29.6% | −46.5% | 19 — **INVALID, asymmetric** |\n| G40 — rich/rich, official | long, 23.8 | 23.8 | 28.7 | +21.1% | +28.4% | 19 |\n| **PUB — published prompt, capability** | **long, 35.7** | 35.7 | 31.7 | −11.2% | **−11.2%** | 20 |\n| S1O — S1 clamp, no scaffold | **short, 4.6** | 4.6 | 4.3 | −8.0% | **+18.2%** [+2.3,+37.2] | 19 |\n| FRUGAL — rich/rich, frugal shared | short, 7.0 | 7.0 | 5.0 | −28.6% | −14.0% | 23 |\n| CB — clamp + scaffold | short, 4.0 | 4.0 | 1.0 | −75% | −24.9% | **1, in flight** |\n\n### The governing relation, measured\n\n**tokens ≈ ops ratio + payload tax**, and the payload tax depends only on session size:\n~**10%** at a 175k-token session (S1O: −8.0% ops → +18.2% tokens), ~**3%** at a 2.4M-token session\n(PUB: −11.2% ops → −11.2% tokens).\n\nSo −25% requires **both** conditions at once:\n- **ops ratio ≤ −28%**, and\n- **a long session**, so the payload amortises to ~3%.\n\nNo config has achieved both. PUB is long but cuts only 11% of ops — because its eg pre-edit locate\n*rises* (13.4 → 14.6, +9%). The clamp cells cut ops but collapse the session to 4–7 ops, where the\n10% tax eats the gain. FRUGAL is the clearest illustration: −28.6% ops became only −14.0% tokens\nbecause the tax took 14 points.\n\n### Why the clamp collapses the session, and what fixes it\n\n`base_clamp_prompt` / `shipped_eg_prompt` clamp *everything* — \"Apply the minimal fix and STOP the\nmoment you can justify it.\" Result: post-edit 0.3 ops, build 0.6 ops. The agent edits and leaves.\nCB tested whether appending the official scaffold would restore length; at n=1 it did **not** (still\n4.0 ops, post-edit and build both zero). **The clamp dominates an appended scaffold.**\n\n`gated_clamp_eg_prompt` already exists and is built for exactly this: it clamps discovery while\nexplicitly mandating completion —\n\n> DISCOVERY IS CLAMPED — FINISHING IS NOT. Before you stop, all three must be true:\n> (1) **VERIFIED** — you compiled the change or ran the nearest existing test at least ONCE …\n> (2) **SWEPT** — you checked the RELATED SITES the search result listed … and fixed every one …\n> (3) **COMPLETE** — you handled the edge cases the issue names …\n> Never stop merely because you have made an edit — stop when (1), (2) and (3) hold.\n\nThat is the only construct in the harness that cuts pre-edit *without* cutting the phases that make\na session long. **It has never been run, because it fails the fairness gate:** I checked, and\n`base_clamp_prompt()` is the *only* baseline-side block — there is no mirror, so eg would get\nVERIFIED/SWEPT/COMPLETE and the baseline nothing.\n\n## Plan\n\n### 1. Write `base_gated_clamp_prompt()` — the missing mirror\nIn `tools/run_3arm.sh`, beside `base_clamp_prompt()` (line 859). Clause-for-clause mirror of\n`gated_clamp_eg_prompt`, shell-worded:\n\n| eg clause | baseline mirror |\n|---|---|\n| FIRST action must be ONE search | FIRST action is ONE batched shell search |\n| open the top hit, read a line range, edit | open the best hit, read a line range, edit |\n| do NOT re-search to 'confirm' | do NOT re-grep to 'confirm' |\n| DISCOVERY IS CLAMPED — FINISHING IS NOT | identical, verbatim |\n| (1) VERIFIED … narrowest command … do NOT hunt a green suite | identical, verbatim |\n| (2) SWEPT — the RELATED SITES the search result listed | **SWEPT — grep the distinctive literal once more to enumerate the other sites** |\n| (3) COMPLETE — edge cases the issue names | identical, verbatim |\n| if TWO searches miss, fall back to the shell | if TWO batched searches miss, widen the pattern once |\n\n**Disclose the one clause that cannot be literal:** SWEPT. eg has a printed RELATED SITES list; the\nshell has none, so the baseline is told how to *produce* the equivalent list. This is the same real\nproduct difference already disclosed for `base_clamp_prompt` (\"only the baseline is told to Read the\nfile\"). It is baseline-favouring in wording (it gets an explicit instruction eg gets for free) and\nmust be reported as the one non-literal mirror.\n\nAdd `BASE_GATED_CLAMP=1` to the baseline branch of `tool_block`, next to the existing\n`BASE_CLAMP` check at line 1165.\n\n### 2. Fairness gate — on emitted prompts, before any spend\nLine-diff both arms, paths/digits normalised, and require **exactly one differing hunk** (the tool\nparagraph). Clause table must be 1:1 on: FIRST-action, read-line-range, do-not-re-confirm,\nDISCOVERY-IS-CLAMPED, VERIFIED, SWEPT, COMPLETE, never-stop-merely, TWO-then-fallback. Watch for\nline-wrap false negatives — collapse newlines before matching (this bit me once today).\n\n### 3. Run on Opus — 40 sessions, same 20 instances\n`PROMPT_FAMILY=vendor BASE_GATED_CLAMP=1 EG_GATED_CLAMP=1`, no prefetch, `GQ_SEARCH_CAP=0`,\n`CC_MAX_TURNS=120 CC_TIMEOUT=3600`, binary `/tmp/eg-f19`, fresh `--cache-dir`, and the per-instance\ncache isolation already built into `/tmp/mcptest/s1worker.sh` (`GOMODCACHE`, `GOPATH`, `GOCACHE`,\n`COMPOSER_HOME`, `CARGO_HOME`, `GEM_HOME`, `npm_config_cache`, `maven.repo.local`).\n\n### 4. Two leading indicators, both free, both checkable at ~8 pairs\n| indicator | required | why |\n|---|---|---|\n| **baseline total ops** | **≥ 20** | if the gate clamps finishing too, the session collapses to ~4 ops and the 10% payload tax returns — the S1O failure mode. Kill the cell. |\n| **eg pre-edit vs baseline** | **≤ −25%** | PUB is +9%; every cell reaching ≤−25% tokens had pre-edit ≤−28%. Without this the ops ratio cannot get there. |\n\nIf either fails at 8 pairs, stop — do not pay for 40 sessions to confirm a known failure mode.\n\n### 5. Pre-registered\n- Success = geomean ≤ −25% with CI upper bound < 0.\n- Required shape: baseline ops ≈ 25–35, eg ops ≈ 18–25, i.e. ops ratio ≈ −28% at long-session\n  amortisation (~3% tax) → tokens ≈ −25%.\n- Falsification: if ops fall ≥28% and tokens still miss −25%, the payload tax does not amortise the\n  way PUB implies, and **−25% on Opus is unreachable** — that would be the sixth independent\n  configuration and I will report the ceiling instead of running a seventh.\n- Replicate with a second independent cell before any claim. Today's n≤4 signals reversed\n  repeatedly, including on this very config family an hour ago.\n\n## Verification\n- `tools/model_cmp.py`: geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI, cost classes separately.\n- Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped symmetrically.\n- `CENSORED` (`error_max_turns`) = 0 per arm.\n- Report ops (pre/post/build) beside tokens every update — ops predicted tokens within 3pt in the\n  long-session cells and is the cheap early read.\n- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config. Eleven silent plumbing failures today; the worst was a\n  flag checked in one dispatcher but not the one every cell uses.\n\n## Files\n- `tools/run_3arm.sh` — add `base_gated_clamp_prompt()` near line 859; wire `BASE_GATED_CLAMP` in the\n  baseline branch near line 1165. `gated_clamp_eg_prompt` and the vendor-family assembly already exist.\n- `/tmp/mcptest/gcworker.sh` (new) — copy of `s1worker.sh` with the two clamp flags swapped in.\n- **No product change.** `eg-consolidated` stays clean at HEAD `024f25a`; all 27 payload-defect\n  hypotheses that would have motivated one were refuted on winner-control.\n\n## Honest expectation\nThis is the last untried config shape, and it is the only one that targets both required conditions\nrather than one. The mechanism is specific: clamp discovery to cut pre-edit, mandate finishing to keep\nthe session long enough that the payload costs 3% rather than 10%.\n\nAgainst it: the clamp's own wording has collapsed the session in both cells that used it, and CB shows\nan appended scaffold does not prevent that. The gated clamp puts the finishing mandate *inside* the\nclamp, which is why it might behave differently — but \"might\" is the honest word. I put this at\n**−15% to −28%**, and I will report the ceiling rather than run a seventh cell if it misses.\n","isAgent":false,"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/modular-cooking-cupcake.md"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b3321996-efb6-4db2-bb59-bbe5c0b2953b","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
