{"parentUuid":"69282029-1086-4219-bdc7-3271b1726c5b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgJquqs2t3SSHE2M61X1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Writing the missing baseline mirror:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3784,"cache_read_input_tokens":571249,"output_tokens":1762,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3784,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1762,"cache_read_input_tokens":571249,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3784,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3784},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgJqnjyd5kL21kgiSJGN","type":"assistant","uuid":"2d92bb89-affa-4778-b237-63961442cc4b","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:43:42.989Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"2d92bb89-affa-4778-b237-63961442cc4b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgJquqs2t3SSHE2M61X1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GUecwzMxm18HnmQvVJjuaJ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench/agentic-swebench\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport io\np='tools/run_3arm.sh'; s=io.open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\nanchor='base_clamp_prompt() {'\nnew = '''# BASE_GATED_CLAMP=1 — the missing mirror of gated_clamp_eg_prompt.\n#\n# Why it did not exist: gated_clamp_eg_prompt clamps DISCOVERY while mandating COMPLETION\n# (VERIFIED / SWEPT / COMPLETE). base_clamp_prompt clamps everything and mandates nothing, so running\n# EG_GATED_CLAMP against it hands the eg arm a three-clause completion contract the baseline has no\n# equivalent of. That is the instruction asymmetry that invalidated every withdrawn headline on this\n# suite, so the gated clamp has never been measured.\n#\n# Why the config matters (measured today, Opus, same 20 instances):\n#   tokens ~= ops ratio + payload tax, and the tax depends only on session size --\n#   ~10% at a 175k session, ~3% at a 2.4M session.\n#   PUB    long  (35.7 ops)  ops -11.2% -> tokens -11.2%   (eg pre-edit RISES +9%)\n#   S1O    short ( 4.6 ops)  ops  -8.0% -> tokens +18.2%   (tax eats it)\n#   FRUGAL short ( 7.0 ops)  ops -28.6% -> tokens -14.0%   (tax takes 14pt)\n#   -25% needs ops <= -28% AND a long session. Full clamps cut ops but collapse the session; the\n#   published scaffold keeps it long but does not cut pre-edit. The GATED clamp is the only construct\n#   that targets both: clamp discovery, mandate finishing.\n#\n# ONE clause cannot be a literal mirror, and it is disclosed: SWEPT. The eg payload PRINTS a RELATED\n# SITES list; the shell has none, so the baseline is told how to PRODUCE the equivalent list. That is\n# baseline-favouring in wording (it gets an explicit instruction the eg arm gets for free) and is the\n# same class of real product difference already disclosed for base_clamp_prompt.\nbase_gated_clamp_prompt() {\n  cat <<'TXT'\nNo code-intelligence tool is available for this repository. Locate the fix with the shell BEFORE\nreading anything. Your FIRST action is ONE batched shell search: put every probe you already know you\nneed into a single call joined by ';' — start from the most distinctive literal the issue gives you\n(an error message, an option name, an identifier).\nThen open the best hit with your native Read tool (pass a line range around the matched line) and\nedit. The strongest match is the fix site on most tasks - go straight there; do NOT re-grep to\n'confirm' what the match already showed you. Spend your turns on the FIX, not on looking around:\nevery turn re-reads your whole context, and that is what this task costs.\nDISCOVERY IS CLAMPED - FINISHING IS NOT. Before you stop, all three must be true:\n(1) VERIFIED - you compiled the change or ran the nearest existing test at least ONCE. Pick the\n    narrowest command that would still catch a syntax, type, name or arity error. A patch that does\n    not build fails the whole task; this is the cheapest turn you will spend. Then stop verifying -\n    read the error, fix what it names, re-run once. Do NOT hunt a green suite.\n(2) SWEPT - you enumerated the other sites that need the same change (grep the distinctive literal\n    once more to list them) and fixed every one that has the same bug. A fix is usually not one edit\n    in one place.\n(3) COMPLETE - you handled the edge cases the issue names (empty, nil, negative, unicode, error\n    paths).\nIf a pattern did not land it, search again with different words; if TWO batched searches miss, widen\nthe pattern once more rather than staying stuck. Never stop merely because you have made an edit -\nstop when (1), (2) and (3) hold.\nTXT\n}\nbase_clamp_prompt() {'''\nassert s.count(anchor)==1\ns=s.replace(anchor,new,1)\nold='      if [ \"${BASE_CLAMP:-0}\" = 1 ]; then base_clamp_prompt; return; fi'\nnew2='      if [ \"${BASE_GATED_CLAMP:-0}\" = 1 ]; then base_gated_clamp_prompt; return; fi\\n'+old\nassert s.count(old)==1\ns=s.replace(old,new2,1)\nio.open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('base_gated_clamp_prompt() added and wired via BASE_GATED_CLAMP')\nPY\nbash -n tools/run_3arm.sh && echo \"syntax OK\"","description":"Add the baseline gated-clamp mirror"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3784,"cache_read_input_tokens":571249,"output_tokens":1762,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3784,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1762,"cache_read_input_tokens":571249,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3784,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3784},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgJqnjyd5kL21kgiSJGN","type":"assistant","uuid":"6ad4c7eb-2fcb-475c-9da1-562cb710101b","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:44:01.307Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
