Path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208/workflows/scripts/eg-catastrophe-forensics-wf_94f6083d-7f0.js"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f0d21122-a127-4238-adc2-a10e3d43e605","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"ca237e77-765e-47d1-8b4f-a3982e15f0ce","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgKFjUwmjhAzAepUn2zd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Workflow launched — 11 agents, running alongside the two live cells.\n\n**The design point that makes this one stronger than the last sweep:** I'm not asking \"why did this instance lose\". I'm asking \"why did *this same instance* lose by +161% under one config and win by −18% under another\". Same repo, same gold patch, same model, so task difficulty is held exactly constant and the whole swing is attributable. Each instance is its own control, which is precisely what killed 27 of 28 findings last time — and here it's built into the question instead of applied afterwards.\n\nAssignments:\n\n| agent | instance | swing |\n|---|---|---|\n| fmt2457 | fmt-2457 | −18% (PUB) → +109% (S1O) → **+161%** (G40) — two independent catastrophes on one instance |\n| docusaurus | docusaurus-10130 | −38% → **+142%** — largest single swing, 180pt |\n| hugo | hugo-12204 | −15% → **+103%** |\n| carbon | carbon-2752 | **+107% everywhere** — the only instance with no winning config |\n| g40trio | preact-3010, micropython-15898, laravel-48636 | all G40-only; cross-checked against their rep30 counterparts |\n\nI also handed the agents the 27 refuted hypotheses with their numbers so they don't re-file them, the confirmed cache-leak finding so they can look for further instances of it, and the measured token model (`tokens ≈ ops ratio + payload tax`, tax ~10% short / ~3% long) so their arithmetic has to reconcile against `cc_out.json` totals — a mechanism claimed to cost 400k in a 235k session gets refuted on arithmetic alone.\n\nMeanwhile: **GC (the symmetric gated clamp) is running** — 4/20 per arm, load 18, zero bad jobs, and the live prompts confirm both arms carry `DISCOVERY IS CLAMPED`, `VERIFIED`, `SWEPT`, `COMPLETE`. CB is at 7/40. I'll report GC's two leading indicators — baseline ops ≥ 20 and eg pre-edit ≤ −25% — as soon as ~8 pairs land, and kill it early if either fails rather than paying for all 40."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7035,"cache_read_input_tokens":586982,"output_tokens":754,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7035,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":754,"cache_read_input_tokens":586982,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7035,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7035},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgKFcWk5LwCgiuGrSirv","type":"assistant","uuid":"47815a91-56b7-4052-a196-abd9b2498426","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:49:16.622Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
