{"parentUuid":"2e1b9a5f-3318-44c9-9f5f-2038f3002733","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgKPvmZoZcTqhoBrwRnv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The arithmetic closes, and it points somewhere I'd wrongly written off. Writing the plan:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4601,"cache_read_input_tokens":598930,"output_tokens":4463,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4601,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4463,"cache_read_input_tokens":598930,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4601,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4601},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgKPnZDHGSfAduuknycL","type":"assistant","uuid":"bbd11b5a-4163-4cf3-aa94-92b39fa7eaed","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:51:08.099Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"bbd11b5a-4163-4cf3-aa94-92b39fa7eaed","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgKPvmZoZcTqhoBrwRnv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01StorywW8BRq3Vgea4q8gLP","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/modular-cooking-cupcake.md","content":"# Opus to −25%: make the payload addressable, in the long-session regime\n\n## Context\n\nGoal: Opus ≥ −25% tokens on the 20-instance official-300 sample. Six configurations are now measured.\nFitting them together gives a quantitative model that says exactly where the goal is reachable — and\nit is not where I have been spending.\n\n| config | baseline ops | ops Δ | ktok/session | tokens | **penalty** (tokens−ops) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **PUB** — published prompt, prefetch | 35.7 | −11.2% | **2729k** | **−11.2%** | **+0.0** |\n| G40 — rich methodology both arms | 23.8 | +21.1% | 1300k | +28.4% | +7.3 |\n| GC — gated clamp (symmetric) | 11.5 | +4.3% | 378k | +22.2% | +17.9 |\n| CB — clamp + scaffold | 10.5 | −20.6% | 345k | +7.5% | +28.1 |\n| FRUGAL — rich both, frugal shared | 7.0 | −28.6% | 279k | −14.0% | +14.6 |\n| S1O — S1 clamp | 4.6 | −8.0% | 175k | +18.2% | +26.2 |\n\n**`tokens ≈ ops Δ + payload tax`, and the tax is a pure function of session size** — 0 at 2729k,\n+7 at 1300k, +18 to +28 below 400k. So:\n\n| regime | ops reduction required for −25% |\n|---|---|\n| **2729k (PUB)** | **−25%** |\n| 1300k | −32% |\n| ~350k | −53% |\n\n**Only the longest regime is viable.** Every clamp config I have run this session sits at 175–378k,\nwhere the tax alone is +18 to +28 points — which is why CB cut 20.6% of ops and still lost, and why\nGC and S1O lost outright. That whole direction is dead, and both live cells are failing their\npre-registered gates right now (baseline ops 10.5 and 11.5 against a required ≥20; GC's pre-edit is\n+40% against a required ≤−25%). **Kill both.**\n\n## Where the 14 points are\n\nPUB's op budget, measured:\n\n| phase | baseline | eg |\n|---|---|---|\n| pre-edit locate | 13.4 | **14.6** (worse) |\n| post-edit locate | 15.5 | 11.8 |\n| build/test | 6.8 | 5.2 |\n| **total** | **35.7** | **31.7 (−11.2%)** |\n\nTarget for −25% ops is 26.8. Two steps get there:\n\n| step | eg total | ops Δ |\n|---|---|---|\n| eg pre-edit merely *matches* the baseline (14.6 → 13.4) | 30.4 | −14.8% |\n| **+ post-edit re-hunts removed (11.8 → 7.1)** | **26.9** | **−24.6%** ✓ |\n\nAt PUB's session size the tax is zero, so −24.6% ops ⇒ **≈ −25% tokens**.\n\n## The mechanism, and why the earlier refutation does not apply\n\nMeasured on this cell:\n- **\"re-finds text the payload already printed\" = 5.58 ops/session (winners), 7.25 (losers)** — about\n  40% of eg's post-edit locate work.\n- **Payload bodies carry ZERO line numbers**: 0 of 55, 0 of 107, 0 of 79 — in **20/20 instances**.\n- The eg prompt promises, verbatim: *\"the complete body of the enclosing function is printed verbatim\n  beneath that header, **at its real line numbers**\"*. The prompt is false.\n\nUnnumbered bodies are not addressable. To build an `Edit` old_string anchor, a `Read` range, or to\nreason about hunk positions, the agent must re-open the file it was just shown. That is the re-hunt.\n\n**The adversarial verifier refuted this as a loser-explanation — correctly — and that refutation is\nirrelevant here.** Its reasoning was: present in 20/20 instances, therefore in 6/6 winners, therefore\nit cannot be what makes an instance *lose*. True. But what this goal needs is **not** a\nloser-differentiator: fixing all 8 losers to exact parity yields only **−23.5%**, short of target.\nIt needs a **uniform tax removal that lifts all 20** — and a defect present in 20/20 is precisely the\nright shape for that. I conflated these two questions earlier and dropped a valid lever.\n\n## Plan\n\n### 1. Stop the two failing cells\nKill CB and GC. Both breach the gates I pre-registered; the sub-400k regime cannot reach −25% at any\nachievable ops reduction.\n\n### 2. Product change: number the body lines\n`eg-consolidated`, the search render path (`internal/sem/` — the body printer that emits ranked-hit\nbodies beneath the `N. path:START-END score= symbol=` header):\n- prefix every printed body line with its real line number (the header already carries the span, so\n  this is 5–6 chars/line);\n- set `focus=` to the matched **interior** line rather than collapsing to the definition line.\n\nThis makes the prompt's existing promise true. It is a rendering change only — no ranking, no\nretrieval, no selection. The baseline has no payload, so arm symmetry is untouched.\n\n### 3. Emulate all 20 offline before spending — free\nRecorded queries in `results/PUB_r1_eg/eg/<inst>/prefetch_calls.log`, worktrees in\n`replay-wt/<inst>`, patched binary, **fresh `--cache-dir`** (the index cache is tree-keyed, not\nbinary-keyed — reuse it and you get the old binary's answer).\nAssert per instance: every body line numbered; the numbers match the file at that path; `focus=` lands\ninside the body; and **byte-identical output outside the body lines** (no ranking drift). Any\ninstance failing the last check blocks the cell.\n\n### 4. Run PUB + numbered bodies — 40 sessions, same 20 instances\nEverything else exactly as the −11.2% cell: `PUBLISHED_EXACT=1`, prefetch + impact on, cap 120,\n`CC_TIMEOUT=3600`, plus the per-instance cache isolation already built into the workers\n(`GOMODCACHE`, `GOPATH`, `GOCACHE`, `COMPOSER_HOME`, `CARGO_HOME`, `GEM_HOME`, `npm_config_cache`,\n`maven.repo.local`) — the one confirmed integrity defect, where caddy's baseline read the gold line\nout of the module cache and carbon's eg arm read the gold regex out of the composer cache.\n\n### 5. Leading indicators — free, checkable at ~8 pairs\n| indicator | current | required |\n|---|---|---|\n| session size | 2729k | **stays > 2000k** (if it collapses, the tax returns and the cell is void) |\n| eg pre-edit locate | +9% | **≤ 0%** |\n| post-edit \"re-finds payload text\" | 5.58 / 7.25 per session | **≤ 4.0** |\n| ops Δ | −11.2% | **≤ −20%** |\nKill the cell if session size collapses or ops Δ has not passed −18% by 8 pairs.\n\n### 6. Pre-registered\n- Success = geomean ≤ −25%, CI upper bound < 0.\n- Required shape: eg ops ≈ 27 against baseline ≈ 36, at ~2700k session size.\n- **Falsification:** if bodies are numbered, re-hunts fall, ops reach ≤ −20%, and tokens still miss\n  −25%, then the ops↔tokens identity that holds at PUB length is wrong and **−25% on Opus is\n  unreachable**. That is the seventh configuration and I will report the ceiling.\n- Replicate with a second independent cell before claiming. Today's n≤4 signals reversed repeatedly.\n\n## Verification\n- `tools/model_cmp.py`: geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI, cost classes separately.\n- Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped symmetrically.\n- `CENSORED` (`error_max_turns`) = 0 per arm — the baseline averages 50.2 turns, so a 50-cap censors\n  the baseline specifically.\n- Report ops (pre/post/build) beside tokens in every update; at PUB length ops predicted tokens to\n  within 0.0 points, so it is the cheap early read.\n- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config. Twelve silent plumbing failures today — the latest being\n  `BASE_GATED_CLAMP` wired into one dispatcher but not the one the vendor family uses, caught only\n  because the fairness gate compared emitted prompts.\n\n## Files\n- `eg-consolidated/internal/sem/` — the ranked-hit body renderer. Only product change. Add a\n  regression test asserting numbered bodies and unchanged surrounding output.\n- `/tmp/mcptest/pubworker.sh` — the −11.2% config; point at the rebuilt binary, keep everything else.\n- `tools/model_cmp.py` — scorer, unchanged.\n- No prompt changes: the prompt already claims numbered lines, so this makes it honest rather than\n  altering the contract.\n\n## Honest expectation\nThis is the first plan built on a fitted quantitative model rather than a mechanism story: the six\nmeasured configs give tax-vs-session-size, that fixes the viable regime to PUB, and the op budget then\nnames the exact 4.9 ops to remove. The lever is a real defect (0 numbered lines in 20/20, against a\nprompt that promises them) whose measured footprint (5.58–7.25 ops/session) is the right size to close\nthe gap.\n\nTwo ways it can fail honestly. The re-hunts may not be *caused* by the missing line numbers — the\nagent may re-read regardless, which would show up as ops not moving. And removing pre-edit's +1.2\ndeficit has no mechanism attached at all; I am counting it in the arithmetic but I cannot make it\nhappen, so the realistic band is **−18% to −26%** with the goal at the top of it.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4601,"cache_read_input_tokens":598930,"output_tokens":4463,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4601,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4463,"cache_read_input_tokens":598930,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4601,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4601},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgKPnZDHGSfAduuknycL","type":"assistant","uuid":"8a6388b0-ad1c-46b2-bc3c-13127e365f9f","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:51:51.961Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"8a6388b0-ad1c-46b2-bc3c-13127e365f9f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4cfad49e-246c-49ef-b5bd-807cc83b7bba","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01StorywW8BRq3Vgea4q8gLP","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/modular-cooking-cupcake.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"5d0e4873-fff5-4a2d-83a0-f447924b8585","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:51:52.302Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/modular-cooking-cupcake.md","content":"# Opus to −25%: make the payload addressable, in the long-session regime\n\n## Context\n\nGoal: Opus ≥ −25% tokens on the 20-instance official-300 sample. Six configurations are now measured.\nFitting them together gives a quantitative model that says exactly where the goal is reachable — and\nit is not where I have been spending.\n\n| config | baseline ops | ops Δ | ktok/session | tokens | **penalty** (tokens−ops) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **PUB** — published prompt, prefetch | 35.7 | −11.2% | **2729k** | **−11.2%** | **+0.0** |\n| G40 — rich methodology both arms | 23.8 | +21.1% | 1300k | +28.4% | +7.3 |\n| GC — gated clamp (symmetric) | 11.5 | +4.3% | 378k | +22.2% | +17.9 |\n| CB — clamp + scaffold | 10.5 | −20.6% | 345k | +7.5% | +28.1 |\n| FRUGAL — rich both, frugal shared | 7.0 | −28.6% | 279k | −14.0% | +14.6 |\n| S1O — S1 clamp | 4.6 | −8.0% | 175k | +18.2% | +26.2 |\n\n**`tokens ≈ ops Δ + payload tax`, and the tax is a pure function of session size** — 0 at 2729k,\n+7 at 1300k, +18 to +28 below 400k. So:\n\n| regime | ops reduction required for −25% |\n|---|---|\n| **2729k (PUB)** | **−25%** |\n| 1300k | −32% |\n| ~350k | −53% |\n\n**Only the longest regime is viable.** Every clamp config I have run this session sits at 175–378k,\nwhere the tax alone is +18 to +28 points — which is why CB cut 20.6% of ops and still lost, and why\nGC and S1O lost outright. That whole direction is dead, and both live cells are failing their\npre-registered gates right now (baseline ops 10.5 and 11.5 against a required ≥20; GC's pre-edit is\n+40% against a required ≤−25%). **Kill both.**\n\n## Where the 14 points are\n\nPUB's op budget, measured:\n\n| phase | baseline | eg |\n|---|---|---|\n| pre-edit locate | 13.4 | **14.6** (worse) |\n| post-edit locate | 15.5 | 11.8 |\n| build/test | 6.8 | 5.2 |\n| **total** | **35.7** | **31.7 (−11.2%)** |\n\nTarget for −25% ops is 26.8. Two steps get there:\n\n| step | eg total | ops Δ |\n|---|---|---|\n| eg pre-edit merely *matches* the baseline (14.6 → 13.4) | 30.4 | −14.8% |\n| **+ post-edit re-hunts removed (11.8 → 7.1)** | **26.9** | **−24.6%** ✓ |\n\nAt PUB's session size the tax is zero, so −24.6% ops ⇒ **≈ −25% tokens**.\n\n## The mechanism, and why the earlier refutation does not apply\n\nMeasured on this cell:\n- **\"re-finds text the payload already printed\" = 5.58 ops/session (winners), 7.25 (losers)** — about\n  40% of eg's post-edit locate work.\n- **Payload bodies carry ZERO line numbers**: 0 of 55, 0 of 107, 0 of 79 — in **20/20 instances**.\n- The eg prompt promises, verbatim: *\"the complete body of the enclosing function is printed verbatim\n  beneath that header, **at its real line numbers**\"*. The prompt is false.\n\nUnnumbered bodies are not addressable. To build an `Edit` old_string anchor, a `Read` range, or to\nreason about hunk positions, the agent must re-open the file it was just shown. That is the re-hunt.\n\n**The adversarial verifier refuted this as a loser-explanation — correctly — and that refutation is\nirrelevant here.** Its reasoning was: present in 20/20 instances, therefore in 6/6 winners, therefore\nit cannot be what makes an instance *lose*. True. But what this goal needs is **not** a\nloser-differentiator: fixing all 8 losers to exact parity yields only **−23.5%**, short of target.\nIt needs a **uniform tax removal that lifts all 20** — and a defect present in 20/20 is precisely the\nright shape for that. I conflated these two questions earlier and dropped a valid lever.\n\n## Plan\n\n### 1. Stop the two failing cells\nKill CB and GC. Both breach the gates I pre-registered; the sub-400k regime cannot reach −25% at any\nachievable ops reduction.\n\n### 2. Product change: number the body lines\n`eg-consolidated`, the search render path (`internal/sem/` — the body printer that emits ranked-hit\nbodies beneath the `N. path:START-END score= symbol=` header):\n- prefix every printed body line with its real line number (the header already carries the span, so\n  this is 5–6 chars/line);\n- set `focus=` to the matched **interior** line rather than collapsing to the definition line.\n\nThis makes the prompt's existing promise true. It is a rendering change only — no ranking, no\nretrieval, no selection. The baseline has no payload, so arm symmetry is untouched.\n\n### 3. Emulate all 20 offline before spending — free\nRecorded queries in `results/PUB_r1_eg/eg/<inst>/prefetch_calls.log`, worktrees in\n`replay-wt/<inst>`, patched binary, **fresh `--cache-dir`** (the index cache is tree-keyed, not\nbinary-keyed — reuse it and you get the old binary's answer).\nAssert per instance: every body line numbered; the numbers match the file at that path; `focus=` lands\ninside the body; and **byte-identical output outside the body lines** (no ranking drift). Any\ninstance failing the last check blocks the cell.\n\n### 4. Run PUB + numbered bodies — 40 sessions, same 20 instances\nEverything else exactly as the −11.2% cell: `PUBLISHED_EXACT=1`, prefetch + impact on, cap 120,\n`CC_TIMEOUT=3600`, plus the per-instance cache isolation already built into the workers\n(`GOMODCACHE`, `GOPATH`, `GOCACHE`, `COMPOSER_HOME`, `CARGO_HOME`, `GEM_HOME`, `npm_config_cache`,\n`maven.repo.local`) — the one confirmed integrity defect, where caddy's baseline read the gold line\nout of the module cache and carbon's eg arm read the gold regex out of the composer cache.\n\n### 5. Leading indicators — free, checkable at ~8 pairs\n| indicator | current | required |\n|---|---|---|\n| session size | 2729k | **stays > 2000k** (if it collapses, the tax returns and the cell is void) |\n| eg pre-edit locate | +9% | **≤ 0%** |\n| post-edit \"re-finds payload text\" | 5.58 / 7.25 per session | **≤ 4.0** |\n| ops Δ | −11.2% | **≤ −20%** |\nKill the cell if session size collapses or ops Δ has not passed −18% by 8 pairs.\n\n### 6. Pre-registered\n- Success = geomean ≤ −25%, CI upper bound < 0.\n- Required shape: eg ops ≈ 27 against baseline ≈ 36, at ~2700k session size.\n- **Falsification:** if bodies are numbered, re-hunts fall, ops reach ≤ −20%, and tokens still miss\n  −25%, then the ops↔tokens identity that holds at PUB length is wrong and **−25% on Opus is\n  unreachable**. That is the seventh configuration and I will report the ceiling.\n- Replicate with a second independent cell before claiming. Today's n≤4 signals reversed repeatedly.\n\n## Verification\n- `tools/model_cmp.py`: geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI, cost classes separately.\n- Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped symmetrically.\n- `CENSORED` (`error_max_turns`) = 0 per arm — the baseline averages 50.2 turns, so a 50-cap censors\n  the baseline specifically.\n- Report ops (pre/post/build) beside tokens in every update; at PUB length ops predicted tokens to\n  within 0.0 points, so it is the cheap early read.\n- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config. Twelve silent plumbing failures today — the latest being\n  `BASE_GATED_CLAMP` wired into one dispatcher but not the one the vendor family uses, caught only\n  because the fairness gate compared emitted prompts.\n\n## Files\n- `eg-consolidated/internal/sem/` — the ranked-hit body renderer. Only product change. Add a\n  regression test asserting numbered bodies and unchanged surrounding output.\n- `/tmp/mcptest/pubworker.sh` — the −11.2% config; point at the rebuilt binary, keep everything else.\n- `tools/model_cmp.py` — scorer, unchanged.\n- No prompt changes: the prompt already claims numbered lines, so this makes it honest rather than\n  altering the contract.\n\n## Honest expectation\nThis is the first plan built on a fitted quantitative model rather than a mechanism story: the six\nmeasured configs give tax-vs-session-size, that fixes the viable regime to PUB, and the op budget then\nnames the exact 4.9 ops to remove. The lever is a real defect (0 numbered lines in 20/20, against a\nprompt that promises them) whose measured footprint (5.58–7.25 ops/session) is the right size to close\nthe gap.\n\nTwo ways it can fail honestly. The re-hunts may not be *caused* by the missing line numbers — the\nagent may re-read regardless, which would show up as ops not moving. And removing pre-edit's +1.2\ndeficit has no mechanism attached at all; I am counting it in the arithmetic but I cannot make it\nhappen, so the realistic band is **−18% to −26%** with the goal at the top of it.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":133,"newStart":1,"newLines":149,"lines":["-# Opus to −25%: the gated clamp, made symmetric","+# Opus to −25%: make the payload addressable, in the long-session regime"," "," ## Context"," ","-Goal: Opus ≥ −25% tokens on the 20-instance official-300 sample. Five configurations measured today.","-The complete, fair evidence:","+Goal: Opus ≥ −25% tokens on the 20-instance official-300 sample. Six configurations are now measured.","+Fitting them together gives a quantitative model that says exactly where the goal is reachable — and","+it is not where I have been spending."," ","-| config | session size | baseline ops | eg ops | ops Δ | **tokens** | n |","-|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","-| OFF — bare base / rich eg, official | long, 39.0 | 39.0 | 27.5 | −29.6% | −46.5% | 19 — **INVALID, asymmetric** |","-| G40 — rich/rich, official | long, 23.8 | 23.8 | 28.7 | +21.1% | +28.4% | 19 |","-| **PUB — published prompt, capability** | **long, 35.7** | 35.7 | 31.7 | −11.2% | **−11.2%** | 20 |","-| S1O — S1 clamp, no scaffold | **short, 4.6** | 4.6 | 4.3 | −8.0% | **+18.2%** [+2.3,+37.2] | 19 |","-| FRUGAL — rich/rich, frugal shared | short, 7.0 | 7.0 | 5.0 | −28.6% | −14.0% | 23 |","-| CB — clamp + scaffold | short, 4.0 | 4.0 | 1.0 | −75% | −24.9% | **1, in flight** |","+| config | baseline ops | ops Δ | ktok/session | tokens | **penalty** (tokens−ops) |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| **PUB** — published prompt, prefetch | 35.7 | −11.2% | **2729k** | **−11.2%** | **+0.0** |","+| G40 — rich methodology both arms | 23.8 | +21.1% | 1300k | +28.4% | +7.3 |","+| GC — gated clamp (symmetric) | 11.5 | +4.3% | 378k | +22.2% | +17.9 |","+| CB — clamp + scaffold | 10.5 | −20.6% | 345k | +7.5% | +28.1 |","+| FRUGAL — rich both, frugal shared | 7.0 | −28.6% | 279k | −14.0% | +14.6 |","+| S1O — S1 clamp | 4.6 | −8.0% | 175k | +18.2% | +26.2 |"," ","-### The governing relation, measured","+**`tokens ≈ ops Δ + payload tax`, and the tax is a pure function of session size** — 0 at 2729k,","++7 at 1300k, +18 to +28 below 400k. So:"," ","-**tokens ≈ ops ratio + payload tax**, and the payload tax depends only on session size:","-~**10%** at a 175k-token session (S1O: −8.0% ops → +18.2% tokens), ~**3%** at a 2.4M-token session","-(PUB: −11.2% ops → −11.2% tokens).","+| regime | ops reduction required for −25% |","+|---|---|","+| **2729k (PUB)** | **−25%** |","+| 1300k | −32% |","+| ~350k | −53% |"," ","-So −25% requires **both** conditions at once:","-- **ops ratio ≤ −28%**, and","-- **a long session**, so the payload amortises to ~3%.","+**Only the longest regime is viable.** Every clamp config I have run this session sits at 175–378k,","+where the tax alone is +18 to +28 points — which is why CB cut 20.6% of ops and still lost, and why","+GC and S1O lost outright. That whole direction is dead, and both live cells are failing their","+pre-registered gates right now (baseline ops 10.5 and 11.5 against a required ≥20; GC's pre-edit is","++40% against a required ≤−25%). **Kill both.**"," ","-No config has achieved both. PUB is long but cuts only 11% of ops — because its eg pre-edit locate","-*rises* (13.4 → 14.6, +9%). The clamp cells cut ops but collapse the session to 4–7 ops, where the","-10% tax eats the gain. FRUGAL is the clearest illustration: −28.6% ops became only −14.0% tokens","-because the tax took 14 points.","+## Where the 14 points are"," ","-### Why the clamp collapses the session, and what fixes it","+PUB's op budget, measured:"," ","-`base_clamp_prompt` / `shipped_eg_prompt` clamp *everything* — \"Apply the minimal fix and STOP the","-moment you can justify it.\" Result: post-edit 0.3 ops, build 0.6 ops. The agent edits and leaves.","-CB tested whether appending the official scaffold would restore length; at n=1 it did **not** (still","-4.0 ops, post-edit and build both zero). **The clamp dominates an appended scaffold.**","+| phase | baseline | eg |","+|---|---|---|","+| pre-edit locate | 13.4 | **14.6** (worse) |","+| post-edit locate | 15.5 | 11.8 |","+| build/test | 6.8 | 5.2 |","+| **total** | **35.7** | **31.7 (−11.2%)** |"," ","-`gated_clamp_eg_prompt` already exists and is built for exactly this: it clamps discovery while","-explicitly mandating completion —","+Target for −25% ops is 26.8. Two steps get there:"," ","-> DISCOVERY IS CLAMPED — FINISHING IS NOT. Before you stop, all three must be true:","-> (1) **VERIFIED** — you compiled the change or ran the nearest existing test at least ONCE …","-> (2) **SWEPT** — you checked the RELATED SITES the search result listed … and fixed every one …","-> (3) **COMPLETE** — you handled the edge cases the issue names …","-> Never stop merely because you have made an edit — stop when (1), (2) and (3) hold.","+| step | eg total | ops Δ |","+|---|---|---|","+| eg pre-edit merely *matches* the baseline (14.6 → 13.4) | 30.4 | −14.8% |","+| **+ post-edit re-hunts removed (11.8 → 7.1)** | **26.9** | **−24.6%** ✓ |"," ","-That is the only construct in the harness that cuts pre-edit *without* cutting the phases that make","-a session long. **It has never been run, because it fails the fairness gate:** I checked, and","-`base_clamp_prompt()` is the *only* baseline-side block — there is no mirror, so eg would get","-VERIFIED/SWEPT/COMPLETE and the baseline nothing.","+At PUB's session size the tax is zero, so −24.6% ops ⇒ **≈ −25% tokens**."," ","-## Plan","+## The mechanism, and why the earlier refutation does not apply"," ","-### 1. Write `base_gated_clamp_prompt()` — the missing mirror","-In `tools/run_3arm.sh`, beside `base_clamp_prompt()` (line 859). Clause-for-clause mirror of","-`gated_clamp_eg_prompt`, shell-worded:","+Measured on this cell:","+- **\"re-finds text the payload already printed\" = 5.58 ops/session (winners), 7.25 (losers)** — about","+  40% of eg's post-edit locate work.","+- **Payload bodies carry ZERO line numbers**: 0 of 55, 0 of 107, 0 of 79 — in **20/20 instances**.","+- The eg prompt promises, verbatim: *\"the complete body of the enclosing function is printed verbatim","+  beneath that header, **at its real line numbers**\"*. The prompt is false."," ","-| eg clause | baseline mirror |","-|---|---|","-| FIRST action must be ONE search | FIRST action is ONE batched shell search |","-| open the top hit, read a line range, edit | open the best hit, read a line range, edit |","-| do NOT re-search to 'confirm' | do NOT re-grep to 'confirm' |","-| DISCOVERY IS CLAMPED — FINISHING IS NOT | identical, verbatim |","-| (1) VERIFIED … narrowest command … do NOT hunt a green suite | identical, verbatim |","-| (2) SWEPT — the RELATED SITES the search result listed | **SWEPT — grep the distinctive literal once more to enumerate the other sites** |","-| (3) COMPLETE — edge cases the issue names | identical, verbatim |","-| if TWO searches miss, fall back to the shell | if TWO batched searches miss, widen the pattern once |","+Unnumbered bodies are not addressable. To build an `Edit` old_string anchor, a `Read` range, or to","+reason about hunk positions, the agent must re-open the file it was just shown. That is the re-hunt."," ","-**Disclose the one clause that cannot be literal:** SWEPT. eg has a printed RELATED SITES list; the","-shell has none, so the baseline is told how to *produce* the equivalent list. This is the same real","-product difference already disclosed for `base_clamp_prompt` (\"only the baseline is told to Read the","-file\"). It is baseline-favouring in wording (it gets an explicit instruction eg gets for free) and","-must be reported as the one non-literal mirror.","+**The adversarial verifier refuted this as a loser-explanation — correctly — and that refutation is","+irrelevant here.** Its reasoning was: present in 20/20 instances, therefore in 6/6 winners, therefore","+it cannot be what makes an instance *lose*. True. But what this goal needs is **not** a","+loser-differentiator: fixing all 8 losers to exact parity yields only **−23.5%**, short of target.","+It needs a **uniform tax removal that lifts all 20** — and a defect present in 20/20 is precisely the","+right shape for that. I conflated these two questions earlier and dropped a valid lever."," ","-Add `BASE_GATED_CLAMP=1` to the baseline branch of `tool_block`, next to the existing","-`BASE_CLAMP` check at line 1165.","+## Plan"," ","-### 2. Fairness gate — on emitted prompts, before any spend","-Line-diff both arms, paths/digits normalised, and require **exactly one differing hunk** (the tool","-paragraph). Clause table must be 1:1 on: FIRST-action, read-line-range, do-not-re-confirm,","-DISCOVERY-IS-CLAMPED, VERIFIED, SWEPT, COMPLETE, never-stop-merely, TWO-then-fallback. Watch for","-line-wrap false negatives — collapse newlines before matching (this bit me once today).","+### 1. Stop the two failing cells","+Kill CB and GC. Both breach the gates I pre-registered; the sub-400k regime cannot reach −25% at any","+achievable ops reduction."," ","-### 3. Run on Opus — 40 sessions, same 20 instances","-`PROMPT_FAMILY=vendor BASE_GATED_CLAMP=1 EG_GATED_CLAMP=1`, no prefetch, `GQ_SEARCH_CAP=0`,","-`CC_MAX_TURNS=120 CC_TIMEOUT=3600`, binary `/tmp/eg-f19`, fresh `--cache-dir`, and the per-instance","-cache isolation already built into `/tmp/mcptest/s1worker.sh` (`GOMODCACHE`, `GOPATH`, `GOCACHE`,","-`COMPOSER_HOME`, `CARGO_HOME`, `GEM_HOME`, `npm_config_cache`, `maven.repo.local`).","+### 2. Product change: number the body lines","+`eg-consolidated`, the search render path (`internal/sem/` — the body printer that emits ranked-hit","+bodies beneath the `N. path:START-END score= symbol=` header):","+- prefix every printed body line with its real line number (the header already carries the span, so","+  this is 5–6 chars/line);","+- set `focus=` to the matched **interior** line rather than collapsing to the definition line."," ","-### 4. Two leading indicators, both free, both checkable at ~8 pairs","-| indicator | required | why |","-|---|---|---|","-| **baseline total ops** | **≥ 20** | if the gate clamps finishing too, the session collapses to ~4 ops and the 10% payload tax returns — the S1O failure mode. Kill the cell. |","-| **eg pre-edit vs baseline** | **≤ −25%** | PUB is +9%; every cell reaching ≤−25% tokens had pre-edit ≤−28%. Without this the ops ratio cannot get there. |","+This makes the prompt's existing promise true. It is a rendering change only — no ranking, no","+retrieval, no selection. The baseline has no payload, so arm symmetry is untouched."," ","-If either fails at 8 pairs, stop — do not pay for 40 sessions to confirm a known failure mode.","+### 3. Emulate all 20 offline before spending — free","+Recorded queries in `results/PUB_r1_eg/eg/<inst>/prefetch_calls.log`, worktrees in","+`replay-wt/<inst>`, patched binary, **fresh `--cache-dir`** (the index cache is tree-keyed, not","+binary-keyed — reuse it and you get the old binary's answer).","+Assert per instance: every body line numbered; the numbers match the file at that path; `focus=` lands","+inside the body; and **byte-identical output outside the body lines** (no ranking drift). Any","+instance failing the last check blocks the cell."," ","-### 5. Pre-registered","-- Success = geomean ≤ −25% with CI upper bound < 0.","-- Required shape: baseline ops ≈ 25–35, eg ops ≈ 18–25, i.e. ops ratio ≈ −28% at long-session","-  amortisation (~3% tax) → tokens ≈ −25%.","-- Falsification: if ops fall ≥28% and tokens still miss −25%, the payload tax does not amortise the","-  way PUB implies, and **−25% on Opus is unreachable** — that would be the sixth independent","-  configuration and I will report the ceiling instead of running a seventh.","-- Replicate with a second independent cell before any claim. Today's n≤4 signals reversed","-  repeatedly, including on this very config family an hour ago.","+### 4. Run PUB + numbered bodies — 40 sessions, same 20 instances","+Everything else exactly as the −11.2% cell: `PUBLISHED_EXACT=1`, prefetch + impact on, cap 120,","+`CC_TIMEOUT=3600`, plus the per-instance cache isolation already built into the workers","+(`GOMODCACHE`, `GOPATH`, `GOCACHE`, `COMPOSER_HOME`, `CARGO_HOME`, `GEM_HOME`, `npm_config_cache`,","+`maven.repo.local`) — the one confirmed integrity defect, where caddy's baseline read the gold line","+out of the module cache and carbon's eg arm read the gold regex out of the composer cache."," ","+### 5. Leading indicators — free, checkable at ~8 pairs","+| indicator | current | required |","+|---|---|---|","+| session size | 2729k | **stays > 2000k** (if it collapses, the tax returns and the cell is void) |","+| eg pre-edit locate | +9% | **≤ 0%** |","+| post-edit \"re-finds payload text\" | 5.58 / 7.25 per session | **≤ 4.0** |","+| ops Δ | −11.2% | **≤ −20%** |","+Kill the cell if session size collapses or ops Δ has not passed −18% by 8 pairs.","+","+### 6. Pre-registered","+- Success = geomean ≤ −25%, CI upper bound < 0.","+- Required shape: eg ops ≈ 27 against baseline ≈ 36, at ~2700k session size.","+- **Falsification:** if bodies are numbered, re-hunts fall, ops reach ≤ −20%, and tokens still miss","+  −25%, then the ops↔tokens identity that holds at PUB length is wrong and **−25% on Opus is","+  unreachable**. That is the seventh configuration and I will report the ceiling.","+- Replicate with a second independent cell before claiming. Today's n≤4 signals reversed repeatedly.","+"," ## Verification"," - `tools/model_cmp.py`: geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI, cost classes separately."," - Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped symmetrically.","-- `CENSORED` (`error_max_turns`) = 0 per arm.","-- Report ops (pre/post/build) beside tokens every update — ops predicted tokens within 3pt in the","-  long-session cells and is the cheap early read.","-- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config. Eleven silent plumbing failures today; the worst was a","-  flag checked in one dispatcher but not the one every cell uses.","+- `CENSORED` (`error_max_turns`) = 0 per arm — the baseline averages 50.2 turns, so a 50-cap censors","+  the baseline specifically.","+- Report ops (pre/post/build) beside tokens in every update; at PUB length ops predicted tokens to","+  within 0.0 points, so it is the cheap early read.","+- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config. Twelve silent plumbing failures today — the latest being","+  `BASE_GATED_CLAMP` wired into one dispatcher but not the one the vendor family uses, caught only","+  because the fairness gate compared emitted prompts."," "," ## Files","-- `tools/run_3arm.sh` — add `base_gated_clamp_prompt()` near line 859; wire `BASE_GATED_CLAMP` in the","-  baseline branch near line 1165. `gated_clamp_eg_prompt` and the vendor-family assembly already exist.","-- `/tmp/mcptest/gcworker.sh` (new) — copy of `s1worker.sh` with the two clamp flags swapped in.","-- **No product change.** `eg-consolidated` stays clean at HEAD `024f25a`; all 27 payload-defect","-  hypotheses that would have motivated one were refuted on winner-control.","+- `eg-consolidated/internal/sem/` — the ranked-hit body renderer. Only product change. Add a","+  regression test asserting numbered bodies and unchanged surrounding output.","+- `/tmp/mcptest/pubworker.sh` — the −11.2% config; point at the rebuilt binary, keep everything else.","+- `tools/model_cmp.py` — scorer, unchanged.","+- No prompt changes: the prompt already claims numbered lines, so this makes it honest rather than","+  altering the contract."," "," ## Honest expectation","-This is the last untried config shape, and it is the only one that targets both required conditions","-rather than one. The mechanism is specific: clamp discovery to cut pre-edit, mandate finishing to keep","-the session long enough that the payload costs 3% rather than 10%.","+This is the first plan built on a fitted quantitative model rather than a mechanism story: the six","+measured configs give tax-vs-session-size, that fixes the viable regime to PUB, and the op budget then","+names the exact 4.9 ops to remove. The lever is a real defect (0 numbered lines in 20/20, against a","+prompt that promises them) whose measured footprint (5.58–7.25 ops/session) is the right size to close","+the gap."," ","-Against it: the clamp's own wording has collapsed the session in both cells that used it, and CB shows","-an appended scaffold does not prevent that. The gated clamp puts the finishing mandate *inside* the","-clamp, which is why it might behave differently — but \"might\" is the honest word. I put this at","-**−15% to −28%**, and I will report the ceiling rather than run a seventh cell if it misses.","+Two ways it can fail honestly. The re-hunts may not be *caused* by the missing line numbers — the","+agent may re-read regardless, which would show up as ops not moving. And removing pre-edit's +1.2","+deficit has no mechanism attached at all; I am counting it in the arithmetic but I cannot make it","+happen, so the realistic band is **−18% to −26%** with the goal at the top of it."]}],"originalFile":"# Opus to −25%: the gated clamp, made symmetric\n\n## Context\n\nGoal: Opus ≥ −25% tokens on the 20-instance official-300 sample. Five configurations measured today.\nThe complete, fair evidence:\n\n| config | session size | baseline ops | eg ops | ops Δ | **tokens** | n |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| OFF — bare base / rich eg, official | long, 39.0 | 39.0 | 27.5 | −29.6% | −46.5% | 19 — **INVALID, asymmetric** |\n| G40 — rich/rich, official | long, 23.8 | 23.8 | 28.7 | +21.1% | +28.4% | 19 |\n| **PUB — published prompt, capability** | **long, 35.7** | 35.7 | 31.7 | −11.2% | **−11.2%** | 20 |\n| S1O — S1 clamp, no scaffold | **short, 4.6** | 4.6 | 4.3 | −8.0% | **+18.2%** [+2.3,+37.2] | 19 |\n| FRUGAL — rich/rich, frugal shared | short, 7.0 | 7.0 | 5.0 | −28.6% | −14.0% | 23 |\n| CB — clamp + scaffold | short, 4.0 | 4.0 | 1.0 | −75% | −24.9% | **1, in flight** |\n\n### The governing relation, measured\n\n**tokens ≈ ops ratio + payload tax**, and the payload tax depends only on session size:\n~**10%** at a 175k-token session (S1O: −8.0% ops → +18.2% tokens), ~**3%** at a 2.4M-token session\n(PUB: −11.2% ops → −11.2% tokens).\n\nSo −25% requires **both** conditions at once:\n- **ops ratio ≤ −28%**, and\n- **a long session**, so the payload amortises to ~3%.\n\nNo config has achieved both. PUB is long but cuts only 11% of ops — because its eg pre-edit locate\n*rises* (13.4 → 14.6, +9%). The clamp cells cut ops but collapse the session to 4–7 ops, where the\n10% tax eats the gain. FRUGAL is the clearest illustration: −28.6% ops became only −14.0% tokens\nbecause the tax took 14 points.\n\n### Why the clamp collapses the session, and what fixes it\n\n`base_clamp_prompt` / `shipped_eg_prompt` clamp *everything* — \"Apply the minimal fix and STOP the\nmoment you can justify it.\" Result: post-edit 0.3 ops, build 0.6 ops. The agent edits and leaves.\nCB tested whether appending the official scaffold would restore length; at n=1 it did **not** (still\n4.0 ops, post-edit and build both zero). **The clamp dominates an appended scaffold.**\n\n`gated_clamp_eg_prompt` already exists and is built for exactly this: it clamps discovery while\nexplicitly mandating completion —\n\n> DISCOVERY IS CLAMPED — FINISHING IS NOT. Before you stop, all three must be true:\n> (1) **VERIFIED** — you compiled the change or ran the nearest existing test at least ONCE …\n> (2) **SWEPT** — you checked the RELATED SITES the search result listed … and fixed every one …\n> (3) **COMPLETE** — you handled the edge cases the issue names …\n> Never stop merely because you have made an edit — stop when (1), (2) and (3) hold.\n\nThat is the only construct in the harness that cuts pre-edit *without* cutting the phases that make\na session long. **It has never been run, because it fails the fairness gate:** I checked, and\n`base_clamp_prompt()` is the *only* baseline-side block — there is no mirror, so eg would get\nVERIFIED/SWEPT/COMPLETE and the baseline nothing.\n\n## Plan\n\n### 1. Write `base_gated_clamp_prompt()` — the missing mirror\nIn `tools/run_3arm.sh`, beside `base_clamp_prompt()` (line 859). Clause-for-clause mirror of\n`gated_clamp_eg_prompt`, shell-worded:\n\n| eg clause | baseline mirror |\n|---|---|\n| FIRST action must be ONE search | FIRST action is ONE batched shell search |\n| open the top hit, read a line range, edit | open the best hit, read a line range, edit |\n| do NOT re-search to 'confirm' | do NOT re-grep to 'confirm' |\n| DISCOVERY IS CLAMPED — FINISHING IS NOT | identical, verbatim |\n| (1) VERIFIED … narrowest command … do NOT hunt a green suite | identical, verbatim |\n| (2) SWEPT — the RELATED SITES the search result listed | **SWEPT — grep the distinctive literal once more to enumerate the other sites** |\n| (3) COMPLETE — edge cases the issue names | identical, verbatim |\n| if TWO searches miss, fall back to the shell | if TWO batched searches miss, widen the pattern once |\n\n**Disclose the one clause that cannot be literal:** SWEPT. eg has a printed RELATED SITES list; the\nshell has none, so the baseline is told how to *produce* the equivalent list. This is the same real\nproduct difference already disclosed for `base_clamp_prompt` (\"only the baseline is told to Read the\nfile\"). It is baseline-favouring in wording (it gets an explicit instruction eg gets for free) and\nmust be reported as the one non-literal mirror.\n\nAdd `BASE_GATED_CLAMP=1` to the baseline branch of `tool_block`, next to the existing\n`BASE_CLAMP` check at line 1165.\n\n### 2. Fairness gate — on emitted prompts, before any spend\nLine-diff both arms, paths/digits normalised, and require **exactly one differing hunk** (the tool\nparagraph). Clause table must be 1:1 on: FIRST-action, read-line-range, do-not-re-confirm,\nDISCOVERY-IS-CLAMPED, VERIFIED, SWEPT, COMPLETE, never-stop-merely, TWO-then-fallback. Watch for\nline-wrap false negatives — collapse newlines before matching (this bit me once today).\n\n### 3. Run on Opus — 40 sessions, same 20 instances\n`PROMPT_FAMILY=vendor BASE_GATED_CLAMP=1 EG_GATED_CLAMP=1`, no prefetch, `GQ_SEARCH_CAP=0`,\n`CC_MAX_TURNS=120 CC_TIMEOUT=3600`, binary `/tmp/eg-f19`, fresh `--cache-dir`, and the per-instance\ncache isolation already built into `/tmp/mcptest/s1worker.sh` (`GOMODCACHE`, `GOPATH`, `GOCACHE`,\n`COMPOSER_HOME`, `CARGO_HOME`, `GEM_HOME`, `npm_config_cache`, `maven.repo.local`).\n\n### 4. Two leading indicators, both free, both checkable at ~8 pairs\n| indicator | required | why |\n|---|---|---|\n| **baseline total ops** | **≥ 20** | if the gate clamps finishing too, the session collapses to ~4 ops and the 10% payload tax returns — the S1O failure mode. Kill the cell. |\n| **eg pre-edit vs baseline** | **≤ −25%** | PUB is +9%; every cell reaching ≤−25% tokens had pre-edit ≤−28%. Without this the ops ratio cannot get there. |\n\nIf either fails at 8 pairs, stop — do not pay for 40 sessions to confirm a known failure mode.\n\n### 5. Pre-registered\n- Success = geomean ≤ −25% with CI upper bound < 0.\n- Required shape: baseline ops ≈ 25–35, eg ops ≈ 18–25, i.e. ops ratio ≈ −28% at long-session\n  amortisation (~3% tax) → tokens ≈ −25%.\n- Falsification: if ops fall ≥28% and tokens still miss −25%, the payload tax does not amortise the\n  way PUB implies, and **−25% on Opus is unreachable** — that would be the sixth independent\n  configuration and I will report the ceiling instead of running a seventh.\n- Replicate with a second independent cell before any claim. Today's n≤4 signals reversed\n  repeatedly, including on this very config family an hour ago.\n\n## Verification\n- `tools/model_cmp.py`: geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI, cost classes separately.\n- Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped symmetrically.\n- `CENSORED` (`error_max_turns`) = 0 per arm.\n- Report ops (pre/post/build) beside tokens every update — ops predicted tokens within 3pt in the\n  long-session cells and is the cheap early read.\n- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config. Eleven silent plumbing failures today; the worst was a\n  flag checked in one dispatcher but not the one every cell uses.\n\n## Files\n- `tools/run_3arm.sh` — add `base_gated_clamp_prompt()` near line 859; wire `BASE_GATED_CLAMP` in the\n  baseline branch near line 1165. `gated_clamp_eg_prompt` and the vendor-family assembly already exist.\n- `/tmp/mcptest/gcworker.sh` (new) — copy of `s1worker.sh` with the two clamp flags swapped in.\n- **No product change.** `eg-consolidated` stays clean at HEAD `024f25a`; all 27 payload-defect\n  hypotheses that would have motivated one were refuted on winner-control.\n\n## Honest expectation\nThis is the last untried config shape, and it is the only one that targets both required conditions\nrather than one. The mechanism is specific: clamp discovery to cut pre-edit, mandate finishing to keep\nthe session long enough that the payload costs 3% rather than 10%.\n\nAgainst it: the clamp's own wording has collapsed the session in both cells that used it, and CB shows\nan appended scaffold does not prevent that. The gated clamp puts the finishing mandate *inside* the\nclamp, which is why it might behave differently — but \"might\" is the honest word. I put this at\n**−15% to −28%**, and I will report the ceiling rather than run a seventh cell if it misses.\n","userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8a6388b0-ad1c-46b2-bc3c-13127e365f9f","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"type":"last-prompt","lastPrompt":"make a plan and meet ur damn goal","leafUuid":"5d0e4873-fff5-4a2d-83a0-f447924b8585","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208"}
{"type":"ai-title","aiTitle":"opus-token-optimization-testing","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208"}
{"type":"agent-name","agentName":"opus-token-optimization-testing","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208"}
{"type":"mode","mode":"normal","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208"}
