{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","prNumber":71,"prUrl":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/71","prRepository":"entireio/entire-graph","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:51:52.696Z"}
{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01P6EtEZrtka8BvMWBZeka4V","lastSequenceNum":0}
{"parentUuid":"5d0e4873-fff5-4a2d-83a0-f447924b8585","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgKUPDeymYCUTtprvhBp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Kk8oQy9kP8YE3cGuaCRVdR","name":"ExitPlanMode","input":{"plan":"# Opus to −25%: make the payload addressable, in the long-session regime\n\n## Context\n\nGoal: Opus ≥ −25% tokens on the 20-instance official-300 sample. Six configurations are now measured.\nFitting them together gives a quantitative model that says exactly where the goal is reachable — and\nit is not where I have been spending.\n\n| config | baseline ops | ops Δ | ktok/session | tokens | **penalty** (tokens−ops) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **PUB** — published prompt, prefetch | 35.7 | −11.2% | **2729k** | **−11.2%** | **+0.0** |\n| G40 — rich methodology both arms | 23.8 | +21.1% | 1300k | +28.4% | +7.3 |\n| GC — gated clamp (symmetric) | 11.5 | +4.3% | 378k | +22.2% | +17.9 |\n| CB — clamp + scaffold | 10.5 | −20.6% | 345k | +7.5% | +28.1 |\n| FRUGAL — rich both, frugal shared | 7.0 | −28.6% | 279k | −14.0% | +14.6 |\n| S1O — S1 clamp | 4.6 | −8.0% | 175k | +18.2% | +26.2 |\n\n**`tokens ≈ ops Δ + payload tax`, and the tax is a pure function of session size** — 0 at 2729k,\n+7 at 1300k, +18 to +28 below 400k. So:\n\n| regime | ops reduction required for −25% |\n|---|---|\n| **2729k (PUB)** | **−25%** |\n| 1300k | −32% |\n| ~350k | −53% |\n\n**Only the longest regime is viable.** Every clamp config I have run this session sits at 175–378k,\nwhere the tax alone is +18 to +28 points — which is why CB cut 20.6% of ops and still lost, and why\nGC and S1O lost outright. That whole direction is dead, and both live cells are failing their\npre-registered gates right now (baseline ops 10.5 and 11.5 against a required ≥20; GC's pre-edit is\n+40% against a required ≤−25%). **Kill both.**\n\n## Where the 14 points are\n\nPUB's op budget, measured:\n\n| phase | baseline | eg |\n|---|---|---|\n| pre-edit locate | 13.4 | **14.6** (worse) |\n| post-edit locate | 15.5 | 11.8 |\n| build/test | 6.8 | 5.2 |\n| **total** | **35.7** | **31.7 (−11.2%)** |\n\nTarget for −25% ops is 26.8. Two steps get there:\n\n| step | eg total | ops Δ |\n|---|---|---|\n| eg pre-edit merely *matches* the baseline (14.6 → 13.4) | 30.4 | −14.8% |\n| **+ post-edit re-hunts removed (11.8 → 7.1)** | **26.9** | **−24.6%** ✓ |\n\nAt PUB's session size the tax is zero, so −24.6% ops ⇒ **≈ −25% tokens**.\n\n## The mechanism, and why the earlier refutation does not apply\n\nMeasured on this cell:\n- **\"re-finds text the payload already printed\" = 5.58 ops/session (winners), 7.25 (losers)** — about\n  40% of eg's post-edit locate work.\n- **Payload bodies carry ZERO line numbers**: 0 of 55, 0 of 107, 0 of 79 — in **20/20 instances**.\n- The eg prompt promises, verbatim: *\"the complete body of the enclosing function is printed verbatim\n  beneath that header, **at its real line numbers**\"*. The prompt is false.\n\nUnnumbered bodies are not addressable. To build an `Edit` old_string anchor, a `Read` range, or to\nreason about hunk positions, the agent must re-open the file it was just shown. That is the re-hunt.\n\n**The adversarial verifier refuted this as a loser-explanation — correctly — and that refutation is\nirrelevant here.** Its reasoning was: present in 20/20 instances, therefore in 6/6 winners, therefore\nit cannot be what makes an instance *lose*. True. But what this goal needs is **not** a\nloser-differentiator: fixing all 8 losers to exact parity yields only **−23.5%**, short of target.\nIt needs a **uniform tax removal that lifts all 20** — and a defect present in 20/20 is precisely the\nright shape for that. I conflated these two questions earlier and dropped a valid lever.\n\n## Plan\n\n### 1. Stop the two failing cells\nKill CB and GC. Both breach the gates I pre-registered; the sub-400k regime cannot reach −25% at any\nachievable ops reduction.\n\n### 2. Product change: number the body lines\n`eg-consolidated`, the search render path (`internal/sem/` — the body printer that emits ranked-hit\nbodies beneath the `N. path:START-END score= symbol=` header):\n- prefix every printed body line with its real line number (the header already carries the span, so\n  this is 5–6 chars/line);\n- set `focus=` to the matched **interior** line rather than collapsing to the definition line.\n\nThis makes the prompt's existing promise true. It is a rendering change only — no ranking, no\nretrieval, no selection. The baseline has no payload, so arm symmetry is untouched.\n\n### 3. Emulate all 20 offline before spending — free\nRecorded queries in `results/PUB_r1_eg/eg/<inst>/prefetch_calls.log`, worktrees in\n`replay-wt/<inst>`, patched binary, **fresh `--cache-dir`** (the index cache is tree-keyed, not\nbinary-keyed — reuse it and you get the old binary's answer).\nAssert per instance: every body line numbered; the numbers match the file at that path; `focus=` lands\ninside the body; and **byte-identical output outside the body lines** (no ranking drift). Any\ninstance failing the last check blocks the cell.\n\n### 4. Run PUB + numbered bodies — 40 sessions, same 20 instances\nEverything else exactly as the −11.2% cell: `PUBLISHED_EXACT=1`, prefetch + impact on, cap 120,\n`CC_TIMEOUT=3600`, plus the per-instance cache isolation already built into the workers\n(`GOMODCACHE`, `GOPATH`, `GOCACHE`, `COMPOSER_HOME`, `CARGO_HOME`, `GEM_HOME`, `npm_config_cache`,\n`maven.repo.local`) — the one confirmed integrity defect, where caddy's baseline read the gold line\nout of the module cache and carbon's eg arm read the gold regex out of the composer cache.\n\n### 5. Leading indicators — free, checkable at ~8 pairs\n| indicator | current | required |\n|---|---|---|\n| session size | 2729k | **stays > 2000k** (if it collapses, the tax returns and the cell is void) |\n| eg pre-edit locate | +9% | **≤ 0%** |\n| post-edit \"re-finds payload text\" | 5.58 / 7.25 per session | **≤ 4.0** |\n| ops Δ | −11.2% | **≤ −20%** |\nKill the cell if session size collapses or ops Δ has not passed −18% by 8 pairs.\n\n### 6. Pre-registered\n- Success = geomean ≤ −25%, CI upper bound < 0.\n- Required shape: eg ops ≈ 27 against baseline ≈ 36, at ~2700k session size.\n- **Falsification:** if bodies are numbered, re-hunts fall, ops reach ≤ −20%, and tokens still miss\n  −25%, then the ops↔tokens identity that holds at PUB length is wrong and **−25% on Opus is\n  unreachable**. That is the seventh configuration and I will report the ceiling.\n- Replicate with a second independent cell before claiming. Today's n≤4 signals reversed repeatedly.\n\n## Verification\n- `tools/model_cmp.py`: geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI, cost classes separately.\n- Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped symmetrically.\n- `CENSORED` (`error_max_turns`) = 0 per arm — the baseline averages 50.2 turns, so a 50-cap censors\n  the baseline specifically.\n- Report ops (pre/post/build) beside tokens in every update; at PUB length ops predicted tokens to\n  within 0.0 points, so it is the cheap early read.\n- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config. Twelve silent plumbing failures today — the latest being\n  `BASE_GATED_CLAMP` wired into one dispatcher but not the one the vendor family uses, caught only\n  because the fairness gate compared emitted prompts.\n\n## Files\n- `eg-consolidated/internal/sem/` — the ranked-hit body renderer. Only product change. Add a\n  regression test asserting numbered bodies and unchanged surrounding output.\n- `/tmp/mcptest/pubworker.sh` — the −11.2% config; point at the rebuilt binary, keep everything else.\n- `tools/model_cmp.py` — scorer, unchanged.\n- No prompt changes: the prompt already claims numbered lines, so this makes it honest rather than\n  altering the contract.\n\n## Honest expectation\nThis is the first plan built on a fitted quantitative model rather than a mechanism story: the six\nmeasured configs give tax-vs-session-size, that fixes the viable regime to PUB, and the op budget then\nnames the exact 4.9 ops to remove. The lever is a real defect (0 numbered lines in 20/20, against a\nprompt that promises them) whose measured footprint (5.58–7.25 ops/session) is the right size to close\nthe gap.\n\nTwo ways it can fail honestly. The re-hunts may not be *caused* by the missing line numbers — the\nagent may re-read regardless, which would show up as ops not moving. And removing pre-edit's +1.2\ndeficit has no mechanism attached at all; I am counting it in the arithmetic but I cannot make it\nhappen, so the realistic band is **−18% to −26%** with the goal at the top of it.\n","planFilePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/modular-cooking-cupcake.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4524,"cache_read_input_tokens":603531,"output_tokens":31,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4524,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":31,"cache_read_input_tokens":603531,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4524,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4524},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgKUGcHNZdcTKMrDmETQ","type":"assistant","uuid":"ab578ed4-0a28-41aa-b29e-41002dead213","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:51:57.667Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"ab578ed4-0a28-41aa-b29e-41002dead213","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4cfad49e-246c-49ef-b5bd-807cc83b7bba","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"User has approved your plan. You can now start coding. Start with updating your todo list if applicable\n\nYour plan has been saved to: /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/modular-cooking-cupcake.md\nYou can refer back to it if needed during implementation.\n\n## Approved Plan:\n# Opus to −25%: make the payload addressable, in the long-session regime\n\n## Context\n\nGoal: Opus ≥ −25% tokens on the 20-instance official-300 sample. Six configurations are now measured.\nFitting them together gives a quantitative model that says exactly where the goal is reachable — and\nit is not where I have been spending.\n\n| config | baseline ops | ops Δ | ktok/session | tokens | **penalty** (tokens−ops) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **PUB** — published prompt, prefetch | 35.7 | −11.2% | **2729k** | **−11.2%** | **+0.0** |\n| G40 — rich methodology both arms | 23.8 | +21.1% | 1300k | +28.4% | +7.3 |\n| GC — gated clamp (symmetric) | 11.5 | +4.3% | 378k | +22.2% | +17.9 |\n| CB — clamp + scaffold | 10.5 | −20.6% | 345k | +7.5% | +28.1 |\n| FRUGAL — rich both, frugal shared | 7.0 | −28.6% | 279k | −14.0% | +14.6 |\n| S1O — S1 clamp | 4.6 | −8.0% | 175k | +18.2% | +26.2 |\n\n**`tokens ≈ ops Δ + payload tax`, and the tax is a pure function of session size** — 0 at 2729k,\n+7 at 1300k, +18 to +28 below 400k. So:\n\n| regime | ops reduction required for −25% |\n|---|---|\n| **2729k (PUB)** | **−25%** |\n| 1300k | −32% |\n| ~350k | −53% |\n\n**Only the longest regime is viable.** Every clamp config I have run this session sits at 175–378k,\nwhere the tax alone is +18 to +28 points — which is why CB cut 20.6% of ops and still lost, and why\nGC and S1O lost outright. That whole direction is dead, and both live cells are failing their\npre-registered gates right now (baseline ops 10.5 and 11.5 against a required ≥20; GC's pre-edit is\n+40% against a required ≤−25%). **Kill both.**\n\n## Where the 14 points are\n\nPUB's op budget, measured:\n\n| phase | baseline | eg |\n|---|---|---|\n| pre-edit locate | 13.4 | **14.6** (worse) |\n| post-edit locate | 15.5 | 11.8 |\n| build/test | 6.8 | 5.2 |\n| **total** | **35.7** | **31.7 (−11.2%)** |\n\nTarget for −25% ops is 26.8. Two steps get there:\n\n| step | eg total | ops Δ |\n|---|---|---|\n| eg pre-edit merely *matches* the baseline (14.6 → 13.4) | 30.4 | −14.8% |\n| **+ post-edit re-hunts removed (11.8 → 7.1)** | **26.9** | **−24.6%** ✓ |\n\nAt PUB's session size the tax is zero, so −24.6% ops ⇒ **≈ −25% tokens**.\n\n## The mechanism, and why the earlier refutation does not apply\n\nMeasured on this cell:\n- **\"re-finds text the payload already printed\" = 5.58 ops/session (winners), 7.25 (losers)** — about\n  40% of eg's post-edit locate work.\n- **Payload bodies carry ZERO line numbers**: 0 of 55, 0 of 107, 0 of 79 — in **20/20 instances**.\n- The eg prompt promises, verbatim: *\"the complete body of the enclosing function is printed verbatim\n  beneath that header, **at its real line numbers**\"*. The prompt is false.\n\nUnnumbered bodies are not addressable. To build an `Edit` old_string anchor, a `Read` range, or to\nreason about hunk positions, the agent must re-open the file it was just shown. That is the re-hunt.\n\n**The adversarial verifier refuted this as a loser-explanation — correctly — and that refutation is\nirrelevant here.** Its reasoning was: present in 20/20 instances, therefore in 6/6 winners, therefore\nit cannot be what makes an instance *lose*. True. But what this goal needs is **not** a\nloser-differentiator: fixing all 8 losers to exact parity yields only **−23.5%**, short of target.\nIt needs a **uniform tax removal that lifts all 20** — and a defect present in 20/20 is precisely the\nright shape for that. I conflated these two questions earlier and dropped a valid lever.\n\n## Plan\n\n### 1. Stop the two failing cells\nKill CB and GC. Both breach the gates I pre-registered; the sub-400k regime cannot reach −25% at any\nachievable ops reduction.\n\n### 2. Product change: number the body lines\n`eg-consolidated`, the search render path (`internal/sem/` — the body printer that emits ranked-hit\nbodies beneath the `N. path:START-END score= symbol=` header):\n- prefix every printed body line with its real line number (the header already carries the span, so\n  this is 5–6 chars/line);\n- set `focus=` to the matched **interior** line rather than collapsing to the definition line.\n\nThis makes the prompt's existing promise true. It is a rendering change only — no ranking, no\nretrieval, no selection. The baseline has no payload, so arm symmetry is untouched.\n\n### 3. Emulate all 20 offline before spending — free\nRecorded queries in `results/PUB_r1_eg/eg/<inst>/prefetch_calls.log`, worktrees in\n`replay-wt/<inst>`, patched binary, **fresh `--cache-dir`** (the index cache is tree-keyed, not\nbinary-keyed — reuse it and you get the old binary's answer).\nAssert per instance: every body line numbered; the numbers match the file at that path; `focus=` lands\ninside the body; and **byte-identical output outside the body lines** (no ranking drift). Any\ninstance failing the last check blocks the cell.\n\n### 4. Run PUB + numbered bodies — 40 sessions, same 20 instances\nEverything else exactly as the −11.2% cell: `PUBLISHED_EXACT=1`, prefetch + impact on, cap 120,\n`CC_TIMEOUT=3600`, plus the per-instance cache isolation already built into the workers\n(`GOMODCACHE`, `GOPATH`, `GOCACHE`, `COMPOSER_HOME`, `CARGO_HOME`, `GEM_HOME`, `npm_config_cache`,\n`maven.repo.local`) — the one confirmed integrity defect, where caddy's baseline read the gold line\nout of the module cache and carbon's eg arm read the gold regex out of the composer cache.\n\n### 5. Leading indicators — free, checkable at ~8 pairs\n| indicator | current | required |\n|---|---|---|\n| session size | 2729k | **stays > 2000k** (if it collapses, the tax returns and the cell is void) |\n| eg pre-edit locate | +9% | **≤ 0%** |\n| post-edit \"re-finds payload text\" | 5.58 / 7.25 per session | **≤ 4.0** |\n| ops Δ | −11.2% | **≤ −20%** |\nKill the cell if session size collapses or ops Δ has not passed −18% by 8 pairs.\n\n### 6. Pre-registered\n- Success = geomean ≤ −25%, CI upper bound < 0.\n- Required shape: eg ops ≈ 27 against baseline ≈ 36, at ~2700k session size.\n- **Falsification:** if bodies are numbered, re-hunts fall, ops reach ≤ −20%, and tokens still miss\n  −25%, then the ops↔tokens identity that holds at PUB length is wrong and **−25% on Opus is\n  unreachable**. That is the seventh configuration and I will report the ceiling.\n- Replicate with a second independent cell before claiming. Today's n≤4 signals reversed repeatedly.\n\n## Verification\n- `tools/model_cmp.py`: geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI, cost classes separately.\n- Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped symmetrically.\n- `CENSORED` (`error_max_turns`) = 0 per arm — the baseline averages 50.2 turns, so a 50-cap censors\n  the baseline specifically.\n- Report ops (pre/post/build) beside tokens in every update; at PUB length ops predicted tokens to\n  within 0.0 points, so it is the cheap early read.\n- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config. Twelve silent plumbing failures today — the latest being\n  `BASE_GATED_CLAMP` wired into one dispatcher but not the one the vendor family uses, caught only\n  because the fairness gate compared emitted prompts.\n\n## Files\n- `eg-consolidated/internal/sem/` — the ranked-hit body renderer. Only product change. Add a\n  regression test asserting numbered bodies and unchanged surrounding output.\n- `/tmp/mcptest/pubworker.sh` — the −11.2% config; point at the rebuilt binary, keep everything else.\n- `tools/model_cmp.py` — scorer, unchanged.\n- No prompt changes: the prompt already claims numbered lines, so this makes it honest rather than\n  altering the contract.\n\n## Honest expectation\nThis is the first plan built on a fitted quantitative model rather than a mechanism story: the six\nmeasured configs give tax-vs-session-size, that fixes the viable regime to PUB, and the op budget then\nnames the exact 4.9 ops to remove. The lever is a real defect (0 numbered lines in 20/20, against a\nprompt that promises them) whose measured footprint (5.58–7.25 ops/session) is the right size to close\nthe gap.\n\nTwo ways it can fail honestly. The re-hunts may not be *caused* by the missing line numbers — the\nagent may re-read regardless, which would show up as ops not moving. And removing pre-edit's +1.2\ndeficit has no mechanism attached at all; I am counting it in the arithmetic but I cannot make it\nhappen, so the realistic band is **−18% to −26%** with the goal at the top of it.\n","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kk8oQy9kP8YE3cGuaCRVdR"}]},"uuid":"6d0da2e7-be9a-454a-a9a3-4d860fb3608c","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:52:44.843Z","toolUseResult":{"plan":"# Opus to −25%: make the payload addressable, in the long-session regime\n\n## Context\n\nGoal: Opus ≥ −25% tokens on the 20-instance official-300 sample. Six configurations are now measured.\nFitting them together gives a quantitative model that says exactly where the goal is reachable — and\nit is not where I have been spending.\n\n| config | baseline ops | ops Δ | ktok/session | tokens | **penalty** (tokens−ops) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **PUB** — published prompt, prefetch | 35.7 | −11.2% | **2729k** | **−11.2%** | **+0.0** |\n| G40 — rich methodology both arms | 23.8 | +21.1% | 1300k | +28.4% | +7.3 |\n| GC — gated clamp (symmetric) | 11.5 | +4.3% | 378k | +22.2% | +17.9 |\n| CB — clamp + scaffold | 10.5 | −20.6% | 345k | +7.5% | +28.1 |\n| FRUGAL — rich both, frugal shared | 7.0 | −28.6% | 279k | −14.0% | +14.6 |\n| S1O — S1 clamp | 4.6 | −8.0% | 175k | +18.2% | +26.2 |\n\n**`tokens ≈ ops Δ + payload tax`, and the tax is a 