ly as the −11.2% cell: `PUBLISHED_EXACT=1`, prefetch + impact on, cap 120,\n`CC_TIMEOUT=3600`, plus the per-instance cache isolation already built into the workers\n(`GOMODCACHE`, `GOPATH`, `GOCACHE`, `COMPOSER_HOME`, `CARGO_HOME`, `GEM_HOME`, `npm_config_cache`,\n`maven.repo.local`) — the one confirmed integrity defect, where caddy's baseline read the gold line\nout of the module cache and carbon's eg arm read the gold regex out of the composer cache.\n\n### 5. Leading indicators — free, checkable at ~8 pairs\n| indicator | current | required |\n|---|---|---|\n| session size | 2729k | **stays > 2000k** (if it collapses, the tax returns and the cell is void) |\n| eg pre-edit locate | +9% | **≤ 0%** |\n| post-edit \"re-finds payload text\" | 5.58 / 7.25 per session | **≤ 4.0** |\n| ops Δ | −11.2% | **≤ −20%** |\nKill the cell if session size collapses or ops Δ has not passed −18% by 8 pairs.\n\n### 6. Pre-registered\n- Success = geomean ≤ −25%, CI upper bound < 0.\n- Required shape: eg ops ≈ 27 against baseline ≈ 36, at ~2700k session size.\n- **Falsification:** if bodies are numbered, re-hunts fall, ops reach ≤ −20%, and tokens still miss\n  −25%, then the ops↔tokens identity that holds at PUB length is wrong and **−25% on Opus is\n  unreachable**. That is the seventh configuration and I will report the ceiling.\n- Replicate with a second independent cell before claiming. Today's n≤4 signals reversed repeatedly.\n\n## Verification\n- `tools/model_cmp.py`: geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI, cost classes separately.\n- Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped symmetrically.\n- `CENSORED` (`error_max_turns`) = 0 per arm — the baseline averages 50.2 turns, so a 50-cap censors\n  the baseline specifically.\n- Report ops (pre/post/build) beside tokens in every update; at PUB length ops predicted tokens to\n  within 0.0 points, so it is the cheap early read.\n- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config. Twelve silent plumbing failures today — the latest being\n  `BASE_GATED_CLAMP` wired into one dispatcher but not the one the vendor family uses, caught only\n  because the fairness gate compared emitted prompts.\n\n## Files\n- `eg-consolidated/internal/sem/` — the ranked-hit body renderer. Only product change. Add a\n  regression test asserting numbered bodies and unchanged surrounding output.\n- `/tmp/mcptest/pubworker.sh` — the −11.2% config; point at the rebuilt binary, keep everything else.\n- `tools/model_cmp.py` — scorer, unchanged.\n- No prompt changes: the prompt already claims numbered lines, so this makes it honest rather than\n  altering the contract.\n\n## Honest expectation\nThis is the first plan built on a fitted quantitative model rather than a mechanism story: the six\nmeasured configs give tax-vs-session-size, that fixes the viable regime to PUB, and the op budget then\nnames the exact 4.9 ops to remove. The lever is a real defect (0 numbered lines in 20/20, against a\nprompt that promises them) whose measured footprint (5.58–7.25 ops/session) is the right size to close\nthe gap.\n\nTwo ways it can fail honestly. The re-hunts may not be *caused* by the missing line numbers — the\nagent may re-read regardless, which would show up as ops not moving. And removing pre-edit's +1.2\ndeficit has no mechanism attached at all; I am counting it in the arithmetic but I cannot make it\nhappen, so the realistic band is **−18% to −26%** with the goal at the top of it.\n","isAgent":false,"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/modular-cooking-cupcake.md"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ab578ed4-0a28-41aa-b29e-41002dead213","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
