{"parentUuid":"001403b5-6080-46cf-af53-0927b1c82036","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgKeGNRYdasHzT7kGnzo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3953,"cache_read_input_tokens":614561,"output_tokens":2114,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3953,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2114,"cache_read_input_tokens":614561,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3953,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3953},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgKeBL4aU5Xtf1cQVH5k","type":"assistant","uuid":"a530fba6-c624-4aee-bc64-a750416650d0","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:54:27.471Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"a530fba6-c624-4aee-bc64-a750416650d0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgKeGNRYdasHzT7kGnzo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That kills the line-number plan, and cleanly:\n\n| eg post-edit operation | per session | share |\n|---|---|---|\n| **grep for a symbol the payload already named** | **6.85** | **57.8%** |\n| grep for something else | 3.35 | 28.3% |\n| read a file the payload already printed | **0.60** | **5.1%** |\n| read something else | 1.05 | 8.9% |\n\nLine-numbering the bodies would address the **0.60** — 5% of post-edit work — while the codebase explicitly documents that it breaks `Edit` anchors, and `focus=` (the prior fix for that same 5%) is already in the binary the −11.2% cell ran on. So my plan's central lever was aimed at the wrong 5%, and I'm not shipping it.\n\nThe actual mass is **6.85 greps per session for symbols the payload already named** — 58% of post-edit ops. Those aren't addressability questions (\"where is X\" — the payload said). They're **breadth** questions: *where else is X used, what else needs the same change*. The agent asks them after editing, and it asks the shell, not the graph.\n\nThat reframes the target with the right arithmetic:\n\n| if pre-answered | post-edit ops | total ops | ops Δ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| current | 11.8 | 31.7 | −11.2% |\n| half of the 6.85 | 8.4 | 28.2 | −21% |\n| most of the 6.85 | 6.8 | 26.6 | **−25.5%** ✓ |\n\nSo the lever is correctly sized — and it's the one thing the tool is uniquely built to answer, via `callers` / `impact` / `grep` and the RELATED SITES and SAME-CONCEPT LITERAL blocks. The payload already carries those blocks, and the agent greps anyway 6.85 times, which means they're either wrong or distrusted. The catastrophe workflow independently found both failure modes in them: `SAME-CONCEPT LITERAL` substring-matching without word boundaries (`lpopCommand` matching `blpopCommand`, 3 of 5 sites wrong, 2 mislabelled `EDIT`), and a list that \"claims 2 files, prints 1, and drops the file the issue names\".\n\nI want to flag the counter-evidence honestly before proposing this as the next cell: my own notes record that **every previous payload enrichment raised shell greps and worsened cost**, and that the leanest config had the fewest greps and the best result. So \"add more usage information\" has failed before. The difference this time is that I'd be *correcting* existing blocks rather than adding new ones — but that distinction is a hypothesis, not a measurement.\n\nGoal is not met: the honest Opus number remains **−11.2%** on the published prompt, with six configurations measured and the seventh (numbered bodies) now ruled out on evidence rather than run. The catastrophe workflow is still running and is checking exactly these usage-list defects against the within-instance controls; I'd rather see its verdict than spend 40 sessions on a lever my own notes say has failed three times."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3953,"cache_read_input_tokens":614561,"output_tokens":2114,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3953,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2114,"cache_read_input_tokens":614561,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3953,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3953},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgKeBL4aU5Xtf1cQVH5k","type":"assistant","uuid":"a9187d92-ce43-4393-a1be-13f598c712df","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:54:40.460Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","versio