{"parentUuid":"ae519c7e-dffd-4fb6-be4a-32c818ae8596","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgKiCpy9po86yQL4ZgVb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Update — nothing is running; the catastrophe workflow is mid-investigation.**\n\n| | state |\n|---|---|\n| load / launchers | 0 / 0 — CB and GC killed for breaching their gates |\n| catastrophe workflow | 5 investigators started, **0 of 5 returned** |\n| Opus best fair number | **−11.2%** [−27.8, +9.6], n=20, published prompt |\n\nSince the last update I did one thing and it was worth doing: I killed my own plan before spending on it.\n\nThe plan was to line-number the payload bodies, on the theory that unaddressable bodies force re-reads. Two independent checks refuted it:\n\n- The renderer at `internal/cli/search.go:473` carries an explicit warning that decorating body lines **breaks `Edit` anchors** — agents copy snippet text verbatim as `old_string`, so numbers in the body turn a navigation aid into a failed patch. And `focus=`, the prior fix for that same problem, is already in the binary the −11.2% cell ran on.\n- Classifying eg's post-edit operations showed the target was the wrong 5%: **reads of a payload file are 0.60/session**, while **greps for a symbol the payload already named are 6.85/session (57.8%)**.\n\nSo the real mass is breadth questions after editing — *where else is this symbol used* — asked of the shell rather than the graph, 6.85 times a session. That's correctly sized to close the gap (pre-answering most of them puts ops at −25.5%), and it's the one thing the tool is uniquely built for. It's also the thing my notes say has failed three times as \"payload enrichment\", which is why I want the workflow's within-instance verdicts on the specific usage-list defects it found — substring-matched literals, truncated file lists — before spending another 40 sessions.\n\nWhere the goal stands, plainly: **not met.** Seven configurations now assessed, six by measurement and one refuted on evidence before running. The ops↔tokens model is solid and says −25% needs a −25% op cut at long session length; the only lever left of the right size is the post-edit breadth question, and its evidence is pending."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":873,"cache_read_input_tokens":620631,"output_tokens":703,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":873,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":703,"cache_read_input_tokens":620631,"cache_creation_input_tokens":873,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":873},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgKi5jKxkvFLEF6K6fWh","type":"assistant","uuid":"c1757fd6-3435-4b7a-9916-c36103891cad","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:55:14.750Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
