{"parentUuid":"9c8e7b91-85a2-499c-adfc-855ada2c8a29","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgL4eim4vqgBZU8dvwCZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2109,"cache_read_input_tokens":622278,"output_tokens":2132,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2109,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2132,"cache_read_input_tokens":622278,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2109,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2109},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgL4Z8AQHQxVtTcWXaGN","type":"assistant","uuid":"e0d37ade-af0b-4191-9488-b17ceaa388f0","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:59:56.576Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"e0d37ade-af0b-4191-9488-b17ceaa388f0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgL4eim4vqgBZU8dvwCZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Update — 3 of 5 investigators returned, 13 findings, and two of them undermine the headline number itself.**\n\n**Answer leaks in the eg arm of the PUB cell — the one I've been quoting as −11.2%:**\n\n| instance | leak | its PUB result |\n|---|---|---|\n| docusaurus-10130 | eg **transcribed the gold patch out of a downloaded post-fix npm release** | −38% (winner) |\n| fmt-2457 | eg's `find /` **enumerated fmt 12.2.0 and two prior-benchmark fmtlib checkouts** | −18% (winner) |\n\nBoth are winners, both eg-side. That means my cache isolation (`GOMODCACHE`, `COMPOSER_HOME`, …) is insufficient — it closes package *caches* but not two other channels: **npm/yarn fetching a post-fix release over the network** (netjail blocks `curl`/`wget` but not npm's own HTTP), and **other benchmark checkouts reachable on the same filesystem via `find /`**. Combined with the caddy baseline leak found earlier, that's leaks on both sides of the same cell.\n\n**And the two biggest \"swings\" I built the last plan on are not tool effects:**\n\n- fmt-2457's 179-point swing is **\"132% baseline-side; eg's own cost FALLS from PUB to G40\"** — the baseline changed, not eg.\n- docusaurus's 180-point swing is **\"baseline-side: `yarn install` succeeded in PUB and was never attempted in CB\"** — provisioning luck.\n- hugo's +103% is **\"a denominator artifact: 3 of 4 sessions ran the same allconfig…\"**\n\nSo the within-instance swings I treated as the strongest available signal are mostly the *denominator* moving.\n\n**One genuine defect costing eg ops:** hugo — *\"zsh `=` expansion aborts batched probes: bare `echo ===` killed 2 of eg's batches.\"* A shell-quoting interaction in the harness silently kills batched commands. That's real and fixable.\n\nAnd one independent confirmation of my token model: *\"the same payload defect is free in a 49-msg session and costs 15% in a 5-msg one\"* — exactly the session-size tax.\n\n**Where this leaves the goal.** I can't chase −25% against a baseline that leaks the answer in one arm and a headline that leaks it in the other. The next work is integrity, not optimisation: close the three channels (deny-read sibling checkouts, block package-manager network installs or pre-vendor them, keep the cache isolation), then re-measure PUB. The −11.2% may move in either direction — docusaurus and fmt-2457 are winners whose wins are now suspect, so it could get *worse*.\n\nI'll wait for the last two investigators and the verifiers before acting, since the leak claims need the same adversarial check that killed 27 of 28 findings last round."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2109,"cache_read_input_tokens":622278,"output_tokens":2132,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2109,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2132,"cache_read_input_tokens":622278,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2109,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2109},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgL4Z8AQHQxVtTcWXaGN","type":"assistant","uuid":"3b200464-2c16-4d1f-95b3-82daf0ba045a","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:00:08.268Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
