{"parentUuid":"9286e612-b199-4650-89bc-0da6e3b3fa30","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgLGmSQsyz1ujHDCUbJX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2728,"cache_read_input_tokens":626557,"output_tokens":1316,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2728,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1316,"cache_read_input_tokens":626557,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2728,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2728},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgLGgZiT7YexHDBeBrmU","type":"assistant","uuid":"7399bfae-ba25-4e51-a7e2-60d3c56f3906","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:02:33.102Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"7399bfae-ba25-4e51-a7e2-60d3c56f3906","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgLGmSQsyz1ujHDCUbJX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Ran it. It doesn't get there, and the fair version of it goes backwards:\n\n| adjustment | n | geomean |\n|---|---|---|\n| raw headline | 20 | **−11.2%** |\n| median instance | 20 | −16.1% |\n| **winsorize carbon (+107%) to the median** | 20 | **−15.1%** |\n| drop carbon only | 19 | −15.1% |\n| **drop all leak-contaminated instances, by rule** | 16 | **−9.6%** |\n\nTwo things fall out.\n\n**It doesn't reach the goal.** Winsorizing the one instance above +100% gives **−15.1%**, not −25%. Carbon is a single instance out of twenty, so capping it is worth ~4 points. There is no arrangement of this data that reaches −25% — I showed earlier that even setting *all eight* losers to exact parity only gives −23.5%.\n\n**And the rule can't be applied to just that one.** Carbon qualifies for removal because the forensic sweep found its eg arm read the gold regex out of the composer cache. But three other instances have the same defect — and they're all **winners**: caddy (−56%, baseline read the gold line and the PR's own test fixture), docusaurus (−38%, eg transcribed the gold patch from a post-fix npm release), fmt-2457 (−18%, eg's `find /` enumerated other fmtlib checkouts). Apply \"drop instances where an arm read the answer\" honestly and you drop three winners and one loser: **−9.6%, worse than the headline.**\n\nRemoving only the leaking loser and keeping the three leaking winners would be selecting on outcome. I'll report the median (−16.1%) as a disclosed robust statistic alongside the geomean if that's useful — it's legitimate as a secondary number — but not as \"the savings\", and it isn't 25% either way.\n\nThe one path that could still move this legitimately is fixing the leaks and re-measuring: three channels are open (package caches — now closed in my workers; npm/yarn pulling post-fix releases over the network, which netjail doesn't block; and sibling benchmark checkouts reachable via `find /`). Since three of the four known leaks favour eg, closing them will most likely make the honest number *worse* than −11.2% — but it would be the first Opus number with no known contamination in either arm, which is worth more than the current one."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2728,"cache_read_input_tokens":626557,"output_tokens":1316,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2728,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1316,"cache_read_input_tokens":626557,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2728,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2728},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgLGgZiT7YexHDBeBrmU","type":"assistant","uuid":"803b958f-7bca-49e3-96a5-7899972e1ea0","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:02:43.461Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
