{"parentUuid":"e80c290e-b3a5-417d-8ac2-0e00a924f998","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgLumTgSPAEr5VMfLCUJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**10 of 12 now resolve, up from 3.** fmt-1683, fmt-2457, jekyll, lucene, three.js, redis-11734 and valkey are all new.\n\n| instance | resolved test |\n|---|---|\n| lucene | `…/src/test/org/…/TestOpenNLPSentenceBreakIterator.java` |\n| gson | `gson/src/test/java/…/JsonTreeReaderTest.java` |\n| docusaurus | `packages/docusaurus/src/server/__tests__/brokenLinks.test.ts` |\n| fpm | `spec/fpm/package/deb_spec.rb` |\n| **jekyll** | `test/test_utils.rb` |\n| **fmt-1683** | `test/printf-test.cc` |\n| **fmt-2457** | `test/ranges-test.cc` |\n| **three.js** | `test/unit/src/core/Object3D.tests.js` |\n| **redis-11734** | `tests/unit/bitops.tcl` |\n| **valkey** | `tests/unit/acl.tcl` |\n\nTwo still miss, and both for honest reasons. **redis-10095** exhausts the 256-probe budget — `tests/unit/type/list.tcl` is in the candidate set but arrives too late, and every probe is a real file read so I won't inflate the bound. **phpspreadsheet** needs `src/PhpSpreadsheet/Calculation/LookupRef/HLookup.php` → `tests/PhpSpreadsheetTests/Calculation/**Functions/**LookupRef/HLookupTest.php` — the mirror both renames a directory *and inserts* a segment, which no path rule expresses.\n\nThree things worth being straight about before I run anything:\n\n**This test is optimistic by construction.** My harness makes the true test the *only* file that exists, so a pass proves the candidate set contains it. In a real repo other candidates exist too and an earlier one could match first, returning a plausible-but-wrong test. The real check is running it against the actual checkouts.\n\n**The ceiling is 10, not 20.** Of the 20 instances, 8 have a gold test that no path rule can reach — carbon's test is named after the *method* (`IsTest.php` for `->is()`), and hugo, nushell, preact, prometheus and core-11739 have their gold test in a **different package with an unrelated name**. So this recovers roughly half the addressable gap, not all of it.\n\n**Which revises the projection down.** Eliminating *all* 5.6 pre-edit test-hunt ops projected −29.4%. At ~10/20 coverage it's about half that: ops 28.8 → ~26, i.e. **≈ −21%** against baseline 32.9 — short of −25%, though a real gain on −11.2%.\n\nNext: verify against the real checkouts (free, catches the false-positive risk), then run the PUB cell with everything else identical so it's a clean single-variable comparison."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4781,"cache_read_input_tokens":668356,"output_tokens":975,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4781,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":975,"cache_read_input_tokens":668356,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4781,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4781},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgLueiNc8EfQ8aa3mshp","type":"assistant","uuid":"4c0d0923-9028-420d-86fa-d5acf72d2fe4","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:11:00.956Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/eg-consolidated","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
