{"parentUuid":"bf635a87-1595-44b3-be6f-f5f15bd59aef","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgM4pJ6L89k6vDerwQ2k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Important negative first: **my change is inert on real checkouts.** f19 and f20 produce byte-identical payloads — 1644, 2110, 3876 bytes, identical:\n\n| instance | f19 COVERING TEST | f20 COVERING TEST |\n|---|---|---|\n| fmt-2457 | NONE | **NONE** |\n| redis-10095 | NONE | **NONE** |\n| lucene | resolved | resolved (same) |\n\nThe 10/12 was an artifact of my own harness — it fabricated an evidence layer where the true test was the *only* file that existed, which is exactly the false-positive risk I flagged. On a real repo the mirror either isn't reached (`testPath` already set by the ranked covering-test section) or an earlier candidate wins. The `COVERING TEST` **block** comes from ranked results, not from the mirror; the mirror only feeds the `VERIFY` command. So I improved the wrong path. Reverting rather than shipping something inert:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1552,"cache_read_input_tokens":676715,"output_tokens":2765,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1552,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2765,"cache_read_input_tokens":676715,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1552,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1552},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgM4j54hX81Dg8SdgHdg","type":"assistant","uuid":"48a552c3-3ff3-4608-9eb2-fb936e9b5fa6","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:13:18.211Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/de