{"parentUuid":"684763ae-5446-486d-bb20-41acd66d8bb0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgMZbxVGaTmqxfTFLCGL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Simple and clear result:\n\n| instance | `grep <sym>` | `callers <sym>` | **test-scoped `search`** |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| fmt-2457 | no | no | **YES — found `ranges-test.cc`** |\n| redis-10095 | no | no | no |\n| lucene | no | (timed out) | — |\n\nSo a **test-scoped search finds the test** where the test is in an indexed language. redis fails for a different and simpler reason: its tests are `.tcl`, which the indexer doesn't cover at all — the graph literally cannot see them.\n\nSo the fix is exactly what you said: the payload already prefetches a search and an impact; it should prefetch the **test location** too. That's one more call using an existing verb, no product change:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3274,"cache_read_input_tokens":685938,"output_tokens":2901,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3274,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2901,"cache_read_input_tokens":685938,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3274,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3274},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgMZWMPtBZpFdEzEAv1k","type":"assistant","uuid":"00642e3e-d70d-4809-91b3-c915ba1ae726","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:19:36.349Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"00642e3e-d70d-4809-91b3-c915ba1ae726","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgMZbxVGaTmqxfTFLCGL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CRrWGAjq2sepTtkypLtUjb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench/agentic-swebench\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport io\np='tools/run_3arm.sh'; s=io.open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\nanchor='''    if [ -s \"$out/prefetch.payload\" ]; then'''\nnew='''    # EG_PREFETCH_TEST=1 — THIRD prefetch stage: locate the covering TEST.\n    #\n    # Measured on PUB (Opus, published prompt, n=20): test-hunting is 39% of ALL eg locate operations\n    # (11.3 per session: 5.6 pre-edit + 5.7 post-edit) and eg does MORE pre-edit test-hunting than the\n    # no-tool baseline (5.6 vs 5.2). The payload carries a COVERING TEST block in only 5 of 20\n    # instances, so the largest single slice of the locate phase is one the tool declines to answer and\n    # the agent pays for with the shell: `grep -n \"trailing\" brokenLinks.test.ts`,\n    # `cat TestOpenNLPSentenceBreakIterator.java`, `grep -n BITCOUNT tests/unit/bitops.tcl`.\n    #\n    # Verified offline on real checkouts before wiring: a test-scoped search DOES find the gold test\n    # where the test is in an indexed language (fmt-2457 -> test/ranges-test.cc), while `grep` and\n    # `callers` on the fix symbol do not. redis/valkey stay out of reach because their tests are .tcl,\n    # which the indexer does not cover at all -- a coverage gap, not a ranking one.\n    if [ \"${EG_PREFETCH_TEST:-0}\" = 1 ] && [ -s \"$out/prefetch.payload\" ]; then\n      pf_sym3=$(\"$PY\" -c \"\nimport re\ntry:\n    for ln in open('$out/prefetch.payload', errors='ignore'):\n        m = re.search(r'symbol=(\\\\S+)', ln)\n        if m:\n            print(m.group(1).split('.')[-1]); break\nexcept Exception: pass\" 2>/dev/null)\n      if [ -n \"$pf_sym3\" ]; then\n        GQLOG=\"$out/prefetch_calls.log\" \"$gq\" search \"test for $pf_sym3\" > \"$out/prefetch_test.payload\" 2>/dev/null || true\n      fi\n    fi\n    if [ -s \"$out/prefetch.payload\" ]; then'''\nassert s.count(anchor)==1\ns=s.replace(anchor,new,1)\n# append the test block to PREFETCH_BLOCK in both preamble variants\nold_tail='''</graph_search_result>$( [ -s \"$out/prefetch_impact.payload\" ] && printf '\\\\n\\\\n<graph_impact_result>\\\\nBlast radius of the top hit -- the other places this change lands.\\\\n\\\\n%s\\\\n</graph_impact_result>' \"$(cat \"$out/prefetch_impact.payload\")\" )\"'''\nnew_tail='''</graph_search_result>$( [ -s \"$out/prefetch_impact.payload\" ] && printf '\\\\n\\\\n<graph_impact_result>\\\\nBlast radius of the top hit -- the other places this change lands.\\\\n\\\\n%s\\\\n</graph_impact_result>' \"$(cat \"$out/prefetch_impact.payload\")\" )$( [ -s \"$out/prefetch_test.payload\" ] && printf '\\\\n\\\\n<graph_test_result>\\\\nThe existing tests that cover this code -- read one of these instead of hunting for it, and use it\\\\nas the model for reproducing the issue.\\\\n\\\\n%s\\\\n</graph_test_result>' \"$(cat \"$out/prefetch_test.payload\")\" )\"'''\nn=s.count(old_tail); assert n>=1, n\ns=s.replace(old_tail,new_tail)\nold_tail2='''</graph_search_result>$( [ -s \"$out/prefetch_impact.payload\" ] && printf '\\\\n\\\\n<graph_impact_result>\\\\nBlast radius of the top hit -- the other places this change lands. You do not need to look these\\\\nup yourself.\\\\n\\\\n%s\\\\n</graph_impact_result>' \"$(cat \"$out/prefetch_impact.payload\")\" )\"'''\nnew_tail2='''</graph_search_result>$( [ -s \"$out/prefetch_impact.payload\" ] && printf '\\\\n\\\\n<graph_impact_result>\\\\nBlast radius of the top hit -- the other places this change lands. You do not need to look these\\\\nup yourself.\\\\n\\\\n%s\\\\n</graph_impact_result>' \"$(cat \"$out/prefetch_impact.payload\")\" )$( [ -s \"$out/prefetch_test.payload\" ] && printf '\\\\n\\\\n<graph_test_result>\\\\nThe existing tests that cover this code -- read one of these instead of hunting for it, and use it\\\\nas the model for reproducing the issue.\\\\n\\\\n%s\\\\n</graph_test_result>' \"$(cat \"$out/prefetch_test.payload\")\" )\"'''\nif s.count(old_tail2): s=s.replace(old_tail2,new_tail2)\nio.open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('EG_PREFETCH_TEST wired as prefetch stage 3 + <graph_test_result> block')\nPY\nbash -n tools/run_3arm.sh && echo \"syntax OK\"","description":"Wire a third prefetch stage that locates the covering test"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3274,"cache_read_input_tokens":685938,"output_tokens":2901,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3274,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2901,"cache_read_input_tokens":685938,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3274,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3274},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgMZWMPtBZpFdEzEAv1k","type":"assistant","uuid":"970975f1-a08d-4a7c-a40f-4d416eda1e32","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:19:53.061Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
