{"parentUuid":"886e4ba3-b833-461d-b76d-8a061f4bcb99","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ef28e9cf-7b14-4e67-9de3-876392b959f4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JcwLcLb3NxyiUfcX5TbJVC","type":"tool_result","content":"Command running in background with ID: bep2zgxvc. Output is being written to: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208/tasks/bep2zgxvc.output. You will be notified when it completes. To check interim output, use Read on that file path.\nSession cwd remains /Users/suhaan/devenv; directory changes made by the backgrounded command do not apply to subsequent commands.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"fdd3524e-e142-4b50-9b05-426c9854647b","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:23:23.467Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"backgroundTaskId":"bep2zgxvc","backgroundCwdHint":"Session cwd remains /Users/suhaan/devenv; directory changes made by the backgrounded command do not apply to subsequent commands."},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"886e4ba3-b833-461d-b76d-8a061f4bcb99","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"fdd3524e-e142-4b50-9b05-426c9854647b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[],"itemCount":0},"type":"attachment","uuid":"184360c7-b47f-46e5-a6e2-50a5990265f9","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:23:23.556Z","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"184360c7-b47f-46e5-a6e2-50a5990265f9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgMspKtM2v31zvNaZgxE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Vd5WK8HFDwNayBfethhfhd","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Compare winners vs losers tool usage","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Read-only forensic comparison. Do not modify anything. Suite root: /Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench/agentic-swebench\n\nTASK: exhaustively compare TOOL CALLS and GRAPH USAGE between the instances where a code-search tool (\"entire-graph\", wrapper `eg-q.run`) WON on tokens and where it LOST. Find every systematic difference.\n\nDATA\n  results/PUB_r1_eg/eg/<instance>/         prompt.txt, prefetch.payload, prefetch_impact.payload, gq_calls.log, cc_out.json, patch.diff\n  results/PUB_r1_baseline/baseline/<inst>/ same, no payload (no tool)\n  Transcript: read cc_out.json -> \"session_id\", then ~/.claude/projects/*/<session_id>.jsonl\n  JSONL. Assistant records: type==\"assistant\", message.content[] blocks of type \"thinking\"|\"text\"|\"tool_use\".\n  tool_use has .name (Bash/Read/Grep/Glob/Edit/Write) and .input (.command/.file_path/.pattern/.offset/.limit).\n  A graph call is a Bash tool_use whose .command contains \"eg-q.run\".\n  gq_calls.log = the agent's OWN graph calls (empty file = zero). prefetch_calls.log = harness-issued, not the agent's.\n\nTHE CELL (Opus, Anthropic's published SWE-bench prompt verbatim to both arms; eg additionally gets a capability paragraph + a prefetched search+impact payload). Cell result -11.2% tokens, n=20.\n\nWINNERS (token ratio vs own baseline): jekyll-8167 -58, caddy-5995 -56, preact-2757 -54, lucene-13170 -52, fpm-1829 -40, docusaurus-10130 -38, core-11739 -24, valkey-1842 -21, three.js-25687 -18, fmt-2457 -18, hugo-12204 -15, nushell-12901 -9\nLOSERS: gson-1014 +10, prometheus-10633 +20, fmt-1683 +27, phpspreadsheet-3570 +31, ruff-15626 +35, redis-10095 +65, redis-11734 +96, carbon-2752 +107\n\nALREADY MEASURED - do not re-derive, extend:\n- agent graph calls 0.20/session overall; 16 of 20 sessions make ZERO. Only docusaurus (1x def), core-11739 (2x def/search), nushell (1x def) used it.\n- Phase split (paired). WINNERS baseline->eg: pre-edit locate 13.9->15.0, post-edit 19.1->8.9, build/test 10.7->6.5, edits 6.8->4.5, reproduce scripts 11->5.\n  LOSERS: pre-edit 11.5->13.0, post-edit 6.5->13.8, build/test 6.2->6.2, edits 3.8->5.6, repro 8->9.\n- eg post-edit op composition per session (winners/losers): re-finds text the payload already printed 5.58/7.25; searches inside a payload-returned file 1.58/2.00; genuinely new 2.67/3.50; build-test 5.08/6.88.\n- Post-edit op classification across all 20: grep for a symbol the payload already named 6.85/session (57.8%); grep for something else 3.35; Read of a payload file 0.60; Read other 1.05.\n- Test-hunting (any locate op whose target matches test|spec|snapshot|fixture|__tests__|.tcl) is 39% of all eg locate ops: pre-edit 5.6 (baseline 5.2), post-edit 5.7 (baseline 7.4). COVERING TEST block present in only 5 of 20 payloads.\n- corr(baseline post-edit locate count, log token ratio) = -0.484.\n\nWHAT I WANT, with numbers for WINNERS vs LOSERS side by side:\n1. Tool-name histogram per group (Bash/Read/Grep/Glob/Edit/Write), per session. Which tool differs most?\n2. Bash sub-classification per group: grep/rg, find, ls, cat, sed, git, build-or-test, package-install (composer/npm/yarn/pip/cargo/go mod/make), writing a heredoc script, other. Per session.\n3. Graph usage: which instances called it, which verb, at what point in the session (before/after first edit, and as what fraction through the session). Did calling it correlate with winning?\n4. Distinct FILES touched (read or edited) per group; how many were named in the payload vs discovered independently.\n5. Turn-by-turn shape: for each group, the mean call index of the first Edit, and the mean number of calls after the LAST edit (the tail).\n6. Whether the losers' extra work is concentrated in a contiguous block (an \"episode\" like an environment-provisioning project) or spread thin. Quantify: largest run of consecutive same-category ops.\n7. Anything else systematic you find that separates the groups.\n\nRULES\n- Every claim needs a number and the derivation. State n.\n- A difference that is equally present in winners is NOT a difference - say so explicitly. 27 of 28 previously-claimed defects died exactly this way.\n- Do not speculate about fixes. I want the measured comparison only.\n- If a metric shows no separation, report that too - negatives are useful here.\n\nOUTPUT: extremely terse. Tables of numbers. Fragments, not prose. No preamble, no restating the task. Lead with the three biggest separations by effect size."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1661,"cache_read_input_tokens":696643,"output_tokens":1986,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1661,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1986,"cache_read_input_tokens":696643,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1661,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1661},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgMsfCi77EJt9M2HHVkC","type":"assistant","uuid":"e53de07b-ec2d-4aba-b976-e58b9e888239","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:23:56.327Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
