{"parentUuid":"babd807d-713b-4085-bf1a-c45dfc6f6dfd","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/modular-cooking-cupcake.md","snippet":"1\t# Opus to −25%: make the payload addressable, in the long-session regime\n2\t\n3\t## Context\n4\t\n5\tGoal: Opus ≥ −25% tokens on the 20-instance official-300 sample. Six configurations are now measured.\n6\tFitting them together gives a quantitative model that says exactly where the goal is reachable — and\n7\tit is not where I have been spending.\n8\t\n9\t| config | baseline ops | ops Δ | ktok/session | tokens | **penalty** (tokens−ops) |\n10\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n11\t| **PUB** — published prompt, prefetch | 35.7 | −11.2% | **2729k** | **−11.2%** | **+0.0** |\n12\t| G40 — rich methodology both arms | 23.8 | +21.1% | 1300k | +28.4% | +7.3 |\n13\t| GC — gated clamp (symmetric) | 11.5 | +4.3% | 378k | +22.2% | +17.9 |\n14\t| CB — clamp + scaffold | 10.5 | −20.6% | 345k | +7.5% | +28.1 |\n15\t| FRUGAL — rich both, frugal shared | 7.0 | −28.6% | 279k | −14.0% | +14.6 |\n16\t| S1O — S1 clamp | 4.6 | −8.0% | 175k | +18.2% | +26.2 |\n17\t\n18\t**`tokens ≈ ops Δ + payload tax`, and the tax is a pure function of session size** — 0 at 2729k,\n19\t+7 at 1300k, +18 to +28 below 400k. So:\n20\t\n21\t| regime | ops reduction required for −25% |\n22\t|---|---|\n23\t| **2729k (PUB)** | **−25%** |\n24\t| 1300k | −32% |\n25\t| ~350k | −53% |\n26\t\n27\t**Only the longest regime is viable.** Every clamp config I have run this session sits at 175–378k,\n28\twhere the tax alone is +18 to +28 points — which is why CB cut 20.6% of ops and still lost, and why\n29\tGC and S1O lost outright. That direction has not paid off so far, and both live cells are failing their\n30\tpre-registered gates right now (baseline ops 10.5 and 11.5 against a required ≥20; GC's pre-edit is\n31\t+40% against a required ≤−25%). **Kill both.**\n32\t\n33\t## Where the 14 points are\n34\t\n35\tPUB's op budget, measured:\n36\t\n37\t| phase | baseline | eg |\n38\t|---|---|---|\n39\t| pre-edit locate | 13.4 | **14.6** (worse) |\n40\t| post-edit locate | 15.5 | 11.8 |\n41\t| build/test | 6.8 | 5.2 |\n42\t| **total** | **35.7** | **31.7 (−11.2%)** |\n43\t\n44\tTarget for −25% ops is 26.8. Two steps get there:\n45\t\n46\t| step | eg total | ops Δ |\n47\t|---|---|---|\n48\t| eg pre-edit merely *matches* the baseline (14.6 → 13.4) | 30.4 | −14.8% |\n49\t| **+ post-edit re-hunts removed (11.8 → 7.1)** | **26.9** | **−24.6%** ✓ |\n50\t\n51\tAt PUB's session size the tax is zero, so −24.6% ops ⇒ **≈ −25% tokens**.\n52\t\n53\t## The mechanism, and why the earlier refutation does not apply\n54\t\n55\tMeasured on this cell:\n56\t- **\"re-finds text the payload already printed\" = 5.58 ops/session (winners), 7.25 (losers)** — about\n57\t  40% of eg's post-edit locate work.\n58\t- **Payload bodies carry ZERO line numbers**: 0 of 55, 0 of 107, 0 of 79 — in **20/20 instances**.\n59\t- The eg prompt promises, verbatim: *\"the complete body of the enclosing function is printed verbatim\n60\t  beneath that header, **at its real line numbers**\"*. The prompt is false.\n61\t\n62\tUnnumbered bodies are not addressable. To build an `Edit` old_string anchor, a `Read` range, or to\n63\treason about hunk positions, the agent must re-open the file it was just shown. That is the re-hunt.\n64\t\n65\t**The adversarial verifier refuted this as a loser-explanation — correctly — and that refutation is\n66\tirrelevant here.** Its reasoning was: present in 20/20 instances, therefore in 6/6 winners, therefore\n67\tit cannot be what makes an instance *lose*. True. But what this goal needs is **not** a\n68\tloser-differentiator: fixing all 8 losers to exact parity yields only **−23.5%**, short of target.\n69\tIt needs a **uniform tax removal that lifts all 20** — and a defect present in 20/20 is precisely the\n70\tright shape for that. I conflated these two questions earlier and dropped a valid lever.\n71\t\n72\t## Plan\n73\t\n74\t### 1. Stop the two failing cells\n75\tKill CB and GC. Both breach the gates I pre-registered; the sub-400k regime cannot reach −25% at any\n76\tachievable ops reduction.\n77\t\n78\t### 2. Product change: number the body lines\n79\t`eg-consolidated`, the search render path (`internal/sem/` — the body printer that emits ranked-hit\n80\tbodies beneath the `N. path:START-END score= symbol=` header):\n81\t- prefix every printed body line with its real line number (the header already carries the span, so\n82\t  this is 5–6 chars/line);\n83\t- set `focus=` to the matched **interior** line rather than collapsing to the definition line.\n84\t\n85\tThis makes the prompt's existing promise true. It is a rendering change only — no ranking, no\n86\tretrieval, no selection. The baseline has no payload, so arm symmetry is untouched.\n87\t\n88\t### 3. Emulate all 20 offline before spending — free\n89\tRecorded queries in `results/PUB_r1_eg/eg/<inst>/prefetch_calls.log`, worktrees in\n90\t`replay-wt/<inst>`, patched binary, **fresh `--cache-dir`** (the index cache is tree-keyed, not\n91\tbinary-keyed — reuse it and you get the old binary's answer).\n92\tAssert per instance: every body line numbered; the numbers match the file at that path; `focus=` lands\n93\tinside the body; and **byte-identical output outside the body lines** (no ranking drift). Any\n94\tinstance failing the last check blocks the cell.\n95\t\n96\t### 4. Run PUB + numbered bodies — 40 sessions, same 20 instances\n97\tEverything else exactly as the −11.2% cell: `PUBLISHED_EXACT=1`, prefetch + impact on, cap 120,\n98\t`CC_TIMEOUT=3600`, plus the per-instance cache isolation already built into the workers\n99\t(`GOMODCACHE`, `GOPATH`, `GOCACHE`, `COMPOSER_HOME`, `CARGO_HOME`, `GEM_HOME`, `npm_config_cache`,\n100\t`maven.repo.local`) — the one confirmed integrity defect, where caddy's baseline read the gold line\n101\tout of the module cache and carbon's eg arm read the gold regex out of the composer cache.\n102\t\n103\t### 5. Leading indicators — free, checkable at ~8 pairs\n104\t| indicator | current | required |\n105\t|---|---|---|\n106\t| session size | 2729k | **stays > 2000k** (if it collapses, the tax returns and the cell is void) |\n107\t| eg pre-edit locate | +9% | **≤ 0%** |\n108\t| post-edit \"re-finds payload text\" | 5.58 / 7.25 per session | **≤ 4.0** |\n109\t| ops Δ | −11.2% | **≤ −20%** |\n110\tKill the cell if session size collapses or ops Δ has not passed −18% by 8 pairs.\n111\t\n112\t### 6. Pre-registered\n113\t- Success = geomean ≤ −25%, CI upper bound < 0.\n114\t- Required shape: eg ops ≈ 27 against baseline ≈ 36, at ~2700k session size.\n115\t- **Falsification:** if bodies are numbered, re-hunts fall, ops reach ≤ −20%, and tokens still miss\n116\t  −25%, then the ops↔tokens identity that holds at PUB length is wrong and **−25% on Opus is\n117\t  unreachable**. That is the seventh configuration and I will report the ceiling.\n118\t- Replicate with a second independent cell before claiming. Today's n≤4 signals reversed repeatedly.\n119\t\n120\t## Verification\n121\t- `tools/model_cmp.py`: geomean of per-instance ratios + bootstrap CI, cost classes separately.\n122\t- Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped symmetrically.\n123\t- `CENSORED` (`error_max_turns`) = 0 per arm — the baseline averages 50.2 turns, so a 50-cap censors\n124\t  the baseline specifically.\n125\t- Report ops (pre/post/build) beside tokens in every update; at PUB length ops predicted tokens to\n126\t  within 0.0 points, so it is the cheap early read.\n127\t- Verify on emitted artifacts, never config. Twelve silent plumbing failures today — the latest being\n128\t  `BASE_GATED_CLAMP` wired into one dispatcher but not the one the vendor family uses, caught only\n129\t  because the fairness gate compared emitted prompts.\n130\t\n131\t## Files\n132\t- `eg-consolidated/internal/sem/` — the ranked-hit body renderer. Only product change. Add a\n133\t  regression test asserting numbered bodies and unchanged surrounding output.\n134\t- `/tmp/mcptest/pubworker.sh` — the −11.2% config; point at the rebuilt binary, keep everything else.\n135\t- `tools/model_cmp.py` — scorer, unchanged.\n136\t- No prompt changes: the prompt already claims numbered lines, so this makes it honest rather than\n137\t  altering the contract.\n138\t\n139\t## Honest expectation\n140\tThis is the first plan built on a fitted quantitative model rather than a mechanism story: the six\n141\tmeasured configs give tax-vs-session-size, that fixes the viable regime to PUB, and the op budget then\n\n... [8 lines truncated] ..."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ef069b6d-3e26-4a38-a207-395fbde2f0c0","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:24:52.573Z","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
