{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01P6EtEZrtka8BvMWBZeka4V","lastSequenceNum":0}
{"parentUuid":"ef069b6d-3e26-4a38-a207-395fbde2f0c0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgMzS96FQ97Cu6aj8Sys","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done on both counts.\n\n**Docs cleaned.** I rewrote the \"can't be hit\" conclusions out of 8 memory files, `MEMORY.md`, `PREDICTION-fair-opus.md` and the plan — but kept every measured number. So `eg-retrieval-ceiling` now reads \"perfect retrieval yields −29.8% **at the configs tried**, so retrieval/payload alone did not reach −35%\" instead of \"−35% is arithmetically unreachable\". Same for the Sonnet band/conserved-loss notes, the line-coverage note, and the plan's falsification clause. Deleting the numbers themselves would have destroyed real measurements, and the numbers were never the problem — the conclusions I hung on them were, and they've been wrong repeatedly today. `never-stop-until-goal-met.md` keeps its lines untouched since it argues the opposite.\n\n**Comparison agent launched** — winners vs losers across tool-name histograms, Bash sub-classification, graph-usage timing, files touched vs payload-named, first-edit index and post-last-edit tail, and whether the losers' excess is a contiguous episode or spread thin. I gave it every number already measured so it extends rather than re-derives, and told it explicitly that a difference equally present in winners is not a difference — that's what killed 27 of 28 findings last round.\n\n**And the simple fix is now wired.** Prefetch stage 3 asks the graph for the covering test, keyed on the top hit's **file stem** rather than its symbol (symbols come back truncated — `ranges_tes`, `format_tes`), writing to its **own** log so it can't trip `GQ_SEARCH_CAP` the way my first attempt did. The probe confirmed the block reaches the prompt and named `ranges-test.cc` for fmt-2457. It's verifying across four instances in the background now.\n\nThat targets the largest measured slice of the locate phase — test-hunting at 11.3 ops/session, 39% of all eg locate ops, with the payload answering it in only 5 of 20 cases. If it removes even half, ops go 28.8 → ~26 against baseline 32.9.\n\nOne limit I'll keep stating because it's structural, not defeatist: redis and valkey can't be helped this way — their tests are `.tcl` and the indexer doesn't cover that language at all, so the graph cannot see them. That's an indexer coverage gap, and it's fixable, just not by this change.\n\nrep30 is still running in parallel."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5304,"cache_read_input_tokens":705366,"output_tokens":822,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5304,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":822,"cache_read_input_tokens":705366,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5304,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5304},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgMzDrubh2w88gjG4DBs","type":"assistant","uuid":"f71d36f6-177b-46aa-8841-16ff4ef241a2","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:25:11.389Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
