{"parentUuid":"d93e423c-0d52-4c12-976c-788969ffa58f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"38ad7d33-6f2d-41cd-8e8c-1a44118ae431","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AQgzdz82EvvwKQsouHqoAF","type":"tool_result","content":"# entire-graph provider command. Canonical name after the sem->graph rename is `entire graph`\n# (what `entire plugin install entire-graph` registers). Override with ENTIRE_GRAPH=... for a\n# host that still has the legacy `entire sem` plugin.\nGRAPH=\"${ENTIRE_GRAPH:-entire graph}\"\n\n# Exclude test-fixture / generated / vendored files from the graph (uniform pre-registered filter,\n# see tools/graph_exclude.globs) so `symbols`/`def` aren't polluted by noise the agent never edits.\n# Passed to BOTH passes identically or the two dumps disagree. Empty if the file is absent.\nIGN=\"${GRAPH_IGNORE_FILE:-$SUITE/tools/graph_exclude.globs}\"\nIGN_FLAG=\"\"; [ -f \"$IGN\" ] && IGN_FLAG=\"--ignore-file $IGN\"\n\necho \"[graph] symbols…\"\n# Capture the provider's stderr to a log (do NOT discard it): an OOM/kill must be diagnosable,\n# and its exit status must be checkable — a killed provider silently shipped a half-graph before.\n$GRAPH symbols --repo \"$cache\" --format ndjson $IGN_FLAG > \"$out/graph.symbols.ndjson\" 2> \"$out/graph_symbols.err\"\nsym_rc=$?\necho \"[graph] edges… (piped through filter_edges.py: caps CALLS fan-out; see that file)\"\n# `entire graph edges` emits CALLS via a name-based resolution cascade with GRADED per-edge\n# confidence (~0.92 same-file down to ~0.55-0.62 ambiguous), whose low-confidence tail is\n# quadratic on large repos (10+ GB dumps that OOM graph-query / exhaust Docker disk).\n# filter_edges.py keeps all non-CALLS and spends a bounded per-symbol CALLS fan-out on the\n=== usage ===\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Build the entire-graph NDJSON dump for one repo @ base_commit, on the HOST (native binary).\n# Output: <out>/graph.symbols.ndjson + <out>/graph.edges.ndjson  (fed into the treated container).\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/suhaan/devenv","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b1c69b1a-7d77-48b4-8b93-4d88ac47a9ab","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:29:20.422Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# entire-graph provider command. Canonical name after the sem->graph rename is `entire graph`\n# (what `entire plugin install entire-graph` registers). Override with ENTIRE_GRAPH=... for a\n# host that still has the legacy `entire sem` plugin.\nGRAPH=\"${ENTIRE_GRAPH:-entire graph}\"\n\n# Exclude test-fixture / generated / vendored files from the graph (uniform pre-registered filter,\n# see tools/graph_exclude.globs) so `symbols`/`def` aren't polluted by noise the agent never edits.\n# Passed to BOTH passes identically or the two dumps disagree. Empty if the file is absent.\nIGN=\"${GRAPH_IGNORE_FILE:-$SUITE/tools/graph_exclude.globs}\"\nIGN_FLAG=\"\"; [ -f \"$IGN\" ] && IGN_FLAG=\"--ignore-file $IGN\"\n\necho \"[graph] symbols…\"\n# Capture the provider's stderr to a log (do NOT discard it): an OOM/kill must be diagnosable,\n# and its exit status must be checkable — a killed provider silently shipped a half-graph before.\n$GRAPH symbols --repo \"$cache\" --format ndjson $IGN_FLAG > \"$out/graph.symbols.ndjson\" 2> \"$out/graph_symbols.err\"\nsym_rc=$?\necho \"[graph] edges… (piped through filter_edges.py: caps CALLS fan-out; see that file)\"\n# `entire graph edges` emits CALLS via a name-based resolution cascade with GRADED per-edge\n# confidence (~0.92 same-file down to ~0.55-0.62 ambiguous), whose low-confidence tail is\n# quadratic on large repos (10+ GB dumps that OOM graph-query / exhaust Docker disk).\n# filter_edges.py keeps all non-CALLS and spends a bounded per-symbol CALLS fan-out on the\n=== usage ===\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Build the entire-graph NDJSON dump for one repo @ base_commit, on the HOST (native binary).\n# Output: <out>/graph.symbols.ndjson + <out>/graph.edges.ndjson  (fed into the treated container).","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/suhaan/devenv","