{"parentUuid":"1e373c62-b670-432e-8205-72ad3166d316","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgNVhz9Ec7A1SwhHqoxg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2338,"cache_read_input_tokens":735847,"output_tokens":2248,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2338,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2248,"cache_read_input_tokens":735847,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2338,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2338},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgNVcguPo5LC5f4ijWvD","type":"assistant","uuid":"44ccf4a5-a339-4540-80fa-37194a7b595f","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:31:51.257Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"44ccf4a5-a339-4540-80fa-37194a7b595f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgNVhz9Ec7A1SwhHqoxg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Let me be precise, because I flip-flopped and only one version is right.\n\n**My original finding was correct; my retraction was wrong.** The retraction used `repo_root` from the file's *header* line as the path key. With the real key (`file_path`), on fmt-2457:\n\n| graph | symbols | test-path symbols | symbols in gold `ranges-test.cc` |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| shipped | 1,795 | **0** | **0** |\n| keep-tests rebuild | 6,543 | **4,748** | **50** |\n\nSo tests genuinely are excluded from the symbol index, and lifting the filter genuinely indexes them.\n\n**But the consequence I drew from it is still wrong**, and this is the part that matters: the keep-tests graph produced **byte-identical search output**, and the gold test `test/ranges-test.cc:203-220` was already at **rank 2** in both. So `eg-q search` surfaces test files by content regardless of the symbol index — indexing tests is not the lever for search results, and the missing `COVERING TEST` block has some other cause. I've removed the keep-tests artifacts.\n\n**Meanwhile the catastrophe workflow returned 5 verified survivors, and two are serious:**\n\n**1. docusaurus-10130 — the eg arm network-fetched the fix and transcribed it.** Call #29: `npm pack @docusaurus/core@3.4.0` → extract `package/lib/server/brokenLinks.js` → #31 grep it → **the very next call is the Edit, whose `new_string` is that printed block detranspiled**: same six `??` branches in the same order, same three comments. The issue number `10116` in the submitted patch appears **nowhere** in the prompt, so it can only have come from the tarball. This is a **−38% \"winner\" inside the cell I've been quoting as −11.2%.** netjail blocks `curl`/`wget` but not `npm pack`. The verifier also found 67% of that session's cache_read went to a `/tmp` harness project that never ran the repo's own tests.\n\n**2. fmt-2457's 179-point swing is 132% baseline-side.** eg's absolute cost *falls* from PUB to G40 (4.25M → 2.94M) while the baseline collapses (5.16M → 1.13M). Log decomposition is exact: eg term −0.368, baseline term +1.521. And PUB's eg \"win\" there was bought by **17 baseline messages** running a two-compiler `orig-vs-new` differential matrix — `g++-15` appears 7 times in the baseline and **0 times in eg** — costing 1.69M tokens, which is **163% of the entire PUB delta** for that instance.\n\nSo two of the twelve PUB winners are compromised: one read the answer off the network, one won because its baseline ran a compiler matrix. That's the same cell as the −11.2%.\n\nI'm not going to keep tuning configs against a measurement with a live network leak in it. The next thing that has to happen is closing egress and re-running PUB — that's a harness fix with a definite outcome, unlike another prompt variant. rep30 is still running and carries the same exposure, so I'll treat its number the same way."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2338,"cache_read_input_tokens":735847,"output_tokens":2248,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2338,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2248,"cache_read_input_tokens":735847,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2338,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2338},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgNVcguPo5LC5f4ijWvD","type":"assistant","uuid":"797e3fb7-bbfc-4bf4-8735-c067cabb4a6b","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:32:03.718Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/s