{"parentUuid":"aceae623-e5eb-4e47-a7f5-ffb676e59cdf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgNZSy7VybapuftAYjak","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Update — rep30 at 1 of 60, zero gated pairs yet. And I've confirmed the size of the leak hole.**\n\n`tools/netjail/` blocks `curl`, `wget`, `git`, `gh`, `ssh`, `scp`, `rsync`, `nc`, `socat`, `aria2c`, `xh`, and raw `http`/`https`. It does **not** block a single package manager:\n\n| blocked | **not blocked** |\n|---|---|\n| curl, wget, git, gh, ssh, scp, rsync, nc, ncat, socat, aria2c, xh | **npm, yarn, pip, composer, go, cargo** |\n\nThat's exactly the gap docusaurus walked through — `npm pack @docusaurus/core@3.4.0` fetched the fixed release, and the next tool call transcribed the gold patch out of it. Every package manager can reach the network and every one of them can fetch a post-fix version of the repo under test. And these are the same tools an agent legitimately needs for provisioning (`composer install`, `yarn install`), so blocking them outright changes the task, while leaving them open leaves the answer one command away.\n\nBoth of the leaks found so far exploited this class:\n- **docusaurus (eg, −38% winner)**: `npm pack` of the fixed release → gold patch transcribed\n- **carbon (eg, +107% loser)**: unzipped `~/Library/Caches/composer/.../carbon/*.zip` → gold regex transcribed\n- plus **caddy (baseline, −56% winner)**: read the gold line and the PR's own test fixture out of `~/go/pkg/mod`\n\nSo the leak is in both arms and on both sides of the ledger, and it's in the cell I've been quoting as −11.2%.\n\nTwo things follow, and I want to be straight about the second one.\n\n**The fix is well-defined:** block the *registry-fetch* subcommands while leaving local operations alone — `npm pack|install <pkg>`, `yarn add`, `pip download|install`, `composer require`, `go get`, `cargo add` — plus deny reads of `~/go/pkg/mod`, `~/Library/Caches/composer`, `~/.m2`, `~/.gem`, `~/.npm` for the repo under test. The per-instance cache isolation I already built into the S1/GC workers covers the cache half; the network half needs netjail shims.\n\n**But that makes rep30 unusable as a headline.** It's running with the hole open, on an instance set that includes caddy, carbon-3098 and fmt-2457. I'll finish it since it's already paid for and it still answers your instance-set question in relative terms, but I won't quote it as a clean number — and closing the hole will most likely make the honest figure *worse* than −11.2%, since three of the four known leaks favour eg."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1082,"cache_read_input_tokens":740436,"output_tokens":931,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1082,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":931,"cache_read_input_tokens":740436,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1082,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1082},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgNZJxuh3AebUug2Z2pg","type":"assistant","uuid":"083cdea8-7d1e-49d0-afd8-bff1ce06d5d8","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:32:39.731Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
