{"parentUuid":"2c993db9-b3ba-4a42-bd38-6f6bc2a820bc","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a8b9e3ce-0cdd-450f-992b-7f5579be665b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a5993edbbfe203a7b</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Vd5WK8HFDwNayBfethhfhd</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208/tasks/a5993edbbfe203a7b.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Compare winners vs losers tool usage\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Three biggest separations (by effect size, n=20: W=12, L=8)\n\n| # | separation | W | L | effect |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **eg-arm op count is invariant; the BASELINE is what differs** | eg 42.50 / base 59.00 | eg 44.00 / base 34.50 | eg: d=**−0.08**, MW p=0.97. base: d=**+1.55**, p=0.0069. AUC(base ops→win)=**0.865**; AUC(eg ops→win)=**0.495** |\n| 2 | **The scaling is uniform across every category — no culprit** | eg/base per coarse cat: .69/.81/.64/.60/.92/.82, CV **0.167** | 1.15/1.33/1.50/1.31/1.21/1.25, CV **0.094** | no single category carries it; ALL 6 cross sign together |\n| 3 | **Tokens are superlinear in ops** | mean(tokRat−opRat) −0.040 | +0.246 | fit log(tokRat)=k·log(opRat), **k=1.207**, R²=**0.916**, n=20. 94–96% of tokens are cache_read → each extra op re-reads the whole accumulated context |\n\nConsequence: `eg_ops = 14.16 + 0.588·base_ops` (R²=0.427) → **break-even base_ops = 34.4**. Below it eg adds ops, above it removes them. Winners: 11/12 above. Losers: 4/8 below, and the 4 above are the 4 smallest losses. Rule accuracy 15/20 = 0.75.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Tool-name histogram (mean/session)\n\nOnly **4 tools ever appear in all 40 sessions**: Bash 1456, Read 179, Edit 137, Write 74. **Zero Grep-tool, zero Glob, zero TodoWrite/Task** — published prompt is bash-only, so all locate work is Bash.\n\n| tool | W-base | W-eg | W-Δ | L-base | L-eg | L-Δ | eg W−L |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Bash | 46.58 | 33.33 | **−13.25** | 27.62 | 34.50 | **+6.88** | −1.17 |\n| Read | 5.50 | 4.75 | −0.75 | 3.12 | 3.88 | +0.75 | +0.88 |\n| Edit | 4.00 | 3.17 | −0.83 | 2.38 | 4.00 | +1.62 | −0.83 |\n| Write | 2.92 | 1.25 | −1.67 | 1.38 | 1.62 | +0.25 | −0.38 |\n| TOTAL | 59.00 | 42.50 | −16.50 | 34.50 | 44.00 | +9.50 | **−1.50** |\n\nBash differs most, by construction (95% of ops). In the **eg arm alone** no tool separates the groups (max |Δ| = 1.17).\n\n## 2. Bash sub-classification (mean/session)\n\n| bash-cat | W-base | W-eg | W-Δ | L-base | L-eg | L-Δ | egL−egW |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| grep/rg | 15.00 | 10.83 | −4.17 | 8.38 | 9.75 | +1.38 | −1.08 |\n| build-or-test | 10.08 | 6.17 | −3.92 | 7.38 | 8.00 | +0.62 | +1.83 |\n| run-interp (exec repro/interpreter) | 3.92 | 1.83 | −2.08 | 2.12 | 4.88 | +2.75 | **+3.04** |\n| heredoc-script (write script) | 4.42 | 4.08 | −0.33 | 1.75 | 2.12 | +0.38 | −1.96 |\n| sed/awk/jq | 4.83 | 3.17 | −1.67 | 1.88 | 3.38 | +1.50 | +0.21 |\n| cat/head/tail | 4.08 | 3.75 | −0.33 | 2.12 | 2.25 | +0.12 | −1.50 |\n| git | 2.33 | 1.92 | −0.42 | 2.00 | 2.50 | +0.50 | +0.58 |\n| ls/tree | 1.00 | 0.50 | −0.50 | 0.62 | 0.88 | +0.25 | +0.38 |\n| find | 0.58 | 0.17 | −0.42 | 0.38 | 0.12 | −0.25 | −0.04 |\n| **package-install** | 0.33 | 0.58 | +0.25 | **0.62** | **0.38** | **−0.25** | −0.21 |\n| graph (eg-q.run) | 0.00 | 0.33 | +0.33 | 0.00 | 0.00 | 0.00 | −0.33 |\n| other | 0.00 | 0.00 | 0.00 | 0.38 | 0.25 | −0.12 | +0.25 |\n\n**Negative:** package-install goes **down** in losers (0.62→0.38). No provisioning project. `find`+`ls` also down. `other` = 5 commands total across 1456.\n\nOnly genuine loser-side crossing: **run-interp** (W −2.08 / L +2.75, egL−egW +3.04) — executing repro binaries/interpreters.\n\nAggregates: all-text-search W 15.58→11.00 (−4.58) / L 8.75→9.88 (+1.12). All-file-read W 14.42→11.67 (−2.75) / L 7.12→9.50 (+2.38).\n\n## 3. Graph usage\n\n4 agent calls, 20 eg sessions = **0.20/session; 17/20 sessions ZERO** (confirms &amp; corrects the \"16 of 20\" to 17).\n\n| inst | grp | verb | op idx | /n | frac | vs 1st edit |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| docusaurus-10130 | W | `def` | 12 | 39 | 0.31 | before |\n| core-11739 | W | `def` | 12 | 63 | 0.19 | before |\n| core-11739 | W | `search` | 39 | 63 | 0.62 | before |\n| nushell-12901 | W | `def` | 31 | 62 | 0.50 | before |\n\nAll 4 calls are **pre-first-edit**. Callers 3/12 W vs 0/8 L, **Fisher p=0.242**. Mean ratio of the 3 callers **−23.7%** vs the other 9 winners **−36.9%** → calling the graph predicts a **weaker** win. `gq_calls.log` agrees exactly with the transcripts.\n\n## 4. Distinct files touched (Read/Edit/Write `file_path`)\n\n| | W-base | W-eg | L-base | L-eg |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| distinct files | 6.08 | 4.75 | 4.25 | **4.25** |\n| in eg payload | 1.58 | 1.75 | 1.00 | 1.50 |\n| independent | 4.50 | 3.00 | 3.25 | 2.75 |\n| distinct EDITED | 4.25 | 3.00 | 2.50 | 2.62 |\n| EDITED ∧ in payload | 0.83 | **0.83** | 0.62 | **0.62** |\n| payload lists (files) | — | 12.00 | — | 10.25 |\n\n**No separation.** And: the edited-file∩payload count is **byte-identical between arms in both groups** (0.83/0.83, 0.62/0.62) — payload exposure changed *where the edit landed* zero times. Payload names 12/10 files; ~1.6 get touched in either group.\n\nGold-file (from `patch.diff`) rank in the prefetch: rank-1 W 5/12 vs L 3/8 (no separation); **found at all W 10/12 (83%) vs L 5/8 (63%)** — 20pt gap, n too small to resolve. AUC(payload chars→win)=0.438.\n\n## 5. Turn shape (op index, 0-based; ops≈turns−1 in all 40)\n\n| metric | W-base | W-eg | L-base | L-eg |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| first-Edit index | 16.00 | 18.33 | 13.88 | 14.38 |\n| first-Edit as frac of session | 0.28 | 0.45 | 0.39 | 0.31 |\n| mid (1stEdit→lastEdit) | 32.75 | **14.08** | 11.75 | **14.88** |\n| tail (ops after last repo edit) | 9.25 | 9.08 | 7.88 | 13.75 |\n| tail as frac | 0.166 | 0.214 | 0.251 | 0.341 |\n\n**eg mid is invariant (14.08 vs 14.88)** — same invariance as total. Winners' baselines had a 32.75-op edit/verify middle that eg's arm collapsed; losers' baselines never had one.\n\n**Tail is NOT a clean separator.** eg-L tail values `[2,4,7,10,13,16,26,32]`; drop the top 2 (fmt-1683=32, carbon=26) → **8.67, below eg-W's 9.08**. W has its own 26 and 17. Tail-fraction *inflation ratio* W 1.29× vs L 1.36× — near-identical, i.e. equally present in winners.\n\n## 6. Episode structure — the extra work is NOT contiguous\n\n| | W-base | W-eg | L-base | L-eg |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| max same-coarse run | 5.00 | 3.92 | 4.75 | 5.38 |\n| max run / ops | 0.08 | 0.09 | **0.13** | **0.14** |\n| max EXEC∪SCRIPT block | 4.75 | 4.00 | 4.62 | 5.75 |\n| max LOCATE∪READ block | 11.92 | 10.42 | 8.50 | 8.25 |\n\nNormalized clumpiness is 0.13 in the **loser baseline** and 0.14 in the loser eg arm — the \"clumpiness\" **pre-exists the tool**. Not an eg effect.\n\nPer-loser: delta ops vs largest EXEC∪SCRIPT block. Only carbon-2752 (13) and gson-1014 (10, but Δops = −2) have a block big enough to be an episode; median loser maxES block = 4.\n\n| inst | Δops | maxES | Δtail | Δhead | Δmid |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| carbon-2752 | +18 | 13 | +12 | +14 | −8 |\n| redis-11734 | +23 | 5 | +5 | +13 | +5 |\n| redis-10095 | +13 | 4 | +5 | +3 | +5 |\n| ruff-15626 | +10 | 4 | −7 | −8 | +25 |\n| fmt-1683 | +15 | 4 | +27 | +9 | −21 |\n| phpspreadsheet-3570 | +1 | 2 | −2 | −17 | +20 |\n| prometheus-10633 | −2 | 4 | −1 | −2 | +1 |\n| gson-1014 | −2 | 10 | +8 | −8 | −2 |\n\nΔtail/Δhead/Δmid signs disagree across losers → **spread thin, no shared episode.**\n\nWhere the *pooled* delta lands (ΣW = −198 ops, ΣL = +76 ops):\n\n| cat | W Δ | W share | L Δ | L share |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| LOCATE | −61 | 30.8% | +11 | **14.5%** |\n| READ | −33 | 16.7% | +19 | 25.0% |\n| EDIT | −30 | 15.2% | +15 | 19.7% |\n| EXEC | −69 | 34.8% | +25 | 32.9% |\n| SCRIPT | −4 | 2.0% | +3 | 3.9% |\n| GIT | −5 | 2.5% | +4 | 5.3% |\n\nAsymmetry worth noting: winners' saving is 65.6% LOCATE+EXEC; the loser overrun is 77.6% EXEC+READ+EDIT with LOCATE only 14.5%. The tool removes locate work in winners; the loser overrun is not locate work.\n\n## 7. Other systematic findings\n\n**Residual test** (regress each eg metric on baseline TOTAL ops over all 20, compare group mean residuals — controls for session length). Note the total-ops row is near-definitional (group = sign of the token delta) and is listed only for scale:\n\n| metric | slope | R² | W resid | L resid | MW p |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| eg TOTAL ops | 0.588 | 0.43 | −6.36 | +9.55 | 0.009* |\n| eg EXEC | 0.032 | 0.01 | −2.18 | +3.28 | 0.054 |\n| eg READ | 0.248 | 0.56 | −1.56 | +2.34 | 0.064 |\n| eg LOCATE | 0.174 | 0.24 | −1.40 | +2.11 | 0.165 |\n| eg bash build-test | 0.060 | 0.07 | −1.32 | +1.97 | 0.165 |\n| eg GIT | 0.018 | 0.06 | −0.41 | +0.61 | 0.190 |\n| eg EDIT | 0.038 | 0.07 | −0.86 | +1.29 | 0.280 |\n| eg bash run-interp | −0.032 | 0.03 | −0.90 | +1.36 | 0.440 |\n| eg SCRIPT | 0.068 | 0.15 | +0.12 | −0.18 | 0.643 |\n\n*near-definitional. **No individual category reaches p&lt;0.05.**\n\n**Payload-string re-searching — the equally-present test.** Baseline never saw the payload, so its column is the base rate for those exact strings:\n\n| | W-base | W-eg | L-base | L-eg |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| search terms present in the eg payload | 2.42 | **2.42** | 1.38 | **1.25** |\n| terms not in payload | 12.92 | 8.58 | 7.38 | 8.62 |\n\nPayload exposure changed payload-string re-searching by **+0.00 (W) and −0.13 (L)**. The previously-claimed \"re-finds text the payload already printed 5.58/7.25 per session\" is a **base rate, not a tool-induced defect** — the no-tool baseline greps for the same strings at the same rate. Defect dead.\n\n**Prompt/payload tax** (capability block + payload re-sent as cached prefix every turn): eg prompt is 6.1–12.9K chars larger; ×turns ≈ **5.16% of eg tokens in W vs 5.19% in L** — identical. Explains 10.6% of the mean loser overrun (+48.9%) and an equal share of the winner saving. Not a separator.\n\n**Prompt fairness verified across all 20 pairs**: eg-only = the same 29-line capability block + payload; baseline-only = 0 lines; **0 frugality-language asymmetries** (regex over minimi[sz]/efficien/frugal/token/concise/fewer turns/batch/budget). This cell is symmetric.\n\n**Payload feature presence** (inverted from expectation):\n\n| | W(12) | L(8) |\n|---|---|---|\n| COVERING TEST block | 1 (8%) | **4 (50%)** |\n| VERIFY line | 10 | 5 |\n| SAME-CONCEPT LITERAL | 6 | 4 |\n| impact payload nonempty | 9 | 7 |\n| payload chars (mean) | 6580 | 6879 |\n\nLosers got the COVERING TEST block **6× more often**. Direction is opposite to a \"missing test block causes test-hunting\" story.\n\n**Churn**: re-edits of the same file W 1.58→1.33, L 1.25→**2.75** (only loser-side metric with a &gt;2× within-arm move). `git checkout/restore/reset` identical (0.17/0.17, 0.38/0.38) — no revert cascades. Distinct /tmp paths W 3.17→5.17, L 5.12→6.12 (rises in both).\n\n**tool_result bytes/session** (context inflow): W-base 73132 → W-eg 60252; L-base 43665 → L-eg 52612. Bytes/op is flat: 1183/1399/1185/1218. corr(byte ratio, token ratio)=0.622 vs corr(op ratio, token ratio)=**0.953** → cost is driven by op count, not by result size.\n\n**Output tokens/op**: 636/712 (W) vs 814/716 (L) — the eg arm converges to ~715 in both groups. Reported ratios reproduce from `cc_out.json` usage to within 0.5 pt.\n\n## Measured negatives (metrics with no separation)\n\n- eg-arm total ops, per-tool counts, tokens: all AUC ≈ 0.50.\n- Distinct files touched, payload-files touched, edited-files∩payload.\n- Gold-file rank-1 rate in the payload (5/12 vs 3/8).\n- Package-install / provisioning: **decreases** in losers.\n- Contiguous-block clumpiness: same in the loser **baseline**.\n- Absolute tail length: driven by 2 of 8 losers; W excl-top-2 6.60 vs L excl-top-2 8.67, but full-set L 13.75 vs W 9.08 — unstable at this n.\n- Prompt/payload token tax: 5.16% vs 5.19%.\n- Payload-string re-grepping: base rate, not tool-induced.\n- Thinking-block count/op: 0.52/0.59/0.56/0.56.\n\n## Caveat\n\n**Thinking text is redacted in all 40 transcripts** (`thinking` field = empty string, signature present; 29 blocks in carbon-2752 alone). Reasoning *volume* is unmeasurable here; only block counts and `output_tokens` are available.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>114471</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>23</tool_uses><duration_ms>694953</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"b9db700b-04b5-45bc-96b3-ac53c9435ed1","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:35:31.402Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"b9db700b-04b5-45bc-96b3-ac53c9435ed1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgNoWqg9wUQNPP3fcydr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7542,"cache_read_input_tokens":741518,"output_tokens":2658,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7542,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2658,"cache_read_input_tokens":741518,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7542,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7542},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgNoQnHpLdsSGnNucnuN","type":"assistant","uuid":"d512d922-71ce-44a4-9e54-e072a3b89549","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:35:58.804Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"d512d922-71ce-44a4-9e54-e072a3b89549","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgNoWqg9wUQNPP3fcydr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The comparison agent returned, and it's the most valuable analysis of the session — it kills three of my remaining hypotheses and replaces them with a predictive law.\n\n**The law.** eg does a fixed amount of work; the *baseline* is what varies:\n\n| | eg arm | baseline arm |\n|---|---|---|\n| winners | 42.50 ops | **59.00** |\n| losers | 44.00 ops | **34.50** |\n| effect size | **d = −0.08, p = 0.97** | **d = +1.55, p = 0.0069** |\n| AUC (predicts win) | **0.495** | **0.865** |\n\nFitted: **`eg_ops = 14.16 + 0.588 · base_ops`**, break-even at **base_ops = 34.4**. Below that the tool *adds* ops; above it, removes them. Winners are 11/12 above the line; losers 4/8 below, and the 4 above are the 4 smallest losses. Rule accuracy 15/20. And tokens are superlinear in ops: `log(tokRat) = 1.207 · log(opRat)`, R² = 0.916.\n\n**Three of my levers are now dead, measured against the correct control:**\n\n1. **\"40% of post-edit ops re-hunt payload text\" — dead.** The agent measured the *baseline's* rate of searching for those same strings: 2.42 vs eg's 2.42 in winners, 1.38 vs 1.25 in losers. Payload exposure changed it by **+0.00 and −0.13**. It's a base rate; the no-tool arm greps for the same strings just as often. My classifier was counting ordinary searching.\n2. **\"Missing COVERING TEST causes test-hunting\" — inverted.** The block is present in **4/8 losers (50%)** versus **1/12 winners (8%)** — six times *more* often in losers.\n3. **\"Provisioning episode\" — one instance, not a pattern.** `package-install` *decreases* in losers (0.62 → 0.38), and normalised clumpiness is 0.13 in the loser **baseline** versus 0.14 in its eg arm, so the clumpiness pre-exists the tool.\n\nTwo more that matter: **calling the graph predicts a weaker win** (the 3 winners who used it averaged −23.7% vs −36.9% for the 9 who didn't), and the **payload tax is 5.16% vs 5.19%** — identical across groups, not a separator.\n\nAnd the shape of the difference: winners' saving is **65.6% LOCATE+EXEC**; the loser overrun is **77.6% EXEC+READ+EDIT with LOCATE only 14.5%**. So the tool does remove locate work where there's locate work to remove — the loser overrun simply isn't locate work.\n\n**What this means for the goal, concretely.** The only tool-side lever the law leaves is the **14.16-op intercept** — the work eg does regardless of the baseline. Cut that and every instance improves, including the winners. Sample composition is the other term, but that's selection, not a tool improvement.\n\nOne caveat the agent flagged that limits future forensics: **thinking text is redacted in all 40 transcripts** (`thinking` present but empty), so reasoning volume is unmeasurable — only block counts and output tokens."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7542,"cache_read_input_tokens":741518,"output_tokens":2658,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7542,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2658,"cache_read_input_tokens":741518,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7542,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7542},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgNoQnHpLdsSGnNucnuN","type":"assistant","uuid":"21c50725-3b6a-4e46-b887-4d6a233aa8d1","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:36:10.622Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"