{"parentUuid":"819d26cb-439a-444e-9c60-3f3af6c469dd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgNvqLrcCDb95PY6GYYB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Update — rep30 has its first gated pairs and they look strong, and I checked the break-even law against the data.**\n\n**rep30, n=4 gated: −40.9%, CI [−55.1, −21.2], winners 4/4** — lucene −58%, caddy −52%, django −35%, ruff −7%.\n\nThat's well ahead of the 20-instance cell's −11.2%, and it's consistent with your instinct: rep30's baselines are simply more wasteful, which is where the tool pays. But n=4 with 7 of 60 jobs done, and today's n≤4 signals have reversed repeatedly — the same ruff instance is +35% in the 20-set and −7% here, and caddy is the instance whose baseline reads the gold line out of the Go module cache. So I'm not treating −40.9% as a number yet.\n\n**The break-even law holds at 15/20 on the PUB cell** — every instance with baseline ops > 34.4 should win:\n\n| misses | baseline ops | actual |\n|---|---|---|\n| ruff-15626 | 47 | +35% |\n| fmt-1683 | 39 | +27% |\n| phpspreadsheet-3570 | 48 | +31% |\n| redis-11734 | 39 | +96% |\n| three.js-25687 | 21 | −18% |\n\nFour of the five misses are instances just above the line (39–48 ops) that lost anyway, plus one below the line that won. So the law is sharpest at the extremes — everything at 54+ ops won, everything at 34 or below except three.js lost — and mushy in the 35–50 band, which is exactly where the marginal instances sit.\n\nThat gives a concrete read on the goal that doesn't depend on any of my dead hypotheses: **rep30 is a higher-baseline-ops sample than the official 20**, which is why it's starting at −40.9%. If that holds as n grows, the goal is met on rep30 — but on the sample composition, not on a tool improvement, and I'll say so plainly when I report it.\n\nTwo integrity caveats stand: rep30 runs with the **npm/pip/composer/go/cargo network hole open** and without cache isolation, and it includes caddy, carbon-3098 and fmt-2457 — two of which have confirmed leaks in the other cell."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1990,"cache_read_input_tokens":751721,"output_tokens":747,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1990,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":747,"cache_read_input_tokens":751721,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1990,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1990},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgNvjHUVrcRaqTHA5Sna","type":"assistant","uuid":"299feb34-02cd-4905-864d-8944e4c900db","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:37:29.435Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
