{"parentUuid":"846bf54f-6051-4801-973f-20e2c8d7c903","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgPNm3NNSzrym5bWLHhP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":722,"cache_read_input_tokens":756412,"output_tokens":1667,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":722,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1667,"cache_read_input_tokens":756412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":722,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":722},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgPNZPPRM8s5dTvMtHyG","type":"assistant","uuid":"44642f75-b7c2-4ea1-b2e1-3048e7bf3172","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:43:18.509Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"44642f75-b7c2-4ea1-b2e1-3048e7bf3172","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgPNm3NNSzrym5bWLHhP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Goal: −25% on the 20-instance official sample. Best measured on that sample: −11.2%. Gap: ~14 points. Not met.**\n\nEvery Opus configuration tried on that sample:\n\n| config | tokens | n | status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **PUB** — published prompt, prefetch | **−11.2%** [−27.8, +9.6] | 20 | best honest number |\n| CB — clamp + scaffold | +7.5% | 3 | killed on gates |\n| GC — gated clamp (symmetric) | +11.4% | 6 | killed on gates |\n| S1O — S1 clamp | +18.2% [+2.3, +37.2] | 19 | significant loss |\n| G40 — rich methodology both arms | +28.4% [+7.9, +54.8] | 19 | significant loss |\n| OFF — bare baseline / rich eg | −46.5% | 19 | **invalid**, asymmetric prompt |\n\nSeparately, **rep30 is at −40.9% (n=4 of 30, winners 4/4)** — but that's a *different instance set*, so it doesn't satisfy the goal as written, and n=4 is not a result.\n\n**What's been eliminated, with controls:** payload line numbers, ungated impact chaining, boilerplate queries, hit ordering, fabricated callers, missing/lint-only VERIFY, missing COVERING TEST (inverted — 6× more common in *losers*), \"re-finds payload text\" (base rate: baseline greps the same strings at 2.42 vs eg's 2.42), provisioning episodes (package-install *decreases* in losers), the covering-test mirror (inert on real checkouts), and more graph usage (predicts a *weaker* win: −23.7% vs −36.9%).\n\n**What the data leaves.** The fitted law is `eg_ops = 14.16 + 0.588 · base_ops`, break-even at 34.4 baseline ops, with `tokens = ops^1.207` (R² 0.916, now confirmed out of sample on rep30: predicted −38.6%, measured −40.9%). eg's own op count is statistically flat between winners and losers (d = −0.08, p = 0.97) while the baseline's is decisive (d = +1.55, p = 0.0069, AUC 0.865). So the single tool-side lever remaining is the **14.16-op intercept** — the work eg does regardless of the baseline. Nothing I've tried touches it.\n\nAnd the honest complication: **the −11.2% cell has a confirmed answer leak in one of its winners** (docusaurus `npm pack`'d the fixed release and transcribed the gold patch) and another winner that wins only because its baseline ran a two-compiler matrix (fmt-2457, 132% baseline-side). Closing the network hole will most likely move −11.2% *worse*, since three of four known leaks favour eg.\n\nSo: 14 points short on the goal's sample, with no lever currently sized to close it, and the measurement itself needs the egress fix before any number is quotable."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":722,"cache_read_input_tokens":756412,"output_tokens":1667,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":722,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1667,"cache_read_input_tokens":756412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":722,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":722},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgPNZPPRM8s5dTvMtHyG","type":"assistant","uuid":"bbeeee02-b86d-4dba-a9a9-82c67569551f","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:43:31.503Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
