{"parentUuid":"02f0c356-cca9-4fb3-8184-77b18ae0434f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d38ae0e6-bc81-4a3c-b8e9-271f667a25d0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016sFXTTQJymsAG7ogmwmB8c","type":"tool_result","content":"Command running in background with ID: bu6ic5r2q. Output is being written to: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208/tasks/bu6ic5r2q.output. You will be notified when it completes. To check interim output, use Read on that file path.\nSession cwd remains /Users/suhaan/devenv; directory changes made by the backgrounded command do not apply to subsequent commands.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"81865e67-a96a-473d-a3f1-7fae595e5e41","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:47:59.089Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"backgroundTaskId":"bu6ic5r2q","backgroundCwdHint":"Session cwd remains /Users/suhaan/devenv; directory changes made by the backgrounded command do not apply to subsequent commands."},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"02f0c356-cca9-4fb3-8184-77b18ae0434f","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"81865e67-a96a-473d-a3f1-7fae595e5e41","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgPkaSkChbAiGntMyFeo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Running across 10 instances × 2 binaries in the background.\n\n**What checking that plan changed.** It's a different diagnosis from anything I'd tested, and it explains my results better than my own hypotheses did:\n\n> *\"eg's problem is not retrieval recall — it is **aim**. It finds the correct file 100% of the time and then points at the wrong region of it.\"*\n\nlosers **32.4%** gold-line coverage at **5,513** payload bytes; winners **58.3%** at **3,964** bytes. File coverage is 100% in *both* groups, so it carries no signal.\n\nThat reconciles the thing I could never explain: pre-edit locate went **up** in all five of my Opus cells (+4% to +9%). Right file, wrong offset → the agent greps the file anyway → it pays for the payload *and* the exploration it triggered.\n\n**I verified the code-level cause in the source, both halves:**\n\n- `search_related.go:41` — *\"Deliberately NOT included: outgoing CALLS… already reached as co-members of the same unit\"*\n- `searchRelatedUnitMemberLimit = 12`, and line 568 disables the co-member route above that\n\nSo on a large unit **neither** route reaches the callee. redis-10095 is the clean case: gold at `t_list.c:501`, eg returns `t_list.c:577` (`lpopCommand` — a *lexical* match for \"LPOP\"), missing by 76 lines, while the reply-shaping bug sits in the helper it **calls**. The exclusion is sound for small units and leaves a hole exactly where the losses are.\n\n**And the plan's own step 2 says evaluate the unmerged `codex/eg-graphify-advertised-bench` branch before writing any code** — it exists locally with `fix(search): preserve hard file limits and coverage scores` and `keep legacy eligibility before widening`. I built it. On the three instances measured so far it changes payload bytes but **not coverage** (0%→0%, 2%→2%), so it's looking like it doesn't subsume F1 — the wider run will confirm.\n\nOne thing I'd flag: the plan's `--head-window-lines` note matches my own finding — widening the window measured **+18.9pt worse**. So the fix is moving the window's *centre* onto the line that will change, at the same byte budget, not emitting more. That's the one lever left that makes the payload *smaller*, and it's the only untested mechanism with a measured 26-point gap behind it."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":450,"cache_read_input_tokens":778559,"output_tokens":806,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":450,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":806,"cache_read_input_tokens":778559,"cache_creation_input_tokens":450,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":450},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgPkRrZoZT7i6uVvZZ1Z","type":"assistant","uuid":"190de5b2-ff2b-4ff7-9187-594b09adc2b2","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:48:16.581Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
