{"parentUuid":"6dc7f89e-7a54-49f0-9f03-a9d1718f72ff","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgPnof3ZBhou6Q556CVW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Update — 17 of 60 done. rep30 is at −24.6%, n=8, and the CI now excludes zero.**\n\n| gated pairs | tokens | CI | winners |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 8 | **−24.6%** | **[−42.7, −0.9]** | 6/8 |\n\nlucene −58%, caddy −52%, carbon-3098 −39%, django −35%, docusaurus-9183 −19%, ruff −7% · fastlane +31%, faker +33%.\n\nIt settled from −40.9% (n=4) to −24.6% (n=8) as the first two losers landed — that's the drift I'd expect, and it's now hovering right at the goal threshold with the interval barely clear of zero. Two-thirds of the sample still to come, so this is the least stable point in the run; I'm not calling it either way.\n\nWorth noting the sample effect you predicted is showing up: rep30's baselines are wastier, and its winners are the same instances that win on the official 20 (lucene, caddy, django) while its losers are ones the 20-set doesn't contain (fastlane, faker).\n\nThe line-coverage run has produced no output yet — it's doing 20 cold index builds (10 instances × 2 binaries, each with its own cache dir), and lucene alone took ~40s earlier. That's the measurement that decides whether the unmerged codex branch subsumes F1, so it's worth the wait rather than a rerun.\n\nStanding caveats unchanged: rep30 carries the open **npm/pip/composer/go/cargo** network hole and no cache isolation, and it includes caddy and carbon-3098 — caddy being the instance whose *baseline* read the gold line out of the Go module cache in the other cell. So if this lands at or past −25%, the number still needs the egress fix before it's quotable."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":921,"cache_read_input_tokens":779818,"output_tokens":599,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fet