{"parentUuid":"e5cedf20-db81-4adc-9725-805de18a5301","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"queued_command","prompt":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>bu6ic5r2q</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_016sFXTTQJymsAG7ogmwmB8c</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208/tasks/bu6ic5r2q.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Background command \"Line coverage across the plan's loser and winner sets, both binaries\" completed (exit code 0)</summary>\n</task-notification>","commandMode":"task-notification","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:50:49.478Z"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a56bf652-37aa-4eae-b80c-f735c948bb85","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:50:49.478Z","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"a56bf652-37aa-4eae-b80c-f735c948bb85","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgPyUUwJnrGNLrZSx1zG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Prediction, quantified two ways — and they disagree by 10×, which is the honest answer.**\n\n| route | basis | per loser | 20-set geomean |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **A — the plan's own fit** | 9.6% tokens per residual shell call; 26pt coverage gap ≈ 3 calls | **−29%** | **−22.6%** |\n| **B — my category decomposition** | LOCATE is only **14.5%** of the +76-op loser overrun → 1.4 ops/loser, via `tokens = ops^1.207` | **−3.8%** | **−12.7%** |\n\nGoal is −25%, current −11.2%. So Route A gets close and Route B barely moves.\n\nThe disagreement is a real, identifiable unknown, not hedging: **how many residual shell calls does one point of line-coverage buy back?** The plan asserts 9.6% tokens per call and infers the calls; my paired decomposition measures where the loser overrun actually sits and finds LOCATE is the *smallest* recoverable slice — the overrun is 77.6% EXEC+READ+EDIT. If aim fixes only touch LOCATE, Route B is right and this is worth ~1.5 points. If misaim *causes* the downstream EXEC/READ/EDIT churn too, Route A is right.\n\nNothing I've measured settles that, and the line-coverage run just finished, so I can now test the link directly — correlate per-instance line coverage against per-instance residual locate ops. That's the discriminator, it's free, and it decides whether F1/F2 is worth implementing or is another 2-point lever.\n\n**On the branch question the plan told me to settle first:** the codex branch changed payload bytes but not coverage on every instance measured so far, so it does not appear to subsume F1.\n\nAnd separately, **rep30 is at −24.6% [−42.7, −0.9], n=8** — at the goal line on that sample, though still carrying the network hole and 22 jobs outstanding."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"u