{"parentUuid":"cd9f944f-a8f2-4ee4-ae10-7838ae96e5e2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgQBm3vAqqJ96TvefmMP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1196,"cache_read_input_tokens":788082,"output_tokens":2061,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1196,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2061,"cache_read_input_tokens":788082,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1196,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1196},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgQBcdAAbhJbodSev8Ht","type":"assistant","uuid":"17fa6ee8-5843-411b-bff1-fc3371f2bde2","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:54:02.562Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"17fa6ee8-5843-411b-bff1-fc3371f2bde2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgQBm3vAqqJ96TvefmMP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Two results, one solid and one that limits the answer.**\n\n**Solid: the codex branch is settled — it changes nothing.** Coverage identical on all 10 instances, mean **4.5% both**, while payload bytes move (redis 2092→3140, micropython 2699→4304). Same measurement applied to both binaries, so that comparison holds regardless of anything else. Per the plan's own step 2, it does **not** subsume F1.\n\n**Limiting: I could not reproduce the plan's coverage split.** I agree with it on the low instances and disagree on every high one:\n\n| instance | plan | mine |\n|---|---|---|\n| redis-10095 | 0% | 0% ✓ |\n| gson-2158 | 0% | 0% ✓ |\n| fmt-2457 | 3% | 2% ✓ |\n| rubocop-13680 | 0% | 0% ✓ |\n| micropython-15898 | 0% | 0% ✓ |\n| gson-2479 | 57% | 43% ~ |\n| **django-13821** | **50%** | **0%** |\n| **lucene-13170** | **100%** | **0%** |\n| **faker-2970** | **100%** | **0%** |\n| **immutable-2006** | **100%** | **0%** |\n\nThe tell is in my own output: I detected only **2 gold lines** for lucene and faker, 6 for django. Real patches have more than that, so my anchor-matching resolver is under-detecting on multi-hunk patches — my bug, not the plan's. Which means I can't yet validate the `9.6% tokens per residual shell call` conversion that Route A rests on, and I can't run the coverage-vs-residual-ops correlation that would collapse A and B.\n\n**So the direct answer to your question: taking the plan at face value, Route A predicts −22.6% on the 20-instance sample.** That's the aim fix delivering its full 26-point coverage gain at 3 residual calls saved per loser, and it still lands **~2 points short of −25%**. Clearing the goal that way needs ~3.5 calls per loser, not 3. My own decomposition gives −12.7% for the same fix, because LOCATE is only 14.5% of the +76-op loser overrun.\n\nMeanwhile **rep30 is at −24.6% [−42.7, −0.9], n=8** — which is at the goal line on that sample, and currently the closest thing to meeting it, though it still needs the egress fix and 22 more jobs."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1196,"cache_read_input_tokens":788082,"output_tokens":2061,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1196,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2061,"cache_read_input_tokens":788082,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1196,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1196},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgQBcdAAbhJbodSev8Ht","type":"assistant","uuid":"f96d6f66-f7a1-4cd3-8e45-873c58fd5a4d","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:54:12.146Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
