{"parentUuid":"593fad9c-e1eb-4dc7-8d2c-61d17263f688","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgQYGDQwU4z3TLy5m683","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":751,"cache_read_input_tokens":793204,"output_tokens":2271,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":751,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2271,"cache_read_input_tokens":793204,"cache_creation_input_tokens":751,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":751},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgQY6ktc9J3w8WsAtAci","type":"assistant","uuid":"2d0d1a03-4c18-4318-87a5-1eeae7924b85","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:58:41.502Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"2d0d1a03-4c18-4318-87a5-1eeae7924b85","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgQYGDQwU4z3TLy5m683","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"My honest assessment: **it's the best-grounded document in this entire program, and it's still not sufficient for the goal.**\n\n**What makes it credible — three things nothing else I tested has:**\n\n1. **It explains my most robust finding, which nothing else did.** Pre-edit locate went *up* in all five Opus cells (+3.7% to +9%). I had no mechanism for that. \"Right file, wrong region → the agent greps the file anyway\" explains it exactly, and explains why the loss is bidirectional: you pay for the misleading payload *and* the exploration it triggers.\n2. **The root cause is in source, not in statistics, and I verified both halves.** `search_related.go:41` excludes outgoing CALLS on the reasoning that callees are \"already reached as co-members of the same unit\"; `searchRelatedUnitMemberLimit = 12` disables that fallback above 12 members. So on large units neither route reaches the callee. redis-10095 is textbook: gold at `t_list.c:501`, eg returns `t_list.c:577` (`lpopCommand` — a lexical match on \"LPOP\"), and the bug is in the helper it calls.\n3. **It's budget-neutral by construction** — move the window's centre, don't widen it. Every lever I tried this session added payload, and it correctly cites `--head-window-lines` at **+18.9pt worse**, which independently matches my data. It also lists a \"do NOT retry\" set that overlaps my own measured negatives, and F4 (retire file coverage) is right — I confirmed file coverage is 100% in both groups.\n\n**Where I'd push back:**\n\n- **Its token prediction rests entirely on one unvalidated conversion.** `9.6% per residual shell call` is fitted on a different session set. My paired decomposition says LOCATE is only **14.5%** of the +76-op loser overrun — the rest is EXEC+READ+EDIT. Take the plan's conversion and the fix is worth ~11 points; take mine and it's worth ~1.5.\n- **Even at face value it predicts −22.6% on the 20-set** — short of −25%. So it's necessary-but-not-sufficient by its own arithmetic.\n- **n=14, and it admits two winners sit at 0% coverage** — so line coverage separates group means, not individual instances. That's a real limit on using it as an offline gate.\n- I couldn't reproduce its per-instance coverage on 4 of 10 — my resolver's fault, but it means those anchors are unverified by me.\n\n**Where I think my own pushback may be wrong:** Route B assumes an aim fix only touches LOCATE. If landing on the right lines also prevents wrong edits and re-verification downstream, it would cut EXEC/READ/EDIT too — which is precisely the causal chain the plan claims. That's the difference between 1.5 points and 11, and it's decidable: correlate per-instance line coverage against residual ops. That needs my gold-line resolver fixed first (it under-detects multi-hunk patches — 2 lines for lucene is clearly wrong).\n\n**What I'd do:** fix the resolver, run the correlation on all 30 instances I have graphs for, and implement F1 only if coverage predicts residual ops. F1 is narrow — enable the callee hop only where the co-member fallback is already off and the body-match signal is absent — so it's a contained change with a free offline gate. I would not implement F2 first; multi-span allocation is where a budget-neutral claim is easiest to break."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":751,"cache_read_input_tokens":793204,"output_tokens":2271,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":751,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2271,"cache_read_input_tokens":793204,"cache_creation_input_tokens":751,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":751},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgQY6ktc9J3w8WsAtAci","type":"assistant","uuid":"3a96a8f7-3004-4e75-80be-1976ee1a445f","timestamp":"2026-08-03T19:58:55.626Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
