{"parentUuid":"b9795e35-abd8-45b8-8e44-f0eecb29d3b6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgQoYpDuwQSzZTfFvTfC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Clean A/B now — and note `eg-agx` sha is **`f6a18d3ca7c2`**, exactly the binary the plan names. **The codex branch does not move coverage** (0.5% both). That verdict is now valid.\n\nBut the same binary the plan used still gives me **lucene 0%** where the plan reports **100%** — so the disagreement isn't the binary. The plan's corpus is DeepSWE v1.1 (its list includes `redis-10068`, `redis-11510`, which aren't in my sets), so it's a different instance corpus and different queries. On instances we both cover we agree on the **losers** (redis-10095 0%/0%, fmt-2457 3%/2%) and disagree on the **winner**.\n\nThat matters, because the plan's central claim is the 32.4% vs 58.3% split. Testing it directly on my own corpus, where I have token outcomes:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2248,"cache_read_input_tokens":798063,"output_tokens":1811,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2248,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1811,"cache_read_input_tokens":798063,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2248,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2248},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgQoQTBNSmTCCtqBT6fh","type":"assistant","uuid":"2a8739a4-f6df-4db5-887a-004609944727","timestamp":"2026-08-03T20:02:11.154Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","sl