{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01P6EtEZrtka8BvMWBZeka4V","lastSequenceNum":0}
{"parentUuid":"487608df-d494-469c-ab7e-e39682d450ee","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgQz6qLPs2bjuvcZF9Lr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**This settles it, and it's a striking confirmation of the plan's diagnosis — stronger than the plan itself claims.**\n\n**File coverage: 9/9 = 100%**, exactly as the plan reports. So my measurement works. And in every single case the payload lands in the right file at the **wrong region**:\n\n| instance | gold line | payload's spans in that same file | miss |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| lucene-13170 | 148 | 34-36, 27, 181-188, 118-124 | brackets it, never covers it |\n| caddy-5995 | 133 | 343-465, 59 | −74 / +210 |\n| carbon-3098 | 497 | 1201-1228 | +704 |\n| django-13821 | 64 | 431-487 | +367 |\n| docusaurus-9183 | 313 | 375 | +62 |\n| ruff-15626 | 25 | 37-41 | +12 |\n| fastlane-19765 | 101 | 357-366, 214-229 | +113 |\n| faker-2970 | 65 | 33-49 | −16 |\n| fmt-2457 | 357 | 682 | +325 |\n\n**Right file 100% of the time, right region 0% of the time.** That is the plan's thesis — *\"not retrieval recall, it is aim\"* — reproduced independently on my corpus, with the plan's own binary.\n\nTwo ways my result differs from the plan's, and both matter:\n\n**It's worse than the plan says.** The plan reports losers at 32.4% and winners at 58.3%. I measure **~0% for both** — including its own named winners (lucene, faker, django). So on my corpus there is no winner/loser split to close, because *nothing* is aimed correctly.\n\n**Which cuts both ways for the goal.** It kills the plan's F1 sizing argument — you can't recover a 26-point gap that isn't there — but it makes the underlying defect much larger than diagnosed. The lucene case is the cleanest: four separate spans printed from the gold file (34-36, 27, 181-188, 118-124) and gold sits at 148, bracketed on both sides and never covered. That's not a near-miss, it's systematic misaim.\n\nAnd it finally explains the one thing that held across all five of my Opus cells and that no other hypothesis touched: **pre-edit locate rose every time (+3.7% to +9%)**. The agent is handed the correct file with a wrong offset, so it greps the file itself — paying for the payload *and* the exploration it triggered.\n\nSo the aim defect is real, verified in source (`search_related.go:41` excluding outgoing CALLS, with the co-member fallback dead above 12 members), and now measured at 100% file / ~0% line on nine instances. Whether fixing it is worth 2 points or 11 is still the open question — but it's the first mechanism this session that is both confirmed and untried."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2339,"cache_read_input_tokens":803702,"output_tokens":938,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2339,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":938,"cache_read_input_tokens":803702,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2339,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2339},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgQywRHkSJ5oBj7cahxp","type":"assistant","uuid":"30770178-15c5-4fef-ac4c-a9bfaa8cf0a7","timestamp":"2026-08-03T20:04:27.306Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
