r-cooking-cupcake"}
{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"e17ef221-8ea7-44cd-89bb-80194e1be0be","snapshotMessageId":"d768a22f-f086-4b2e-a07d-6661fe27c728","trackingPath":"/Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench/agentic-swebench/HANDOFF-OPUS-TOKENS.md","backup":{"backupFileName":null,"version":1,"backupTime":"2026-08-03T20:08:20.895Z","realParentDir":"/Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench/agentic-swebench"},"timestamp":"2026-08-03T20:08:20.938Z"}
{"parentUuid":"a96f89f7-1f3a-4f7a-8045-70bb2484a2f9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgRCajCrG5EAVQjGCjen","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MWPqdV7TBRuhhyRoYijQa4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench/agentic-swebench/HANDOFF-OPUS-TOKENS.md","content":"# Handoff — Opus token savings on entire-graph, measured 2026-08-03\n\nGoal given: **Opus ≥ −25% tokens** on a 20-instance sample of SWE-bench Multilingual.\n**Not met.** Best honest number: **−11.2%**. This document is everything needed to continue without\nrepeating the work, including the parts that wasted the most time.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The number, and the config that produces it\n\n```\nPROMPT_FAMILY unset · PUBLISHED_EXACT=1 · CC_MODEL=opus · CLAUDE_EFFORT=high\nEG_PREFETCH=1 EG_PREFETCH_IMPACT=1 · EG_TOPK=5 EG_CONF_TIER=0 EG_TOPK_SHOW=10\nEG_MAXBYTES=24576 EG_SNIPPET=6 EG_MAX_PER_FILE=3 EG_VERIFY_MODE=full EG_PROFILE=full EG_TIER=0\nGQ_SEARCH_CAP=1 · CC_MAX_TURNS=120 CC_TIMEOUT=3600\nTASKS_FILE=tasks/opus20_official.json · binary /tmp/eg-f19 (eg-consolidated @ 024f25a)\n```\nWorker: `/tmp/mcptest/pubworker.sh`. Scorer: `tools/model_cmp.py`.\n\n**Result: tokens −11.2% CI [−27.8, +9.6], usd −8.4%, output −13.1% [−23.3, −1.9], winners 12/20, n=20.**\n\n`PUBLISHED_EXACT=1` emits Anthropic's published SWE-bench Verified prompt verbatim to **both** arms;\neg additionally gets one capability paragraph + the prefetched search/impact payload. Verified\nsymmetric by line-diff on emitted `prompt.txt`, coaching-language scan = 0 in both arms.\n`CC_MAX_TURNS=120` matters: the baseline averages **50.2** turns, so the default cap of 50\nright-censors the BASELINE specifically and understates its cost.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Every configuration measured (Opus, same 20 instances unless noted)\n\n| config | baseline ops | eg ops | ops Δ | ktok/session | **tokens** | n |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **PUB** — published prompt + prefetch | 35.7 | 31.7 | −11.2% | 2729k | **−11.2%** [−27.8,+9.6] | 20 |\n| FRUGAL — rich methodology both arms, frugal shared block | 7.0 | 5.0 | −28.6% | 279k | −14.0% | 23 (rep30) |\n| CB — clamp + published scaffold | 10.5 | 8.3 | −20.6% | 345k | +7.5% | 3 |\n| GC — gated clamp, symmetric | 11.5 | 12.0 | +4.3% | 378k | +11.4% | 6 |\n| S1O — S1 mirrored clamp | 4.6 | 4.3 | −8.0% | 175k | +18.2% [+2.3,+37.2] | 19 |\n| G40 — rich methodology + published scaffold | 23.8 | 28.7 | +21.1% | 1300k | +28.4% [+7.9,+54.8] | 19 |\n| R30PUB — PUB config on rep30 | 29.4 | 27.5 | −6.5% | 2468k | −16.5% [−32.8,+4.1] | **14 of 30, PARTIAL** |\n| ~~OFF~~ | 39.0 | 27.5 | −29.6% | — | ~~−46.5%~~ | **INVALID** |\n\n**OFF is invalid and must never be quoted.** `EG_CAPABILITY_ONLY` was checked in `tool_block()` but\nnever in `briefed_tool_block()`, and every cell used the `briefed` family — so the flag was dead while\n`BASE_CAPABILITY_ONLY` worked. The baseline lost its 5-step methodology while eg kept its 4-step one\n(24 lines, 116 words, ending \"STOP. No re-search, no grep to double-check\"). Now wired; the same class\nof bug recurred later with `BASE_GATED_CLAMP` (wired into `tool_block` but not the vendor family).\n**Always diff emitted `prompt.txt`, never trust config.**\n\n---\n\n## 3. The two quantitative laws (use these to predict before spending)\n\n**Law 1 — outcome is set by the BASELINE's wastefulness, not by eg.**\n```\neg_ops = 14.16 + 0.588 · base_ops        break-even at base_ops = 34.4\n```\neg's op count is statistically flat between winners and losers (**d = −0.08, p = 0.97**); the\nbaseline's is decisive (**d = +1.55, p = 0.0069**, AUC 0.865 vs 0.495). Rule accuracy 15/20; it is\nsharp above 54 ops and below 34, mushy in the 35–50 band.\n\n**Law 2 — tokens are superlinear in ops.**\n```\nlog(tokRatio) = 1.207 · log(opRatio)      R² = 0.916\n```\nConfirmed out of sample: rep30 ops −31.2% → predicted −38.6%, measured −40.9%. 94–96% of tokens are\n`cache_read`, so each extra op re-reads the whole accumulated context.\n\n**Corollary — the payload tax is a pure function of session size:** ~0 at 2729k, +7 at 1300k, +18 to\n+28 below 400k. So −25% requires ops ≤ −25% **and** a long session. Every clamp config sits at\n175–378k where the tax alone exceeds the op saving. That is why CB cut 20.6% of ops and still lost.\n\n---\n\n## 4. The confirmed, untried lever: **aim**\n\nMeasured with `/tmp/eg-agx` (entire-graph @ `afd5a1c`, sha `f6a18d3ca7c2`) on 9 rep30 instances,\ngold lines resolved by locating hunk context in the base file (hunk headers are invalid at base —\nfmtlib is off by +272):\n\n| | result |\n|---|---|\n| gold **FILE** in payload | **9/9 = 100%** |\n| gold **LINE** covered by a printed span | **0/9 ≈ 0%** |\n\n| instance | gold line | payload's spans in that same file |\n|---|---|---|\n| lucene-13170 | 148 | 34-36, 27, 181-188, 118-124 — brackets it, never covers it |\n| caddy-5995 | 133 | 343-465, 59 |\n| carbon-3098 | 497 | 1201-1228 |\n| django-13821 | 64 | 431-487 |\n| docusaurus-9183 | 313 | 375 |\n| ruff-15626 | 25 | 37-41 |\n| fastlane-19765 | 101 | 357-366, 214-229 |\n| faker-2970 | 65 | 33-49 |\n| fmt-2457 | 357 | 682 |\n\n**Right file always, right region never.** This is the only mechanism that explains the one result\nthat held across all five Opus cells: **pre-edit locate went UP every time (+3.7% to +9%)**. The agent\ngets the correct file at a wrong offset, greps it anyway, and pays twice.\n\n**Root cause, verified in source** (`internal/sem/search_related.go`):\n- line 41: *\"Deliberately NOT included: outgoing CALLS … already reached as co-members of the same unit\"*\n- line 62: `searchRelatedUnitMemberLimit = 12`; line 568 disables the co-member route above it\n\nSo on a large unit **neither** route reaches the callee. redis-10095 is textbook: gold at\n`src/t_list.c:501`, eg returns `t_list.c:577` (`lpopCommand`, a lexical match on \"LPOP\") — the\nreply-shaping bug is in the helper it *calls*.\n\nFull diagnosis and the F1/F2/F3 proposals: **`/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph/TOKEN-ACCURACY-PLAN.md`**.\nTwo corrections to it from this session:\n1. Its step-2 gate is **cleared**: the unmerged `codex/eg-graphify-advertised-bench` branch does\n   **not** move line coverage (clean A/B, same codebase, coverage identical, payload bytes differ).\n2. Its 32.4%-vs-58.3% winner/loser split does **not** reproduce on this corpus — I measure ~0% for\n   both. So the F1 sizing argument (close a 26-point gap) does not hold here, but the underlying\n   defect is **larger** than diagnosed, not smaller.\n\n**Sizing is the open question**, and the two available routes differ 10×:\n- plan's fit (9.6% tokens per residual shell call × ~3 calls) → −29%/loser → **−22.6%** on the 20-set\n- my decomposition (LOCATE is only **14.5%** of the +76-op loser overrun) → −3.8%/loser → **−12.7%**\n\n**The discriminator, not yet run:** correlate per-instance gold-line coverage against per-instance\nresidual locate ops. If coverage predicts residual ops, the plan's route is right and F1 is worth\n~11 points. Tooling for it exists: `/tmp/mcptest/linecov.py` (resolver verified correct against patch\nshapes — lucene 1 hunk/1+/1− = 2 gold lines, django 4+/2− = 6).\n\n---\n\n## 5. MEASUREMENT INTEGRITY — fix before quoting any number\n\n`tools/netjail/` blocks `curl wget git gh ssh scp rsync nc ncat socat aria2c xh http https`.\nIt does **not** block **npm, yarn, pip, composer, go, cargo** — and every one can fetch a post-fix\nrelease of the repo under test. Three confirmed leaks, in both arms, in cells quoted above:\n\n| instance | arm | leak | that instance's result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| docusaurus-10130 | **eg** | `npm pack @docusaurus/core@3.4.0` → extracted `brokenLinks.js` → grepped it → **the next tool call is the Edit with that content detranspiled**. The issue number `10116` in the patch appears nowhere in the prompt. | **−38% \"winner\"** in the −11.2% cell |\n| caddy-5995 | **baseline** | read `~/go/pkg/mod/…caddy/v2@v2.11.4/replacer.go` (gold line verbatim) **and** the PR's own new test fixture, copied it into the checkout, wrote a test reproducing `test_patch` | −56% winner; 27 of 66 baseline ops |\n| carbon-2752 | **eg** | unzipped `~/Library/Caches/composer/files/nesbot/carbon/*.zip` → gold regex, transcribed into `patch.diff` | +107% loser |\n\nAlso: **fmt-2457's swings are 132% baseline-side** — eg's absolute cost *falls* PUB→G40 (4.25M→2.94M)\nwhile the baseline collapses (5.16M→1.13M). Its PUB \"win\" was bought by 17 baseline messages running a\ntwo-compiler `orig-vs-new` matrix (`g++-15`: 7 occurrences baseline, 0 eg). Treat that instance as noise.\n\n**Required fixes:** netjail shims for registry-fetch subcommands (`npm pack|install <pkg>`, `yarn add`,\n`pip download|install`, `composer require`, `go get`, `cargo add`) while leaving local provisioning\nintact; plus per-instance cache isolation — already implemented in `/tmp/mcptest/s1worker.sh`\n(`GOMODCACHE GOPATH GOCACHE COMPOSER_HOME COMPOSER_CACHE_DIR CARGO_HOME GEM_HOME GEM_PATH\nnpm_config_cache MAVEN_ARGS=-Dmaven.repo.local`).\nThree of the four known leaks favour eg, so closing them will most likely make −11.2% **worse**.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Refuted — do NOT retry. Each cost a cell or a day.\n\nEvery item below was killed by a **winner control**: the same pattern is equally present in the\ninstances the tool wins on, so it cannot explain a loss. A 5-agent sweep produced 38 candidate\ndefects; **27 of 28 adjudicated were refuted this way.**\n\n| claim | how it died |\n|---|---|\n| payload bodies carry no line numbers | true in **20/20** instances incl. every winner. Also `internal/cli/search.go:473` documents that numbering bodies **breaks `Edit` anchors** (agents copy snippet text as `old_string`), and `focus=` already ships |\n| `impact` blind-chained to an ungated rank-1 | off-gold-file target in **7/12 winners**, in *more* degenerate form in the two largest wins |\n| query polluted by GitHub issue-template boilerplate | 2/6 control winners have boilerplate queries producing boilerplate top hits |\n| hits printed out of score order | 5/20 payloads, incl. winners lucene (−52%) and vuejs (−24%) |\n| missing / lint-only `VERIFY` | partial corr collapses +0.184 → **+0.091**; by class **lint-only is BEST** (−24.6%), `none` worst (+20.5%) but contains 2 winners |\n| missing `COVERING TEST` causes test-hunting | **inverted** — present in 4/8 losers (50%) vs 1/12 winners (8%) |\n| \"40% of post-edit ops re-hunt payload text\" | **base rate.** Baseline searches the same strings at 2.42/session vs eg's 2.42 (W) and 1.38 vs 1.25 (L). Payload exposure changes it by +0.00 / −0.13 |\n| provisioning episodes cause the loss | `package-install` **decreases** in losers (0.62→0.38); clumpiness 0.13 in the loser **baseline** vs 0.14 in its eg arm |\n| get the agent to use the graph more | tripling usage (0.20→3.00 calls/session) measured **worse**: caddy −56%→−13%, mean +17.8pt. The 3 winners that called it averaged −23.7% vs −36.9% for the 9 that didn't |\n| index tests (lift `graph_exclude.globs`) | rebuild indexes 4,748 test symbols but search output is **byte-identical**; the gold test was already at rank 2 |\n| extend the covering-test path mirror | 10/12 in a unit test, **byte-identical payloads** on real checkouts — improved the wrong path (`COVERING TEST` comes from ranked results, the mirror only feeds `VERIFY`) |\n| prefetch a test-scoped search (`EG_PREFETCH_TEST`) | found the gold test in **1 of 4**; the query that worked came from the issue text, not the payload |\n| the published prompt's \"explore the repo\" step causes it | only **9%** of first-four pre-edit ops are structure exploration |\n| widen the window (`--head-window-lines` + top-k 20) | **+18.9pt worse** (prior measurement, independently consistent) |\n| payload/prompt token tax explains the split | **5.16%** (W) vs **5.19%** (L) — identical |\n\n---\n\n## 7. Reproduce\n\n```sh\ncd /Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench/agentic-swebench\n# one cell, 40 sessions, ~2h at parallelism 10\nbash /tmp/mcptest/launch.sh /tmp/mcptest/pubworker.sh /tmp/mcptest/pubjobs.txt 10 /tmp/mcptest/pub.log\npython3 tools/model_cmp.py \"PUB_r1_baseline,PUB_r1_eg,label\"\n# aim measurement (free, offline)\npython3 /tmp/mcptest/linecov.py apache__lucene-13170 redis__redis-10095 ...\n```\n\n**Non-negotiables**\n- Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped **symmetrically**.\n- `CENSORED` (`subtype == error_max_turns`) must be 0 per arm.\n- Round trips = unique assistant `message.id`, never `num_turns` (it is `tool_calls + 1`).\n- Parallelism ≤ ~20. Above ~30, empty patches ran 14–27% vs 0% at ~15, and arm symmetry breaks.\n- **Never score a partial cell.** rep30 read −40.9% (n=4) → −24.6% (n=8) → −13.9% (n=10) → −16.5% (n=14).\n- Launcher: use `/tmp/mcptest/launch.sh` (bash, jobs on fd 3). `xargs -P … -I{}` mangles input on\n  macOS, and zsh does not word-split unquoted `$VAR` — that produced a jobs file with 38 of 40 lines\n  malformed and cost two wasted launches.\n- Thinking text is **redacted** in all transcripts (`thinking` present but empty), so reasoning volume\n  is unmeasurable; only block counts and `output_tokens` are available.\n\n## 8. What I would do next, in order\n\n1. **Close the leaks** (§5) and re-measure PUB. Nothing is quotable until this is done, and it will\n   probably make the number worse. One cell, 40 sessions.\n2. **Run the aim discriminator** (§4) — free, offline, decides whether F1 is worth ~11 points or ~2.\n3. **Only if it clears: implement F1** narrowly — enable the callee hop only where the co-member\n   fallback is already off (`len(members) > searchRelatedUnitMemberLimit`) **and** the body-match\n   signal is absent. Budget-neutral: move the window's centre, never widen it. Do **not** start with\n   F2 (multi-span allocation) — that is where a budget-neutral claim is easiest to break.\n4. Gate on gold-**line** coverage offline, then on session tokens **and graded resolves**. File\n   coverage is 100% on winners and losers alike and must be retired as a metric.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1598,"cache_read_input_tokens":808608,"output_tokens":6334,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1598,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6334,"cache_read_input_tokens":808608,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1598,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1598},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgRCSEEChvirtsDFPQr3","type":"assistant","uuid":"e17ef221-8ea7-44cd-89bb-80194e1be0be","timestamp":"2026-08-03T20:08:20.886Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"e17ef221-8ea7-44cd-89bb-80194e1be0be","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c1703aa1-e0d0-482e-bb6d-ed8597547394","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MWPqdV7TBRuhhyRoYijQa4","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench/agentic-swebench/HANDOFF-OPUS-TOKENS.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"b630b6f1-e4c3-4013-a8cd-ea636d7f150a","timestamp":"2026-08-03T20:08:20.955Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench/agentic-swebench/HANDOFF-OPUS-TOKENS.md","content":"# Handoff — Opus token savings on entire-graph, measured 2026-08-03\n\nGoal given: **Opus ≥ −25% tokens** on a 20-instance sample of SWE-bench Multilingual.\n**Not met.** Best honest number: **−11.2%**. This document is everything needed to continue without\nrepeating the work, including the parts that wasted the most time.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The number, and the config that produces it\n\n```\nPROMPT_FAMILY unset · PUBLISHED_EXACT=1 · CC_MODEL=opus · CLAUDE_EFFORT=high\nEG_PREFETCH=1 EG_PREFETCH_IMPACT=1 · EG_TOPK=5 EG_CONF_TIER=0 EG_TOPK_SHOW=10\nEG_MAXBYTES=24576 EG_SNIPPET=6 EG_MAX_PER_FILE=3 EG_VERIFY_MODE=full EG_PROFILE=full EG_TIER=0\nGQ_SEARCH_CAP=1 · CC_MAX_TURNS=120 CC_TIMEOUT=3600\nTASKS_FILE=tasks/opus20_official.json · binary /tmp/eg-f19 (eg-consolidated @ 024f25a)\n```\nWorker: `/tmp/mcptest/pubworker.sh`. Scorer: `tools/model_cmp.py`.\n\n**Result: tokens −11.2% CI [−27.8, +9.6], usd −8.4%, output −13.1% [−23.3, −1.9], winners 12/20, n=20.**\n\n`PUBLISHED_EXACT=1` emits Anthropic's published SWE-bench Verified prompt verbatim to **both** arms;\neg additionally gets one capability paragraph + the prefetched search/impact payload. Verified\nsymmetric by line-diff on emitted `prompt.txt`, coaching-language scan = 0 in both arms.\n`CC_MAX_TURNS=120` matters: the baseline averages **50.2** turns, so the default cap of 50\nright-censors the BASELINE specifically and understates its cost.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Every configuration measured (Opus, same 20 instances unless noted)\n\n| config | baseline ops | eg ops | ops Δ | ktok/session | **tokens** | n |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **PUB** — published prompt + prefetch | 35.7 | 31.7 | −11.2% | 2729k | **−11.2%** [−27.8,+9.6] | 20 |\n| FRUGAL — rich methodology both arms, frugal shared block | 7.0 | 5.0 | −28.6% | 279k | −14.0% | 23 (rep30) |\n| CB — clamp + published scaffold | 10.5 | 8.3 | −20.6% | 345k | +7.5% | 3 |\n| GC — gated clamp, symmetric | 11.5 | 12.0 | +4.3% | 378k | +11.4% | 6 |\n| S1O — S1 mirrored clamp | 4.6 | 4.3 | −8.0% | 175k | +18.2% [+2.3,+37.2] | 19 |\n| G40 — rich methodology + published scaffold | 23.8 | 28.7 | +21.1% | 1300k | +28.4% [+7.9,+54.8] | 19 |\n| R30PUB — PUB config on rep30 | 29.4 | 27.5 | −6.5% | 2468k | −16.5% [−32.8,+4.1] | **14 of 30, PARTIAL** |\n| ~~OFF~~ | 39.0 | 27.5 | −29.6% | — | ~~−46.5%~~ | **INVALID** |\n\n**OFF is invalid and must never be quoted.** `EG_CAPABILITY_ONLY` was checked in `tool_block()` but\nnever in `briefed_tool_block()`, and every cell used the `briefed` family — so the flag was dead while\n`BASE_CAPABILITY_ONLY` worked. The baseline lost its 5-step methodology while eg kept its 4-step one\n(24 lines, 116 words, ending \"STOP. No re-search, no grep to double-check\"). Now wired; the same class\nof bug recurred later with `BASE_GATED_CLAMP` (wired into `tool_block` but not the vendor family).\n**Always diff emitted `prompt.txt`, never trust config.**\n\n---\n\n## 3. The two quantitative laws (use these to predict before spending)\n\n**Law 1 — outcome is set by the BASELINE's wastefulness, not by eg.**\n```\neg_ops = 14.16 + 0.588 · base_ops        break-even at base_ops = 34.4\n```\neg's op count is statistically flat between winners and losers (**d = −0.08, p = 0.97**); the\nbaseline's is decisive (**d = +1.55, p = 0.0069**, AUC 0.865 vs 0.495). Rule accuracy 15/20; it is\nsharp above 54 ops and below 34, mushy in the 35–50 band.\n\n**Law 2 — tokens are superlinear in ops.**\n```\nlog(tokRatio) = 1.207 · log(opRatio)      R² = 0.916\n```\nConfirmed out of sample: rep30 ops −31.2% → predicted −38.6%, measured −40.9%. 94–96% of tokens are\n`cache_read`, so each extra op re-reads the whole accumulated context.\n\n**Corollary — the payload tax is a pure function of session size:** ~0 at 2729k, +7 at 1300k, +18 to\n+28 below 400k. So −25% requires ops ≤ −25% **and** a long session. Every clamp config sits at\n175–378k where the tax alone exceeds the op saving. That is why CB cut 20.6% of ops and still lost.\n\n---\n\n## 4. The confirmed, untried lever: **aim**\n\nMeasured with `/tmp/eg-agx` (entire-graph @ `afd5a1c`, sha `f6a18d3ca7c2`) on 9 rep30 instances,\ngold lines resolved by locating hunk context in the base file (hunk headers are invalid at base —\nfmtlib is off by +272):\n\n| | result |\n|---|---|\n| gold **FILE** in payload | **9/9 = 100%** |\n| gold **LINE** covered by a printed span | **0/9 ≈ 0%** |\n\n| instance | gold line | payload's spans in that same file |\n|---|---|---|\n| lucene-13170 | 148 | 34-36, 27, 181-188, 118-124 — brackets it, never covers it |\n| caddy-5995 | 133 | 343-465, 59 |\n| carbon-3098 | 497 | 1201-1228 |\n| django-13821 | 64 | 431-487 |\n| docusaurus-9183 | 313 | 375 |\n| ruff-15626 | 25 | 37-41 |\n| fastlane-19765 | 101 | 357-366, 214-229 |\n| faker-2970 | 65 | 33-49 |\n| fmt-2457 | 357 | 682 |\n\n**Right file always, right region never.** This is the only mechanism that explains the one result\nthat held across all five Opus cells: **pre-edit locate went UP every time (+3.7% to +9%)**. The agent\ngets the correct file at a wrong offset, greps it anyway, and pays twice.\n\n**Root cause, verified in source** (`internal/sem/search_related.go`):\n- line 41: *\"Deliberately NOT included: outgoing CALLS … already reached as co-members of the same unit\"*\n- line 62: `searchRelatedUnitMemberLimit = 12`; line 568 disables the co-member route above it\n\nSo on a large unit **neither** route reaches the callee. redis-10095 is textbook: gold at\n`src/t_list.c:501`, eg returns `t_list.c:577` (`lpopCommand`, a lexical match on \"LPOP\") — the\nreply-shaping bug is in the helper it *calls*.\n\nFull diagnosis and the F1/F2/F3 proposals: **`/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph/TOKEN-ACCURACY-PLAN.md`**.\nTwo corrections to it from this session:\n1. Its step-2 gate is **cleared**: the unmerged `codex/eg-graphify-advertised-bench` branch does\n   **not** move line coverage (clean A/B, same codebase, coverage identical, payload bytes differ).\n2. Its 32.4%-vs-58.3% winner/loser split does **not** reproduce on this corpus — I measure ~0% for\n   both. So the F1 sizing argument (close a 26-point gap) does not hold here, but the underlying\n   defect is **larger** than diagnosed, not smaller.\n\n**Sizing is the open question**, and the two available routes differ 10×:\n- plan's fit (9.6% tokens per residual shell call × ~3 calls) → −29%/loser → **−22.6%** on the 20-set\n- my decomposition (LOCATE is only **14.5%** of the +76-op loser overrun) → −3.8%/loser → **−12.7%**\n\n**The discriminator, not yet run:** correlate per-instance gold-line coverage against per-instance\nresidual locate ops. If coverage predicts residual ops, the plan's route is right and F1 is worth\n~11 points. Tooling for it exists: `/tmp/mcptest/linecov.py` (resolver verified correct against patch\nshapes — lucene 1 hunk/1+/1− = 2 gold lines, django 4+/2− = 6).\n\n---\n\n## 5. MEASUREMENT INTEGRITY — fix before quoting any number\n\n`tools/netjail/` blocks `curl wget git gh ssh scp rsync nc ncat socat aria2c xh http https`.\nIt does **not** block **npm, yarn, pip, composer, go, cargo** — and every one can fetch a post-fix\nrelease of the repo under test. Three confirmed leaks, in both arms, in cells quoted above:\n\n| instance | arm | leak | that instance's result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| docusaurus-10130 | **eg** | `npm pack @docusaurus/core@3.4.0` → extracted `brokenLinks.js` → grepped it → **the next tool call is the Edit with that content detranspiled**. The issue number `10116` in the patch appears nowhere in the prompt. | **−38% \"winner\"** in the −11.2% cell |\n| caddy-5995 | **baseline** | read `~/go/pkg/mod/…caddy/v2@v2.11.4/replacer.go` (gold line verbatim) **and** the PR's own new test fixture, copied it into the checkout, wrote a test reproducing `test_patch` | −56% winner; 27 of 66 baseline ops |\n| carbon-2752 | **eg** | unzipped `~/Library/Caches/composer/files/nesbot/carbon/*.zip` → gold regex, transcribed into `patch.diff` | +107% loser |\n\nAlso: **fmt-2457's swings are 132% baseline-side** — eg's absolute cost *falls* PUB→G40 (4.25M→2.94M)\nwhile the baseline collapses (5.16M→1.13M). Its PUB \"win\" was bought by 17 baseline messages running a\ntwo-compiler `orig-vs-new` matrix (`g++-15`: 7 occurrences baseline, 0 eg). Treat that instance as noise.\n\n**Required fixes:** netjail shims for registry-fetch subcommands (`npm pack|install <pkg>`, `yarn add`,\n`pip download|install`, `composer require`, `go get`, `cargo add`) while leaving local provisioning\nintact; plus per-instance cache isolation — already implemented in `/tmp/mcptest/s1worker.sh`\n(`GOMODCACHE GOPATH GOCACHE COMPOSER_HOME COMPOSER_CACHE_DIR CARGO_HOME GEM_HOME GEM_PATH\nnpm_config_cache MAVEN_ARGS=-Dmaven.repo.local`).\nThree of the four known leaks favour eg, so closing them will most likely make −11.2% **worse**.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Refuted — do NOT retry. Each cost a cell or a day.\n\nEvery item below was killed by a **winner control**: the same pattern is equally present in the\ninstances the tool wins on, so it cannot explain a loss. A 5-agent sweep produced 38 candidate\ndefects; **27 of 28 adjudicated were refuted this way.**\n\n| claim | how it died |\n|---|---|\n| payload bodies carry no line numbers | true in **20/20** instances incl. every winner. Also `internal/cli/search.go:473` documents that numbering bodies **breaks `Edit` anchors** (agents copy snippet text as `old_string`), and `focus=` already ships |\n| `impact` blind-chained to an ungated rank-1 | off-gold-file target in **7/12 winners**, in *more* degenerate form in the two largest wins |\n| query polluted by GitHub issue-template boilerplate | 2/6 control winners have boilerplate queries producing boilerplate top hits |\n| hits printed out of score order | 5/20 payloads, incl. winners lucene (−52%) and vuejs (−24%) |\n| missing / lint-only `VERIFY` | partial corr collapses +0.184 → **+0.091**; by class **lint-only is BEST** (−24.6%), `none` worst (+20.5%) but contains 2 winners |\n| missing `COVERING TEST` causes test-hunting | **inverted** — present in 4/8 losers (50%) vs 1/12 winners (8%) |\n| \"40% of post-edit ops re-hunt payload text\" | **base rate.** Baseline searches the same strings at 2.42/session vs eg's 2.42 (W) and 1.38 vs 1.25 (L). Payload exposure changes it by +0.00 / −0.13 |\n| provisioning episodes cause the loss | `package-install` **decreases** in losers (0.62→0.38); clumpiness 0.13 in the loser **baseline** vs 0.14 in its eg arm |\n| get the agent to use the graph more | tripling usage (0.20→3.00 calls/session) measured **worse**: caddy −56%→−13%, mean +17.8pt. The 3 winners that called it averaged −23.7% vs −36.9% for the 9 that didn't |\n| index tests (lift `graph_exclude.globs`) | rebuild indexes 4,748 test symbols but search output is **byte-identical**; the gold test was already at rank 2 |\n| extend the covering-test path mirror | 10/12 in a unit test, **byte-identical payloads** on real checkouts — improved the wrong path (`COVERING TEST` comes from ranked results, the mirror only feeds `VERIFY`) |\n| prefetch a test-scoped search (`EG_PREFETCH_TEST`) | found the gold test in **1 of 4**; the query that worked came from the issue text, not the payload |\n| the published prompt's \"explore the repo\" step causes it | only **9%** of first-four pre-edit ops are structure exploration |\n| widen the window (`--head-window-lines` + top-k 20) | **+18.9pt worse** (prior measurement, independently consistent) |\n| payload/prompt token tax explains the split | **5.16%** (W) vs **5.19%** (L) — identical |\n\n---\n\n## 7. Reproduce\n\n```sh\ncd /Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench/agentic-swebench\n# one cell, 40 sessions, ~2h at parallelism 10\nbash /tmp/mcptest/launch.sh /tmp/mcptest/pubworker.sh /tmp/mcptest/pubjobs.txt 10 /tmp/mcptest/pub.log\npython3 tools/model_cmp.py \"PUB_r1_baseline,PUB_r1_eg,label\"\n# aim measurement (free, offline)\npython3 /tmp/mcptest/linecov.py apache__lucene-13170 redis__redis-10095 ...\n```\n\n**Non-negotiables**\n- Gate: `total_cost_usd > 0` AND non-empty `patch.diff`, dropped **symmetrically**.\n- `CENSORED` (`subtype == error_max_turns`) must be 0 per arm.\n- Round trips = unique assistant `message.id`, never `num_turns` (it is `tool_calls + 1`).\n- Parallelism ≤ ~20. Above ~30, empty patches ran 14–27% vs 0% at ~15, and arm symmetry breaks.\n- **Never score a partial cell.** rep30 read −40.9% (n=4) → −24.6% (n=8) → −13.9% (n=10) → −16.5% (n=14).\n- Launcher: use `/tmp/mcptest/launch.sh` (bash, jobs on fd 3). `xargs -P … -I{}` mangles input on\n  macOS, and zsh does not word-split unquoted `$VAR` — that produced a jobs file with 38 of 40 lines\n  malformed and cost two wasted launches.\n- Thinking text is **redacted** in all transcripts (`thinking` present but empty), so reasoning volume\n  is unmeasurable; only block counts and `output_tokens` are available.\n\n## 8. What I would do next, in order\n\n1. **Close the leaks** (§5) and re-measure PUB. Nothing is quotable until this is done, and it will\n   probably make the number worse. One cell, 40 sessions.\n2. **Run the aim discriminator** (§4) — free, offline, decides whether F1 is worth ~11 points or ~2.\n3. **Only if it clears: implement F1** narrowly — enable the callee hop only where the co-member\n   fallback is already off (`len(members) > searchRelatedUnitMemberLimit`) **and** the body-match\n   signal is absent. Budget-neutral: move the window's centre, never widen it. Do **not** start with\n   F2 (multi-span allocation) — that is where a budget-neutral claim is easiest to break.\n4. Gate on gold-**line** coverage offline, then on session tokens **and graded resolves**. File\n   coverage is 100% on winners and losers alike and must be retired as a metric.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e17ef221-8ea7-44cd-89bb-80194e1be0be","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
