{"parentUuid":"b630b6f1-e4c3-4013-a8cd-ea636d7f150a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgRJjSjrx44zyKqiBjyx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012XY4iPNQtNekb48jgJxU3S","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench/agentic-swebench\nmkdir -p handoff-config\nfor f in /tmp/mcptest/pubworker.sh /tmp/mcptest/s1worker.sh /tmp/mcptest/launch.sh /tmp/mcptest/linecov.py \\\n         /tmp/mcptest/pubjobs.txt; do [ -f \"$f\" ] && cp \"$f\" handoff-config/ && echo \"  + $(basename $f)\"; done\ncp tasks/opus20_official.json handoff-config/ 2>/dev/null && echo \"  + opus20_official.json\"\ncat > handoff-config/README.md <<'EOF'\n# handoff-config — everything needed to reproduce the measured cells\n\n- `pubworker.sh`   the config that produces the best honest Opus number (-11.2%, n=20).\n- `s1worker.sh`    same shape, plus the per-instance package-cache isolation (GOMODCACHE, COMPOSER_HOME,\n                   CARGO_HOME, GEM_HOME, npm_config_cache, maven.repo.local). Copy that block into\n                   pubworker.sh when re-measuring with the leaks closed -- see HANDOFF §5.\n- `launch.sh`      parallel launcher. Use this, not `xargs -P .. -I{}` (mangles input on macOS).\n- `linecov.py`     offline gold-LINE coverage measurement. Resolver verified against patch shapes.\n                   This is the tool for the aim discriminator in HANDOFF §4.\n- `pubjobs.txt`    the 40 jobs (20 instances x 2 arms).\n- `opus20_official.json`  the instance set, language-stratified from SWE-bench Multilingual's 300.\n\nScorer lives in the suite: `tools/model_cmp.py`.\nEOF\necho \"  + README.md\"\nrm -f tools/eg-q.bak tools/run_3arm.sh.bak tools/run_3arm.sh.headversion 2>/dev/null\ngit checkout -b opus-token-handoff 2>&1 | tail -1\ngit add -A HANDOFF-OPUS-TOKENS.md handoff-config/ tools/run_3arm.sh tools/eg-q tools/model_cmp.py tools/_egverify.py tools/_eglitdrop.py 2>/dev/null\ngit status --por