{"parentUuid":"9acdf7f7-016f-4bf3-bfe4-d8fdf4dac39c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgRKqXdvAqZTMhZ7nD8v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ERQg6n6zNSpNy2M5aNgHca","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench/agentic-swebench\ngit diff --cached --stat | tail -12\necho \"=== commit ===\"\ngit commit -q -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nhandoff: Opus token measurement — best honest number, two laws, and the one untried lever\n\nGoal was Opus >= -25% tokens on a 20-instance SWE-bench Multilingual sample. Not met.\nBest honest result -11.2% CI [-27.8,+9.6] (n=20) under PUBLISHED_EXACT=1, which gives\nAnthropic's published prompt verbatim to BOTH arms.\n\nHarness changes, all measurement-integrity fixes:\n- PUBLISHED_EXACT=1: the published SWE-bench prompt as the WHOLE prompt, no bolted-on\n  coaching. The prior OFFICIAL_SCAFFOLD path appended this harness's own frugality block,\n  so the emitted prompt contradicted itself (\"spend as few turns as possible\" 20 lines\n  above \"use tools as much as possible, ideally more than 100 times\").\n- EG_CAPABILITY_ONLY wired into briefed_tool_block(). It was only checked in tool_block(),\n  and every cell uses the briefed family, so the flag was DEAD while BASE_CAPABILITY_ONLY\n  worked -- the baseline lost its 5-step methodology while eg kept its 4-step one. That\n  asymmetry produced the withdrawn -46.5%.\n- BASE_GATED_CLAMP + base_gated_clamp_prompt(): the missing symmetric mirror of\n  gated_clamp_eg_prompt, wired into BOTH dispatchers (the vendor family has its own\n  baseline branch -- the same class of bug recurred there).\n- EG_PREFETCH_NOSUPPRESS, EG_PREFETCH_TEST: prefetch variants, each with its own GQLOG so\n  it cannot consume the agent's GQ_SEARCH_CAP budget.\n- tools/model_cmp.py: paired scorer, geomean + bootstrap CI, cost classes reported\n  separately. Reproduces every historical cell.\n\nhandoff-config/ carries the exact worker, launcher, jobs and instance set, plus the\noffline gold-line coverage tool for the open question.\n\nSee HANDOFF-OPUS-TOKENS.md. Key content: two fitted laws (outcome is set by the BASELINE's\nop count, break-even 34.4; tokens = ops^1.207, R2=0.916), 13 refuted mechanisms with the\nwinner-control that killed each, 3 confirmed answer leaks via unblocked package managers,\nand the one confirmed untried lever -- aim: gold FILE coverage 9/9 = 100%, gold LINE\ncoverage ~0%.\nEOF\n)\"\ngit log -1 --format='  %h %s' | head -2\necho \"=== branch state ===\"\ngit status --porcelain | wc -l | tr -d ' ' | sed 's/^/  uncommitted remaining: /'\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the handoff branch"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1436,"cache_read_input_tokens":816613,"output_tokens":1120,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1436,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1120,"cache_read_input_tokens":816613,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1436,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1436},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgRKimbNKD97WiivUZvp","type":"assistant","uuid":"f1a3518d-2940-4ba5-92f4-914ffd8c6713","timestamp":"2026-08-03T20:08:56.347Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
