{"parentUuid":"4ccd62be-1df2-429f-ab34-52f4cc0a3730","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgRzPQboknFgdMcKimxD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Total tokens.**\n\n**This session: 0.64B tokens across 361 sessions, $560.**\n\n| cell | sessions | tokens | usd |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| PUB baseline / eg | 20 / 20 | 55M / 48M | $52.78 / $48.09 |\n| R30PUB baseline / eg | 16 / 16 | 47M / 35M | $49.26 / $37.41 |\n| OFF r1+r2 (invalid) | 78 | 176M | $174.72 |\n| G40 baseline / eg | 20 / 20 | 29M / 37M | $32.49 / $37.82 |\n| HOFF (haiku) | 40 | 82M | $14.24 |\n| SOFF (sonnet) | 40 | 71M | $38.07 |\n| S1O | 40 | 9M | $15.93 |\n| CB + GC | 39 | 17M | $28.05 |\n| USEA + USEB probes | 12 | 31M | $30.93 |\n\n**Whole suite, all time: 12.90B tokens across 11,965 sessions, $5,328.**\n\nClass split across all of it — this is the cost model the whole analysis rests on:\n\n| class | tokens | share |\n|---|---|---|\n| cache_read | 12.35B | **95.7%** |\n| cache_creation | 405M | 3.1% |\n| output | 147M | 1.1% |\n| input | 2.2M | — |\n\nThat 95.7% is why the ops law works: nearly every token is a re-read of accumulated context, so cost tracks the *number of messages*, not the size of any single result — which is exactly why `tokens = ops^1.207` fits at R² 0.916.\n\nTwo things I'd flag about my own spend. **$175 of the $560 went to the OFF cells**, which turned out to be invalid on prompt asymmetry — that's 31% spent on a number I had to withdraw. And the clamp configs (S1O, CB, GC) cost only $44 combined because they collapse sessions to 4–11 ops, which is also precisely why they couldn't win: at 175–378k per session the payload tax exceeds any op saving.\n\nrep30's resume is still running and will add roughly $50–70 more."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2003,"cache_read_input_tokens":833563,"output_tokens":732,"server_tool_use"