{"parentUuid":"0b92d0fc-a95a-4d2d-ac82-781009b95bf3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgSBkBKWmrYML6rfGtzA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3324,"cache_read_input_tokens":836355,"output_tokens":2538,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3324,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2538,"cache_read_input_tokens":836355,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3324,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3324},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgSBaX9JhrkS5kkYm4Rc","type":"assistant","uuid":"9090ca0f-f16b-418e-a326-1b94a428c93a","timestamp":"2026-08-03T20:20:22.860Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"9090ca0f-f16b-418e-a326-1b94a428c93a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgSBkBKWmrYML6rfGtzA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Answer to your tip, and it's measured — the graph currently does *not* reduce cache_read via smaller context. It reduces it purely by cutting messages, and its payload works against it.**\n\n`cache_read = messages × context-per-message`, PUB cell, per session:\n\n| | msgs | cache_read | ctx/msg | prompt bytes | tool-result bytes | output tokens |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| baseline | 46.9 | 2,623k | 56k | 2,950 | 61k | 34,581 |\n| eg | 40.0 | 2,315k | **58k** | **12,251** | 57k | 30,661 |\n| delta | **−14.6%** | **−11.8%** | **+3.3%** | **+315%** | **−6.8%** | −11.3% |\n\nLog-attribution of the −11.8% cache_read saving:\n\n- **message count: +126% of it** — it does more than all the work\n- **context-per-message: −26% of it** — it actively *subtracts* from the saving\n\nSo the payload adds **+9.3 KB to the cached prefix of every single message** (+315% prompt) while removing only **6.8%** of tool-result bytes. The graph's answers are not replacing the volume of file reads.\n\n**And here's why \"return smaller answers\" is a weak lever, which I think is the real answer to your question.** Per session the context content is roughly: prompt ~740 tokens + tool results ~15,250 tokens + agent output ~34,581 tokens ≈ 50k. Yet average context *per message* is **56k** — higher than the total content. That means there's a large **fixed prefix** (system prompt + tool definitions) that dominates, and it's re-read on every message regardless of what the tool returns.\n\nWhich is exactly why `tokens = ops^1.207` fits at R² 0.916 while every byte-level change I made moved nothing: **cache_read is near-linear in message count and nearly indifferent to payload size.** Shrinking the payload buys ~3%; deleting a message buys ~2%*of the whole session*.\n\nSo the graph's lever on cache_read is real but singular — it must **delete turns**. The two ways it could: aim correctly so the agent doesn't grep the file it was handed (the confirmed 100%-file/0%-line defect), or shrink the agent's own output, which is 2.3× the tool-result volume and the largest single component of context growth.\n\n**rep30 now: n=17/30, −22.9% CI [−40.1, −3.3], winners 11/17.** 82M tokens burned in that cell so far (46M baseline + 36M eg)."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3324,"cache_read_input_tokens":836355,"output_tokens":2538,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3324,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2538,"cache_read_input_tokens":836355,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3324,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3324},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgSBaX9JhrkS5kkYm4Rc","type":"assistant","uuid":"5c702264-9cd1-4e2d-b40a-6d2f4fcf14bf","timestamp":"2026-08-03T20:20:33.246Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
