{"parentUuid":"76b1aba0-60dd-4da0-9dd9-c3d4f2fae4b3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgSFbo9i1DKZcMN6Wn14","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Update — 6 of 30 resume jobs done, still 17 gated pairs: −22.9% [−40.1, −3.3], winners 11/17.**\n\nFive more sessions finished but no new *pairs* — they're single arms waiting on their partner to land, which is normal mid-cell.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| **wins (11)** | framework-48636 −79%, lucene −58%, caddy −52%, micropython-15898 −41%, carbon-3098 −39%, gson-2479 −37%, hugo-12204 −36%, django −35%, gson-2158 −33%, docusaurus-9183 −19%, ruff −7% |\n| **losses (6)** | fmt-2457 +46%, fluentd +45%, faker +33%, hugo-12562 +32%, fastlane +31%, nushell-13246 +21% |\n\nTwo details worth noting while it runs. **hugo splits both ways** — hugo-12204 at −36% and hugo-12562 at +32%, same repo, opposite outcomes — which is more evidence that language and repo aren't stable predictors and the break-even law (baseline op count) is doing the real work. And **micropython-15898 came in at −41%**, which is interesting because the aim measurement showed it at 0% gold-line coverage; another confirmation that wins are coming from replacing a wasteful baseline rather than from aiming well.\n\n13 pairs to go. Waiter still armed; I'll build the artifact off the complete n=30 and then hand over the continuation prompt."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":935,"cache_read_input_tokens":842220,"output_tokens":871,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":935,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":871,"cache_read_input_tokens":842220,"cache_creation_input_tokens":935,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_inp