{"parentUuid":"55268e68-5180-486a-9643-b0c7cbdfb0bc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgSsHCDU7B4sXaoQg4HL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**rep30 total token savings — n=19/30 gated (a 19th pair landed as I ran this), still partial:**\n\n| | baseline | eg | delta |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **total tokens** | 54.1M | 42.6M | **−11.5M** |\n| per session | 2,850k | 2,245k | −605k |\n| total usd | $57.19 | $46.03 | −$11.17 |\n\n- **Aggregate token saving: −21.2%** (11.5M tokens fewer)\n- **Geomean per-instance: −21.8%**, CI [−38.0, −3.7]\n- usd −19.5%, winners 12/19\n\nAggregate and geomean agree closely (−21.2% vs −21.8%), which means the result isn't an artefact of how ratios are averaged — a handful of instances aren't carrying it.\n\nBy cost class:\n\n| class | baseline | eg | delta |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| cache_read | 52.1M | 40.9M | **−21.5%** |\n| output | 0.7M | 0.5M | **−22.3%** |\n| cache_creation | 1.4M | 1.2M | −12.8% |\n\nAll three move together, and output falls as much as cache_read — that's the healthy pattern. Output is the expensive class for Opus (~$24.73/Mtok vs $0.50 for cache_read), so a saving concentrated there is worth more per point than the headline implies, which is why usd is only −19.5% while tokens are −21.2%.\n\nStanding caveats: **11 pairs still outstanding and they're loser-weighted** on prior evidence (redis-10095 has lost in all four configs it's appeared in; preact-3010 and lombok-3486 lost under FRUGAL), so I expect this to drift up. And this cell carries the open **npm/pip/composer/go/cargo** network hole with no cache isolation, so it isn't a quotable number even when complete."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1387,"cache_read_input_tokens":846419,"output_tokens":636,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_cre