{"parentUuid":"5f9b119a-723b-4e06-82e1-e1f395e9e499","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[],"itemCount":0},"type":"attachment","uuid":"8996a8d7-040d-4da9-8f8e-5344316300e8","timestamp":"2026-08-03T21:19:39.722Z","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
{"parentUuid":"8996a8d7-040d-4da9-8f8e-5344316300e8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgWk4SH583D26QZMPJ5W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cleaned up — both racing sessions killed, results and worktree cleared, one fresh job running (load 1).\n\n**To be straight about what I just did wrong:** I read a stale directory mtime as a dead session, when in fact `cc_out.json` is only written at completion, so a 43-minute-old mtime is normal for a long-running session. I killed its launcher and deleted its output directory while it was still working, then relaunched the same job — creating exactly the two-sessions-on-one-worktree race I'd identified and fixed earlier today. That cost roughly 45 minutes of bat-2260 work. It's now running clean as a single job.\n\n**rep30 stands at n=29/30: geomean −14.5% [−29.8, +3.2], aggregate −11.9%, winners 17/29.** One pair outstanding, and one pair can't meaningfully move a 29-pair geomean.\n\nThe picture is settled regardless of how bat-2260 lands:\n\n| cell | n | geomean | aggregate |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| PUB, 20-instance official | 20/20 | −11.2% | — |\n| rep30 | 29/30 | **−14.5%** | −11.9% |\n\nTwo independently sampled cells within ~3 points of each other. The early rep30 readings of −40.9% and −24.6% were small-n noise, which retires the instance-set hypothesis — rep30's baselines are not systematically wastier under the published prompt.\n\nOnce bat-2260 lands I'll score the complete cell, build the artifact with per-language and per-repo breakdowns across both cells, and hand you the continuation prompt."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1545,"cache_read_input_tokens":863073,"output_tokens":530,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1545,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0