{"parentUuid":"a2cb498f-9282-410f-b451-b444b6332385","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgYZmTGzDVKVBmEVeTym","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Artifact published:** https://claude.ai/code/artifact/d16079e5-7734-46b0-b7a4-a61e9845c7d0\n\nIt carries the verdict panel, both cells, per-language and per-repo breakdowns, every instance with signed bars, the two fitted laws, the aim defect, the 12 refuted mechanisms with the control that killed each, the leak warning, and the next steps.\n\n**Final numbers:**\n\n| cell | n | geomean | CI | aggregate | winners |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 20-instance official | 20 | **−11.2%** | [−27.8, +9.6] | −11.4% | 12/20 |\n| rep30 | 29 | **−14.5%** | [−29.7, +3.4] | −11.9% | 17/29 |\n\nTarget was −25%. **Not reached in either cell.** Both agree within ~3 points and aggregate matches geomean in both, so no single instance is carrying the result.\n\nNow the continuation prompt for the next agent:\n\n---\n\n> Pick up the Opus token work in `/Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench/agentic-swebench`, branch `opus-token-handoff`. Read `HANDOFF-OPUS-TOKENS.md` first, then `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph/TOKEN-ACCURACY-PLAN.md`. Config to reproduce is in `handoff-config/`.\n>\n> Goal: **Opus ≥ −25% tokens**, honestly measured. Current best is −11.2% (n=20) and −14.5% (n=29). Do not accept those as the ceiling — 12 mechanisms are refuted with numbers, but one is confirmed and untried.\n>\n> **Do these in order and do not skip step 1.**\n>\n> 1. **Close the answer leaks, then re-measure.** `tools/netjail/` blocks curl/wget/git but not npm, pip, composer, go or cargo. Three instances read the fix: docusaurus-10130's tool arm ran `npm pack @docusaurus/core@3.4.0` and transcribed the gold patch; caddy's baseline read the gold line out of `~/go/pkg/mod`; carbon's tool arm read it from the composer cache. Add netjail shims for registry fetches only, keep local provisioning working, and use the cache isolation already in `handoff-config/s1worker.sh`. Expect the number to get *worse* — three of four leaks favour the tool. A number measured with the hole open is not a number.\n> 2. **Run the aim discriminator.** Free, offline, no sessions: correlate per-instance gold-line coverage against per-instance residual locate ops, using `handoff-config/linecov.py`. Measured: gold **file** coverage 9/9 = 100%, gold **line** coverage ~0%. Two estimates of what fixing it is worth differ by 10× (−22.6% vs −12.7% on the 20-set); this decides which.\n> 3. **If it clears, implement the callee hop** in `entire-graph/internal/sem/search_related.go`. Line 41 excludes outgoing CALLS because callees are \"already reached as co-members of the same unit\"; line 62 sets `searchRelatedUnitMemberLimit = 12` and line 568 disables that fallback above it — so on a large unit neither route reaches the callee. Enable the hop **only** where the fallback is already off and the body-match signal is absent. Budget-neutral: move the window's centre, never widen it (wider measured +18.9pt worse).\n>\n> **Rules that cost me a day each.** Verify on emitted artifacts, never config — a flag checked in one dispatcher but not the one every cell uses produced a −46.5% headline I had to withdraw. Never score a partial cell — rep30 read −40.9% at n=4 and −14.5% at n=29. A stale directory mtime does not mean a dead session; `cc_out.json` is written only at completion, and I destroyed 45 minutes of work by assuming otherwise. Every candidate defect must be checked against the instances the tool *wins* on; that killed 27 of 28 of mine. And when a prediction fails, say so and find the mechanism — don't retune the framing.\n>\n> The two fitted laws are your predictor: `eg_ops = 14.16 + 0.588 · base_ops` (break-even 34.4) and `tokens = ops^1.207` (R² 0.916). Use them to size a change *before* spending 40 sessions on it."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":507,"cache_read_input_tokens":879849,"output_tokens":1500,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":507,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1500,"cache_read_input_tokens":879849,"cache_creation_input_tokens":507,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":507},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgYZbZTZeQSEBNFPoYQW","type":"assistant","uuid":"4747be73-3e93-45a6-9a05-0c9c2cb67dc4","timestamp":"2026-08-03T21:44:00.426Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
