{"parentUuid":"304e0059-c3e9-4afb-a95e-d7a406d42961","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdgYnU1QE6aYhbbaBQgZt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Update — everything is delivered. One session still finishing in the background.**\n\n| deliverable | state |\n|---|---|\n| branch | `opus-token-handoff` @ `ed21139`, committed |\n| handoff doc | `HANDOFF-OPUS-TOKENS.md` |\n| config bundle | `handoff-config/` — 7 files |\n| artifact | [published](https://claude.ai/code/artifact/d16079e5-7734-46b0-b7a4-a61e9845c7d0) |\n| continuation prompt | given in my previous message |\n\n**Final numbers: −11.2% (n=20, official) and −14.5% (n=29, rep30).** Target was −25%, not reached.\n\nbat-2260's eg arm is at 27 minutes (load 1). It's the 30th pair and cannot move a 29-pair geomean by more than a fraction of a point, so the artifact and handoff are built on final data. If it lands I'll note it; if it times out at the 3600s cap the cell closes at n=29, which is what everything already reports.\n\nTwo things I'd want you to carry forward, because they're the parts I'd defend:\n\n**The measurement is now trustworthy in a way it wasn't this morning.** The −46.5% headline came from a dead flag that stripped the baseline's methodology while leaving the tool's intact; that's wired and verified on emitted prompts. Two independently sampled cells now agree within 3 points.\n\n**And there's one confirmed defect nobody has tried to fix** — gold file coverage 9/9, gold line coverage ~0%, root-caused to `search_related.go:41` excluding outgoing CALLS with the co-member fallback dead above 12 members. It's the only thing that explains pre-edit locate rising in all five configurations, and the discriminator to size it is free.\n\nI didn't hit the goal. The honest reason is that the tool's op-count saving is bounded by how wasteful the no-tool baseline happens to be on a given instance, and on Opus that averages out to the low teens — not that there's a config left untried, but that the one real defect remains unfixed and unsized."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":979,"cache_read_input_tokens":881859,"output_tokens":690,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":979,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":690,"cache_read_input_tokens":881859,"cache_creation_input_tokens":979,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":979},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdgYnLVhxJFZ6BhphzSJw","type":"assistant","uuid":"51937b0a-79c1-43c2-b5c3-cae7a654d236","timestamp":"2026-08-03T21:46:41.638Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"modular-cooking-cupcake"}
